 ```
 
+On Linux x86-64 GNU, the default prebuilt sherpa library and whisper.cpp must
+use the same libstdc++ string ABI. The CI toolchain sets this for whisper.cpp;
+for a standalone build, opt into it from the repository root:
+
+```bash
+export CMAKE_TOOLCHAIN_FILE="$PWD/packages/rust_transcription/cmake/linux-ci-toolchain.cmake"
+# Required once when migrating an existing build: whisper-rs-sys does not
+# automatically rebuild when this toolchain file changes.
+cargo clean --manifest-path packages/rust_transcription/Cargo.toml -p whisper-rs-sys
+cargo build --locked --manifest-path packages/rust_transcription/Cargo.toml --release --bin rust-transcription-cpu
+```
+
+Without the toolchain, an x86-64 GNU build can abort while loading SenseVoice.
+The flag is scoped to that target and the pinned sherpa archive. It takes
+precedence over global C++ flags; custom native libraries, toolchains or
+target-specific compiler flags may require a different configuration. Desktop
+sidecar preparation selects this toolchain automatically when none is specified,
+and uses an ABI-versioned subdirectory of the normal Cargo target directory so
+old native objects cannot be reused. A custom generic or target-scoped CMake
+toolchain is preserved with a warning; its ABI and cache invalidation remain
+the caller's responsibility. When host- and target-scoped settings conflict,
+preparation conservatively treats either custom setting as caller-managed even
+if it would not apply to the current build. GPU and other platform behavior has
+not been verified by the Linux CPU check.
