d. Typed callback buffers now use callback-scoped views; typed output is zeroed before creating Rust sample references, metadata and overlap are checked, and the owned input allocation is validated after rendering. Data and Sample are now unsafe traits: these are API and output-initialization behavior changes. Unpacked 24-bit PCM and contradictory numeric flags are rejected. Parsed ASBDs validate rates, channels, frame strides and packet sizes; the AudioUnit setter uses checked conversion. Public `to_asbd` now returns a `Result` and rejects overflow instead of panicking or wrapping; `try_to_asbd` remains an alias. Packed formats with high-aligned flags are rejected. This is a breaking API change; the updated examples have not been compiled on an Apple target. Typed multi-byte views reject foreign-endian samples while byte views preserve them. Simulated buffer tests and compile-fail checks passed, while real CoreAudio driver assumptions and iOS compilation remain unverified. Other platform-gated JACK, WebAudio, Emscripten, ASIO, Android and WASAPI findings need independent assessment on their targets.\n- WASAPI worker-priority setup now passes the current-thread pseudo-handle instead of a thread ID, so the existing best-effort time-critical request can take effect. Portable mock tests and a Windows-target type-check passed. The standalone native Windows priority test step passed in CI on this head; physical audio behavior and scheduling contention remain unverified.\n- ALSA playback pause now returns native unsupported and I/O errors instead of silently succeeding. Null-device fault injection covers those errors and a simulated successful return. The playback `play` path still ignores resume errors and needs separate state-handling work; physical playback is unverified.\n- ALSA capture-capability invalidation is now limited to checked open failures reporting ENODEV or ENOENT; setup failures and transient busy or permission errors retain the prior observation. Nine capture-only null-device/preload cases verify discovery and continuing callbacks while another stream is live, and reprobe after checked release. For other failures the cache may be stale until probing is possible again; physical-device behavior remains unverified.\n- CPAL CoreAudio `asbd_from_config` now sets signed-integer flags for signed formats and floating-point flags for both F32 and F64. The portable adapter reproduced the incorrect flags before the fix and covers all ten CPAL sample formats and their layout afterward. It does not prove a device supports those formats; macOS lint and the packaged build passed on head `a2fecfa3`, but iOS compilation and physical-device behavior remain unverified.\n- AssemblyAI, ElevenLabs and Deepgram retain partial text while propagating a provider failure warning, with provider tests. The Socket `web-sys` alert has not been fully assessed. WASAPI `Device::name()` still has an `OpenPropertyStore` panic and unsafe property decoding requiring separate assessment and target verification.\n- Isolated ALSA unit suite depends in part on physical/default PCM and sequencer devices absent here. The null-device fault cases above do not prove physical-driver behavior. Desktop package builds passed on macOS and Windows CI, but physical devices, release packaging and signing remain unverified (sandbox coverage gaps G12 and G14 and accepted platform gaps).\n- Sonar reanalysis of `04a6a3bf` reports zero new issues and zero annotations. Fallow's warning-level exit does not mean all clone groups or complexity findings were eliminated.\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>Review requests and babysitting</summary>\n\n- On `04a6a3bf`, [CodeAnt re-review](https://github.com/maus-inc/mausVoice/pull/322#issuecomment-6747796389) approved; [CodeRabbit re-review](https://github.com/maus-inc/mausVoice/pull/322#issuecomment-6747801955) skipped because 176 files exceed its 150-file limit. Buoy flagged a pre-existing MUI spacing multiplier, not an 8px lite