+      "description": "## Summary\n\nVendors the `stageshow` skill (benjitaylor/skills, MIT) into `.agents/skills/` byte for byte with a `skills-lock.json` entry, and makes it mandatory for any change that touches any form of UI in any file. `engineering/design-skills.md` gains a `## Stageshow on every UI touch` section with a two-mode rule: product mode (desktop, preview, Rust pills, installer) takes the skill's judgment only, never its kit or `--ss-*` tokens, and `DESIGN.md` wins every conflict; illustrated mode (docs site, marketing, README assets, PR GIFs) takes the whole skill from a scratch copy. `AGENTS.md`, `.agents/PREFLIGHT.md`, `apps/desktop/DESIGN.md` and the design-system baseline all bind to it, and `docs/decisions/stageshow-on-every-ui-touch.md` records the decision and what was read before making it.\n\nVendoring surfaced a real hazard: the root `.gitignore` ignores every `package-lock.json`, `stageshow` ships one, and a plain `git add` staged 371 of 372 files, so the first fresh checkout would have failed the hash. The second commit turns that from a manual check into a gate. `scripts/ci/verify-skills.mjs` now runs `git check-ignore --no-index` over every file of every locked tree and fails with an `IGNORED` line naming the file and the fix; a new `node:test` suite drives it in a `git init` temp repo; and a new `verify-skills.yml` workflow runs both on push, because until now the only executor was the pre-commit hook.\n\nNo application code changes. Touches `.agents/`, `engineering/`, `docs/`, `scripts/ci/`, `.github/workflows/`, `lefthook.yml`, `.gitignore`, and two desktop design documents.\n\n## Verification gate\n\nHead SHA: `2c2ae1b7c506b1841f978a04000f6b14300bbdbc`\n\n- `pnpm install --frozen-lockfile`: passed (with `--ignore-scripts` and `CHROMEDRIVER_SKIP_DOWNLOAD=true`; the sandbox cannot fetch the chromedriver binary)\n- `pnpm run lint`: passed\n- `pnpm run check-types`: passed\n- `pnpm run build`: passed (11 tasks)\n- `pnpm run test`: 406