sumers see the change: none\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>Code research gate</summary>\n\n- Queries searched: \"Stageshow skill GitHub\", \"benjitaylor skills stageshow\", upstream repo at `benjitaylor/skills` HEAD `299140f`; local greps for `ui-capture`, `skills:verify`, `verify-skills`, `check-ignore`, `node --test` across workflows\n- Sources, with the assumption each one verified: upstream `SKILL.md`, all 15 references, every script header and `browser.mjs`/`dev.mjs`/`film.mjs` in full (assumption: no network imports in scripts, verified by grep for `node:http/https/net/dns`); benji.org/stageshow (MIT, released 2026-10-31); `scripts/ci/check-workspace-hygiene.test.mjs` (assumption: a new `.test.mjs` must be wired to a workflow, verified by the guard failing until the workflow existed)\n- Pattern class named, plus every other location where the same root cause could recur: \"a root `.gitignore` rule swallows a file inside a vendored, whole-folder-hashed tree\". Other root rules that can do the same to a future skill: `build`, `dist`, `models`, `coverage`, `*.log`, `out/`. The gate covers all of them because it asks git, not a fixed list.\n- Edge cases considered and their disposition: force-added ignored file (still flagged, `--no-index`, tested); skill with no files (short-circuit, tested); `git check-ignore` exit codes 0/1/other (list, none, throw); `installMode: \"copy\"` in the lock entry (inert to the verifier, documented); running the skill's scripts inside the vendored folder (forbidden, `npm install` there measured as DRIFT)\n- Failed attempts: first Execution-limits row landed in the routing table, moved; hand-written tables failed prettier, fixed with `--write`; `film.mjs --still` exits 2 without Chrome, recorded as gap G9\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>Proactive and deep refinement evidence</summary>\n\nProactive protocol.\n\n- Intent hypothesis, 1 to 2 sentences: the human wants Stageshow available offline in the repo and wants no UI change, in any file type, to escape it.\n- Pattern class and instances found, with search evidence: every document that already binds a design skill (`design-skills.md` routing table, `AGENTS.md` design section, `PREFLIGHT.md`, `DESIGN.md`, the baseline) was found by grepping `ui-capture` and `stitch-design-taste`; each gained a Stageshow binding.\n- Proposal presented, minimal against comprehensive scope, file list, and the verification that proves the class is fixed: the `.gitignore` gate was proposed as a follow-up after the first commit and the human said \"continue\"; the test suite and the workflow prove it.\n- Human confirmation evidence: the follow-up was offered in the session and accepted before it was built.\n\nDeep refinement.\n\n- Detail gaps checked: not a UI change; both theme modes not applicable.\n- Edge cases enumerated and dispositioned, with the verification for each: see the research gate above, each with a test in `verify-skills.test.mjs`.\n- Missing features researched: a CI executor for `skills:verify` (must, implemented); `--strict` mode for unrecorded skills (already existed, now tested).\n- Refinement verification: focused `node --test` per edit, full gate on the final tree.\n\nDepth pass, from `AGENTS.md` section 2b.\n\n- Field named: supply-chain hygiene for vendored agent skills.\n- Moves taken that the task did not ask for: the ignored-file gate, the workflow, the test suite, the lefthook glob widening.\n- Rawest material started from: the upstream tree at a pinned commit and `git add -n` output.\n- Methods and tools used: `diff -rq` against upstream, `git add -n`, `git check-ignore`, a fresh `git clone --no-local`.\n- Gate per claim: every claim above was run; none is a hypothesis.\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>Design and UI confirmation</summary>\n\n- Product UI touched: no\n- Design files read before the first edit: `apps/desktop/DESIGN.md` and `apps/desktop/docs/design-system-baseline.md`, read to place the Stageshow binding; no