+      "description": "## Summary\n\nThis change adds matte 3D shortcut keys to onboarding, the dashboard, settings and the release dialog. It also makes onboarding shortcut capture save completed chords, cancel on focus loss, and recover from failed writes without letting older saves replace newer ones.\n\n## Verification gate\n\nHead SHA: `419c4dd82fbb91f7a511c331047ca7c72e82bb5d`\n\n- Frozen-lockfile install: passed with `CHROMEDRIVER_SKIP_DOWNLOAD=true`.\n- Workspace lint, typecheck and build: passed with `turbo run ... --concurrency=1`.\n- Workspace test: failed because 54 provider-backed tests in three files need `GROQ_API_KEY`. The run passed 4,067 desktop tests, 523 voice-ai tests, 24 agent tests and 22 preview tests.\n- Focused keycap and shortcut regression suites: 137 passed across eight files.\n- Formatting, skill verification and secret-history scan: passed. The secret scan exercised the real gitleaks binary.\n- CI guard tests: 399 passed.\n- i18n extract and sync: passed in the previous review-fix pass; CI catalog sync passed on this head.\n- Desktop runner script tests: four passed.\n- Native bindings: not applicable. No command signatures or generated bindings changed.\n- Desktop WebDriver and OS input: not run. A packaged native desktop runtime and physical input were not available for these scenarios. Browser preview and component tests are substitutes, not native evidence.\n- Native desktop clippy and 419 library tests passed in an earlier run of the same native sources with the CI sidecar override. They were not rerun after the final TypeScript-only changes. Packaging was not verified.\n\n<details>\n<summary>Changes and scope</summary>\n\nThe renderer lives in `apps/desktop/src/components/common/Keycap3d.tsx` and its geometry, raster, texture and worker modules. `KeyPressSimulator.tsx` owns the onboarding motion. `KeybindingsForm.tsx` owns capture and save coordination. The consumers are the dashboard, settings and release dialog. `apps/preview/specs/keycap-3d.md` records the provisional geometry and the unverified reference match. The bundled Geist Pixel font and its license are under `packages/shared-fonts/geist-pixel/` and the desktop assets.\n\nNo dependency, native command, migration, capability, CSP or workflow changed. The new locale strings have translations in all supported locales, but those translations have not been reviewed by native speakers.\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>Code research and review</summary>\n\nThe review traced keycap raster scheduling, canvas recovery, press animation, shortcut capture, persistence and native sync. Searches covered worker failure and cancellation, canvas restoration, focus loss during shortcut capture, React effect cleanup and reduced motion. Sources included [MDN canvas restoration](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/API/HTMLCanvasElement/contextrestored_event), [MDN accessibility media queries](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/CSS/Guides/Media_queries/Using_for_accessibility), [React effect cleanup](https://react.dev/learn/synchronizing-with-effects), and [a comparable shortcut focus-loss fix](https://github.com/Juliusolsson05/agent-code/pull/1308).\n\nThe relevant pattern is asynchronous work outliving its owner. Tests cover queued worker work, cancellation, failure fallback, capture blur and unmount, writes completing out of order, failed writes, a form remount during a pending write, and a local-data clear while a write is pending. A remount race and a clear race were reproduced before their fixes. Native shortcut sync also has a store subscription outside this form. Onboarding, individual hotkey settings, and dictation-language settings now share a persistence queue; a cross-editor race was reproduced and tested. The separate style-hotkey editor and the independent native-sync subscriber are not serialized by this queue.\n\nThe original matched-size visual reference was unavailable in this pass. One-to-one visual fidelity remains unverified. Worker and local raster comparison, forced-color emulation and reduced-motion checks were performed in the earlier browser pass. Emulation does not establish native WebKit or Windows behavior.\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>Design and UI confirmation</summary>\n\nThe work follows `apps/desktop/DESIGN.md`, `apps/desktop/docs/design-system-baseline.md`, `engineering/design-skills.md` and `engineering/motion-design.md`. The real `Keycap3d` preview was inspected in Chromium at device pixel ratio 2 in light and dark modes. Both the front and angled renders appeared, and the page reported no browser errors. With workers disabled, the fully rendered fallback screenshot was pixel-identical to the previous screenshot. The development preview still showed long startup tasks in both worker and workerless runs, largely attributed by a browser CPU profile to React development-mode JSX; this is not a production performance benchmark. The preview is not a native desktop runtime.\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>Review requests and outstanding verification</summary>\n\nThe user requested bot review. The supplied DeepScan diagnostics and available actionable CodeAnt and CodeRabbit feedback were addressed on this head. DeepScan passed, CodeAnt approved, and CodeRabbit reported no new inline actionable comments, but its docstring-coverage pre-merge assessment is 0% for two analyzed functions and did not identify their locations. The platform builds passed. The preceding DeepSource JavaScript report listed 171 findings but only a partial inventory was accessible. At head `419c4dd`, DeepSource reported 38 JavaScript findings and grades A overall, A security, A reliability, A complexity and A hygiene. The full finding inventory is not accessible, so complete remediation is not verified. CodeRabbit suggested canceling the 2D context-loss event; that is contrary to the documented 2D behavior and was declined with a source citation. Native input, actual high-contrast settings, multi-monitor DPR transitions, screen readers, installers, and a matched reference comparison still need verification. Style-hotkey edits and the independent native-sync subscriber remain outside the shared shortcut persistence queue.\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>Review and babysit log</summary>\n\n| Round | Head | Result |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| 1 | `bf84de3` | CodeAnt identified synchronous fallback and cross-editor ordering; CodeRabbit identified activation-key capture. DeepScan reported one issue without accessible details. Sonar quality gate passed with ten annotations. |\n| 2 | `c8066bc` | Fixes and regression tests for actionable comments; Sonar findings addressed. DeepScan reported two issues. |\n| 3 | `80f7339` | Updated the inherited base; implemented available analyzer and bot feedback, including a reproduced cross-editor deletion race. DeepScan passed; DeepSource listed 124 findings. CodeRabbit requested shared save coordination. |\n| 4 | `24234ef` | Moved transaction coordination into the shared queue, fixed cross-editor rollback races, and addressed further analyzer findings. DeepScan passed; DeepSource reported 121 findings; CodeRabbit identified incorrect native-sync failure feedback. |\n| 5 | `4815620` | Corrected activation-failure feedback, verified regressions, and addressed analyzer findings. CI completed; DeepSource reported 78 findings and hygiene B. CodeRabbit confirmed the prior inline finding was fixed; its requested head review was skipped. |\n| 6 | `debc759` | Addressed further worker and geometry-test findings. DeepSource reported 70 findings and A in all graded dimensions. CodeRabbit requested stronger activation-error assertions. |\n| 7 | `02aa9a3` | Strengthened activation-error assertions. DeepSource reported 46 findings with A grades. CodeRabbit noted a possible future test flake but did not verify a present defect. |\n| 8 | `419c4dd` | Made deferred test actions use the explicit async effect flush; local gate