+      "description": "## **User description**\n## Summary\n\nThis change implements the acceptance work for five desktop issues in mausVoice, a Tauri 2 desktop dictation app whose renderer is React 19 with MUI: #299 (setting-row switch press transform), #300 (saved-audio startup latency), #301 (sidebar route prefetch), #307 (version-tag overlap in the dashboard menu), and #308 (eye toggle in the preview popup). Alongside the five, it includes one verification-discovered rescue: the metal-fx WebGL2 selection path crashed on unsupported GPU stacks and now falls back to the backend that reported readiness. The work spans `apps/desktop` (components, store, actions, tests), `apps/docs`, and `apps/preview`, with no Rust, workflow, or generated-binding changes. The full native `test:webdriver` acceptance suite passes 6/6 on the vendored GTK toolchain, and every gate below ran on this head.\n\n## Verification gate\n\nHead SHA: `f5fe1bff`\n\n- `pnpm install --frozen-lockfile`: passed\n- `pnpm run lint`: passed\n- `pnpm run check-types`: passed (9 tasks)\n- `pnpm run build`: passed (11/11)\n- `pnpm run test`: passed except the `GROQ_API_KEY` integration family — utilities 137/137, preview 22/22, voice-ai 518/518, agent 24/24, desktop 3767/3821 with 54 GROQ-keyed tests skipped\n- `pnpm run format:check`: passed\n- `pnpm run skills:verify`: passed\n- `pnpm run test:secret-scan`: passed\n- `node --test scripts/ci/*.test.mjs`: passed (393 assertions, 0 failures)\n- `pnpm gen:bindings` produced no diff: not applicable — the diff contains no Rust command, event, or type changes that `bindings.ts` mirrors\n\nPer-package gates, when the change touches that package:\n\n- `pnpm --filter desktop check-types` and `pnpm --filter desktop lint`: passed\n- `pnpm --filter desktop test`: 3767/3821; the 54 failures are the `GROQ_API_KEY`-keyed integration tests in the desktop suite (same family as the root run)\n- `pnpm --filter @maus-inc/voice-ai test`: passed (518/518)\n- `pnpm --filter @repo/agent test`: passed (24/24)\n- `pnpm --filter @maus-inc/preview test`: passed (22/22)\n- `pnpm --filter desktop test:integration`: 2 GROQ-keyed failures; the non-network cases pass\n- `pnpm --filter desktop test:webdriver`: passed 6/6 (app.render 1/1, contracts 5/5) against a debug build of this head on the vendored GTK sysroot toolchain (tauri-driver + WebKitWebDriver + Xvfb)\n\nRust gates, when the change touches any of the seven Cargo workspaces:\n\n- `cargo fmt --check` in the six gated crates: not applicable — no `.rs` file changed (the covered paths would be `apps/desktop/src-tauri`, `packages/rust_transcription`, `packages/rust_pill_shared`, `packages/rust_gtk_pill`, `apps/desktop/src-tauri/src/commands.rs`, `apps/desktop/src-tauri/src/database/rows/user.rs` and their workspace siblings)\n- `cargo clippy --locked -- -D warnings` in `apps/desktop/src-tauri`, and `--all-targets` in `packages/rust_pill_shared`: not applicable, same reason\n- `CARGO_BUILD_JOBS=1 cargo test --locked --lib` in `apps/desktop/src-tauri` and `packages/rust_transcription`, `cargo test --locked` in `packages/rust_pill_shared`, and `xvfb-run -a cargo test --locked` in `packages/rust_gtk_pill`: not applicable, same reason\n- `packages/rust_transcription/tests/sidecar_integration.rs`: not applicable, same reason\n\n<details>\n<summary>Changes</summary>\n\n- Files changed: 44 files, +2825/−231 across `apps/desktop/src` (components, store, actions, utils, hooks, tests), `apps/desktop/webdriver`, `apps/docs`, `apps/preview`, and test support files\n- Behaviour or policy changed: setting rows report `role=\"switch\"` with a press transform that reduced-motion removes; saved-audio startup loads once with a driver-load retry instead of re-entering per probe; the sidebar prefetches lazy route chunks on hover intent with a matching warm-navigation contract; the version tag no longer overlaps the Settings tile; the preview popup's eye toggle reads as a state toggle at webview level; the metal-fx probe falls back when WebGL2 selection crashes; the audio entry guard reports `onStop(\"replaced\")` when entered on an already-aborted signal\n- Packages touched under `packages/` that need a rebuild before consumers see the change: none\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>Code research gate</summary>\n\n- Queries searched: WAI-ARIA APG switch pattern and `role=\"switch\"` naming; React 19 `inert` support; React Router 6 `lazy` route semantics; MUI `Switch` `slotProps` handler forwarding; the `AbortError` contract and `AbortSignal: reason`; CSS `:active` matching through flat-tree ancestors; Vitest fake-timer cancellation semantics; `overflow-wrap: anywhere` versus `break-word`\n- Sources, with the assumption each one verified: the ten-row research record in `.mausagent/verification/REVIEW-2026-11-05.md` (MDN, WAI-ARIA APG, React 19 release notes, React Router source semantics, MUI Switch source, RFC 6949 abort conventions) — each row names the assumption it verified\n- Pattern class named, plus every other location where the same root cause could recur: interactive-row event forwarding must reach the shell handlers from the row's own props (the removed hover-layer button used to swallow the chain); stale per-row session state on row identity change; silent early-return on the abort path of async entry guards. Search evidence for the row-event class: every `ListTile` call site passes `shellProps` through; the identity-change class: `AudioPlayerPill` and `useTranscriptionsStore` both reset on `row?.id` transitions with tests\n- Edge cases considered and their disposition: entry on an already-aborted signal (fixed and pinned by test); double abort; driver-load rejection mid-startup (retried once, then the poll loop); first-run `user_get_one` null against an in-flight creation (cache respected); `:active` persisting after a held release (reset before the success path); reduced motion (every press transform removed under the media query); keyboard placeholder during I