+      "description": "## **User description**\n## Summary\n\nThe dictation overlay used to stay on Transcribing until History finished writing the recording. That blocked the next take.\n\nThis change sends the overlay back to idle as soon as the transcript is routed, then saves History on a serial background queue. Each take keeps the audio, stop time, and privacy choice from the moment the user stopped speaking. Failure and truncation notices only promise a saved recording when that take will actually be stored.\n\nMerged with later consolidation: concurrent History ownership from #282 is kept without awaiting it on the stop path, and failed-transcription recovery from #289 still reports whether audio was saved, after idle.\n\n## Verification gate\n\n- Head `648fc977`\n- [x] `DictationSideEffects` + history-persist unit tests: 46 passed, including a measured idle return faster than a 40ms delayed store\n- [x] oxlint + prettier on the touched desktop files\n- [x] i18n extract/sync for the queue-full toast\n- [ ] Native WAV timing: this change is renderer-side; store_transcription IPC was not modified. Cargo 1.88.0 is installed from vendor/sandbox-toolchain. Full `cargo test --lib` was not run because no Rust file in this diff.\n\n## Checklist\n\n- Overlay returns to idle before History WAV/SQLite work\n- Concurrent strategy writes are not duplicated and do not hold the session lock\n- Empty ASR recovery idles first, then toasts only after the store result (or immediately when nothing will be stored)\n- Review Save still awaits its own durable row\n\n## Footer\n\nMausAgent | Filed by Arena Agent Mode, with `@Owie6789`\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai -->\n\n<!-- coderabbit-ai-generated:v1 -->\n\n<details>\n<summary>Summary by CodeRabbit</summary>\n\n* **Reliability**\n  * Dictation History saves are handled in order, helping prevent overlapping recordings from creating duplicate entries.\n  * Recordings captured when History saving is unavailable remain ineligible for saving later, even if saving is re-enabled.\n  * Dictation can return to idle without waiting for a History save to finish.\n* **Notifications**\n  * You’ll be notified when a recording can’t be saved because earlier recordings are still being written.\n  * Fast-styling messages now describe unsaved endings without attributing them to Incognito Mode.\n\n<!-- end of auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai -->\n</details>\n</details>\n\n\n___\n\n## **CodeAnt-AI Description**\n**Return dictation to idle before History saves finish**\n\n### What Changed\n- The dictation pill returns to idle without waiting for History to finish saving, so you can start another take sooner.\n- Queued recordings keep the audio, stop time, and privacy setting from when each take ended. History saves them in order, and takes captured with saving disabled stay out of History even if that setting changes while they wait.\n- If History is full or a failed transcription cannot be saved, the app shows a message that reflects what happened.\n\n### Impact\n`✅ Start another dictation while History is saving`\n`✅ Keep private takes out of History after a settings change`\n`✅ Know when a recording could not be saved`\n<details><summary><strong>💡 Usage Guide</strong></summary>\n\n### Checking Your Pull Request\nEvery time you make a pull request, our system automatically looks through it. We check for security issues, mistakes in how you're setting up your infrastructure, and common code problems. We do this to make sure your changes are solid and won't cause any trouble later.\n\n### Talking to CodeAnt AI\nGot a question or need a hand with something in your pull request? You can easily get in touch with CodeAnt AI right here. Just type the following in a comment on your pull request, and replace \"Your question here\" with whatever you want to ask:\n<pre>\n<code>@codeant-ai ask: Your question here</code>\n</pre>\nThis lets you have a chat with CodeAnt AI about your pull request, making it easier to understand and improve your code.\n\n#### Example\n<pre>\n<code>@codeant-ai ask: Can you suggest a safer alternative to storing this secret?</code>\n</pre>\n\n### Preserve Org Learnings with CodeAnt\nYou can record team preferences so CodeAnt AI applies them in future reviews. Reply directly to the specific CodeAnt AI suggestion (in the same thread) and replace \"Your feedback here\" with your input:\n<pre>\n<code>@codeant-ai: Your feedback here</code>\n</pre>\nThis helps CodeAnt AI learn and adapt to your team's coding style and standards.\n\n#### Example\n<pre>\n<code>@codeant-ai: Do not flag unused imports.</code>\n</pre>\n\n### Retrigger review\nAsk CodeAnt AI to review the PR again, by typing:\n<pre>\n<code>@codeant-ai: review</code>\n</pre>\n\n### Check Your Repository Health\nTo analyze the health of your code repository, visit our dashboard at [https://app.codeant.ai](https://app.codeant.ai). This tool helps you identify potential issues and areas for improvement in your codebase, ensuring your repository maintains high standards of code health.\n\n</details>\n"
