+      "description": "## Summary\n\nOnboarding tips used to render as quiet in-page rows (PR 287). The owner built a new design on a Paper.design board and asked for a different pattern instead, a small toast anchored to the corner where every other notification in this app already lands. This PR reskins the tip's floating face to match that board: a pattern-image strip on top, an icon next to a title, a one-line body below, and a small dismiss control in the image's own corner.\n\nThe branch this PR targets already landed the underlying delivery mechanism during a separate consolidation merge: `TipToaster` renders each tip through the shared `SonnerToaster` stack, and a `tip-actions` registry maps a tip id to the thing a click should do (the Groq key tip still jumps to and focuses that field in the new routed Settings structure). This PR's own diff started narrow, a reskin of `TipCard`'s face to the pattern-image design, and then grew by one more round: a deep refinement pass over the whole feature, after the owner confirmed the reskin looked right but asked for a closer look at rough edges and missing pieces across the whole implementation.\n\nThat refinement round found and fixed two real gaps. First, a tip with no live action (`writing-styles`, `assistant-mode`, `review-before-insert`, `update-channel`) had no way to mark itself read except the 24px dismiss glyph. The sonner-based implementation this feature replaced made the whole title-and-body row an activation target that fell back to marking the tip read when it had no action, and this PR's own earlier description still claimed that behaviour, but the row lost it across the architecture swap to the routed `TipCardFrame`. `TipCardFrame` now takes an `onActivate` prop that restores this, reusing the existing exit-animation and interrupted-unmount guard rather than a new path. Second, every other toast in this app sits inside Sonner's own `aria-live=\"polite\"` region, so a screen reader hears it the moment it appears. A tip had no equivalent. `TipToaster` now carries its own hidden `role=\"status\"` region that announces a tip's title and body the moment it is newly shown.\n\nTo test it, run the desktop app and open Settings, Styling, History, or a chat. Each page's tip shows as a toast in the stack's own corner with the pattern image on top. For a tip with a live action, that action's own button is the only effect its row has; clicking elsewhere on the title and body does nothing. For a tip with no live action, clicking (or pressing Enter or Space on) the title-and-body area marks it read, the same as the dismiss control does. Clicking the small dismiss control on the image always dismisses without running an action. Help still lists all five tips, dimmed once dismissed, with a working Show again button.\n\n## Verification gate\n\nHead SHA: `e7ea79f54d8af04a0ae174fb17aaac847e569754`\n\n- `pnpm --filter desktop run check-types`: passed, 0 errors\n- `pnpm --filter desktop run lint`: passed (`prettier --check`, `oxlint`, `ui-lint.mjs`), 0 issues\n- `pnpm --filter desktop run i18n:extract` and `i18n:sync`: ran for the one new translatable string (\"Tip:\"), added to all 10 locale catalogs with no other drift\n- `npx vitest run` (desktop, full suite): 337 of 340 files passed, 3723 of 3777 tests passed. The 54 failures are the pre-existing `GROQ_API_KEY`-gated eval and integration suites, which fail the same way on the unmodified base branch in this sandbox; CI injects the real secret. This round added 11 new passing tests across `TipCard.test.tsx` and `TipToaster.test.tsx`\n- `pnpm run build` (root, prior round): passed, 11 turbo tasks successful\n- CI on this head: full matrix green, including `Build Desktop (Linux/Windows/macOS)`, `Lint Desktop (Linux/Windows/macOS)`, `Desktop TS Unit Tests`, `Desktop Integration Tests`, `Desktop Rust Unit Tests`, `Desktop i18n Catalog Sync`, `i18n Extractor Idempotence`, `SonarCloud Code Analysis`, and the DeepSource, DeepScan, CodeAnt, and Socket Security scans. `reviewDecision: APPROVED`, `mergeStateStatus: CLEAN`, 0 unresolved review threads, cubic's AI reviewer reported 0 issues at 5/5 confidence on this head's diff\n\nRust gates: not applicable. This diff touches only TypeScript, one shared style helper, `DESIGN.md`, and the i18n locale catalogs. No Rust source, no `src-tauri` crate, and no `packages/rust_*` workspace is in the diff.\n\n<details>\n<summary>Changes</summary>\n\n- Files changed this round: `apps/desktop/DESIGN.md`, `apps/desktop/src/components/onboarding/TipCard.tsx`, `apps/desktop/src/components/onboarding/TipCard.test.tsx`, `apps/desktop/src/components/onboarding/TipToaster.tsx`, `apps/desktop/src/components/onboarding/TipToaster.test.tsx`, `apps/desktop/src/components/settings/SettingsLayout.tsx`, `apps/desktop/src/styles/a11y.ts` (new), and all ten `apps/desktop/src/i18n/locales/*.json` catalogs (one new key).\n- Behaviour or policy changed: a tip with no live action now marks itself read when its title-and-body row is clicked or keyboard-activated, not only when the small dismiss glyph is clicked. A tip with a live action is unaffected; its one button stays the row's only effect. A newly shown tip now announces its title and body to a screen reader through a hidden live region, matching the announcement every other toast in this app already gets from Sonner. `TipCardFrame`'s unused `onDismiss` prop (dead code since neither caller used it after the dismiss control moved onto the pattern image) was removed. The `visuallyHidden` style object `SettingsLayout.tsx` already had is now shared from `styles/a11y.ts`, used by both call sites instead of existing as two copies of the same shape.\n- Packages touched under `packages/` that need a rebuild before consumers see the change: none, this diff is entirely inside `apps/desktop`.\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>Code research gate</summary>\n\n- Queries searched: direct inspection of the deleted sonner-based `TipToast.tsx` (`git show` against its last commit before this feature's architecture swap) to confirm its prior click-to-dismiss and keyboard-activation behaviour. A grep of `apps/desktop/node_modules/sonner/dist/index.mjs` for `aria-live` to confirm Sonner's own toaster wraps every toast in a live region. A grep for the existing `visuallyHidden` / `role=\"status\"` convention already in `SettingsLayout.tsx`. A grep for `TranscriptRow.tsx`'s existing hover-and-press recipe, reused for the new activatable row instead of inventing a new one.\n- Sources, with the assumption each one verified: the deleted `TipToast.tsx` itself, read in full through `git show`, confirmed it made the whole title-and-body row an activation target that ran a tip's live action if one existed or fell back to marking the tip read if it did not. Sonner's own bundled source, read directly, confirmed its toaster container sets `aria-live=\"polite\"`. `SettingsLayout.tsx`, read directly, confirmed this repository's existing visually-hidden-live-region pattern for an unrelated search-result announcement. `TranscriptRow.tsx`, read directly, confirmed the hover wash and transition timing reused here.\n- Pattern class named, plus every other location where the same root cause could recur: \"a feature already shipped once, its UX contract already documented, regressed silently across an unrelated architecture change (the merge that moved tips from a sonner-custom toast onto the routed `TipCardFrame`).\" The two instances found were the missing activation fallback and the missing live-region announcement, both lost in that same merge. A third candidate, duplicating the `visuallyHidden` style object instead of sharing it, was found while fixing the second and fixed alongside it, since letting two copies of the same shape drift apart is the same root cause one level down.\n- Edge cases considered and their disposition: a tip with a live action must not also make its row a second way to trigger that action or to dismiss it