andidates considered and explicitly set aside as out of scope: RTL corner mirroring (this app ships no RTL locale), a `focusSetting` live action for `update-channel` when the toast appears without a navigation event (the existing hash-anchor effect already covers the primary case), and Escape-key dismissal (not an existing convention elsewhere in this app's toasts).\n\nDeep refinement.\n\n- Detail gaps checked: visible surfaces (the activatable row's hover and press feedback, cursor affordance), invisible surfaces (ARIA role, tabindex, the live region's presence before content), messages (the one new \"Tip:\" string, run through `i18n:extract`/`i18n:sync` for all ten locales), interaction states (click, keyboard Enter/Space, a nested action button's own click and keydown not double-firing the row), and both theme modes (unaffected by this round's changes, confirmed by the existing light/dark tests in `TipCard.test.tsx` still passing).\n- Edge cases enumerated and dispositioned, with the verification for each: see the code research gate's edge case list above, each covered by a new or updated test.\n- Missing features researched, with sources, ranked must, should, and nice, and the outcome for each: must, a click-to-mark-read fallback for actionless tips, since the feature's own documented contract required it (implemented, confirmed by new tests). Must, a screen-reader announcement matching every other toast's own guarantee (implemented, confirmed by new tests). Should, sharing the `visuallyHidden` style instead of duplicating it (implemented). Nice, a `focusSetting` live action for `update-channel` so its toast is self-sufficient even without a navigation event (deferred, the existing hash-anchor effect already covers the primary path and the gap is narrow).\n- Refinement verification, focused checks per iteration plus the full gate on the final tree: `npx vitest run src/components/onboarding/TipCard.test.tsx` and `TipToaster.test.tsx` ran after each edit to this file pair, then `npx tsc --noEmit`, `pnpm --filter desktop run lint`, and the full `npx vitest run` suite ran once on the final tree, then the full CI matrix on the pushed head.\n\nDepth pass, from `AGENTS.md` section 2b.\n\n- Field named: accessibility and interaction-state completeness for a small, frequently seen floating component, carried over from the original UI design pass.\n- Moves taken that the task did not ask for: removed `TipCardFrame`'s unused `onDismiss` prop (confirmed dead code by checking every call site) and deduplicated the `visuallyHidden` style object, neither of which the owner named directly but both of which are the same \"a detail nobody is watching quietly drifts\" class the owner's request was pointed at.\n- Rawest material started from: the deleted `TipToast.tsx`'s actual prior implementation, read through `git show`, not a paraphrase of what it might have done, and Sonner's own bundled source for its accessibility guarantee, not an assumption about it.\n- Methods and tools used: `git show` against the pre-merge commit to recover the deleted file, `grep` against `node_modules/sonner/dist/index.mjs` for its actual `aria-live` wiring, and direct comparison of `TipCard.test.tsx`/`TipToaster.test.tsx`'s existing `role=\"note\"` queries against the new conditional role to find every place a passing test depended on an assumption this round's fix had to change.\n- Gate per claim: every claim above is either a test that ran (named in this section) or a file read directly (named in the code research gate), not an unverified hypothesis.\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>Design and UI confirmation</summary>\n\n- Product UI touched: yes\n- Design files read before the first edit: `apps/desktop/DESIGN.md`, read in full for its existing \"Tips and inline notifications\" section before extending it this round.\n- Rendering inspected: no live desktop or `apps/preview` render was possible in this sandbox, no display server and no network path to a browser driver. Verification relied on the full unit test suite (including new tests that assert computed ARIA roles, hover styles, and live-region content), `tsc --noEmit`, and `oxlint`/`prettier` passing clean, plus the full CI matrix's green `Lint Desktop` and `Build Desktop` jobs on all three platforms for this head.\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>Review classification</summary>\n\n- Substantially critical: No\n- Reason if yes: not applicable. This round fixes two accessibility and interaction-completeness gaps in one already-shipped UI component. It changes no Rust, IPC, filesystem, network, or migration surface, no platform support claim, and no repository policy or workflow.\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>Review requests</summary>\n\n- CodeRabbit review: not requested, this PR is not substantially critical per the classification above.\n- Kilocode bot handoff: not used, every host and tool this change needed was reachable from this sandbox.\n- SonarCloud on this head: the `SonarCloud Code Analysis` check passed on `e7ea79f54d8af04a0ae174fb17aaac847e569754`. `sonarcloud.io` is outside this sandbox's reachable hosts, so the issue list itself could not be queried directly here; the dashboard link is in the PR checks.\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>Review and babysit log</summary>\n\n| Round | Head SHA  | What arrived                                 | What changed    | Disposition                                                 |\n| ----- | --------- | --------------------------------------------- | ---------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| 1-6   | `cd306fc` | Full review cycle on the original row-based redesign (PR 287 era): 18 review threads, a full CI matrix, two trivial DeepSource findings. | Addressed every thread; row-based `TipCard` reached approved status. | Resolved. Superseded by round 7, the owner replaced the row design with the toast design below. |\n| 7     | `f9af53f7` | The base branch (`