assed. Desktop unit, voice-ai and agent tests passed; i18n extraction and sync made no catalog changes.\n- The full workspace test ran: 325 desktop files and 3,510 tests passed; 54 tests failed in three integration/evaluation files because `GROQ_API_KEY` is unavailable in this sandbox. This is not a full pass.\n- The native feedback ordering tests use a mocked IPC bridge; real native timing and audio behavior remain unverified. Dictionary rollback is covered by helper and concurrent component tests. CI and fresh bot review are pending on this head.\n\n\n### Verification gate: 8d33b68\n\nThe frozen-lockfile install used `--ignore-scripts`. The utilities package was rebuilt before desktop checks. Root format, typecheck, lint, build, secret scan and skills verification passed, as did desktop unit, utilities, voice-ai and agent tests. i18n extraction and sync produced no catalog changes. Full workspace tests were not rerun for this batch; the preceding run failed 54 credential-dependent tests because `GROQ_API_KEY` was unavailable. Native feedback timing remains unverified; IPC ordering and failure logging were tested with mocks. Cubic reported 0 new issues (5/5) on this head; historical review threads remain open. SonarCloud and Linux build passed; Windows/macOS builds were still pending at the last check.\n\n### Review loop through 43e7059\n\n- 44b5dd6 addressed nine review threads: blocked-write rejection for user and preference mutations, one shared queue/lease helper, localized action error strings in all nine non-English catalogs, the audio-pill playback-session helper, shared elevated button styles, per-slider commit serialization with clear-gate cancellation, and fire-and-forget rejection handling.\n- e39686b addressed the three clear/recording threads: both destructive dialogs wipe persisted data even when a renderer-level stop IPC fails while keeping the clear gate closed for retry; native `start_recording` holds a clear-gated lease across device open, the cle