+      "description": "## **User description**\nLive provider sessions now get a 15-second startup limit with cancellation and cleanup. A pill-body click stops microphone capture before the app waits for the provider, then waits for startup or timeout before finalizing buffered audio. If startup fails, the app reports the failure and preserves the recording for retry when history settings allow. Repeated toggles cannot queue extra sessions, and X still cancels and discards.\n\n<details>\n<summary>Implementation and verification</summary>\n\n- Provider sessions now wait for their provider-ready signal and close pending requests or sockets when startup times out or the user cancels.\n- Azure streaming and one-shot recognition close partially created resources and dispose stalled SDK connections.\n- Failed-transcription recovery only claims that audio was saved when storage returned an audio snapshot.\n- Added regression coverage for startup timeout and cancellation, repeated activation, provider cleanup, and failed-audio retention.\n\nLocal checks passed:\n\n- `pnpm --filter desktop test:unit`: 3,058 tests and 4 Node tests passed.\n- Changed desktop regression tests: 116 tests passed.\n- `pnpm --filter @maus-inc/voice-ai test`: 510 tests passed.\n- `pnpm --filter @repo/agent test`: 24 tests passed.\n- `pnpm run build`, `pnpm run lint`, `pnpm run format:check`, and `pnpm --filter desktop check-types` passed.\n- `pnpm --filter desktop i18n` made no catalog changes.\n\nEnvironment notes: the broader `pnpm --filter desktop test` run could not complete its API-backed evals because `GROQ_API_KEY` is unavailable. The repository-wide `pnpm run check-types` reports existing errors in `apps/preview/src/demos/buttons.tsx`; the changed desktop app type-check passes. No network-throttling reproduction was run. The stalled-start behavior is covered with local tests.\n\n</details>\n\nMausAgent | Filed by Arena.ai Agent Mode, with @Owie6789, on 2026-10-07\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated description by cubic. -->\n<a href=\"https://cubic.dev/pr/maus-inc/mausVoice/pull/289?utm_source=github\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" data-no-image-dialog=\"true\"><picture><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\" srcset=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-dark.svg\"><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\" srcset=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-light.svg\"><img alt=\"Review in cubic\" src=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-dark.svg\"></picture></a> <a href=\"https://www.cubic.dev/action/auto-fix/pr/maus-inc/mausVoice/289?returnTo=https%3A%2F%2Fgithub.com%2Fmaus-inc%2FmausVoice%2Fpull%2F289&source=description\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" data-no-image-dialog=\"true\"><picture><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\" srcset=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/turn-on-auto-fix-dark.svg\"><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\" srcset=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/turn-on-auto-fix-light.svg\"><img alt=\"Turn on auto-fix\" src=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/turn-on-auto-fix-dark.svg\"></picture></a>\n<!-- End of auto-generated description by cubic. -->\n\n## Summary by Sourcery\n\nProtect live dictation from slow or failed provider startup while retaining captured audio and preventing duplicate recording transitions.\n\nNew Features:\n- Bound live transcription provider startup to 15 seconds with cancellation and a connecting status while audio is buffered.\n- Preserve failed dictation audio for retry when persistence is enabled and clearly report whether it was saved.\n\nBug Fixes:\n- Prevent lost initial audio while live providers establish sessions.\n- Prevent repeated toggles from queuing duplicate activation or deactivation operations.\n- Ensure stalled or canceled provider sessions and partially initialized Azure resources are cleaned up safely.\n\nEnhancements:\n- Improve recovery from audio intake subscription failures by retaining the native recording instead of treating capture as failed.\n\nTests:\n- Add regression coverage for provider startup readiness, timeout, cancellation, cleanup, audio retention, and activation sequencing.\n\n\n___\n\n## **CodeAnt-AI Description**\n**Bound live transcription startup and preserve recordings after failures**\n\n### What Changed\n- Live dictation shows a connecting status and stops waiting after 15 seconds if the provider does not become ready.\n- If a live provider fails, captured audio is retained for retry when recording settings allow; the failure notice says whether the audio was actually saved.\n- Provider failures during an active session now reach the same recovery flow, while any transcript already received is kept.\n- Stop and cancel actions clean up pending provider connections, and repeated hotkey or hold-to-talk actions no longer queue conflicting recording sessions.\n\n### Impact\n`✅ Fewer lost recordings after provider connection failures`\n`✅ No dictation stuck indefinitely while connecting`\n`✅ Clearer notices when retry audio was not saved`\n<details><summary><strong>💡 Usage Guide</strong></summary>\n\n### Checking Your Pull Request\nEvery time you make a pull request, our system automatically looks through it. We check for security issues, mistakes in how you're setting up your infrastructure, and common code problems. We do this to make sure your changes are solid and won't cause any trouble later.\n\n### Talking to CodeAnt AI\nGot a question or need a hand with something in your pull request? You can easily get in touch with CodeAnt AI right here. Just type the following in a comment on your pull request, and replace \"Your question here\" with whatever you want to ask:\n<pre>\n<code>@codeant-ai ask: Your question here</code>\n</pre>\nThis lets you have a chat with CodeAnt AI about your pull request, making it easier to understand and improve your code.\n\n#### Example\n<pre>\n<code>@codeant-ai ask: Can you suggest a safer alternative to storing this secret?</code>\n</pre>\n\n### Preserve Org Learnings with CodeAnt\nYou can record team preferences so CodeAnt AI applies them in future reviews. Reply directly to the specific CodeAnt AI suggestion (in the same thread) and replace \"Your feedback here\" with your input:\n<pre>\n<code>@codeant-ai: Your feedback here</code>\n</pre>\nThis helps CodeAnt AI learn and adapt to your team's coding style and standards.\n\n#### Example\n<pre>\n<code>@codeant-ai: Do not flag unused imports.</code>\n</pre>\n\n### Retrigger review\nAsk CodeAnt AI to review the PR again, by typing:\n<pre>\n<code>@codeant-ai: review</code>\n</pre>\n\n### Check Your Repository Health\nTo analyze the health of your code repository, visit our dashboard at [https://app.codeant.ai](https://app.codeant.ai). This tool helps you identify potential issues and areas for improvement in your codebase, ensuring your repository maintains high standards of code health.\n\n</details>\n"
