+      "description": "## Summary\n\nThe onboarding tips that appear on five pages (Settings, Styling, Transcriptions, Chats, and the update channel row) used to render as full-width banners anchored at the top of each page: a heavy card with an icon tile, a drop shadow, and an arrow on the button. They read like ads pinned over the content instead of part of the app, and the Help page listing repeated the card styling by hand, so the two could drift apart.\n\nThis pull request redesigns every tip surface as a quiet row, modeled on Linear's inbox rows and checked against premium design references (Raycast, Vercel, and design-system callout kits), and moves the live tips out of the page flow into a floating stack in the bottom-right toast corner. A tip is now a row with a 1px hairline, a small bare icon, a short title, a one-sentence reason, and at most one quiet action plus a dismiss button. The live tips take the floating-layer material the app's toasts already use (paper face, premium lift, the 356px toast column) and sit in the same corner, under the transient toasts and the MUI overlays; the Help page keeps the in-flow listing of all five, dimmed for dismissed tips, with a Show again control. A top-anchored tip competes with the page heading and forces the reader to scroll around it; a dismissible nudge belongs with the other dismissible things, in the corner, out of the reading path.\n\nThe dismissal behavior is hardened too: if you navigate away in the middle of the dismiss animation, the choice now sticks instead of the tip reappearing on the next visit. To test it, run the desktop app and visit Settings, Styling, Transcriptions, and Chats: each page shows its tip in the bottom-right corner (Settings shows two, stacked). Dismiss one and navigate away mid-animation, then return: it stays dismissed. On the Settings tip, the Add API key button scrolls to and highlights the Groq key row and opens the key dialog in place, with keyboard focus on the field, and the tip stays on screen.\n\n## Verification gate\n\nHead `e583f8e`, base `arena/0.1.6-consolidation` at `fe060ab`. Local results at the pushed head:\n\n- prettier repo-wide `format:check`: passed\n- desktop `check-types` (`tsc --noEmit`): passed\n- desktop lint (oxlint, 688 files): 0 issues\n- desktop unit tests: 3186/3186 (245 files)\n- i18n extractor idempotence: 0 added, catalogs unchanged\n- desktop integration tests: GROQ_API_KEY-gated and not sandbox-available; covered by the secret-backed job (the diff touches no integration file)\n\n## Checklist\n\n- [x] Automated tests\n- [x] Manual verification\n- [x] Code inspection\n\n<details>\n<summary>Details (click to expand)</summary>\n\n### What was built\n\n- `TipCard` and `TipCardFrame` in `apps/desktop/src/components/onboarding/TipCard.tsx` are the single source for all tip presentation. Five tips, one live card component, one presentational frame.\n- `TipToaster` in `apps/desktop/src/components/onboarding/TipToaster.tsx`: one floating stack (fixed, right/bottom 16px, z-index 1100, Portal) mounted once in `DashboardPage`. A tip shows only on the route its feature lives on (`ONBOARDING_TIPS.href`, exact match, trailing slashes normalized) and while undismissed; the two Settings tips stack, siblings reflow with `layout` when one clears. The z-index keeps the stack under the Sonner toasts and MUI dialogs; the column width and corner offset match Sonner's defaults so the two stacks align.\n- Live tip lifecycle: a 160ms ease-out rise on entrance, a 180ms ease-out exit on dismiss. The store update waits for the exit to finish, and an unmount guard persists the dismissal when navigation interrupts the exit. A ref guard keeps persistence to exactly one call across exit completion, unmount, and StrictMode double cleanup.\n- The in-page action uses a `tip-actions` registry instead of a prop: the tip's route page registers its handler on mount and unregisters on unmount, so the floating card can complete a task in place without the route page passing a callback through the toaster. Settings registers the generative-provider action (scroll + highlight the Groq key row, open the key dialog whose input carries autoFocus). The action never dismisses the tip.\n- The Help page keeps the flat in-flow face: a 1px hairline over `level1`, no cast, the five tip rows, dismissed tips dimmed to 0.65, a navigation button per tip, and a Show again text button per dismissed tip.\n- Removed the top-anchored tips from Styling, Transcriptions, Settings, the update channel row, and the chat conversation layout; no empty wrappers remain after dismissal.\n- Tests: `TipToaster.test.tsx` (9 tests: per-route gating including trailing slashes, the two-tip settings stack, dismissed filtering, corner geometry and z-index, persistence on exit completion, persistence on mid-exit unmount, registry action without dismiss). `TipCard.test.tsx` (13 tests) asserts the floating face (paper, hairline, premium lift), the 356px toast column width, and the registry action. `SettingsGenerativeTip.test.tsx` asserts the registration contract (registered on mount, handler completes the task in place, unregistered on unmount). Stale `TipCard` mocks dropped from three unrelated test files.\n- `DESIGN.md` documents the corner placement, the two surfaces (floating live tips vs in-flow listing), and the source for each choice, plus the anti-patterns (top-anchored in-page tips, shadowed in-flow cards, icon tiles behind neutral glyphs, arrows on secondary actions).\n\n### What was reviewed\n\nThe diff went through the `FULL-REVIEW.md` protocol (fetched from main): change inventory, boundary traces, contract review with Given/When/Then for each tip behavior, the security phase (not applicable: no IPC, filesystem, or network changes), a test-validity review, and the verification matrix. For the placement change, the routes were audited against `ONBOARDING_TIPS` hrefs (all five resolve to real routes; both Settings tips stack deliberately), the z-index ordering was checked against Sonner (999999999) and the MUI overlay surfaces (1300+), and the corner geometry was checked against Sonner's defaults (16px offset, 356px width). Review-bot findings on the new code were addressed in follow-up commits: trailing-slash route matching (CodeRabbit) and a non-null assertion in a test (DeepSource).\n\n### Out of scope\n\nNo Rust, IPC, migration, workflow, or dependency changes. No new i18n strings (the Add API key label moved between two scanned source files). The tip ids, dismissal store shape, and analytics events are unchanged.\n\n</details>\n\n## Footer\n\nMausAgent | Filed by Agent Mode (Arena.ai), with @Owie6789, on 2026-11-05\n"
