+      "description": "## **User description**\nDouble-clicking the desktop title bar did not expand the window to full screen, and minimizing, unmaximizing, or restarting the app after a maximized session could leave the window stuck at full-screen width while the title bar compact mode and maximize button showed the wrong state. This pull request fixes title-bar dragging and double-clicking across macOS, Windows, and Linux, reads the real window interior width while ignoring minimized resize events, and repairs saved window-state dimensions so maximizing, restoring, minimizing, and reopening the app all keep the expected window size.\n\n<details>\n<summary>What changed in plain terms</summary>\n\n**Double-clicking the title bar now maximizes and restores the window.** Tauri injects a document-level script named `drag.js` that listens for clicks on `data-tauri-drag-region`. When both `drag.js` and React handled the same double-click, the two handlers toggled the window in opposite directions or the OS move loop swallowed the first click release before the browser could fire a double-click event. `TitleBar` in `apps/desktop/src/components/root/TitleBar.tsx` now stops drag-region mouse events from reaching `document` and handles dragging directly per platform. On macOS, `TitleBar` starts the native drag on the first mouse press and toggles maximize when a stationary second click releases. On Windows and Linux, `TitleBar` starts the native drag only after the pointer moves 4 pixels with the primary mouse button held, so stationary clicks and double-clicks stay inside the webview.\n\n**The whole title bar responds to dragging and double-clicking.** The logo, wordmark, and middle spacer previously sat above the drag layer and blocked pointer events, while the 4-pixel top resize grip in `apps/desktop/src/components/root/WindowResizeHandles.tsx` sat above the top edge even when the window was maximized. Non-interactive title-bar elements now pass pointer events through to the full-bleed drag surface, and `WindowResizeHandles` turns off while the window is maximized.\n\n**Minimizing or narrowing the window no longer confuses the title bar.** `useWindowMetrics` in `apps/desktop/src/components/root/TitleBar.tsx` previously read `outerSize()`, which lags behind window resize events on Linux X11 and Wayland and includes invisible shadow borders or the 160-by-28-pixel minimized taskbar slot on Windows. `useWindowMetrics` now reads `innerSize()`, ignores zero-pixel and minimized resize events, separates width sequence tickets from maximize sequence tickets, and holds optimistic maximize changes until the native window confirms the new state.\n\n**Unmaximizing and restarting remember the normal window size.** Closing the app while maximized on undecorated macOS or Linux caused `tauri-plugin-window-state` to overwrite the saved width and height in `.window-state.json` with full-screen dimensions, and its `RunEvent::Exit` hook could overwrite `.window-state.json` with `maximized: false` after the window hid to the tray. `apps/desktop/src-tauri/src/app.rs` now persists both `SIZE` and `MAXIMIZED`, filters window-state tracking to the `main` window only, records the last normal window size and maximized state during resize events, repairs `.window-state.json` on window close and app exit, and restores both the normal 1100-by-700-pixel fallback geometry and the maximized state on launch even when undecorated macOS reports `false` for both maximize flags.\n\n**Surfacing a maximized window on Windows keeps it maximized.** `surface_main_window` in `apps/desktop/src-tauri/src/platform/windows/window.rs` previously called `ShowWindow` with `SW_RESTORE` every time the user opened the app from the tray or launched a second instance, which unmaximized an already maximized window. `surface_main_window` now calls `SW_RESTORE` only when `is_minimized()` is true.\n\n**The browser preview matches the native window interface.** `PreviewWindow` in `apps/desktop/src/preview/tauri/window.ts` now reports `window.innerWidth` and `window.innerHeight` and implements `isMinimized`, `isFocused`, `scaleFactor`, `onResized`, `onFocusChanged`, and `onCloseRequested`.\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>Files changed</summary>\n\n- `apps/desktop/src/components/root/TitleBar.tsx` updates `useWindowMetrics`, `useWindowControls`, and the drag surface layout so drag and double-click gestures work across macOS, Windows, and Linux without racing `drag.js` or stale resize reads.\n- `apps/desktop/src/components/root/WindowResizeHandles.tsx` adds a `disabled` prop so the custom resize grips do not cover the top edge of the title bar while the window is maximized.\n- `apps/desktop/src-tauri/src/app.rs` adds `WINDOW_STATE_FLAGS`, `LAST_NORMAL_MAIN_SIZE`, `LAST_MAIN_MAXIMIZED`, `is_normal_window_size`, `is_work_area_window_size`, `is_maximized_session`, `record_main_window_resize`, `save_main_window_state`, and `sanitize_restored_main_window`.\n- `apps/desktop/src-tauri/src/platform/windows/window.rs` guards `ShowWindow` `SW_RESTORE` behind `is_minimized()`.\n- `apps/desktop/src/preview/tauri/window.ts` implements the missing window state and listener methods on `PreviewWindow`.\n- `apps/desktop/src/components/root/TitleBar.test.tsx` adds unit tests for consecutive double-click toggles, deferred drag thresholds, macOS stationary double-click release, minimized resize events, and unconfirmed resize snapshots.\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>What I verified</summary>\n\n- `pnpm --filter desktop check-types` passes with zero errors.\n- `pnpm run lint` and `pnpm run format:check` pass across all workspace packages.\n- `pnpm --filter desktop exec vitest run src/components/root/TitleBar.test.tsx src/components/root/WindowResizeHandles.test.ts src/__tests__/csp-capability.contract.test.ts` passes all 62 tests.\n- `node --test scripts/ci/*.test.mjs` passes all 369 CI contract tests.\n- GitHub Actions CI passes `Build Desktop`, `Lint Desktop`, `Desktop Rust Unit Tests`, `Desktop TS Unit Tests`, `Desktop Integration Tests`, `Rust (Windows-gated code)`, `DeepSource`, `SonarCloud`, `CodeAnt`, `CodeRabbit`, and `Kilo Code Review`.\n\n</details>\n\nMausAgent | Filed with `@Owie6789`, on 2026-10-07\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated description by cubic. -->\n<a href=\"https://cubic.dev/pr/maus-inc/mausVoice/pull/283?utm_source=github\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" data-no-image-dialog=\"true\"><picture><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\" srcset=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-dark.svg\"><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\" srcset=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-light.svg\"><img alt=\"Review in cubic\" src=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-dark.svg\"></picture></a> <a href=\"https://www.cubic.dev/action/auto-fix/pr/maus-inc/mausVoice/283?returnTo=https%3A%2F%2Fgithub.com%2Fmaus-inc%2FmausVoice%2Fpull%2F283&source=description\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" data-no-image-dialog=\"true\"><picture><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\" srcset=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/turn-on-auto-fix-dark.svg\"><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\" srcset=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/turn-on-auto-fix-light.svg\"><img alt=\"Turn on auto-fix\" src=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/turn-on-auto-fix-dark.svg\"></picture></a>\n<!-- End of auto-generated description by cubic. -->\n\n## Summary by Sourcery\n\nEnsure desktop title-bar interactions and persisted window geometry remain consistent across platforms and window states.\n\nBug Fixes:\n- Fix title-bar dragging and double-click maximize/restore behavior across macOS, Windows, and Linux.\n- Preserve correct maximized state and normal window dimensions when minimizing, restoring, closing, or reopening the desktop app.\n- Prevent minimized resize events and repeated window surfacing from corrupting title-bar state or unmaximizing the window.\n\nEnhancements:\n- M