+      "description": "## **User description**\n## What changed?\n\nGemini transcription now reads `audioTranscription.text` when Google returns structured audio output. It joins separate speaker turns with spaces and rejects blank results. Text-only responses keep their previous concatenation.\n\nThe model picker reads every page of Google's model catalog, so supported transcription models beyond the first page can appear. The built-in catalog remains the fallback when discovery fails or returns no usable transcription models. The existing 403/404 transcription fallback is unchanged.\n\n<details>\n<summary>Implementation notes</summary>\n\nModel discovery requests up to 1,000 models per page, URL-encodes opaque page tokens, and stops if a token repeats. The JSON Schema converter now uses recursive helpers for nested object and array types. Transcription parsing stays separate from general text parsing. Speaker labels and word timestamps are not returned. Provider capabilities are now read-only flags rather than zero-state methods. Gemini page fetching, pagination, and catalog filtering use separate helpers. The Gemini chat path no longer writes token usage metadata to the browser console.\n\nThis PR is stacked on #236 and targets `arena/0.1.6-consolidation`.\n\n</details>\n\n## How is it tested?\n\n- [x] Automated tests\n  - `corepack pnpm --filter @maus-inc/voice-ai test` (506 tests)\n  - `corepack pnpm --filter desktop test:unit` (3,038 Vitest tests and 4 Node tests)\n  - `corepack pnpm --filter @repo/agent test` (24 tests)\n  - `corepack pnpm --filter @maus-inc/preview test` (22 tests)\n- [ ] Manual verification\n- [x] Code inspection\n\n<details>\n<summary>Additional verification</summary>\n\nThe workspace build, root format check, desktop lint, and desktop type check passed. The workspace `check-types` command still reports two existing MUI `variant=\"blue\"` errors in unchanged `apps/preview/src/demos/buttons.tsx` at lines 25 and 48.\n\nThe local secret-scan 