+      "description": "## **User description**\n## Summary\n\nPull request descriptions in this repository had stopped being readable. Every review round, every babysit poll and every CI log was appended as a new section, so a PR that had lived for a day scrolled for several screens before reaching anything a reviewer needed. This branch makes the description a fixed shape: a visible summary, the verification gate, the checklist and the footer, with everything else inside a collapsible block and one table row per review round. A CI job runs the same checker on every pull request, so the shape is enforced rather than requested.\n\nThe same branch fixes the way the repository's agent documentation talked about its own environment. The sandbox documents stated one measured machine as a standing fact, which is how an agent on an unrestricted host comes to report a gate that would have passed as impossible. It also records the second and third deliveries of the vendored toolchain on the orphan `vendor/sandbox-toolchain` branch: groups G9 to G13, which ship the media tools, the model weights, the WebDriver driver chain, the cross-target Rust standard libraries and the gitleaks binary, and groups G16 to G22, which add debuggers and tracers, native build tools, database clients, OCR, shell and crypto tooling, cross compilers with emulation, and supply-chain scanners. The G17 build tools were incomplete when the third delivery was first recorded, so this branch completes that group and repins every document to the payload that carries it.\n\nEverything below this paragraph is foldable except the gate, the checklist and the footer, which is exactly the rule this branch introduces.\n\n## Verification gate\n\nHead SHA: `2236da2e`\n\n- `pnpm install --frozen-lockfile`: passed in this environment with `CHROMEDRIVER_SKIP_DOWNLOAD=true`; the bare form fails on the `chromedriver` postinstall download (gap G15). No dependency changed in this diff.\n- `pnpm run lint`: not run. No TypeScript, TSX or JavaScript source changed apart from one Node script, which `node --test` covers.\n- `pnpm run check-types`: passed earlier in this session with 9 turbo tasks in 49 seconds. No TypeScript in the diff since.\n- `pnpm run build`: passed earlier in this session with 11 turbo tasks in 68 seconds. No build input changed since.\n- `pnpm run test`: not run. The packages this diff could reach are Markdown and one script with a dedicated suite below.\n- `pnpm run format:check`: passed on this head. Prettier 3.9.6 reports all matched files use the code style.\n- `pnpm run skills:verify`: passed on this head, 53 of 53 locked skills verified, 4 project-owned skills unrecorded.\n- `pnpm run test:secret-scan`: not run. The payload now carries the `gitleaks` binary (G13), but this agent sandbox has not extracted it, so the command has no binary to run. The diff is Markdown, YAML and one checker; no secret material is involved.\n- `node --test scripts/ci/*.test.mjs`: passed on this head, 393 of 393 tests, 22 of them the fold checker suite.\n- `pnpm gen:bindings` produced no diff: not applicable, no command or type surface changed.\n\nPer-package gates: not applicable, no package source changed.\n\nRust gates: not applicable, no Cargo workspace is touched.\n\n<details>\n<summary>Changes</summary>\n\n- Files changed: 26 against the base.\n- Behaviour or policy changed: the PR description shape, now machine checked in CI; a new agent rule that environment claims must name their environment and be measured in it; a rewrite of every sandbox document so its limits are attributed to the Arena agent sandbox rather than stated as universal; the gap register renumbered to the vendor specification's IDs; the second payload delivery recorded as shipped with measured sizes; broken git-hook globs fixed; issue forms requiring the fields they promise.\n- Vendor branch: `vendor/sandbox-toolchain` (orphan) now carries G1 to G13 and G16 to G22 at tip `8442ae0c4e8d0c6a3e2a54072c53e8db5e