+      "description": "## **User description**\n## Summary\n- Polish the style pickers used by Import, Retranscribe, and the reusable ToneSelect with a compact, scrollable menu, consistent selected-row treatment, and an explicit checkmark.\n- Associate visible Style/Language labels with their selectors and label the Retranscribe dialog for assistive technology.\n- Keep Language menus on the generic menu treatment and preserve Import's dialog/selection state when the file action returns no file.\n- Ensure Retranscribe's MUI Select options remain direct MenuItem children so selection and change handling work correctly.\n\nThe visual direction was checked against real product picker references, including [Attio's task popovers and pickers](https://dribbble.com/shots/14651427-Task-Popovers-and-Pickers); the implementation keeps the app's solid, neutral surfaces rather than adding decorative effects.\n\n## Local verification\n- `pnpm --filter desktop check-types` — passed.\n- `pnpm --filter desktop test:unit` — passed (230 Vitest files / 3,043 tests, plus 4 Node TAP tests).\n- `pnpm run lint`, `pnpm run format:check`, and `pnpm --filter desktop run i18n` — passed; i18n catalogs unchanged.\n- `pnpm run build` — passed (11/11 tasks).\n- `pnpm --filter @maus-inc/voice-ai test` — passed (501 tests); `pnpm --filter @maus-inc/preview test` — passed (22 tests).\n- `pnpm run test:secret-scan` — offline assertions passed; live Gitleaks scan was unavailable locally.\n\nThe root-wide `pnpm run check-types` still reports the existing `variant=\"blue\"` errors in unchanged `apps/preview/src/demos/buttons.tsx`; the desktop type-check passes. Provider-dependent integration tests were not run locally because `GROQ_API_KEY` is unavailable; the branch-push integration workflow will cover them.\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated description by cubic. -->\n<a href=\"https://cubic.dev/pr/maus-inc/mausVoice/pull/291?utm_source=github\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" data-no-image-dialog=\"true\"><picture><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\" srcset=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-dark.svg\"><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\" srcset=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-light.svg\"><img alt=\"Review in cubic\" src=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-dark.svg\"></picture></a> <a href=\"https://www.cubic.dev/action/auto-fix/pr/maus-inc/mausVoice/291?returnTo=https%3A%2F%2Fgithub.com%2Fmaus-inc%2FmausVoice%2Fpull%2F291&source=description\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" data-no-image-dialog=\"true\"><picture><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\" srcset=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/turn-on-auto-fix-dark.svg\"><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\" srcset=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/turn-on-auto-fix-light.svg\"><img alt=\"Turn on auto-fix\" src=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/turn-on-auto-fix-dark.svg\"></picture></a>\n<!-- End of auto-generated description by cubic. -->\n\n## Summary by Sourcery\n\nImprove desktop style and language pickers with consistent compact presentation, clearer selection feedback, and stronger accessibility.\n\nNew Features:\n- Polish style and language pickers with compact, scrollable menus and clear selected-state indicators.\n- Provide render-safe English labels for languages whose native scripts may not be available.\n\nBug Fixes:\n- Keep picker dialogs and selected settings intact when file selection returns no file.\n- Ensure selection handling remains reliable for Retranscribe style options.\n\nEnhancements:\n- Standardize menu row styling, sizing, selection treatment, and accessibility across desktop pickers.\n- Improve language and style picker readability with explicit checkmarks and accessible labels.\n\n\n___\n\n## **CodeAnt-AI Description**\n**Make language and style pickers compact and readable**\n\n### What Changed\n- Language and style menus use compact rows and scroll within the window when options exceed the available space.\n- Languages whose native scripts may not render now use English names; Latin and Cyrillic names remain native.\n- Selected rows use a neutral tint and stronger text instead of a left stripe, with checkmarks retained where shown.\n\n### Impact\n`✅ Menus stay within the window`\n`✅ Readable names for non-Latin languages`\n`✅ Easier-to-spot selected options`\n<details><summary><strong>💡 Usage Guide</strong></summary>\n\n### Checking Your Pull Request\nEvery time you make a pull request, our system automatically looks through it. We check for security issues, mistakes in how you're setting up your infrastructure, and common code problems. We do this to make sure your changes are solid and won't cause any trouble later.\n\n### Talking to CodeAnt AI\nGot a question or need a hand with something in your pull request? You can easily get in touch with CodeAnt AI right here. Just type the following in a comment on your pull request, and replace \"Your question here\" with whatever you want to ask:\n<pre>\n<code>@codeant-ai ask: Your question here</code>\n</pre>\nThis lets you have a chat with CodeAnt AI about your pull request, making it easier to understand and improve your code.\n\n#### Example\n<pre>\n<code>@codeant-ai ask: Can you suggest a safer alternative to storing this secret?</code>\n</pre>\n\n### Preserve Org Learnings with CodeAnt\nYou can record team preferences so CodeAnt AI applies them in future reviews. Reply directly to the specific CodeAnt AI suggestion (in the same thread) and replace \"Your feedback here\" with your input:\n<pre>\n<code>@codeant-ai: Your feedback here</code>\n</pre>\nThis helps CodeAnt AI learn and adapt to your team's coding style and standards.\n\n#### Example\n<pre>\n<code>@codeant-ai: Do not flag unused imports.</code>\n</pre>\n\n### Retrigger review\nAsk CodeAnt AI to review the PR again, by typing:\n<pre>\n<code>@codeant-ai: review</code>\n</pre>\n\n### Check Your Repository Health\nTo analyze the health of your code repository, visit our dashboard at [https://app.codeant.ai](https://app.codeant.ai). This tool helps you identify potential issues and areas for improvement in your codebase, ensuring your repository maintains high standards of code health.\n\n</details>\n"
