+      "description": "## Summary\n\nThe Home screen now shows how much you dictated, with a 53-week activity heatmap beside the word totals, and the app keeps those numbers correct when you save, delete, or clear data. In plain terms: the dashboard tells you what you actually did, it does not double count when a recording is saved or backfilled, and clearing local data now blocks every write path until the wipe finishes.\n\n<details>\n<summary>What changed, in detail</summary>\n\n- Home is built around usage metrics and a responsive 53-week, Monday-first daily activity heatmap. Metric cards sit on both sides at desktop widths and stack below 560px. Local-date labels, accessible day details, reduced-motion-aware hover feedback, and the reference's warm palette with Geist Mono labels are kept.\n- Migration 91 adds the daily word aggregate and an idempotency ledger. A bounded keyset backfill fills old history, and live events reconcile against it. Saved-transcription metering commits with the transcription row, so the chart, monthly total, and lifetime total stay consistent.\n- Local persistence is gated during a clear across browser repositories, app storage, native database and filesystem writes, and remote receiver actions. Leases are held across multi-step and detached writes, and a failed clear keeps retries blocked until native and browser clearing can both finish.\n- Preview scenarios, shared transcription fixtures, regression tests, translations, and clear/backend documentation are added.\n- The remote receiver and sender now share one JSON message writer, and the receiver's two sender-rejection paths share one helper. `complete_local_data_clear` is registered in the Tauri bindings generator and the typed wrapper.\n</details>\n\n## Visual verification\n\nThe before/after pair uses the screenshot baseline you asked for, which is not the same commit as the PR base GitHub reports:\n\n| Role | Commit |\n| --- | --- |\n| Screenshot baseline (before) | `609f2a8724343bbbdbc7f980174d2dcbdbcadb2e` |\n| Screenshot application head (after) | `e6105912e5d6c086b747b035fe77695f18212007` |\n| Live PR base (the branch tip, moves as it lands work) | `arena/0.1.6-consolidation`, `04792bd` at the last update |\n\n- The requested design reference is [`docs/assets/image_253.png`](https://github.com/maus-inc/mausVoice/blob/arena/4337d4b4-mausvoice/docs/assets/image_253.png). It is 1157×727 and includes the visible `Alt` and `X` keycaps.\n- The before capture renders `609f2a8`, which still has the old Home cards and no `HomeAnalyticsGrid`. The after capture renders `e610591`.\n- Both use the `populated` preview route, but the two snapshots carry different fixture dates and streak values. Compare layout, not the sample values.\n- The [visual-check guide](https://github.com/maus-inc/mausVoice/blob/arena/4337d4b4-mausvoice/docs/visual-verification/pr-293-home-metric-grid.md) holds the 1157×727 pair, base/head captures at 768×1000, 390×1000, and 320×1000, an empty no-speed case, measured 559px/560px Home-frame checks, and a manual review flow that needs no app setup.\n- The earlier dark-sidebar difference in the reference-sized pair came from Chromium's graphics mode, not from product styling. The two captures are now rendered with the same graphics settings, and their sidebar crops match pixel for pixel. The guide records the pixel samples behind that conclusion.\n- These are dark browser-preview screenshots, not native Tauri captures. The one-off browser was explicitly authorized for this task and no browser or test harness was added to the repository. The guide discloses that the preview cannot record browser keypresses, that the `Alt+X` fixture was set through the exported store helper, and that a temporary Windows preview setting was restored after capture.\n\n| Screenshot baseline at 609f2a8 | Updated code at e610591 |\n| --- | --- |\n| ![Baseline Home screenshot at 1157×727](https://github.com/maus-inc/mausVoice/blob/arena/4337d4b4-mausvoice/docs/assets/pr-293-home-base-609f2a8-1157x727.png?raw=1) | ![Updated Home screenshot at 1157×727](https://github.com/maus-inc/mausVoice/blob/arena/4337d4b4-mausvoice/docs/assets/pr-293-home-head-e610591-1157x727.png?raw=1) |\n\n## Duplication fix\n\nSonarCloud flags duplication on new code, so the duplicated code was removed instead of suppressed.\n\n- `apps/desktop/src/preview/scenarios.ts` built the same populated fixture object inline for the `populated` and `permission-denied` scenarios. It now builds one `populatedWorkspaceData()` object and both scenarios use it.\n- A regression test asserts the two scenarios stay equal in value and hold distinct arrays and objects, so sharing the builder cannot leak mutable state between renders.\n- `apps/desktop/src-tauri/src/system/remote_receiver.rs` and `remote_sender.rs` each carried their own copy of the newline-delimited JSON write sequence. Both now call one helper, `system::remote_channel::write_json_message`, which takes the direction name so each error message still says which side failed.\n- The receiver repeated the record-the-error-then-send-the-delivery-error pair for both rejected senders (\"not paired\" and \"authentication failed\"). Those two paths now share one `reject_sender` method.\n- `remote_receiver.rs` and `remote_sender.rs` each declared their own copy of the message envelopes, about 47 lines that had to stay in lockstep by hand. Both directions now live once in `system::remote_channel` as `SenderMessage` and `ReceiverMessage`, so a field renamed on one side is a compile error instead of a phone that quietly stops pairing.\n- The rejection reasons were four loose strings used twice each. They are now one `SenderRejection` value that owns the code and the text the companion app shows.\n- `export_transcription` and `export_diagnostics` asked for a save destination with identical dialogs; one helper now asks. The delivered and failed status updates copied the same six event fields; one helper copies them. Eight activity tests rebuilt the same fixed timestamp; one fixture builds it.\n- New tests cover the parts that had none. All eight message kinds round-trip through JSON and keep their `type` tags, two messages written back to back arrive one per line over a real socket, and both rejections keep the exact code and text a phone displays. The receiver previously had a single test and the sender had none.\n- Local jscpd over the Rust sources at 50 tokens and 5 lines: 150 clone pairs and 1,660 duplicated lines before this commit series, 144 pairs and 1,577 lines after.\n- No Sonar exclusion, jscpd ignore, or inline suppression comment was added.\n- SonarCloud now reports **0 duplicated lines on new code (0.0% density)**, down from 40 lines at 0.5%, with 0 new issues, 0 accepted issues, 0 security hotspots, and no annotations. The quality gate passes. A local jscpd scan against the live PR base `86dc7c3`, using Sonar's source scope and exclusions at 100 tokens and 10 lines, reports zero new clone pairs.\n\n### Deliberately left in place\n\n- The PCM frame loops in `apps/desktop/src-tauri/src/system/audio_store.rs` duplicate 33 lines between the float and integer decode paths. Unifying them needs a generic reader over `hound` samples, nothing currently asserts decoded sample values, and a mistake there is inaudible until dictation breaks. That belongs in its own change with audio tests.\n- The `term_*`, `conversation_*`, and `chat_message_*` create/update pairs repeat \"acquire the clear guard, call one query, map the error\". That is one uniform convention across roughly forty commands; converting three of them would make the command layer inconsistent, and converting all of them is a sweep this PR should not carry.\n- `docs/` is still excluded from Prettier. The PR base branch `arena/0.1.6-consolidation` now carries docs files Prettier would rewrite (`docs/sandbox-toolchain-vendor-spec.md` among them), and the formatting check runs on this branch merged into that base, so flipping the gate here would fail on files this PR does not own. It needs a small PR on the base branch that formats `docs/` and drops the ignore line.\n- `apps/desktop/DESIGN.md` said the heatmap is Sunday-first while the code lays weeks out Monday-first; the guide is corrected here, and the code is unchanged.\n\n## Verification\n\n### Current head `c6b456260864089cdad0597c099e2df0338ad916` (the base branch merged in)\n\n- Every non-skipped check passes: desktop builds on Linux, Windows, and macOS ([run](https://github.com/maus-inc/mausVoice/actions/runs/41094191967)), the lint matrix with fmt and clippy on all three platforms ([run](https://github.com/maus-inc/mausVoice/actions/runs/41094191856)), Rust and TypeScript unit tests, i18n catalog sync, the Windows-gated Rust job and the Voice-AI package tests ([run](https://github.com/maus-inc/mausVoice/actions/runs/41094191966)), integration tests ([run](https://github.com/maus-inc/mausVoice/actions/runs/41094191821)), the docs build ([run](https://github.com/maus-inc/mausVoice/actions/runs/41094191825)), repository formatting and i18n idempotence ([run](https://github.com/maus-inc/mausVoice/actions/runs/41094205889)), and Gitleaks ([run](https://github.com/maus-inc/mausVoice/actions/runs/41094205904)).\n- SonarCloud passes with no annotations; CodeAnt (quality, SAST, SCA, SCR, test coverage), DeepScan, Greptile, Buoy, and Socket pass. There are zero unresolved review threads and the PR is mergeable.\n- CodeRabbit, DeepSource, Sourcery, and cubic were skipped on this head, and Deploy Docs does not run for pull requests.\n- The Rust work is validated only by CI, because this environment has no Rust toolchain. The first push of it failed clippy for one real reason: the trust check moved into a `match` guard and left the accepting arm's binding unused, which `-D warnings` rejects. `f8065eb` fixes that, and every job above runs on top of the fix.\n\n### Merged the base branch\n\n- `arena/0.1.6-consolidation` moved while this branch was open, so the branch now merges it. The only conflict was in `updateUserPreferences`, where this branch added a local-data write lease and the base added a `showErrorToast` option: both are kept, with the third parameter becoming one options bag that holds `existingLease` and `showErrorToast`. Callers that already hold a lease pass `{ existingLease: lease }`; the microphone dialog passes `{ showErrorToast: false }`. The toast suppression covers both failure paths, loading the existing preferences and saving them.\n- The microphone dialog test that the base branch added asserted the saved payload as the sole argument to `setUserPreferences`. It now also expects the lease, matching how the other preference tests assert a leased write.\n- Checked locally on the merged tree: type checks pass (9 tasks), lint passes (3 tasks), Prettier passes, the i18n extractor leaves the catalogs unchanged, and the desktop unit suite passes apart from the 54 eval and integration tests that need a `GROQ_API_KEY` this environment does not have. CI runs those.\n\n### Earlier heads\n\n- `f8065eb08caff0e423538ff8ba1e06bfaea087a7` passed the same checks: [desktop builds](https://github.com/maus-inc/mausVoice/actions/runs/41062809510), [lint matrix](https://github.com/maus-inc/mausVoice/actions/runs/41062809116), [unit tests](https://github.com/maus-inc/mausVoice/actions/runs/41062809016), [integration tests](https://github.com/maus-inc/mausVoice/actions/runs/41062809360), [formatting](https://github.com/maus-inc/mausVoice/actions/runs/41062830461), and [Gitleaks](https://github.com/maus-inc/mausVoice/actions/runs/41062830408).\n- `ef15acb3b3860ad8b13e1f4aa5314de616147a36` passed the same checks: [desktop builds](https://github.com/maus-inc/mausVoice/actions/runs/41044513745), [lint matrix](https://github.com/maus-inc/mausVoice/actions/runs/41044513453), [unit tests and i18n sync](https://github.com/maus-inc/mausVoice/actions/runs/41044513469), [integration tests](https://github.com/maus-inc/mausVoice/actions/runs/41044513399), [formatting and i18n idempotence](https://github.com/maus-inc/mausVoice/actions/runs/41044519208), and [Gitleaks](https://github.com/maus-inc/mausVoice/actions/runs/41044519102).\n- `732593ae8c808d3ec532d01c1de6948c424642d7` passed the same checks: [desktop builds](https://github.com/maus-inc/mausVoice/actions/runs/40992787045), [lint matrix](https://github.com/maus-inc/mausVoice/actions/runs/40992786949), [unit tests and i18n sync](https://github.com/maus-inc/mausVoice/actions/runs/40992786948), [integration tests](https://github.com/maus-inc/mausVoice/actions/runs/40992786958), [docs build](https://github.com/maus-inc/mausVoice/actions/runs/40992786947), [formatting and i18n idempotence](https://github.com/maus-inc/mausVoice/actions/runs/40992795457), and [Gitleaks](https://github.com/maus-inc/mausVoice/actions/runs/40992795420).\n- The application code head `e6105912e5d6c086b747b035fe77695f18212007` passed the same build, lint, unit, integration, i18n, formatting, secret-scan, and quality checks: [desktop builds](https://github.com/maus-inc/mausVoice/actions/runs/40966344096), [unit tests and i18n sync](https://github.com/maus-inc/mausVoice/actions/runs/40966344252), [integration tests](https://github.com/maus-inc/mausVoice/actions/runs/40966343995), [lint matrix](https://github.com/maus-inc/mausVoice/actions/runs/40966343947), [format and i18n idempotence](https://github.com/maus-inc/mausVoice/actions/runs/40966354461), and [Gitleaks](https://github.com/maus-inc/mausVoice/actions/runs/40966354473).\n- The screenshot commit `5f0bda1` and the guide commit `00eabc8` were documentation and image changes; the same checks passed on both.\n\n### Local validation\n\n- Root `pnpm run check-types` passes all 9 tasks, root `pnpm run lint` passes both of its tasks, and root `pnpm run build` passes 11 of 11 tasks. The build prints existing non-fatal warnings about unresolved docs assets, `node:crypto` externalization, and large chunks.\n- Desktop preview scenario tests pass (9 of 9) and the preview package passes 22 of 22.\n- The desktop unit suite passes on CI. The full local root test command still needs `GROQ_API_KEY` for 54 desktop eval and integration tests, which the CI integration job covers.\n- This environment has no Rust toolchain, so the Rust changes could not be compiled locally. As a pre-check, a rustfmt-on-WASM build confirmed every touched file parses and is rustfmt-clean. It changes `remote_receiver.rs`, `remote_sender.rs`, `system/mod.rs`, and adds `system/remote_channel.rs`. CI validates it on `ef15acb`: `cargo fmt --check` and `cargo clippy -D warnings` pass on Linux, macOS, and Windows, the desktop Rust unit tests pass, and the Windows-gated Rust job passes. As a local pre-check, a rustfmt-on-WASM build confirmed all four touched files are already rustfmt-clean and parse. No lockfile changed. The repository-owned Rust checks recorded on `e610591` stand: all seven Cargo.lock hashes and offline metadata, formatting for six crates, clippy for desktop/shared/GTK, desktop library tests (399 passed, 1 ignored), transcription library tests (64 passed, 1 ignored), shared pill tests (237), GTK pill tests (42), sidecar integration (7 passed, 4 ignored), and `scripts/check-bindings.sh`. No lockfile changed.\n- Vendor provenance: the repository-owned snapshot at `maus-inc/mausVoice` commit `61fb32959d6ac6a36b0c6356069a767ee7725caa` contains `rust/cargo-vendor.tar.xz.part-00` and `.part-01` (combined SHA-256 `787dd7e4a2d0aedc3634119003e4c5d0aa347310bcd1b596033b45adbbf5182f`). The extracted `cap-fs-ext-4.0.3/` package has registry checksum `56ff379b70af8e08307a8f65e7040c7301cb4a572538ade16b4984f0da77847f`, matching the lockfile.\n- The preview demo used a stale `variant=\"blue\"` on a button that only accepts `contained`, `text`, `flat`, and `chrome`. That broke the root type check on this branch. It is now `chrome`, matching the theme and the screenshot baseline.\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated description by cubic. -->\n<a href=\"https://cubic.dev/pr/maus-inc/mausVoice/pull/293?utm_source=github\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" data-no-image-dialog=\"true\"><picture><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\" srcset=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-dark.svg\"><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\" srcset=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-light.svg\"><img alt=\"View guided diff\" src=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-light.svg\"></picture></a> <a href=\"https://www.cubic.dev/action/auto-fix/pr/maus-inc/mausVoice/293?returnTo=https%3A%2F%2Fgithub.com%2Fmaus-inc%2FmausVoice%2Fpull%2F293&source=description\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" data-no-image-dialog=\"true\"><picture><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\" srcset=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/turn-on-auto-fix-dark.svg\"><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\" srcset=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/turn-on-auto-fix-light.svg\"><img alt=\"Turn on auto-fix\" src=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/turn-on-auto-fix-light.svg\"></picture></a>\n<!-- End of auto-generated description by cubic. -->\n\n\n___\n\n## **CodeAnt-AI Description**\n**See daily dictation activity and usage totals on Home**\n\n### What Changed\n- Home now shows a 53-week daily activity chart with word counts, active-day totals, and accessible day-by-day details.\n- Successful dictations update daily, monthly, and lifetime totals once. Older saved dictations are included when their dates are viewed; failed dictations and dictations received from another device are excluded.\n- Incognito dictations count only when the stats option is enabled, without saving transcript or audio for those events.\n- Monthly usage no longer shows a previous month’s total, and clearing local data also removes activity records.\n\n### Impact\n`✅ Daily dictation history at a glance`\n`✅ Accurate monthly and lifetime word totals`\n`✅ Incognito stats without transcript or audio storage`\n<details><summary><strong>💡 Usage Guide</strong></summary>\n\n### Checking Your Pull Request\nEvery time you make a pull request, our system automatically looks through it. We check for security issues, mistakes in how you're setting up your infrastructure, and common code problems. We do this to make sure your changes are solid and won't cause any trouble later.\n\n### Talking to CodeAnt AI\nGot a question or need a hand with something in your pull request? You can easily get in touch with CodeAnt AI right here. Just type the following in a comment on your pull request, and replace \"Your question here\" with whatever you want to ask:\n<pre>\n<code>@codeant-ai ask: Your question here</code>\n</pre>\nThis lets you have a chat with CodeAnt AI about your pull request, making it easier to understand and improve your code.\n\n#### Example\n<pre>\n<code>@codeant-ai ask: Can you suggest a safer alternative to storing this secret?</code>\n</pre>\n\n### Preserve Org Learnings with CodeAnt\nYou can record team preferences so CodeAnt AI applies them in future reviews. Reply directly to the specific CodeAnt AI suggestion (in the same thread) and replace \"Your feedback here\" with your input:\n<pre>\n<code>@codeant-ai: Your feedback here</code>\n</pre>\nThis helps CodeAnt AI learn and adapt to your team's coding style and standards.\n\n#### Example\n<pre>\n<code>@codeant-ai: Do not flag unused imports.</code>\n</pre>\n\n### Retrigger review\nAsk CodeAnt AI to review the PR again, by typing:\n<pre>\n<code>@codeant-ai: review</code>\n</pre>\n\n### Check Your Repository Health\nTo analyze the health of your code repository, visit our dashboard at [https://app.codeant.ai](https://app.codeant.ai). This tool helps you identify potential issues and areas for improvement in your codebase, ensuring your repository maintains high standards of code health.\n\n</details>\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n