+      "description": "## **User description**\n## What changed?\n\nOne file, `.deepsource.toml`, adding a second `[[overrides]]` block that switches the JavaScript analyzer off for `.agents/**` and `.claude/**`.\n\n`.agents/skills` holds 56 third-party skill trees, byte for byte as published, and `skills-lock.json` records a folder hash for each one. Sixteen of their files are `.js`, `.cjs` or `.mjs`:\n\n- `.agents/skills/impeccable/scripts/modern-screenshot.umd.js`, a minified UMD bundle of 29 KB on 14 lines.\n- `.agents/skills/impeccable/scripts/live-browser.js`, 547 KB hand-written.\n- 7 CommonJS scripts across `brand` and `design-system`.\n- 4 `.mjs` scripts under `ui-capture`.\n\nNone of it is written in this repository and none of it may be edited, because a single reformat changes the folder hash and fails `scripts/ci/verify-skills.mjs`. That is the same trade the marketing vendor bundles already needed: an analyzer reading third-party code reports style findings nobody here can act on, and a gate counting those is a gate nobody reads.\n\nA second block rather than a wider first one, because the reason differs even though the action is identical. `[[overrides]]` has no key to hang a rationale on, so the comment stays next to the block it explains.\n\n`.claude/**` is listed because `.claude/skills` is a symlink onto the same tree, so a checkout that follows symlinks would otherwise analyse it twice.\n\n## What this does not do\n\n**It does not repair the failing DeepScan check on #313.** DeepScan and DeepSource are different services: the failing check points at `deepscan.io` and this file configures `app.deepsource.com`. DeepScan takes its analysis scope from its dashboard and has no in-repo config file, so the JavaScript findings it raised on the vendored tree cannot be excluded from this repository. That needs a maintainer with dashboard access to add `.agents/**` to DeepScan's exclusion list.\n\n`DeepSource: Analysis` was already reporting `skipping` on #313, so this is preventive: it keeps the same wall from appearing once DeepSource does analyse a pull request.\n\n## How is it tested?\n\n- [x] Automated tests\n- [x] Manual verification\n- [x] Code inspection\n\n`check-workspace-hygiene.test.mjs` has a guard, \"every DeepSource exclusion still excludes something\", that reads this file, extracts every `paths` array, compiles each glob and asserts it matches at least one tracked file, so an exclusion cannot rot silently. It passes with both new globs.\n\n| Gate | Result |\n| --- | --- |\n| `node --test scripts/ci/check-workspace-hygiene.test.mjs` | 27 of 27, including that guard |\n| `node --test scripts/ci/*.test.mjs` | 371 of 371 |\n| `pnpm run format:check` | pass |\n| `pnpm run lint` | pass, 0 warnings 0 errors |\n| `pnpm run skills:verify` | 53 of 53 locked, 3 unrecorded |\n\nThe file parses as TOML and yields `version = 1`, one analyzer (`javascript`, enabled), and two overrides, each disabling only `javascript` for its paths. `.claude/skills` resolves to `../.agents/skills` as claimed.\n\nTOML is outside the root `format:check` glob (`**/*.{ts,tsx,md}`), so no formatter covers this file; it was checked by parsing instead.\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated description by cubic. -->\n<a href=\"https://cubic.dev/pr/maus-inc/mausVoice/pull/314?utm_source=github\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" data-no-image-dialog=\"true\"><picture><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\" srcset=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-dark.svg\"><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\" srcset=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-light.svg\"><img alt=\"View guided diff\" src=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-light.svg\"></picture></a> <a href=\"https://www.cubic.dev/action/auto-fix/pr/maus-inc/mausVoice/314?returnTo=https%3A%2F%2Fgithub.com%2Fmaus-inc%2FmausVoice%2Fpull%2F314&source=description\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" data-no-image-dialog=\"true\"><picture><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\" srcset=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/turn-on-auto-fix-dark.svg\"><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\" srcset=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/turn-on-auto-fix-light.svg\"><img alt=\"Turn on auto-fix\" src=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/turn-on-auto-fix-light.svg\"></picture></a>\n<!-- End of auto-generated description by cubic. -->\n\n## Summary by Sourcery\n\nEnhancements:\n- Exclude vendored agent skill trees from DeepSource JavaScript analysis while retaining analysis for repository-owned code.\n\n\n___\n\n## **CodeAnt-AI Description**\n**Exclude vendored agent skills from DeepSource JavaScript checks**\n\n### What Changed\n- DeepSource no longer runs JavaScript analysis on vendored skills under `.agents/**` and `.claude/**`, which cannot be changed in this repository.\n\n### Impact\n`✅ Fewer DeepSource findings from vendored code`\n`✅ JavaScript checks focus on code this repository can change`\n<details><summary><strong>💡 Usage Guide</strong></summary>\n\n### Checking Your Pull Request\nEvery time you make a pull request, our system automatically looks through it. We check for security issues, mistakes in how you're setting up your infrastructure, and common code problems. We do this to make sure your changes are solid and won't cause any trouble later.\n\n### Talking to CodeAnt AI\nGot a question or need a hand with something in your pull request? You can easily get in touch with CodeAnt AI right here. Just type the following in a comment on your pull request, and replace \"Your question here\" with whatever you want to ask:\n<pre>\n<code>@codeant-ai ask: Your question here</code>\n</pre>\nThis lets you have a chat with CodeAnt AI about your pull request, making it easier to understand and improve your code.\n\n#### Example\n<pre>\n<code>@codeant-ai ask: Can you suggest a safer alternative to storing this secret?</code>\n</pre>\n\n### Preserve Org Learnings with CodeAnt\nYou can record team preferences so CodeAnt AI applies them in future reviews. Reply directly to the specific CodeAnt AI suggestion (in the same thread) and replace \"Your feedback here\" with your input:\n<pre>\n<code>@codeant-ai: Your feedback here</code>\n</pre>\nThis helps CodeAnt AI learn and adapt to your team's coding style and standards.\n\n#### Example\n<pre>\n<code>@codeant-ai: Do not flag unused imports.</code>\n</pre>\n\n### Retrigger review\nAsk CodeAnt AI to review the PR again, by typing:\n<pre>\n<code>@codeant-ai: review</code>\n</pre>\n\n### Check Your Repository Health\nTo analyze the health of your code repository, visit our dashboard at [https://app.codeant.ai](https://app.codeant.ai). This tool helps you identify potential issues and areas for improvement in your codebase, ensuring your repository maintains high standards of code health.\n\n</details>\n\n\n<!-- greptile_comment -->\n\n<!-- greptile_summary -->\n\n<h2><a href=\"https://app.greptile.com/api/retrigger?id=90223586\"><picture><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\" srcset=\"https://greptile-static-assets.s3.amazonaws.com/badges/RetriggerDark.svg?v=2\"><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\" srcset=\"https://greptile-static-assets.s3.amazonaws.com/badges/Retrigger.svg?v=2\"><img alt=\"Retrigger\" src=\"https://greptile-static-assets.s3.amazonaws.com/badges/Retrigger.svg?v=2\" align=\"right\"></picture></a><a href=\"https://app.greptile.com/owie/github/maus-inc/mausvoice/-/pull/314?utm_source=greptile_review&amp;utm_medium=github&amp;utm_campaign=view_in_greptile\"><picture><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\" srcset=\"https://greptile-static-assets.s3.amazonaws.com/badges/ViewInGreptileDark.svg?v=2\"><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\" srcset=\"https://greptile-static-assets.s3.amazonaws.com/badges/ViewInGreptile.svg?v=2\"><img alt=\"View in Greptile\" src=\"https://greptile-static-assets.s3.amazonaws.com/badges/ViewInGreptile.svg?v=2\" align=\"right\"></picture></a>Confidence Score: 4/5</h2>\n\n<!-- greptile-risk -->\n\nThe PR appears safe to merge, with a non-blocking concern about excluding project-owned scripts.\n\n<h2>Findings</h2>\n\n1. <img alt=\"P2\" src=\"https://greptile-static-assets.s3.amazonaws.com/badges/p2.svg?v=9\" align=\"top\">&nbsp;**Editable scripts lose checks** <a href=\"https://github.com/maus-inc/mausVoice/pull/314#discussion_r4407490857\">▶</a>\n\n<details><summary>Fix with agent prompt</summary>\n\n`````markdown\n### Issue 1\n.deepsource.toml:39\nThese patterns also disable DeepSource checks for the four project-owned scripts in `.agents/skills/ui-capture/scripts/`. `AGENTS.md` lists `ui-capture` as project-owned, and `verify-skills.mjs` allows these unlocked files to change. Unlike the locked vendor code, findings here can be fixed locally.\n\nNarrow both exclusions to the locked skill folders, and update the comment so it does not describe all 56 skills as immutable.\n\nNote: If this suggestion doesn't match your team's coding style, reply to this and let me know. I'll remember it for next time!\n\n---\n\nFor each issue above, determine whether it is valid and should be fixed. If so, fix it directly.\n`````\n\n</details>\n\n<details><summary><h3>Summary</h3></summary>\n\nAdds a second DeepSource override to disable JavaScript analysis under `.agents/**` and `.claude/**`.\n- DeepSource skips JavaScript checks for the vendored skills.\n</details>\n\n<!-- greptile_confidence_score:4 -->\n\n<sub>Reviews (1) · Last reviewed commit: [\"Exclude the vendored skills from the Dee...\"](https://github.com/maus-inc/mausvoice/commit/b01c0c35cd51dd32949e88f12bf41e892ad50c7e) · [Reviewed by Greptile](https://www.greptile.com/?utm_source=greptile_review&utm_medium=github&utm_campaign=review_public&utm_content=maus-inc/mausvoice)</sub>\n\n<!-- /greptile_comment -->"
