+      "description": "## What changed?\n\nBrings the 56 ported design and UI skills into the repo with their lock, makes them load-bearing, and fixes a typecheck regression in `apps/preview` that no CI job was covering.\n\n**Skills and routing (803 files under `.agents/skills/`)**\n- 56 skills, byte for byte from `better-Shape/app` `mega/absorb-all` at `008b0cbae2b5`, plus `skills-lock.json` and `scripts/ci/verify-skills.mjs`. `find-skills`, `ui-capture` and `unslop` are project-owned and carry no lock entry.\n- `.claude/skills` is a symlink to `.agents/skills`. `.gitignore` changed from `.claude` to `.claude/*` plus `!.claude/skills`, because git cannot re-add a file whose parent directory is excluded.\n- `.prettierignore` now excludes `.agents/` and `.claude/`. Reformatting vendored markdown would break every `computedHash` and fail the verifier.\n- Duplicate check done and recorded in `engineering/design-skills.md`. The single name collision, `find-skills`, is one skill at two fidelities rather than two skills. The 6 byte-identical reference files shared by `banner-design`, `design` and `slides` must stay duplicated, because `computedHash` is a folder hash.\n\n**Engineering docs**\n- `engineering/` carries the toolchain and design material. The two hard constraints, proactive problem solving and deep refinement, are inline in `AGENTS.md` at full depth so a pointer cannot lose them. `engineering/proactive-protocol.md` and `engineering/deep-refinement-protocol.md` remain as fallbacks for a tooling truncation.\n- `AGENTS.md` raises its own budget from 400 to 560 lines with the rationale written down, rather than silently breaking the rule it states.\n- `docs/decisions/` records three durable decisions, including the vendor spec errata for four statements the built branch proved wrong.\n\n**The design spec already existed**\n- `apps/desktop/DESIGN.md` is authoritative, `apps/desktop/docs/design-system-baseline.md` is its short extract, and `apps/preview/specs/` holds 39 generated specs. These now lead the load order in `AGENTS.md`, `engineering/design-skills.md` and `.agents/PREFLIGHT.md`.\n- Corrected two wrong fit claims: `sonner` is a real dependency with `SonnerToaster.tsx`, and this repo has no Tailwind build step despite `tailwind-merge` being present.\n\n**`apps/preview` was failing typecheck on `main`**\n- Two real `TS2769` errors: `<Button variant=\"blue\">` against a union that declares only `flat` and `chrome`. No workflow ran the package, so nothing caught it while the app worked at runtime and its 22 tests passed.\n- The demo now uses `variant=\"chrome\"`, which is declared, is styled at `theme.ts:546`, and is the name `DESIGN.md` uses for the silver and ink accent.\n- `apps/preview` gains a `lint` script and `oxlint` at the version already in the tree, and `test-desktop-unit.yml` now runs its `check-types` and `lint`.\n\n## How is it tested?\n\n- [x] Automated tests\n- [x] Manual verification\n- [x] Code inspection\n\nGates run on this exact tree with the pinned toolchain (`pnpm@10.34.5`, prettier `3.9.6`):\n\n| Gate | Result |\n| --- | --- |\n| `pnpm run format:check` | pass |\n| `pnpm run lint` | pass, 0 warnings 0 errors |\n| `pnpm run check-types` (root, 13 packages) | 9 of 9 tasks, was red before this branch |\n| `pnpm --filter @maus-inc/preview run test` | 22 of 22 |\n| `pnpm run skills:verify` | 53 of 53 locked, 3 unrecorded |\n| `node --test scripts/ci/*.test.mjs` | 371 of 371 |\n\nNot covered: no browser automation exists in this repo, so no recorded UI capture. `apps/preview` was inspected as the substitute surface, which is recorded in `docs/decisions/no-playwright-harness.md`.\n\nThe vendor toolchain branch `vendor/sandbox-toolchain` is deliberately untouched by this PR and still carries no pull request of its own.\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated description by cubic. -->\n<a href=\"https://cubic.dev/pr/maus-inc/mausVoice/pull/313?utm_source=github\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" data-no-image-dialog=\"true\"><picture><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\" srcset=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-dark.svg\"><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\" srcset=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-light.svg\"><img alt=\"View guided diff\" src=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-light.svg\"></picture></a>\n<!-- End of auto-generated description by cubic. -->\n\n\n\n<!-- greptile_comment -->\n\n<!-- greptile_summary -->\n\n<h2><a href=\"https://app.greptile.com/api/retrigger?id=90219427\"><picture><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\" srcset=\"https://greptile-static-assets.s3.amazonaws.com/badges/RetriggerDark.svg?v=2\"><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\" srcset=\"https://greptile-static-assets.s3.amazonaws.com/badges/Retrigger.svg?v=2\"><img alt=\"Retrigger\" src=\"https://greptile-static-assets.s3.amazonaws.com/badges/Retrigger.svg?v=2\" align=\"right\"></picture></a><a href=\"https://app.greptile.com/owie/github/maus-inc/mausvoice/-/pull/313?utm_source=greptile_review&amp;utm_medium=github&amp;utm_campaign=view_in_greptile\"><picture><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\" srcset=\"https://greptile-static-assets.s3.amazonaws.com/badges/ViewInGreptileDark.svg?v=2\"><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\" srcset=\"https://greptile-static-assets.s3.amazonaws.com/badges/ViewInGreptile.svg?v=2\"><img alt=\"View in Greptile\" src=\"https://greptile-static-assets.s3.amazonaws.com/badges/ViewInGreptile.svg?v=2\" align=\"right\"></picture></a>Confidence Score: 4/5</h2>\n\n<!-- greptile-risk -->\n\nThe preview fix appears safe to merge, with non-blocking fixes needed in the new verification tooling and documentation.\n\n<h2>Findings</h2>\n\n1. <img alt=\"P2\" src=\"https://greptile-static-assets.s3.amazonaws.com/badges/p2.svg?v=9\" align=\"top\">&nbsp;**Unchanged skills fail on Windows** <a href=\"https://github.com/maus-inc/mausVoice/pull/313#discussion_r4407462834\">▶</a>\n2. <img alt=\"P2\" src=\"https://greptile-static-assets.s3.amazonaws.com/badges/p2.svg?v=9\" align=\"top\">&nbsp;**CI skips the skill check** <a href=\"https://github.com/maus-inc/mausVoice/pull/313#discussion_r4407462839\">▶</a>\n3. <img alt=\"P2\" src=\"https://greptile-static-assets.s3.amazonaws.com/badges/p2.svg?v=9\" align=\"top\">&nbsp;**Cleanup deletes the Git repository** <a href=\"https://github.com/maus-inc/mausVoice/pull/313#discussion_r4407462843\">▶</a>\n4. <img alt=\"P2\" src=\"https://greptile-static-assets.s3.amazonaws.com/badges/p2.svg?v=9\" align=\"top\">&nbsp;**File read sends POST** <a href=\"https://github.com/maus-inc/mausVoice/pull/313#discussion_r4407462848\">▶</a>\n5. <img alt=\"P2\" src=\"https://greptile-static-assets.s3.amazonaws.com/badges/p2.svg?v=9\" align=\"top\">&nbsp;**Capture sends the wrong click** <a href=\"https://github.com/maus-inc/mausVoice/pull/313#discussion_r4407462854\">▶</a>\n6. <img alt=\"P2\" src=\"https://greptile-static-assets.s3.amazonaws.com/badges/p2.svg?v=9\" align=\"top\">&nbsp;**Click markers leave the pointer** <a href=\"https://github.com/maus-inc/mausVoice/pull/313#discussion_r4407462862\">▶</a>\n7. <img alt=\"P2\" src=\"https://greptile-static-assets.s3.amazonaws.com/badges/p2.svg?v=9\" align=\"top\">&nbsp;**Recording length limit does nothing** <a href=\"https://github.com/maus-inc/mausVoice/pull/313#discussion_r4407462866\">▶</a>\n8. <img alt=\"P2\" src=\"https://greptile-static-assets.s3.amazonaws.com/badges/p2.svg?v=9\" align=\"top\">&nbsp;**Contact sheet misses later actions** <a href=\"https://github.com/maus-inc/mausVoice/pull/313#discussion_r4407462872\">▶</a>\n9. <img alt=\"P2\" src=\"https://greptile-static-assets.s3.amazonaws.com/badges/p2.svg?v=9\" align=\"top\">&nbsp;**Caption check reads wrong frame** <a href=\"https://github.com/maus-inc/mausVoice/pull/313#discussion_r4407462881\">▶</a>\n\n<details><summary>Fix with agent prompt</summary>\n\n`````markdown\n### Issue 1\nscripts/ci/verify-skills.mjs:35\n`relative(root, full)` uses backslashes on Windows, but the committed hashes use forward-slash paths. Locked skills with nested files therefore report `DRIFT` even when unchanged. Normalize the paths before hashing. Also pin the vendored text files to LF so checkout settings cannot change the bytes being checked.\n\n### Issue 2\npackage.json:13\nNo workflow calls `skills:verify` or `verify-skills.mjs`. A changed vendored file can therefore pass CI without matching its lock entry. Add a check that runs when the skills, lock, or verifier changes.\n\n### Issue 3\ndocs/sandbox-toolchain-vendor-spec.md:1284\n`./.[!.]*` matches `.git`, so this cleanup deletes the clone's Git metadata. The following `git add`, `commit`, and `push` commands cannot work. Remove the tracked source with Git or explicitly preserve `.git` during cleanup.\n\n### Issue 4\ndocs/sandbox-toolchain-vendor-spec.md:1344-1347\n`gh api` switches to POST when `-f` supplies a field. This command therefore does not read the file from the requested branch. Add `--method GET` so `ref` becomes a query parameter.\n\n### Issue 5\n.agents/skills/ui-capture/scripts/capture.mjs:251-256\nThe `click` step sends inputs in the wrong order:\n- A right-click step first sends a left click, which can activate the control before its context menu opens.\n- The `holdMs` wait happens before the real mouse press, so the control is never held down.\n\nChoose the button before pressing and put the wait between the matching mouse-down and mouse-up calls.\n\n### Issue 6\n.agents/skills/ui-capture/scripts/overlay.js:120-122\nBoth effects play near the page origin rather than at the clicked control:\n- The ripple never receives a position beyond `top: 0; left: 0`.\n- The ring's animation replaces the `transform` that moves it to the pointer.\n\nPut the position on a wrapper or use separate position properties so the scale animations cannot replace it.\n\n### Issue 7\n.agents/skills/ui-capture/scripts/encode.mjs:153-157\n`--max-seconds` changes only the output frame rate, not the clip's timestamps. For example, 1,800 frames captured at 60 fps still produce a roughly 30-second clip with `--max-seconds 12`. Rescale timestamps to the chosen duration before sampling the frames.\n\n### Issue 8\n.agents/skills/ui-capture/scripts/encode.mjs:194-196\nWith 900 frames at 60 fps, this formula samples at 19 fps and fills its 48 cells in about 2.5 seconds. It misses the rest of the 15-second flow, including the final state. Compute the sampling rate from the clip duration and cell count so the sheet covers the whole recording.\n\n### Issue 9\n.agents/skills/ui-capture/scripts/validate.mjs:239\n`stats.frames` counts encoded GIF frames, but `s.startFrame` and the JPEG filenames count raw capture frames. Encoding drops frames and can merge still frames. For a late final caption, this can select a JPEG just two raw frames after the caption starts, while it is still fading in, and fail OCR despite correct text. Use `tl.capturedFrames` for the final raw-frame boundary.\n\n---\n\nFor each issue above, determine whether it is valid and should be fixed. If so, fix it directly.\n`````\n\n</details>\n\n<details><summary><h3>Summary</h3></summary>\n\nAdds 56 local skills, a folder-hash verifier, design guidance, and offline toolchain documentation. Replaces the preview's unsupported `blue` button variant with `chrome` and adds preview typecheck and lint steps.\n\n- Repository agents can use local design skills under the existing design rules.\n- Agent instructions and engineering guides make the project’s working rules easier to follow.\n- The preview button demo uses the declared chrome variant, and CI checks preview types and lint.\n</details>\n\n<!-- greptile_confidence_score:4 -->\n\n<sub>Reviews (1) · Last reviewed commit: [\"Add vendored design skills, engineering ...\"](https://github.com/maus-inc/mausvoice/commit/3a0c95e0b4788067ef22a551b704e62a1292661d) · [Reviewed by Greptile](https://www.greptile.com/?utm_source=greptile_review&utm_medium=github&utm_campaign=review_public&utm_content=maus-inc/mausvoice)</sub>\n\n<!-- /greptile_comment -->"
