+      "description": "## **User description**\nWhen you finish speaking, the floating dictation pill shows status words like \"Finalizing audio\", \"Transcribing\", \"Polishing\", and \"Inserting\" while the app turns your voice into text. Previously, showing those status words hid the moving loading bar completely, so the pill looked frozen whenever a step took more than a moment. This pull request brings the loading bar back behind the status words at a dim brightness so the words stay easy to read while the bar keeps moving underneath, and it fixes a few places where the pill showed the wrong step name or kept an old step label on screen too long. To test it, record a short dictation and watch the pill after you stop speaking. You should see the dim bar glide behind \"Finalizing audio\", \"Transcribing\", \"Polishing\", and \"Inserting\", and if you turn on Reduce Motion in your system settings, the bar should sit still in the middle of the pill instead of moving.\n\n<details>\n<summary>What changed under the hood</summary>\n\n### Shared pill layout and opacity rules\n\n`packages/rust_pill_shared/src/lib.rs` now owns the loading bar geometry, the opacity levels, the stage text width budget, and the phase clearing rule for all three native pills. When no stage label is on screen, the pill draws the track at `0.15` alpha and the moving bar at `0.70` alpha. When a stage label is present, the pill dims the track to `0.08` alpha and the moving bar to `0.22` alpha beneath the `0.90` alpha text. `unit_progress` clamps the spring expansion progress and bar offset to `0.0..=1.0` so spring overshoot never pushes alpha above `1.0` or sends the bar outside the track. `advance_loading_offset` holds the bar at `0.5` when OS reduced motion is active and scales movement to 60 frames per second otherwise.\n\n### Native pill renderers on macOS, Linux, and Windows\n\n`packages/rust_macos_pill/src/draw.rs`, `packages/rust_gtk_pill/src/draw.rs`, and `packages/rust_windows_pill/src/draw.rs` no longer return early when `stage_text` is set. Each renderer paints the dimmed loading bar first, shortens the stage label with an ellipsis through `rust_pill_shared::text_fit::elide_to_width` if a translation runs wider than the pill, draws the centered `12px` label on top, and paints the edge gradient once at the end. On macOS, `draw_loading` now fills flat-ended rectangles instead of round-capped strokes so the bar matches GTK, Windows, and the paused state, and it drops a redundant inner save and restore pair around `show_text`. In `app.rs` and `pill.rs`, `InMessage::StageText` trims incoming text and ignores whitespace-only strings, and `InMessage::Phase` clears `stage_text` through `should_clear_stage_text_on_phase` so the pill keeps \"Finalizing audio\" when that label arrives right before `Phase::Loading`.\n\n### Desktop stage labels, pipeline traces, and browser preview\n\n- `apps/desktop/src/strategies/dictation.strategy.ts` and `apps/desktop/src/actions/transcribe.actions.ts` resolve `effectiveToneId` before post-processing and skip both the \"Polishing\" pill label and the `polished` pipeline trace mark when the active tone disables post-processing, such as Verbatim.\n- `apps/desktop/src/utils/output-routing.utils.ts` wraps local and remote text delivery in `deliverWithInsertionStage` so the pill shows \"Inserting\" before `handsFreeDelayMs` starts counting down and only records the `inserted` trace mark when the app actually delivers the final text.\n- `apps/desktop/src/strategies/dictation.strategy.ts` sends \"Inserting\" when `handleFinalStreamedTranscript` drains buffered streaming text on stop.\n- `apps/desktop/src/strategies/agent.strategy.ts` clears the pill stage label with `sendPillStageText(null)` before `sendChatMessage` starts streaming the assistant reply.\n- `apps/desktop/src/components/root/DictationSideEffects.tsx` passes `pipelineTraceRef.current` into `storeTranscription` when saving a reviewed transcript and uses `sendPhaseToPill(\"idle\")` when type mode turns on.\n- `apps/preview/src/recreated/native-pill.tsx`, `apps/preview/src/demos/pill.tsx`, and `apps/preview/specs/native-pill.md` mirror the dimmed loading bar and stage label behavior in the browser preview.\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>Verification</summary>\n\n- `pnpm run format:check`\n- `pnpm --filter desktop run i18n && git diff --exit-code -- apps/desktop/src/i18n`\n- `pnpm --filter desktop run check-types` and `pnpm --filter @maus-inc/preview run check-types`\n- `pnpm --filter desktop run lint` and `pnpm --filter @maus-inc/preview run lint`\n- `pnpm --filter desktop run test:unit` and `pnpm --filter @maus-inc/preview run test`\n- `node --test scripts/ci/pr28-contracts.test.mjs scripts/ci/pr37-contracts.test.mjs scripts/ci/check-workspace-hygiene.test.mjs`\n- GitHub Actions CI across Rust unit tests, clippy on Linux, macOS, and Windows, TypeScript unit and integration tests, and full desktop builds on Linux, macOS, and Windows\n\n</details>\n\nMausAgent | Filed by Arena.ai Agent Mode, with `@Owie6789`, on 2026-10-07\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated description by cubic. -->\n<a href=\"https://cubic.dev/pr/maus-inc/mausVoice/pull/286?utm_source=github\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" data-no-image-dialog=\"true\"><picture><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\" srcset=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-dark.svg\"><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\" srcset=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-light.svg\"><img alt=\"Review in cubic\" src=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-dark.svg\"></picture></a> <a href=\"https://www.cubic.dev/action/auto-fix/pr/maus-inc/mausVoice/286?returnTo=https%3A%2F%2Fgithub.com%2Fmaus-inc%2FmausVoice%2Fpull%2F286&source=description\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" data-no-image-dialog=\"true\"><picture><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\" srcset=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/turn-on-auto-fix-dark.svg\"><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\" srcset=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/turn-on-auto-fix-light.svg\"><img alt=\"Turn on auto-fix\" src=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/turn-on-auto-fix-dark.svg\"></picture></a>\n<!-- End of auto-generated description by cubic. -->\n\n## Summary by Sourcery\n\nShow dimmed loading progress beneath stage labels and make pill transcription statuses and transitions accurate across desktop platforms.\n\nNew Features:\n- Render the loading progress indicator behind centered stage labels across native pills and the preview recreation, with dimmed bar layers and text elision.\n- Keep loading animation behavior consistent across platforms, including reduced-motion centering and frame-rate-adjusted progress.\n\nBug Fixes:\n- Harden pill stage-text and loading-state transitions to preserve pre-loading labels and clear stale labels at the appropriate phases.\n- Improve transcript status reporting by limiting polishing indicators to actual post-processing and accurately tracking insertion delivery and cancellation.\n- Propagate pipeline traces through persisted transcript reviews and use the pill phase routing for type-mode transitions.\n\nEnhancements:\n- Centralize loading-bar geometry, opacity, text normalization, and transition behavior in shared Rust helpers used by all native renderers.\n\nCI:\n- Extend contract coverage for loading-bar layering, stage-text transitions, reduced-motion behavior, and cross-platform renderer consistency.\n\nDocumentation:\n- Update preview specifications to document the loading bar with stage text and the additional pill state.\n\nTests:\n- Add desktop strategy and output-routing tests covering polishing, backlog insertion, hands-free delays, superseded sessions, and trace marking.\n- Add shared native pill tests for loading geometry, alpha handling, invalid inputs, text budgets, phase clearing, and animation timing.\n\nChores:\n- Apply formatting-only updates to CI contract test fixtures.\