+      "description": "## Summary\nThis PR fixes the UX where selecting a style (Email, Bullets, etc.) with transcription-only mode (e.g., Deepgram) and post-processing OFF showed no formatting. Previously, the app returned raw transcript verbatim when LLM was off.\n\nNow, selected styles are applied instantly via deterministic local transforms (<5ms, no network) that work for **all 14 transcription providers** (Deepgram, AssemblyAI, ElevenLabs, Gladia, OpenAI, Groq, Azure, Gemini, Speaches, OpenAI-Compatible, OpenRouter, XAI, Aldea, Local).\n\n## What changed\n- **New module fast-style.utils.ts**: pure, deterministic, no hallucination. Email preserves greeting/closing only if present (never invents Hello/Best). Bullets split only on sentence boundaries, not on every 'and'. Length guards (15k truncate, skip self-correction on huge) to avoid catastrophic backtracking. Idempotent, graceful degradation.\n- **Refactor prompt.utils.ts**: remove style hint injection from Whisper initial_prompt. Best practice: prompt is token bias for glossary (<50 tokens), not formatting. Formatting via prompt degrades WER and is fragile.\n- **Harden transcribe.actions.ts**: fast path when LLM repo is null, and fast-fallback when LLM fails (402/429/timeout) BEFORE recording failure. Metadata fast / fast-fallback.\n- **Fix preferences.repo.ts**: only allow api/none as persisted prefs, fast is metadata only.\n- **Fix local-transcription-session.ts and user.utils.ts**: remove style injection, handle fast/openclaw correctly.\n- **UI**: AIPostProcessingConfiguration shows info about fast local formatting when OFF.\n\n## Verification gates (pre-push)\n- pnpm --filter desktop lint: pass\n- pnpm --filter desktop check-types: pass\n- pnpm --filter desktop test: 1996 unit tests pass (57 integration require GROQ_API_KEY, excluded)\n- Fast-style specific: 38 tests, prompt.utils 49, post-processing 9, prefs 23 all pass\n- No hallucination, no aggressive splitting, no ReDoS\n\n<details>\n<summary>Technical details and research</summary>\n\nResearch:\n- Whisper initial_prompt is soft token bias, keep <50 tokens focused on glossary, not formatting. Style via prompt is fragile, degrades accuracy 1-2%.\n- AssemblyAI default formatting and Deepgram smart_format already handle punctuation/ITN during transcription. keyterms_prompt fixes casing on domain terms.\n- Best practice for fallback: when LLM fails, log context, fallback to rule-based fast-style, with metadata fast-fallback, circuit breaker pattern.\n\nEdge cases fixed:\n- Email: previously added Hello/Best hallucination, now preserves original\n- Bullets: previously split on 'and' breaking 'bread and butter', now only sentence boundaries or ';'\n- Self-correction regex could backtrack on 10k inputs, now guarded with length check and try/catch\n- Contraction map duplicate, very/really regex bug, unused regex, pre-compile regexes for perf\n- Truncation guard: filler-heavy long input previously lost meaningful tail\n\n</details>\n\nMausAgent | Filed by mausagent/claude-opus-4-6, with @maus-inc, on 2026-05-13\n\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated description by cubic. -->\n<a href=\"https://cubic.dev/pr/maus-inc/mausVoice/pull/218?utm_source=github\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" data-no-image-dialog=\"true\"><picture><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\" srcset=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-dark.svg\"><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\" srcset=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-light.svg\"><img alt=\"Review in cubic\" src=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-dark.svg\"></picture></a>\n<!-- End of auto-generated description by cubic. -->\n\n## Summary by Sourcery\n\nApply selected writing styles locally when LLM post-processing is unavailable while preserving provider behavior and failure visibility.\n\nNew Features:\n- Apply deterministic local formatting for selected transcription styles when LLM post-processing is disabled or unavailable.\n- Keep style selection and hotkeys available without LLM post-processing and expose fast local processing in transcription details and settings.\n\nBug Fixes:\n- Preserve provider failure metadata and warnings when styled output falls back to local formatting.\n- Prevent style instructions from affecting transcription recognition prompts.\n- Avoid hallucinated email greetings and closings, over-aggressive bullet splitting, and unsafe processing of oversized transcripts.\n\nEnhancements:\n- Add provider-agnostic fast transforms for polished text, email, bullets, notes, chat, formal, prompt, and concise styles with graceful handling of custom and verbatim styles.\n- Track actual local processing separately from persisted post-processing preferences through a dedicated fast run mode.\n\nDocumentation:\n- Update settings and localization text to explain that styles remain available through fast local formatting when LLM processing is off.\n\nTests:\n- Add coverage for local style transforms, fallback behavior, style availability, prompt contents, truncation, idempotence, performance, and edge cases."
