+      "description": "Onboarding now asks before you skip API key setup, and the two console links say what you get from opening them. Before this, the form said \"Open Deepgram API keys\" and \"Open Groq API keys\", and pressing \"Skip for now\" moved you on without a word. A new confirmation explains that local models use more system resources and run slower than API-based models, so nobody lands on local-only setup without knowing the trade-off.\n\n<details>\n<summary>What changed</summary>\n\n- The two console links now read \"Grab your Deepgram API key\" and \"Grab your Groq API key\".\n- Pressing \"Skip for now\" on the API keys step opens the shared `ConfirmDialog` instead of advancing. The title asks \"Skip API key setup?\" and the body explains the performance trade-off plus the fact that keys can be added later in Settings.\n- The safe action, \"Go back\", takes focus when the dialog opens. Escape, a backdrop click, and \"Go back\" all close the dialog without advancing.\n- Only confirming \"Skip for now\" advances, and it keeps this branch's existing `goToOnboardingPage(\"chooseTranscription\", \"skip\")` contract, so step outcomes still record `skip`.\n- `ConfirmDialog` now wires `aria-labelledby` to its title and `aria-describedby` to its body with `useId`. All 8 existing call sites gain a correct accessible name and description.\n- Added translations for all 10 locale catalogs.\n- Added a component test that covers the link copy, the dialog's accessible name and description, the cancel path, and the confirmed skip path.\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>How to test this</summary>\n\n1. Open Onboarding and stop at step 2, \"Connect your API keys\".\n2. Confirm the two console links read \"Grab your Deepgram API key\" and \"Grab your Groq API key\".\n3. Press \"Skip for now\". The dialog opens, \"Go back\" holds focus, and a screen reader announces the title and the warning.\n4. Press Escape, click the backdrop, or press \"Go back\". You stay on step 2.\n5. Press \"Skip for now\" again, then confirm \"Skip for now\". You land on step 3, and the recorded step outcome is `skip`.\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>Verification</summary>\n\n- `pnpm exec turbo run build --filter=desktop^...`\n- `pnpm --filter desktop build`\n- `pnpm --filter desktop run check-types`\n- `pnpm --filter desktop run lint`\n- `pnpm --filter desktop run i18n`, rerun with a clean extraction cache to confirm the catalogs are idempotent\n- `pnpm --filter desktop run test:unit`: 177 files, 1963 tests, all passing\n- `pnpm --filter @maus-inc/voice-ai test`\n- `pnpm --filter @repo/agent test`\n- `pnpm --filter desktop run test:integration` could not run here because the sandbox has no `GROQ_API_KEY`. The test file itself starts with a `describe.skipIf(!key)`, so CI with the secret is the authority on that job.\n\n</details>\n\nMausAgent | Filed by `kilo/stealth/space-bunny-alpha`, with `@Owie6789`, on 2026-09-25\n\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated description by cubic. -->\n<a href=\"https://cubic.dev/pr/maus-inc/mausVoice/pull/210?utm_source=github\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" data-no-image-dialog=\"true\"><picture><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\" srcset=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-dark.svg\"><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\" srcset=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-light.svg\"><img alt=\"Review in cubic\" src=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-dark.svg\"></picture></a>\n<!-- End of auto-generated description by cubic. -->\n\n"
