+      "description": "Supersedes #186 and #185. The same change set as PR 186, plus the final\nCodeSpect fix for proposal toast TTL and ElevenLabs URLSearchParams that\nthe previous session could not push.\n\n## What this fixes\n\nThe two \"automatic dictionary word addition\" features were broken end to\nend. This PR repairs them and makes learned words actually change\nrecognition on every speech provider that supports vocabulary hints. Full\ninvestigation with evidence levels and sources:\nAUTO-LEARN-DICTIONARY-REVIEW.md.\n\n## The nine findings\n\n- F1 \"Learn from corrections\" deadlocked itself. After one ignored prompt,\n  the watcher never polled again until restart. Proposals now self-expire\n  after 12 seconds and are cleared when a watch starts or ends.\n- F2 Case-only corrections were never learned. Fixing sonia to Sonia or\n  nasa to NASA produced nothing. The token diff is now case-aware.\n  Decapitalization still learns nothing.\n- F3 Deepgram, AssemblyAI, ElevenLabs and Azure never received the\n  dictionary at all. Each now gets its documented vocabulary parameter in\n  batch and streaming, with budget caps and a warning when entries are\n  dropped.\n- F4 The whisper initial_prompt glossary was uncapped past the ~224-token\n  ceiling, and the Azure phrase list was fed instruction words like\n  \"Glossary:\" and \"transcribing\" instead of terms. Both fixed.\n- F5 The LLM cleanup prompt told the model to prefer glossary spellings but\n  never showed it the glossary. Every post-processing prompt now includes\n  the user's glossary, and custom templates get a glossary variable.\n- F6 The common-word filter was English-only and incomplete, so German\n  \"Stadt\", \"Monday\" and \"Please\" got learned as names. The stop list now\n  covers politeness, weekday and month words plus a starter set for de,\n  fr, es, it, pt and nl.\n- F7 Settings and Dictionary page copy now states the real scope of each\n  toggle.\n- F8 The add-to-dictionary hotkey now dedupes, caps length, rolls back on\n  failure and reuses createGlossaryTerms.\n- F9 The onboarding checklist now ticks for every path that grows the\n  dictionary, not just the Dictionary page dialog.\n\n## Provider budgets, verified against each provider's docs\n\n| Provider | Parameter | Limits enforced |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| Deepgram | repeated keyterm query params | 100 terms, 1500 chars, well under the documented 500-token total |\n| AssemblyAI batch | word_boost | 1000 words, matches documented capacity |\n| AssemblyAI streaming | keyterms_prompt | 100 terms of at most 50 chars, the API errors above 100 |\n| ElevenLabs batch | repeated keyterms form fields | 100 terms, each under 50 chars and at most 5 words, past 100 triggers 20 s minimum billing |\n| ElevenLabs realtime | repeated keyterms query params | 50 terms of at most 20 chars |\n| Azure | phrase list | 500 phrases, the documented maximum |\n\nNew tests pin every documented limit.\n\n## Review rounds included here\n\n- Log redaction for keyterm values and auth tokens through\n  redactQueryParamValues, with unit tests.\n- applyTemplateVars uses a replacer function and String.raw so dollar\n  patterns in user values are inserted verbatim.\n- ElevenLabs batch and realtime budgets are split to match the docs.\n- Edit-watch stale-proposal test starts the watch before setting the\n  expired proposal, so the TTL branch is actually exercised.\n- PROPOSAL_TOAST_DURATION_MS is the single source for toast duration, and\n  PROPOSAL_TTL_MS is derived from it.\n- ElevenLabs realtime keyterms append through URLSearchParams, matching\n  Deepgram.\n- Docs separate Azure Speech SDK one-shot recognition from Azure Batch\n  Transcription, which does not support phrase lists.\n- Pipeline fence marked as text for markdownlint MD040.\n\n## Verification\n\n- desktop test:unit: 125 files, 1337 tests green\n- voice-ai test: 21 files, 159 tests green\n- turbo build desktop: 7 of 7 tasks green\n- check-types, prettier, oxlint clean\n- i18n catalog idempotent\n\n## Notes for reviewers\n\n- Using ElevenLabs keyterms adds a 20 percent transcription surcharge. It\n  applies only when the dictionary is non-empty. Empty dictionaries send\n  no keyterms.\n- xAI and Aldea still get no vocabulary because neither documents a\n  biasing parameter.\n- Per-language stop lists keyed by dictation language remain an open\n  improvement. The current multi-language stop list is an explicit\n  stopgap.\n- Ito QA noted two pre-existing streaming startup and finalize races\n  outside this change set. They are not addressed here on purpose.\n\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated description by cubic. -->\n<a href=\"https://cubic.dev/pr/maus-inc/mausVoice/pull/187?utm_source=github\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" data-no-image-dialog=\"true\"><picture><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\" srcset=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-dark.svg\"><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\" srcset=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-light.svg\"><img alt=\"Review in cubic\" src=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-dark.svg\"></picture></a>\n<!-- End of auto-generated description by cubic. -->\n\n## Summary by Sourcery\n\nRepair automatic dictionary learning end to end so corrections persist reliably and learned vocabulary improves recognition and post-processing across supported providers.\n\nNew Features:\n- Send learned dictionary terms to Deepgram, AssemblyAI, ElevenLabs, and Azure recognition APIs with provider-specific limits and warnings.\n- Add an opt-in ElevenLabs keyterms setting that explains and confirms the associated transcription surcharge.\n- Expose glossary terms to post-processing prompts and custom templates so learned spellings can affect cleanup.\n\nBug Fixes:\n- Prevent correction-watching from becoming permanently blocked by expired proposals.\n- Learn case-only corrections such as proper-noun capitalization while filtering common words and multilingual stop-list entries.\n- Cap and sanitize glossary prompts and provider vocabulary payloads, including correcting Azure phrase-list inputs.\n- Harden dictionary additions with deduplication, length limits, rollback on failure, and onboarding checklist updates.\n- Redact dictionary terms and authentication values from provider connection logs.\n\nEnhancements:\n- Centralize dictionary value collection, vocabulary budgeting, provider hint construction, and glossary prompt formatting.\n- Clarify dictionary and auto-learning settings copy and platform-specific behavior.\n\nDocumentation:\n- Add a detailed investigation and verification report for automatic dictionary learning and provider vocabulary support.\n\nTests:\n- Add regression and contract coverage for proposal expiry, case-aware learning, multilingual filtering, prompt budgets, provider vocabulary parameters, URL redaction, and ElevenLabs opt-in behavior.\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai -->\n## Summary by CodeRabbit\n\n- **New Features**\n  - Dictionary terms now improve recognition across supported transcription providers.\n  - Glossary terms and replacement rules are included in transcription and post-processing.\n  - Corrected saved transcriptions can automatically contribute new dictionary entries.\n  - ElevenLabs keyterms can be enabled with explicit acknowledgment of the 20% surcharge.\n\n- **Bug Fixes**\n  - Case-only corrections and multilingual filtering are handled more accurately.\n  - Auto-learn prompts expire correctly and no longer interfere with newer dictation.\n  - Duplicate or oversized dictionary selections receive clear feedback.\n  - Vocabulary limits are enforced with truncation warnings.\n\n- **Documentation**\n  - Updated onboarding guidance, dictionary descriptions, platform-specific behavior, and localized help text.\n<!-- end of auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai -->"
