+      "description": "This PR stacks on #187 and fixes the follow up reviews so the change can merge cleanly. It gates the ElevenLabs realtime path behind the same opt in that the batch path uses, fixes the translated setting copy, corrects the glossary budget math, clarifies the Whisper prompt docs, and lowers the cognitive complexity that Sonar flagged.\n\nMausAgent made the changes on `arena/01a08621-mausvoice` against `arena/01a08429-mausvoice` (head of #187 at `0a4d8c4`). You can test by enabling the ElevenLabs provider, toggling the ElevenLabs keyterms setting, dictating with and without a dictionary, and checking that streaming sends no keyterms when off and sends budgeted keyterms when on. Check the localized settings strings for the five locales and the Korean disabled wording, and verify the glossary budget still caps at 2000.\n\n<details>\n<summary>What changed and why</summary>\n\n**1. ElevenLabs realtime now respects the opt in (billing and privacy)**\n- Path `apps/desktop/src/sessions/elevenlabs-transcription-session.ts` previously built and sent keyterms unconditionally in `onRecordingStart`. That bypassed `elevenLabsKeytermsEnabled` which the batch repo in `apps/desktop/src/repos/index.ts` already checked, so streaming could add the 20 percent surcharge without consent and expose dictionary terms.\n- Fix adds import `getMyUserPreferences` from `../utils/user.utils` and gates the call. When the preference is false, the session sends an empty array and logs no warning. When true, it builds the vocabulary with `ELEVENLABS_REALTIME_KEYTERMS_BUDGET` (50 terms, 20 chars each, 1000 total) and logs a warning only if entries were dropped. This mirrors the batch opt in logic and matches the docs that keyterms add a 20 percent surcharge.\n\n**2. Translated settings copy now points at the feature, not the dictionary**\n- Path `apps/desktop/src/i18n/locales/es.json`, `fr.json`, `it.json`, `pt-BR.json`, `pt.json` line 613. The final sentence used a pronoun (`desactivarlo`, `le`, `disattivarlo`, `desativá-lo`) that reads as disabling the dictionary. The pronoun now reads as disabling the keyterm sharing feature. Example es before `puedes desactivarlo en cualquier momento` after `puedes desactivar el envío de términos clave en cualquier momento`. Fr after `vous pouvez désactiver l’envoi des termes clés à tout moment`. It after `puoi disattivare l’invio dei termini chiave in qualsiasi momento`. Pt-BR after `você pode desativar o envio de termos-chave a qualquer momento`. Pt after `pode desativar o envio de termos-chave a qualquer momento`.\n\n**3. Korean disabled wording**\n- Path `apps/desktop/src/i18n/locales/ko.json` line 608. The string `사용이 중지되어 있습니다` suggests usage was stopped. The fix uses `비활성화되어 있습니다` to state the feature is disabled by default, as requested: `기본적으로 비활성화되어 있습니다`.\n\n**4. Whisper initial prompt budget docs now state the heuristic clearly**\n- Paths `apps/desktop/src/utils/prompt.utils.ts` and `AUTO-LEARN-DICTIONARY-REVIEW.md`. The 650 code point cap was described as staying under the roughly 224 token ceiling. The token count for CJK or emoji can exceed one token per code point, so the cap does not guarantee the tokenized prompt fits. The comment in `prompt.utils.ts` and both sections in `AUTO-LEARN-DICTIONARY-REVIEW.md` (around lines 413 and 513) now say the 650 budget is only a heuristic that approximates the ceiling and does not guarantee compliance, and that CJK and emoji heavy glossaries should be verified with the exact tokenizer or with fixtures. `buildLocalizedTranscriptionPrompt` also now notes the heuristic check inside its instruction length handling.\n\n**5. Glossary budget delimiter fix**\n- Path `apps/desktop/src/utils/prompt.utils.ts` line 276. `collectBudgetedGlossary` caps terms and then caps rules from the remaining budget, but `formatGlossaryTemplateVar` joins the two groups with `; ` (2 chars). The previous math did not reserve those 2 chars, so the joined string could exceed `GLOSSARY_PROMPT_BUDGET` (2000) by up to 2 when both groups were present. The fix reserves `delimiterLength = terms.length > 0 && glossary.replacements.length > 0 ? 2 : 0` and subtracts it from `maxCharacters` for the rules budget. Empty groups keep the original behavior.\n\n**6. Sonar cognitive complexity**\n- Path `apps/desktop/src/repos/index.ts` line 353. Sonar flagged `getTranscribeAudioRepo` with complexity 18 vs 15 allowed. The function had a large switch with nested `if` blocks for openai compatible, speaches, openrouter, and the groq fallback. The fix extracts four helpers `buildOpenAICompatibleTranscribeRepo`, `buildSpeachesTranscribeRepo`, `buildOpenRouterTranscribeRepo`, `buildGroqFallbackTranscribeRepo` and simplifies the switch to call them. The file now passes the 15 limit and `pnpm --filter desktop lint` and `check-types` are clean.\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>Verification</summary>\n\n- `corepack pnpm --filter desktop lint` passes after `prettier --write` on the two touched typescript files\n- `corepack pnpm --filter desktop check-types` passes after building `packages/types`, `utilities`, `voice-ai`, `desktop-utils`, `desktop-native-apis`, `agent`\n- `corepack pnpm --filter desktop test:unit` 125 files 1341 tests passed\n- `corepack pnpm --filter @maus-inc/voice-ai test` 22 files 163 tests passed\n- `corepack pnpm --filter @repo/agent test` 1 file 9 tests passed\n- `corepack pnpm --filter desktop build` built in 22 seconds with 16519 modules transformed\n- `prettier --check` on `AUTO-LEARN-DICTIONARY-REVIEW.md` and the locale json files passes\n- `i18n` sync shows 826 existing keys in each locale, 0 added\n\nNo intentional behavior change outside the listed fixes. The branch keeps the same provider budgets that were verified against vendor docs.\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>Review notes and scope</summary>\n\n- The log utils fix to use `parsed.href` and the query params helper already landed in `main` at `0a4d8c4` and needed no change here.\n- The `applyTemplateVars` split join fix also already landed and stays.\n- The `elevenlabsKeytermsEnabled` preference defaults to false and the More settings dialog already shows the toggle only for the ElevenLabs provider.\n- Out of scope: per dictation language stop lists remain a future improvement, and the pill still does not emit a `toast-expired` event. The frontend TTL remains the fix for F1.\n\n</details>\n\nMausAgent | Filed by `arena-agent`, with `@Owie6789`, on 2026-09-09\n\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated description by cubic. -->\n<a href=\"https://cubic.dev/pr/maus-inc/mausVoice/pull/189?utm_source=github\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" data-no-image-dialog=\"true\"><picture><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\" srcset=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-dark.svg\"><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\" srcset=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-light.svg\"><img alt=\"Review in cubic\" src=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-dark.svg\"></picture></a>\n<!-- End of auto-generated description by cubic. -->\n\n## Summary by Sourcery\n\nRespect the ElevenLabs keyterm opt-in across transcription paths and address glossary, documentation, localization, repository complexity, and sidecar build reliability issues.\n\nBug Fixes:\n- Gate ElevenLabs realtime keyterm sharing behind the user's explicit opt-in, preventing unconsented dictionary exposure and surcharges.\n- Correct glossary character budgeting so the formatted glossary remains within the 2000-character limit.\n- Improve localized keyterm setting wording, including clearer Korean disabled-state text.\n\nEnhancements:\n- Clarify that Whisper's 650-code-point initial prompt limit is a heuristic rather than a guarantee of token-limit compliance.\n- Reduce transcription repository selection complexity without changing provider behavior.\n\nBuild:\n- Retry transient Cargo sidecar build failures with bounded exponential backoff and jitter.\n\nDocumentation:\n- Update dictionary review guidance to document Whisper prompt budgeting limitations for CJK- and emoji-heavy glossaries."
