+      "description": "This branch fixes ten confirmed problems found by a full review of PR #63, and adds the review-before-insert feature that review asked for. In plain terms: Gladia no longer crashes the API key settings screen, clicking the pill while paused resumes dictation instead of doing nothing, a pill click plays one sound instead of two, the review window opens next to the pill instead of in the corner of the screen, changing style mid-dictation now styles the whole transcript, and a finished transcript can be checked and edited on the pill itself before it is typed into your app, with Insert, Copy and Cancel right there. Nothing that already worked was changed on purpose, no test or lint rule was loosened, and every fix has a test that fails without it.\n\nThe review write-up lives in `CORRECTIVE-REVIEW.md` at the root of this branch. It lists every claim made on PR #63, what evidence backs it, and which ones turned out to be wrong or already fixed.\n\n<details>\n<summary>How to test it by hand</summary>\n\n1. Open Settings, API keys, and pick Gladia. The screen should stay up. Before this branch it went blank.\n2. Start dictation, pause it, then click the body of the pill. It should carry on recording. Before, the click did nothing.\n3. Click the pill body again and listen. There should be one sound, not two. The style chevrons and the cancel button still have their own click sound.\n4. Turn on review before insert, dictate a sentence, and wait for the transcript on the pill. It loads into the pill's own text box, so you can correct it there. Insert types what the box holds, Copy puts it on the clipboard, Cancel throws it away and leaves it in your history. Enter inserts and Escape cancels, whether or not the box has the keyboard.\n5. With the card open, set the pill to Hidden in settings. The pill should stay on screen until you answer the card.\n6. Dictate something long enough to wrap over several lines. The four buttons must stay visible and clickable, and the panel should scroll.\n7. Dictate a second sentence while a card is still waiting. The second one should wait its turn rather than replace the first.\n8. Start dictating, switch style with the chevrons partway through, then stop. The whole transcript should come back in the style you switched to, and that style should still be selected next time.\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>What each commit does</summary>\n\n| Commit    | What it fixes                                                                                                                              |\n| --------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ |\n| `f93f2bb` | Gladia was missing from the API key form config, so choosing it crashed the settings screen. The list is now typed so a missing provider fails the build instead of the app |\n| `14d438a` | A click on the pill body while paused did nothing. It now resumes                                                                          |\n| `2c7e2a3` | Both the pill and the app played a sound for the same click. The pill no longer plays its own for a body click                             |\n| `1f38d0d` | The review window opened wherever it liked because it never learned where the pill was. The pill now publishes its position on request      |\n| `44f886d` | Switching style during dictation only affected the next recording. It now styles the whole transcript and stays selected                    |\n| `ee3045d` | Formatting on `README.md`, which was the only red check on PR #63                                                                          |\n| `8633a6c` | Review before insert on the pill itself, with Insert, Edit, Copy and Cancel, a queue for a second transcript, and stale clicks ignored      |\n| `8ae2e6b` | With the pill set to Hidden or While active, it hid at the exact moment the card arrived, so the card could not be answered                 |\n| `ab206e0` | A review could be queued before anything was listening for the answer, and a card nobody answered blocked typing for good. It now expires   |\n| `0d3f2b6` | Both bridges read an unknown decision as cancel, which would have thrown away the transcript silently. Unreadable messages are now dropped and logged, leaving the card up |\n| `1446827` | The review card was taller than the panel, so its buttons hid behind the pill on any transcript over about two lines, and the panel would not scroll |\n| `864ab34` | The review moved into the pill's own panel and text box, so the transcript is edited in place and no second window opens |\n| `b1fe214` | Escape answered a review only on Windows. It now cancels on macOS and Linux too, and the macOS box reports every keystroke |\n| `897e259` | The decision parser wrote the whole line to the log, and that line carries the transcript |\n| `084bdd6` | One path through the review queue, one stale id check, and the pill window size decided by a function with tests |\n| `438ae23`, `1829845` | A safe read of the macOS text box, a capped log token, and a busy flag that always clears |\n| `2950ed3` | A review button that had scrolled half out of the panel could still be clicked on the part you cannot see |\n| `c5696c3` | On Linux the review buttons were drawn outside the clickable area of the window, so they could not be pressed at all |\n| `5fa27fd` | The text you send keeps the spacing you left around it, and the Windows box is cleared only when something was sent |\n| `192366b`, `d2a6e5e` | Asking the macOS pill for its position answered fine with nothing sent, so the placement dialog waited forever |\n| `40a9922`, `fd104d1`, `e02be96`, `22a6d10`, `18cd021`, `efce7d8`, `6546939` | The review write-up |\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>Checks that were run</summary>\n\nGreen on this branch head in CI, on Linux, macOS and Windows: Lint Desktop, which runs clippy with warnings treated as errors over the desktop crate and all three native pill crates, Test Desktop Unit, Test Desktop Integration, and Build Desktop, which builds the whole app on all three platforms.\n\nLocally: lint, formatting, types across 8 packages, 1,275 desktop unit tests over 121 files against a baseline of 1,185 over 112, the voice-ai and agent package tests, and the turbo build across 10 packages. The i18n extraction is idempotent and the one new message is translated into all nine locales.\n\nNot run, and still needed before release: the browser driver suite, the integration suite that needs a Groq key, and hands-on testing of the pill on each operating system. Static review does not prove how the desktop app behaves at runtime.\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>Things left for a human to decide</summary>\n\nThe macOS pill clicks on Pause and Resume while Windows and Linux stay silent. The buttons on the pill say Insert, Copy and Cancel in English, the same way the existing permission card is hardcoded, because the pill has no translation system. Release signing that fails closed, the last commit of PR #59, is still missing from this line of work.\n\nOne reported problem could not be fixed from reading the code. The assistant sometimes stops after a tool call with an error about an invalid resource id. The wording comes from Tauri's own resource table, which points at something released inside a native call rather than at the assistant loop, and guessing at it would do more harm than good. It needs a debug build and a stack trace.\n\n</details>\n\n---\n\nMausAgent | Filed by `arena-agent`, with `@Owie6789`, on `2026-09-07`\n\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai -->\n## Summary by CodeRabbit\n\n* **New Features**\n  * Added transcript review before insertion, with editable text and Insert, Copy, or Cancel actions on the desktop pill.\n  * Added review queuing, Escape cancellation, timeout handling, and composer fallback.\n  * Improved pill positioning on first use.\n  * Added Gladia as a supported API key provider.\n\n* **Bug Fixes**\n  * Improved paused-session click behavior and dictation style handling.\n  * Removed duplicate pill click feedback.\n  * Improved reporting of native pill message-delivery failures.\n\n* **Localization**\n  * Added translated messaging when copying fails but the transcript remains saved.\n<!-- end of auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai -->\n"
