+      "description": "## Summary\nCherry-pick of 316e4d100180035f23043c44de01459e0a6cfe96 from PR #181 onto superfix.\n\n- add a compositor-friendly route crossfade/slide for dashboard page changes\n- keep the sidebar persistent while route content transitions\n- preserve the existing shared active-navigation indicator animation\n- replace per-row Framer Motion press wrappers with lightweight CSS press feedback to reduce memory and render overhead\n- respect reduced-motion preferences\n\n## Original PR\n- #181\n- commit 316e4d100180035f23043c44de01459e0a6cfe96\n\n## Changes\n- `DashboardPage.tsx`: Use `AnimatePresence` with `mode=\"popLayout\"` to crossfade routes, key on pathname+search, animate only opacity/transform for compositor performance, respect reduced-motion.\n- `ListTile.tsx`: Replace per-row Framer Motion press wrapper with CSS transform transition (scale 0.975 on :active) to reduce memory overhead.\n\n## Implementation notes\nThis app uses React Router and Framer Motion, so the transition follows the same lifecycle principles as Barba.js without introducing a second DOM/navigation owner. `AnimatePresence` with `mode=\"popLayout\"` allows the outgoing route to overlap the incoming route briefly for a local crossfade, while the sidebar remains mounted.\n\n## Validation\n- Cherry-picked patch applies cleanly on top of fix/superfix-review-findings (9e01cbb)\n- 2 files changed, 38 insertions, 21 deletions\n\n## Summary by Sourcery\n\nImprove dashboard navigation smoothness and reduce list interaction overhead while respecting accessibility motion preferences.\n\nNew Features:\n- Add animated dashboard route transitions that crossfade and slide route content while keeping shared dashboard navigation mounted.\n\nEnhancements:\n- Replace per-row animated press handling with lightweight CSS feedback and disable motion when reduced-motion preferences are enabled.\n\nChores:\n- Clean up incidental whitespace in the README.\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai -->\n\n## Summary by CodeRabbit\n\n* **Style**\n  * Added a subtle press-down animation to list item buttons for clearer interaction feedback.\n  * Respects reduced-motion preferences by disabling the animation when requested.\n\n<!-- end of auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai -->"
