+      "description": "This PR removes the dark strips on the left and bottom of the Windows installer welcome page. The sidebar picture now fills its panel edge to edge. It fixes the source picture, makes the build script warn if a future picture has the same flaw, and adds tests that lock the fix in.\n\n<details>\n<summary>What was wrong</summary>\n\nThe installer sidebar is a small fixed size picture (164 by 314 dots) that gets baked into the setup file when the app is built. The source picture had two flaws:\n\n- Empty see-through margins on the right side and bottom (about 1 in 9 dots). The baked picture format cannot store see-through areas, so those dots turned into flat dark strips.\n- The wrong shape, so the build script shrank the picture and padded the gaps with more dark strips.\n\nI rebuilt the source picture at exactly twice the panel size with no see-through dots, so the baked picture now uses real artwork on every dot.\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>What changed</summary>\n\n- `branding/mausvoice-sidebar-installerimg.png`: rebuilt as a fully solid 328 by 628 picture.\n- `scripts/generate-windows-installer-sidebar.mjs`: warns at build time when a picture has see-through dots; reports \"full-bleed, no letterbox\" when the picture fills the panel; sizing math now rounds down so the picture can never spill past the panel; geometry is computed once and shared.\n- `apps/desktop/scripts/generate-windows-installer-sidebar.test.mjs`: 32 tests covering the new checks, the sizing promise across tricky sizes, and the committed picture itself.\n- `branding/README.md`: states the rule that installer art must be solid and match the panel shape.\n- `README.md`: whitespace cleanup so the repo format check passes (it was already failing before this PR).\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>How I verified it</summary>\n\n- Built the installer picture before and after: identical bytes for the fixed art, and every edge dot is real artwork (no flat strips).\n- Full desktop unit suite: 112 files, 1194 tests, all pass.\n- Type check clean. Format check clean.\n- SonarCloud: 0 new issues. All 6 bot review threads answered and resolved.\n\nNote: setup files built earlier still contain the old picture. The next Windows build remakes it on its own.\n\n</details>\n\n---\nMausAgent | Filed with @Owie6789, on 2026-09-07"
