+      "description": "This branch reviews pull request #63 and fixes the confirmed gaps, regressions and half-finished integrations found across its full history. It does not change PR #63. It adds 34 commits over 55 files (+2368 / -187) on top of the PR head, fixes seven confirmed defects with a regression test for each, and updates the workflow action pins and the bindings CI check that were broken and would have failed CI after September 16, 2026.\n\nThis pull request continues the same review that lived on `arena/01a07713-mausvoice` (PR #179). It adds the two merge blockers found at head `6eec3eea`: Secret Scan failing on setup-node v5's default package-manager cache, and SonarCloud duplication on new code at 9.9 percent (now 0.0 percent).\n\n## What it changes\n\n- Provider retries. Seven AI providers stopped retrying transient failures whenever a caller attached a cancellation signal. Retries now stay on for transient failures and stop only when the signal is actually aborted.\n- Bindings CI. The check that verifies native bindings are in sync was failing for two reasons: an invalid git flag in its guard, and a missing setup value that prevented the generator from building. Both are fixed and the check now runs with a regression test.\n- CI action pins. The pinned actions claimed version 5 but were version 4 commits that run on Node 20. GitHub removes Node 20 from runners on September 16, 2026, so all pins were re-resolved to verified Node 24 releases with correct version comments. A guard test now fails on any unverified pin.\n- Windows resume behavior. The keyboard hook and pill placement are restored after sleep or unlock, and the pill placement push is shared between the settings toggle and the startup re-apply so the two cannot drift.\n- Abort and timeout behavior. Post-processing has an abortable 50 second timeout, cancellation flows through every generate-text repository, and deleting a conversation stops its agent loop.\n- Secret Scan. setup-node v5 defaults package-manager-cache to on and fails when pnpm is not installed. Secret Scan never installs pnpm, so the job now sets package-manager-cache: false. The pin guard requires every setup-node step to set exactly one of cache: pnpm or package-manager-cache: false.\n- Test duplication. The generate-text provider table, Azure deployment coverage, Cerebras/Deepseek OpenAI mocks, and the pin table were restructured so SonarCloud counts 0 duplicated lines on new code. Explicit wrapper it() tests are kept.\n\n## Verification on head 73ee70ed\n\nLocal: desktop types, 112 desktop unit files / 1185 tests, 18 voice-ai files / 148 tests, voice-ai build, prettier, both CI guard tests.\n\nCI:\n\n- Secret Scan: green\n- Format and i18n: green\n- Test Desktop Unit (TS, voice-ai, i18n, Rust including guard tests): green\n- SonarCloud Quality Gate: PASS, new-code duplication 0.0 percent\n- Test Desktop Integration, Lint Desktop, Build Desktop (Windows, Linux, macOS): green on the preceding head that still contained those path-filtered files\n\nWindows manual QA has not been run. The release recommendation stays CONDITIONAL GO until that is done. Do not merge without that QA and explicit approval.\n\n- MausAgent | Filed by `arena-ai-coding-agent`, with @Owie6789, on 2026-09-07\n\n## Summary by Sourcery\n\nRepair confirmed regressions and CI integration gaps from the reviewed desktop and voice-AI changes, while adding regression coverage and safeguards for future workflow and binding failures.\n\nNew Features:\n- Add cancellation support across text-generation providers and abort active post-processing and agent operations.\n- Restore Windows keyboard-listener and pill-placement state after resume and startup.\n- Add CI guards for generated bindings, workflow action pins, setup-node caching, and gitleaks configuration.\n\nBug Fixes:\n- Restore transient provider retries while ensuring genuinely aborted requests do not retry or fall back.\n- Fix bindings CI failures caused by invalid git validation, missing generator configuration, and incomplete workflow triggers.\n- Prevent Secret Scan and Rust CI jobs from failing because setup-node attempts to cache an unavailable package manager.\n- Preserve custom OpenAI-compatible transcription paths and sanitize sensitive credentials from Cerebras errors.\n- Clear edit-watch state on unmount and improve native synchronization and timeout behavior.\n\nEnhancements:\n- Reduce SonarCloud new-code duplication while retaining explicit provider and integration coverage.\n- Update GitHub Actions to verified Node 24-compatible commit pins and add npm discovery for Homebrew installations.\n\nCI:\n- Expand desktop unit workflow coverage to run bindings and workflow guard tests and generated-bindings verification.\n\nDocumentation:\n- Document the completed corrective review, verification status, remaining Windows QA requirement, and conditional release recommendation.\n\nTests:\n- Add regression coverage for provider retry and abort semantics, bindings validation, workflow pins, Windows resume synchronization, timeouts, deletion cancellation, transcription paths, and error redaction.\n\nChores:\n- Remove obsolete Rust lint allowances and an unused Windows Cargo feature.\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai -->\n\n## Summary by CodeRabbit\n\n* **New Features**\n  * Windows now restores keyboard listening after resume and keeps pill placement synchronized.\n  * Added support for custom transcription endpoints with OpenAI-compatible providers.\n  * Added native syncing for interaction chime and feedback volume preferences.\n\n* **Bug Fixes**\n  * Deleting an active conversation now stops its ongoing processing.\n  * Transcript post-processing requests now time out cleanly while preserving the original transcript.\n  * Canceled AI requests no longer trigger unnecessary retries.\n  * Edit-watch polling is cleaned up when leaving the relevant screen.\n\n<!-- end of auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai -->"
