+      "description": "## What this changes\n\nThree defects in retranscription and post-processing history, plus two toast\nbugs found while reviewing the first fix.\n\n### 1. Retranscription left stale durations\n\n`updateStoredTranscription` spread the previous record and never wrote the new\ntimings, so a retranscribed row kept the original run's numbers. It now writes\n`transcriptionDurationMs` and `postprocessDurationMs` from the fresh run.\n\n### 2. Post-processing never recorded which model ran\n\nThe model id was never captured, so the details dialog could not show it. Added\n`postProcessModel` end to end: all 10 generate-text providers, the shared type,\nthe Rust struct, migration `086`, the row mapping, and a \"Model\" row in the\ndetails dialog that falls back to \"Unknown\".\n\nGroq resolves its model after a fallback, so it reports the model that actually\nanswered rather than the one first requested. Azure reports its deployment name.\nNo existing field was renamed or removed.\n\n### 3. Retranscription felt slow\n\nNot a timing problem. The loading toast stayed on screen for its full two\nminute duration after the work finished, which read as a hang. Two causes:\n\n**Toast IPC could arrive out of order.** Each `sync_native_pill_assistant` call\nis its own round trip and nothing sequenced them, so a slow show could land\nafter the dismiss meant to replace it. A test reproduced the pill receiving\n`dismiss_toast` then `toast`, backwards. Commands are now serialized through a\npromise chain that stays alive after a rejection, so one failed toast cannot\nwedge the ones behind it.\n\n**Toast ownership leaked between runs.** The success path set\n`ownsRetranscribeNativeToast = true` and never cleared it. Success now releases\nownership, and a superseded run releases the shared toast without touching the\nnewer run's row state.\n\nAlso `void`s a floating `dismissToast()` in `DictationSideEffects`, matching the\nconvention used directly beside it.\n\n## Two latent test-harness defects fixed\n\nWorth calling out because they were hiding real coverage gaps:\n\n- `transcriptions.actions.test.ts` stubbed `../i18n/intl` with only `getIntl`,\n  but `user.utils.ts` reaches `detectLocale`. That threw, the error was\n  swallowed, and **the retranscribe success path was never actually exercised**\n  despite tests passing green.\n- `vi.clearAllMocks()` stripped the async toast mock implementations, so they\n  returned `undefined` into `.then()`.\n\n## Verification\n\n| Check | Status | Evidence |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| `check-types` | Passed | `tsc --noEmit`, clean at `456a920` |\n| `lint` | Passed | 0 warnings, 0 errors, 502 files |\n| `test:unit` | Passed | 1154 tests / 110 files |\n| `test:integration` | Not run locally | Needs `GROQ_API_KEY`; CI injects it from secrets |\n| Migration replay | Passed | All 83 migrations into real SQLite, 25 columns |\n| SQL bind order | Passed | Executed real INSERT/UPDATE, verified every column |\n| `cargo clippy` / `cargo test` | **Not run** | No Rust toolchain in this sandbox |\n| `check-bindings.sh` | **Not run** | Same, see the handoff comment below |\n\nEach fix has a regression test that was confirmed red before the fix and green\nafter. Three earlier test drafts were discarded because they passed against\nbroken code.\n\n## Known gap\n\n`packages/desktop-native-apis/src/bindings.ts` is missing four fields. One is\nmine, three predate this branch (drift from #167). It is generated output and I\ndid not hand-edit it, per FULL-REVIEW 14.3. Nothing breaks today because no\napplication code imports that type. A follow-up comment on this PR has exact\nsteps for an agent with a Rust toolchain.\n\n## Summary by Sourcery\n\nFix retranscription history and feedback so fresh timing and model metadata are persisted while native toast state remains correctly ordered across completed, failed, and overlapping runs.\n\nNew Features:\n- Record and display the resolved post-processing model for transcription history across supported providers, including fallback and deployment models.\n\nBug Fixes:\n- Refresh transcription and post-processing durations and clear stale values when retranscribing records.\n- Prevent native retranscription toasts from arriving out of order, leaking ownership, or suppressing newer feedback during overlapping runs.\n- Ensure toast failures do not block later commands or hide completion feedback.\n\nEnhancements:\n- Refactor transcription detail metadata rendering around shared field formatting and unknown-value handling.\n- Consolidate OpenAI-compatible text generation providers around shared behavior.\n\nTests:\n- Add regression coverage for duration and model persistence, provider model attribution, toast ordering and failure recovery, overlapping retranscription runs, and transcription detail rendering.\n- Fix test mocks and harness setup so retranscription success and asynchronous toast paths are exercised correctly.\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai -->\n\n## Summary by CodeRabbit\n\n- **New Features**\n  - Transcription details now display the post-processing model used.\n  - Transcriptions record the resolved AI model, including fallback models.\n  - AI provider metadata now identifies the model used for each request.\n\n- **Bug Fixes**\n  - Toast notifications now preserve call order and continue working after failures.\n  - Retranscription feedback handles cancellation, superseded runs, and dismissal failures more reliably.\n  - Retranscription updates now preserve current metadata and durations correctly.\n\n<!-- end of auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai -->"
