+      "description": "This PR clears every open automated-review finding sitting on the 1.6 release branch: the SonarCloud \\\"1 new issue\\\" on PR 63 (unused `width` parameter) plus a second live Sonar issue the badge comment missed (`String.match` in the gitleaks guard), the review-bot suggestions from the PR 172/174 merge round, and a set of pre-existing hygiene problems (test duplication, `.mjs` analyzer parse errors, formatting drift) that the same bots keep re-flagging. Nothing here changes app behavior except two small hardening wins: single-quoted secrets and boolean secret values are now redacted from error text, and the build now also stubs `node:`-prefixed imports from the Gladia SDK.\n\n## How to test it\n\nThe commands below already pass locally on this branch:\n\n- `pnpm --filter desktop run test:unit` — 970 tests pass\n- `pnpm --filter desktop run lint` and `check-types` — clean\n- `pnpm --filter @maus-inc/voice-ai run test`, `@repo/agent`, `@maus-inc/utilities` — pass\n- `node --test scripts/ci/check-gitleaks-config.test.mjs` (10), `updater-manifest.test.mjs` (14), `pr28-contracts.test.mjs` (24) — pass\n- `node scripts/ci/check-gitleaks-config.mjs` and `node scripts/ci/test-secret-history-scan.mjs` — pass\n\n<details>\n<summary>What changed, file by file</summary>\n\n**SonarCloud findings**\n\n- `scripts/generate-windows-installer-sidebar.mjs` — removed the unused `width` parameter from `defilterScanlines` and its call site. This was the \\\"1 new issue\\\" in the PR 63 Sonar comment.\n- `scripts/ci/check-gitleaks-config.mjs` — replaced `String.match` with `RegExp.exec` (SonarCloud S6594, live in the Sonar API even though the badge only showed one issue).\n\n**Review-bot suggestions (kilo/code-spect on PR 174)**\n\n- `packages/utilities/src/error.ts` — `api_key='secret'` with single quotes now redacts in full instead of leaking `'secret`; `true`/`false` no longer count as placeholder values, so `api_key=true` redacts too. Tests added for both.\n- `apps/desktop/vite.config.ts` — the Gladia peer stub now recognizes `node:fs`, `node:ws`, `node:undici` and friends, so an SDK update switching to prefixed builtins cannot smuggle Node transports into the webview bundle. Tests updated to pin this.\n- `apps/desktop/src/actions/transcribe.actions.ts` — split the post-processing dispatch into `applyPostProcessing` and `beginPostProcessingRequest` so `postProcessTranscript` and `runPostProcessingRequest` drop under DeepSource's complexity threshold. Behavior is unchanged; the provider-attribution tests still pass untouched.\n- `.github/workflows/secret-scan.yml` — replaced the duplicated, contradictory comments above the Node setup step with one accurate statement (the version pin lives in `.nvmrc`, read by every workflow in the repo).\n- The `@maus-inc/utilities` circular-dependency suggestion was verified: `utilities` depends only on `@maus-inc/types`; `turbo run build --filter=@repo/agent^...` builds clean with no cycle.\n\n**DeepSource report-card items**\n\n- `.deepsource.toml` (new) — declares ES-module syntax so DeepSource stops reporting fake \\\"'import' and 'export' may appear only with sourceType: module\\\" errors on every `.mjs` file. This should clear the six open parsing threads on PR 63.\n- `apps/desktop/src/utils/global-error-overlay.utils.test.ts` — the `HTMLScriptElement`/`HTMLLinkElement`/`HTMLImageElement` stand-in classes were defined identically in five tests; they now live in two shared helpers. The one remaining empty class is deliberate (the code under test does `instanceof` checks against it).\n\n**Duplication and latent bugs found while fixing**\n\n- `scripts/ci/updater-manifest.test.mjs` — extracted `runReleaseScript`/`buildManifest`; this removes the three duplicated run-and-parse blocks SonarCloud counted toward its 1.3% duplication measure (107 duplicated lines, the largest non-test-app block).\n- `scripts/ci/test-secret-history-scan.mjs` — it duplicated the gitleaks TOML parsing and had the same string-in-value weakness the kilo bot flagged in the guard, plus a latent bug: it grabbed the first `regex` in the file instead of the updater rule specifically. It now imports `rulesSection`/`updaterRulePattern` from the guard, so both scripts test the same rule and the false-match class is gone.\n- `scripts/ci/check-gitleaks-config.mjs` — `section()` and the top-level-table check no longer treat `[allowlist]` inside a TOML string value as a section boundary (`indexOfOutsideStrings`, with tests).\n\n**Formatting drift (pre-existing, format-only diffs)**\n\n- `apps/desktop/webdriver/wdio.conf.js`, `apps/desktop/scripts/generate-windows-installer-sidebar.test.mjs`, `scripts/ci/pr28-contracts.test.mjs`, `scripts/ci/render-cask.mjs`, `apps/docs/scripts/make-card-ascii.mjs`, `packages/types/src/ai-llm.types.ts`, `packages/voice-ai/src/gemini.utils.test.ts` — brought to canonical Prettier output. No logic changes. `packages/desktop-native-apis/src/bindings.ts` also fails the format check but is generated by tauri-specta, so it is intentionally left alone.\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>Findings intentionally not changed, and why</summary>\n\n- **Binary IPC for `PrivateHttpResponse.body` (kilo, PR 63)** — real, and already tracked: `commands.rs` carries a KNOWN COST note pointing at `docs/pr63-pr109-review-findings-audit.md`, because the fix needs regenerated Specta bindings and a Rust toolchain. Doing it blind here would risk the IPC contract.\n- **`.ghtoken` in git history (kilo, PR 63)** — the file is gone from the tree, but purging history rewrites every commit and invalidates forks. That needs the token rotated first and a coordinated force-push; flagging it for a human decision rather than doing it silently.\n- **PR 63's Gladia threads (`onConnectionInterrupted`, `finalizeTimeoutMs` clamping, redaction patterns) and the `modelSize` hardcode** — verified already fixed on the current head; the threads are just not outdated-marked because they sit on old SHAs.\n\n</details>\n\n- MausAgent | Filed by `arena-ai-coding-agent`, with @Owie6789, on 2026-09-05\n\n## Summary by Sourcery\n\nClose automated review findings across the 1.6 branch while hardening secret redaction, gitleaks validation, and Gladia browser stubbing without changing application behavior.\n\nBug Fixes:\n- Harden secret handling so boolean and single-quoted credential values are fully redacted from error messages.\n- Improve gitleaks configuration validation to reliably identify the updater-key rule and ignore structural markers inside TOML strings.\n- Remove the unused PNG scanline parameter and replace the flagged string-matching API to resolve SonarCloud findings.\n\nEnhancements:\n- Refactor transcript post-processing and shared test helpers to reduce complexity and duplication without changing behavior.\n- Support node:-prefixed Gladia SDK imports in browser peer stubs and make E2E npm invocation more portable.\n- Consolidate updater manifest test setup and align affected files with canonical formatting.\n\nBuild:\n- Add DeepSource ES-module configuration to prevent false parsing findings for .mjs files.\n\nCI:\n- Simplify the secret-scan workflow's Node setup documentation and share gitleaks parsing logic between validation scripts.\n\nTests:\n- Expand coverage for secret redaction, gitleaks TOML parsing, updater rule selection, and node:-prefixed Gladia imports.\n\nChores:\n- Clean up pre-existing formatting drift and duplicated test fixtures across the repository."
