+      "description": "<!-- kody-pr-summary:start -->\nThis pull request fixes end-to-end review findings for version 1.6 across several interconnected areas:\n\n**Thock/Haptic Feedback Volume Control:** Added a user-controllable interaction feedback volume (`Option<f32>` in Rust domain, clamped to [0.05, 0.5] at the persistence boundary and on the wire). The volume is applied on both the warm audio path and the fallback path via `AudioRequest::PlayThock { bytes, volume }`, stored in a lock-free atomic, and mirrored from the TS side via a new `set_interaction_feedback_volume` Tauri command. A new `ThockVolumeControl` slider in the Audio dialog reflects the [0.05, 0.5] safe window.\n\n**Cerebras 402 / Provider Error Handling:** Introduced `CerebrasProviderError` and `normalizeCerebrasError` to classify billing/auth/validation failures (status 400–404, 422) as non-retryable terminal errors with actionable user-facing messages. `cebrasGenerateTextResponse` and `cebrasStreamChat` both surface these normalized errors, and `isCerebrasTerminalStatus` prevents wasteful retries on unrecoverable statuses.\n\n**Agent Loop Robustness:** Added `safeSideEffect` in `run-agent.ts` to wrap non-critical side effects (chat-message persistence, streaming-state writes) so a rejected write (e.g., \"resource id is invalid\") never terminates the `for await` loop. `finalizeAssistantMessage` now uses `try/finally` to retire the streaming entry regardless of persistence outcome. The `AgentLoop` class in `packages/agent` added `executeTool` with error isolation — a thrown or failed tool never aborts the loop; it returns a `toolResult` event instead.\n\n**Markdown Rendering on Pill:** Rewrote `markdownToPillText` to preserve structural readability: GFM tables are converted to pipe-separated rows (separator row dropped), lists/headings stay on their own lines, whitespace collapse preserves single newlines between blocks, and a single-pass linear `stripTagsOnce` scanner plus entity decoding neutralizes raw/encoded HTML before length clamping.\n\n**Composer Window Management:** Fixed the \"white flash then vanishes\" failure class by adding an `activeComposer` slot guard against duplicate window creation, a `COMPOSER_READY_TIMEOUT_MS = 15s` safety net that destroys a blank webview and toasts recovery (\"Open history\") if `composer-ready` never arrives, and a `composer-ready` emit from the ComposerPage mount. The ready timeout uses a boolean flag (not a nullable timeout id) to avoid a race where a fast-mounting page gets killed by its own safety net.\n\n**Dictation Style Semantics:** Fixed `getEffectiveToneIdAtFinalize` to use `toneIdAtStart ?? toneIdAtStop ?? liveSelectedToneId` instead of the reverse — the start-time selection is now authoritative for the whole utterance, and a mid-dictation style switch only affects the next recording (matching the pill label shown at start). The stop snapshot becomes a race-safety fallback.\n\n**Audio Energy Silence Gate:** Added `analyzeSilence` (RMS, peak, max-windowed-RMS) to `audio-energy.utils.ts` and integrated it into `BaseTranscribeAudioRepo` so near-silent chunks are skipped before reaching cloud providers, preventing providers biased by their prompt (dictionary/glossary) from hallucinating words into silence.\n\n**Post-Processing Attribution:** Added `postProcessProvider`, `postProcessFailed`, and `postProcessError` fields to the Transcription domain and persistence layer. Provider attribution is written before the network request so a 402, timeout, or cancellation still records which provider was selected. The raw transcript is preserved on failure.\n\n**DB Migrations:** Added migrations 78 (`post_process_attribution` columns on `transcriptions`) and 79 (`interaction_feedback_volume` on `user_profiles`, default 0.35), with a test verifying a legacy 1.5.x database upgrades correctly and legacy rows read back NULL for new columns.\n\n**Pill Click Safety:** Added `can_emit_interaction_feedback` in the shared pill crate so a body click during the Loading phase is inert — no haptic, no audio feedback, no second action dispatch — on all platforms.\n\n**Type System:** Added `interactionFeedbackVolume?: Nullable<number>` to the shared `User` type with Zod validation (`min(0.05).max(0.5)`), and `postProcessProvider/Failed/Error` to the shared `Transcription` type, keeping the TS-Rust contract consistent across packages.\n<!-- kody-pr-summary:end -->"
