tructured logger instead of console.error\"): production error paths in `chat.actions.ts` (`loadConversations`, `applySendToConversation`, `computeIsFirstMessage`, `persistSend` failure) now route through `getLogger().error`. Dev-only context (title/content preview) stays dev-only; `updatedAt` remains always-on for correlation. The chat action test now asserts on the structured logger mock instead of spying on `console.error`.\n\n## Validation (local, pre-push)\n\n- Desktop TS unit tests: **965 passed / 100 files** (`vitest run src scripts`)\n- `@repo/agent` 9 passed, `@maus-inc/utilities` 23 passed, `@maus-inc/voice-ai` 72 passed\n- Desktop `tsc --noEmit` clean; desktop `prettier --check` + `oxlint` clean\n- i18n catalog sync clean (no drift after `pnpm --filter desktop i18n`)\n- Secret-scan guard tests + structure check + history-scan integration pass; dev-surface-contracts pass\n- `pnpm install --frozen-lockfile` clean (lock ↔ manifests consistent)\n\nMerging this PR updates #132's head to contain the current base tip, which makes #132 mergeable.\n\n## Summary by Sourcery\n\nSynchronize the chat changes with the reviewed base, preserve the intended localization updates, and close the remaining review findings.\n\nBug Fixes:\n- Replace direct console error reporting in chat actions with structured logging while preserving development-only diagnostic context.\n- Pin the Node.js version used by secret-scan guard tests to the repository's configured version.\n\nEnhancements:\n- Resolve merge conflicts by retaining the canonical reviewed chat/sidebar implementation and preserving the PR-specific localization changes.\n- Update chat action tests to validate structured logger error reporting.\n\nCI:\n- Make secret-scan guard tests run against the Node.js version specified in .nvmrc.\n\nTests:\n- Update chat action failure-path coverage for structured logging."
