+      "description": "This PR closes the review threads still open on PR #132 and PR #63. It is stacked on PR #132 (`arena/01a0358e-mausvoice`) and also merges the current `fix/superfix-review-findings` base so the two branches stop drifting. Ten files change: secret redaction accepts quoted JSON keys and stops hiding harmless words like `required`, the Gladia bundler stub now fails the build when it silently stops applying, the gitleaks config guard catches a top-level `useDefault = false`, two Rust match arms list every model explicitly, one duplicated Rust test is removed, and a mis-indented `#[cfg]` in `app.rs` is put back where the dev-surface contract test expects it.\n\n<details>\n<summary>What each change does and how to check it</summary>\n\n**Secret redaction (`packages/utilities/src/error.ts`)**\n`unknownToMessage` is the helper that turns any thrown value into a log-safe string.\n- Before: `\"apiKey\":\"secret\"` embedded in a longer message kept the quoted key visible, and `api_key=required` became `api_key=[redacted]`.\n- After: quoted property names match too, and a short list of descriptive words (`required`, `missing`, `invalid`, `expired`, `revoked`, `null`, `undefined`, `none`, `empty`, `true`, `false`) is left readable. Everything else after a secret label is still redacted.\n- Check: `pnpm --filter @maus-inc/utilities test` (3 new cases).\n\n**Gladia peer stubs (`apps/desktop/vite.config.ts`)**\nThe desktop build swaps the Gladia SDK's Node-only imports (`fs`, `path`, `undici`, `ws`) for browser stubs. That swap keyed on a path substring and had no assertion, so an SDK bump that moved to `node:fs` would silently bundle `undici` and `ws` outside the CSP-governed transport.\n- After: the plugin counts applied stubs and throws at `buildEnd` if the SDK was in the graph but zero stubs applied. Verified locally: a normal `vite build` passes, and breaking the peer list makes the build fail with a named error.\n- The plugin also moved into a factory so its counters are not module globals.\n\n**Gitleaks config guard (`scripts/ci/check-gitleaks-config.mjs`)**\n- Added check (e): a top-level `useDefault = false` in `gitleaks.toml` now fails the guard. Verified by prepending that line and running the script.\n\n**Rust model table (`packages/rust_transcription/src/models.rs`)**\n`artifact_set` and `whisper_cpp_sha256` used `_ =>` wildcards. A future model variant would compile and silently get an empty artifact list or no digest. Both arms now name every variant.\n\n**Duplicate test removed (`packages/rust_transcription/tests/sidecar_integration.rs`)**\n`every_downloaded_model_artifact_is_supply_chain_pinned` re-asserted what `models.rs` and `downloads.rs` unit tests already pin. Dropped along with its now-unused import.\n\n**Dev-surface contract (`apps/desktop/src-tauri/src/app.rs`)**\nA `// skipcq` comment had been inserted between `#[cfg(feature = \"debug-assist\")]` and its `if`, and the `if` was over-indented. `scripts/ci/dev-surface-contracts.test.mjs` failed on that. The comment now sits above the attribute.\n\n**Small items**\n- `run-agent.ts`: `safeSideEffect` is an arrow constant like the helpers around it (DeepSource JS-0239).\n- `hallucination.utils.ts`: `joinKeptSegmentTexts` checks the previous segment's trailing boundary instead of the whole accumulated string.\n- `AGENTS.md`: the babysit loop had two step `3.` entries; now `1. 2. 3.` with the duplicate removed.\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>PR #63 threads that were already fixed on the base branch</summary>\n\nMost of the 91 unresolved PR #63 threads describe code that no longer exists on `fix/superfix-review-findings`. I re-read each one against the merged tree before deciding it needed no code change. Examples: `transcription_import_audio` is now picker-owned with an allow-list and a drop guard; `resample_to_rate` returns `Result`; the table cache is LRU with a coefficient budget; SenseVoice has a real revision and digests; `ComposerPage` uses `useCallback` for `finish` and imports `act` from `react`; the four regressed locale strings are translated again; `dictation.strategy` drains through the queue and `cleanup()` advances the nonce; `ContextMenu` portals and captures Escape; `release.yml` has `shell: bash`; Gemini threads `signal`; the DB upgrade path has a test; the DeepSource `.mjs` parse errors point at ESM files that CI runs fine under `\"type\": \"module\"`.\n\nTwo items stay out of band and are already recorded in `docs/pr63-pr109-review-findings-audit.md`: rotating the historical `.ghtoken` credential, and moving private-HTTP bodies to binary IPC.\n\nThreads are resolved individually with a pointer to this head, not in bulk.\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>Verification</summary>\n\n- `pnpm run check-types`: 8 tasks green\n- `pnpm run lint`: green\n- `pnpm --filter desktop test:unit`: 100 files, 964 tests\n- `pnpm --filter @maus-inc/utilities test`: 23 tests\n- `pnpm --filter @maus-inc/voice-ai test`: 72 tests\n- `pnpm --filter @repo/agent test`: 9 tests\n- `node --test scripts/ci/*.test.mjs`: 47 pass, 0 fail (was 46/1 before the `app.rs` fix)\n- `vite build` for the desktop app: passes; with the peer list broken it fails with the new error\n- Rust changes could not be compiled in this sandbox (no network for rustup); the match arms enumerate the exact `WhisperModel` variants and CI's Rust jobs cover them.\n\n</details>\n\nMausAgent | Filed by `claude-sonnet-4-5`, with `@Owie6789`, on 2026-09-05\n\n## Summary by Sourcery\n\nImprove desktop chat lifecycle and sidebar behavior while hardening secret scanning, bundling safeguards, model handling, and related test coverage.\n\nNew Features:\n- Automatically derive conversation titles from the first message and update chat sidebar ordering and timestamps by recent activity.\n- Display compact conversation dates with hover and selection states revealing precise times.\n- Add CI tests and stronger validation for Gitleaks configuration and desktop development-surface contracts.\n\nBug Fixes:\n- Prevent concurrent chat sends and delete races from persisting messages or invoking agents for deleted conversations.\n- Preserve chat state and delivery behavior when conversation metadata updates fail.\n- Improve secret redaction for quoted labels, nested punctuation, and descriptive placeholder values.\n- Fix conversation title truncation around surrogate pairs and grapheme clusters, correct segment joining boundaries, and keep selected chat timestamps readable.\n- Ensure Gladia browser peer stubs are applied during bundling or fail the build when they are not.\n- Replace wildcard Rust model matches with exhaustive variant handling.\n\nEnhancements:\n- Refine chat action persistence, title derivation, recency handling, and deletion coordination.\n- Refactor chat sidebar rendering to use localized short date and time displays with reduced-motion support.\n- Standardize shared React Intl test mocking and expand desktop component and utility coverage.\n- Remove a redundant Rust supply-chain test and apply minor code-quality and documentation cleanups.\n\nBuild:\n- Extend desktop linting and formatting to test files.\n- Add a build-time guard for Gladia SDK browser peer stubs.\n\nCI:\n- Run dedicated Gitleaks configuration guard helper tests in the secret-scan workflow.\n- Strengthen Gitleaks configuration parsing and prevent disabling the default rule set.\n\nDocumentation:\n- Document automatic chat naming, activity ordering, and date/time display behavior.\n- Clarify supported local transcription models and SenseVoice aliases.\n\nTests:\n- Add comprehensive tests for chat send/delete races, persistence failures, title derivation, sidebar rendering, timestamp behavior, accessibility contrast, and reduced motion.\n- Add coverage for Gitleaks TOML comment handling, Gladia SDK module detection, date formatting, and secret-redaction edge cases.\n\nChores:\n- Correct the babysitting procedure numbering, align helper style