+      "description": "This stacked PR fixes the three CodeSpect minor findings on PR 132. Agent side-effect logs now JSON-quote context values and collapse control characters in the error text so a multi-line or comma-filled value cannot break or confuse a log line. `unknownToMessage` redacts bearer tokens and common API key forms, then caps the message at 512 characters so tool-failure text and logs cannot dump secrets or huge payloads.\n\n<details>\n<summary>What changed</summary>\n\n- `safeSideEffect` in `apps/desktop/src/agents/run-agent.ts` runs the error through `sanitizeContextValue` before logging, and writes context as `key=\"value\"` via `JSON.stringify` after the existing single-line truncate.\n- `unknownToMessage` in `packages/utilities/src/error.ts` redacts `Bearer` tokens, provider prefixes (`csk_`, `gsk_`, `sk-ant-`, `xai-`, `sk-`), and labeled `apiKey` / `api_key` / `authorization` / token assignment forms, then truncates at 512 characters.\n- Tests cover quoting, control collapse on the error message, bearer and JSON key redaction, and the length cap.\n\nThe two CodeSpect nitpicks on PR 132 (`AGENTS.md` list numbering and `joinKeptSegmentTexts` previous-segment boundary) are out of scope here.\n\n</details>\n\nMausAgent | Filed by composer, with @Owie6789, on 2026-09-05\n\n## Summary by Sourcery\n\nHarden agent failure logging by making log values safe and parseable while redacting sensitive content and limiting error message size.\n\nBug Fixes:\n- Sanitize agent side-effect logs to prevent control characters and ambiguous context values from breaking or confusing log lines.\n- Redact bearer tokens, provider API keys, and labeled secret values from unknown error messages.\n- Cap unknown error messages at 512 characters to prevent oversized payloads and secret leakage.\n\nEnhancements:\n- Add coverage for safe log formatting, secret redaction, nested values, and message length limits.\n\nTests:\n- Expand agent logging and error utility tests to cover quoting, control-character handling, redaction, and payload limits."
