+      "description": "Closes the last real gaps that still reproduce on PR #132 HEAD. This is a residual-only stack on #132 — not a reimplementation of the 1.6 review work already landed there.\n\n**What changes for users / reviewers**\n- Cancelling an agent mid-tool no longer drops the tool result: once a tool starts, the loop always emits a matching result into history before finishing as aborted.\n- Dictation start waits for the focused app id before the first interim paste can run, so early realtime paste routes with the correct app context.\n- Successful post-processing clears prior failure flags, and retranscribe updates persist provider / failed / error fields.\n- Dropping near-silent Whisper segments keeps natural spacing when segments already carry leading spaces.\n\n<details>\n<summary>Details</summary>\n\n### Root causes addressed\n1. **Agent abort race** — `processToolCalls` returned after `executeTool` (and after `tool-call-start`) without yielding `tool-call-result`, leaving an assistant tool-call without a tool message.\n2. **App-target race** — `DictationStrategy.onBeforeStart` fire-and-forgot `loadAppTarget()`, so `currentAppId` could still be null when interim paste began. Style seeding already runs earlier in `DictationSideEffects`; this await only owns paste routing.\n3. **Post-process attribution on update** — success path never cleared `postProcessFailed` / `postProcessError`; `updateStoredTranscription` omitted the three post-process attribution fields added for create.\n4. **Silence-gate spacing** — rebuilding kept text with a forced `\" \"` join doubled spaces when Whisper segments already included leading whitespace.\n\n### Intentionally not changed\n- Composer still resolves `null` on WebView2 create failure (recovery toast + history retention) — reject would be a product contract change.\n- Prefs realtime/review mutual exclusion already normalizes on `setUserPreferences` read/write path on #132 HEAD.\n- Cerebras stream normalize, `can_emit_interaction_feedback`, and create-path postProcess DB columns are already on #132.\n\n### Tests run\n- `pnpm --filter @repo/agent test` — 9/9 pass (includes new abort-after-start case)\n- `pnpm --filter desktop exec vitest run` on hallucination, dictation strategy, post-processing-failure, user.utils, user.actions, composer, run-agent — 66 tests pass\n- `pnpm --filter desktop check-types` — clean\n- Prettier check on touched files — clean\n\n</details>\n\n---\n*Made with [Arena](https://arena.ai)*\n\n## Summary by Sourcery\n\nClose residual review-path races and metadata inconsistencies across agent cancellation, dictation targeting, post-processing, and transcription cleanup.\n\nBug Fixes:\n- Ensure agent tool calls always emit matching results and history entries when cancellation occurs after tool execution starts.\n- Prevent early dictation interim pastes from racing focused-app target resolution.\n- Clear stale post-processing failure state after successful retranscription and persist provider and failure metadata on updates.\n- Preserve natural spacing and structural whitespace when filtering silent transcription segments.\n\nEnhancements:\n- Sanitize control characters in agent error context before writing single-line logs.\n- Improve post-processing error serialization for non-Error thrown values.\n\nTests:\n- Add coverage for abort-after-tool-start behavior, focused-app resolution, post-processing failure reset, log sanitization, and transcription segment spacing."
