+      "description": "<!-- kody-pr-summary:start -->\n## Pull Request Description\n\nThis pull request implements two interconnected features for the mausVoice chat sidebar:\n\n### 1. Auto-Titling Conversations\n\nConversations now automatically derive their title from the first message sent, replacing the generic \"New conversation\" placeholder. Key behaviors:\n\n- **First message names the conversation**: When a user sends their first message, the sidebar row is titled based on the message content (capped at 4 words / 32 characters, with ellipsis truncation).\n- **Legacy placeholder retitling**: Conversations created before auto-titling (still carrying \"New conversation\" or its localized equivalent) are retitled from their next incoming message.\n- **Follow-up messages preserved**: Subsequent messages do not overwrite an already-derived title.\n- **Concurrent send serialization**: A per-conversation queue ensures that if multiple sends race, the newest timestamp and title persist correctly. A failed conversation update is caught and logged without blocking the message delivery or agent execution, and the next send retries the title/timestamp bump.\n- **Delete race protection**: A `deletingConversationIds` set and queue-management logic prevent a message from being persisted or an agent from running against a conversation that is being deleted between the send being queued and reaching the front of the queue.\n\n### 2. Animated Timestamps in the Sidebar\n\nEach conversation row now displays a compact date (e.g., \"Aug 25\") and switches to the precise time (e.g., \"10:40 PM\") on hover or when the row is selected/opened. The swap between date and time is animated with a crossfade slide effect, and respects `prefers-reduced-motion` for instant swaps. The timestamp lives inside `ListItemText-secondary` slot so it stays readable on the inverted selected-row background in light mode.\n\n### Supporting Changes\n\n- **New date formatting utilities** (`formatShortDate`, `formatShortTime`) replace the previous `formatRelativeTime` to provide compact, local-time formatted strings suitable for sidebar rows.\n- **Title derivation utilities** (`deriveConversationTitle`, `hasPlaceholderTitle`, `nextConversationTitle`) with proper UTF-16 surrogate-pair handling during truncation/ellipsis.\n- **Shared `react-intl` mock** extracted for jsdom component tests.\n- **Updated documentation** describing the new auto-titling behavior and timestamp interaction.\n<!-- kody-pr-summary:end -->\n\n## Summary by Sourcery\n\nAutomatically title conversations from their initial messages and provide interactive, accessible sidebar timestamps while hardening send and deletion behavior.\n\nNew Features:\n- Automatically derive conversation titles from the first message and retitle legacy placeholder conversations while preserving established titles.\n- Display compact conversation dates that crossfade to precise times on hover or selection, with reduced-motion support.\n\nBug Fixes:\n- Prevent concurrent sends and deletion races from persisting messages or running agents against removed conversations.\n- Ensure failed conversation metadata updates do not block message delivery and are retried by subsequent sends.\n- Keep timestamps readable on selected sidebar rows in light mode.\n\nEnhancements:\n- Add localized short date and time formatting plus title derivation utilities with Unicode-safe truncation.\n- Serialize per-conversation sends and improve failure handling around conversation and message persistence.\n\nDocumentation:\n- Document automatic conversation titling, activity ordering, and sidebar timestamp interactions.\n\nTests:\n- Add coverage for title derivation, localized placeholders, Unicode truncation, timestamp formatting, concurrent sends, persistence failures, deletion races, and sidebar rendering.\n\nChores:\n- Centralize the react-intl mock used by jsdom component tests.\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai -->\n\n## Summary by CodeRabbit\n\n* **New Features**\n  * New conversations are automatically titled from their first message and retain meaningful existing titles.\n  * Conversation lists now sort by latest activity.\n  * Rows show the conversation date, switching to the precise time when hovered or selected.\n  * Timestamps respect reduced-motion preferences.\n\n* **Bug Fixes**\n  * Improved reliability when sending messages and deleting conversations concurrently.\n  * Prevented deleted conversations from receiving new messages during deletion.\n  * Conversation metadata now updates more consistently after sending messages.\n\n* **Documentation**\n  * Added documentation describing conversation naming, sorting, and timestamp behavior.\n\n<!-- end of auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai -->"
