+      "description": "<!-- kody-pr-summary:start -->\n## Summary\n\nThis PR addresses code-review findings and removes dead code across the desktop app, native pills, and voice-AI packages. Key functional changes:\n\n**Windows reliability**\n- Adds a hidden notification window that subscribes to `WM_POWERBROADCAST` and `WM_WTSSESSION_CHANGE`, emitting a `desktop_resume` Tauri event so the global hotkey listener can be re-registered after sleep/wake or session unlock (the low-level keyboard hook is torn down across those boundaries).\n- The native Windows pill now periodically re-asserts its topmost z-order, and supports a new **Pill placement** preference (`top`/`bottom`) persisted in the DB and pushed to the pill via IPC.\n\n**Storage behavior**\n- New **Preserve audio on failure** preference (default on). When disabled, failed transcriptions no longer write a WAV snapshot that would otherwise be orphaned on disk with no DB pointer to purge it. Incognito mode continues to never persist audio regardless of the setting.\n- Log directory purging now enforces a total size cap (250 MB) instead of only a file-count floor, fixing oversized log directories caused by a few large legacy files.\n\n**Transcription provider support**\n- OpenRouter now supports speech-to-text transcription (previously generative-only), dispatching through a new repo and the OpenAI-compatible SDK; the selected model is required and warns/falls back to `openai/whisper-1`.\n- OpenAI-compatible providers gain an optional **Transcription path** override (e.g. `/v1/audio/transcriptions` for Open WebUI), stored per API key and applied when building the request URL.\n- Local Whisper output now includes per-segment `no_speech_prob` data, used to filter silence-hallucination fragments (\"thank you\", \"you\") while keeping short real words intact.\n- Aldea transcription now forwards the dictation language as a query parameter (omitted for Auto).\n\n**Linux**\n- On X11 sessions, WebKitGTK workarounds (`WEBKIT_DISABLE_COMPOSITING_MODE=1`, `WEBKIT_DISABLE_DMABUF_RENDERER=1`) are set automatically before the WebView is created, fixing blank-window issues on tiling WMs and certain NVIDIA setups.\n- Super-key classification is expanded to recognize `Meta*`, `OS*`, `Super*`, and `Win*` variants when registering Wayland compositor hotkeys.\n\n**Post-processing and generation**\n- `maxTokens` is now forwarded through the generate-text repos, and post-processing caps output at 600 tokens.\n- Structured-output handling is centralized: JSON schema support is keyed per model, falling back to `json_object` for models/providers that reject `json_schema`.\n\n**Other fixes**\n- Dictionary replacement rules now escape regex metacharacters, so terms like `C++`, `a/b`, or `[bracket]` match literally instead of throwing/over-matching.\n- Signup confirm-password validation no longer shows a mismatch error before both fields are typed.\n- Realtime interim segments bypass the new hands-free output delay; a newer transcript cancels an older delayed one.\n- New `TopCenter` overlay anchor added across Linux/macOS/Windows position logic.\n\n**Cleanup**\n- Removed SenseVoice model listing, unused imports, and obsolete comments; extracted shared utilities (audio conversion, response-format building, OpenAI-compatible message/response helpers) and introduced a shared base API transcription session base class to remove duplicated provider session logic.\n<!-- kody-pr-summary:end -->"
