+      "description": "## What changed?\n\nWhen you retranscribe a clip from history, a \"Retranscribing\" banner appears above the voice pill and stays parked there, sitting right on top of the style selector so you cannot switch transcription style. This PR fixes that: starting a new dictation sweeps the banner away, and while a banner is up, moving the mouse onto the pill swaps it for the style selector so the style arrows are always reachable. The banner comes back once the mouse leaves, until it expires. The same strip also stopped pinning the style selector open for a whole recording session, and everything now behaves identically on Windows, macOS and Linux because the rules live in one shared place.\n\n<details>\n<summary>What was wrong</summary>\n\nTwo problems sat in the strip above the pill:\n\n1. **The retranscribing banner blocked the style selector.** The banner (the native pill toast) and the selector are drawn in the same spot, and the drawing code only painted the selector when no banner was showing. Nothing cleared the banner when dictation started, so a stale \"Retranscribing\" toast sat on the pill for the whole take, blocking style switching.\n2. **The selector pinned itself open while recording.** The visibility rule included \"or while recording\", so the selector appeared above the pill the moment a take started and never faded, with or without the mouse.\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>What the code does now</summary>\n\nAll decision rules live once in `rust_pill_shared` and all three pill ports (Windows, macOS, GTK/Linux) consume the same copies:\n\n- **A new take sweeps stale banners.** On a transition from Idle or Loading into Recording, each port clears the banner via a shared `clear_flash` helper (also reused by the dismiss arm). A resume from Paused keeps banners raised during the take, such as the cancel-dictation confirm.\n- **`flash_banner_target` decides who owns the strip.** A banner without an action button (like \"Retranscribing audio clip\") yields to a revealed style selector: hovering the pill swaps the banner out without cancelling it, and the banner returns when the mouse leaves, until it expires. A banner with an action button keeps the strip, since it is an interactive prompt.\n- **`style_tooltip_visible` + `StyleTooltipGate` govern the selector.** The selector is hover-revealed in every phase except Paused. A take that starts under a parked mouse forces it to fade (the latch); the latch releases when the mouse actually leaves the pill or the take ends, so moving back onto the pill mid-take brings the selector back and a chevron click still switches style on the running take.\n- The GTK port's animation tick was split into `tick_audio_levels` and `tick_flash` sub-tickers after DeepSource flagged its complexity, following the crate's existing pattern.\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>Behavior after this PR</summary>\n\n| Situation | Banner | Style selector |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| Retranscribe started from history | shown above pill | hidden (banner owns the strip) |\n| Same, mouse moves onto the pill | fades out | appears, arrows clickable |\n| Mouse leaves the pill again | returns until it expires | fades |\n| New dictation take starts | swept immediately | fades at take start, even under a parked mouse |\n| Recording, mouse moves onto the pill | n/a | appears, switch applies to the running take |\n| Dictation paused | action banners keep the strip | hidden |\n| Take ends with mouse on the pill | n/a | appears again |\n| In-app retranscribe tooltip on the history row | unchanged | unchanged |\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>Tests</summary>\n\nThirteen unit tests in `rust_pill_shared` pin the rules: banner yields to a revealed selector, action banners keep the strip, banner hidden when not visible, selector fades at take start under a parked mouse, returns after the mouse leaves and re-enters, latch releases when the take ends or when the rule is false for other reasons, Paused stays hidden with a re-latch on resume, and the nothing-to-switch cases. CI runs clippy with `-D warnings` plus the test suites for all four crates on their platform runners.\n\nReview history: an evaluation-order bug in the latch (found by CodeRabbit) and an argument-count error in one test that broke the shared-crate test job are fixed; DeepSource's complexity flag on the GTK tick and its empty-`new()` and redundant-comment notes are addressed.\n\n</details>\n\n## How is it tested?\n\n- [x] Automated tests\n- [ ] Manual verification\n- [x] Code inspection\n\nTo verify by hand on a desktop build: retranscribe a clip from history, then start dictating and confirm the banner disappears and the selector is reachable; hover the pill mid-take and switch style with the arrows; pause and resume and confirm the selector stays hidden on resume until you hover again.\n\nStacked on #63, base is `fix/superfix-review-findings`. Merge after that one.\n\n- MausAgent | Filed by `arena-agent`, with `@Owie6789`, on `2026-09-01`\n"
