+      "description": "## What\n\nReplaces the stock **blue NSIS welcome/finish sidebar** in the Windows setup (`mausVoice_*-setup.exe`) with custom branding art.\n\n## How it works\n\n`branding/mausvoice-sidebar-installerimg.png` (committed art, 548x1008 PNG) is converted to `apps/desktop/src-tauri/icons/nsis-sidebar.bmp` — the 24-bit 164x314 bitmap NSIS requires — by `scripts/generate-windows-installer-sidebar.mjs` (zero-dependency Node: PNG/BMP decode, edge-sampled letterbox composite, contain-fit bilinear resample, verified BMP encode). `tauri.conf.json` sets `bundle.windows.nsis.sidebarImage` to that bitmap. The bitmap is gitignored and always regenerated, so it can never drift from the art.\n\n**Regeneration points** (belt and suspenders):\n\n1. The uncached Tauri wrapper (`apps/desktop/scripts/run-tauri-with-sidecars.mjs`) regenerates it immediately before every `tauri build`, with `--windows-only` keeping mac/Linux hosts (which never bundle NSIS) a fast no-op. Placing it here means Turbo cache hits on the desktop `build` task cannot starve or stale the bitmap.\n2. `build-desktop.yml` and `release.yml` regenerate it in an explicit Windows-only step before the Tauri bundle.\n3. `build-desktop.yml` also triggers on art-only and script-only commits.\n\n**Tests:** `apps/desktop/scripts/generate-windows-installer-sidebar.test.mjs` (runs with `pnpm --filter desktop run test:unit` on every platform) pins all five PNG colour types, all five scanline filters, every rejection path, palette tRNS alpha, background sampling, contain-fit math, the BMP encoder contract, `verifyOutput`, and the CLI end to end.\n\n## Art contract\n\nTo change the art, replace `branding/mausvoice-sidebar-installerimg.png`. PNG (8-bit, non-interlaced) or BMP (24/32-bit uncompressed); full-bleed 164x314 renders edge-to-edge, other aspect ratios are contain-fit with an edge-sampled letterbox. Nothing else to update.\n\n## Review history\n\n- **Kilo**: colour-key `tRNS` silently ignored → now rejected explicitly; Windows-only generator no longer gates mac/Linux builds (fixed via `--windows-only`).\n- **SonarCloud**: S3776 CRITICAL (cognitive complexity 46) on `decodePng` → decomposed into focused helpers, byte-identical output verified; quality gate now passes with 0 new issues.\n- **Sourcery**: Turbo cache-hit starvation → generation moved to the uncached tauri wrapper; cwd-relative generator path → resolved from `import.meta.url` (verified from three working directories).\n"
