+      "description": "## What this is\n\nAn end-to-end pass over the **82 unresolved inline review comments** left by\n`kilo-code-bot[bot]` on PR #63 (`fix/superfix-review-findings`). Every finding\nwas re-verified against the code at the superfix head before any change was\nwritten — no blind implementation.\n\nFull accounting: `docs/kilocode-bot-review-findings-audit.md`\n\n## Result\n\n79 of 82 findings were already addressed on the superfix head by earlier\nreview-fix passes (the GitHub threads were simply never resolved). Three were\nstill live and are fixed here:\n\n- **`db/open.rs` — downgrade quarantines a readable database.** A migration\n  version recorded by a *newer* build was classified as `Integrity`, so\n  `open_app_database` renamed the live DB into `mausvoice.broken-*` and opened\n  an empty one — reachable by installing 1.6 then rolling back to 1.5. Now\n  returned as `OpenError::Other` (surfaced, data preserved); checksum mismatch\n  on a *known* version still quarantines.\n- **`db/open.rs` — no upgrade-path coverage.** Added\n  `existing_database_is_upgraded_to_head_without_quarantine`, seeding a DB with\n  all-but-the-last migration applied and asserting the remainder is applied with\n  no quarantine.\n- **`global-error-overlay` — post-mount asset failures paint the fatal overlay.**\n  `shouldPaintFatalWindowError` (and the inline `index.html` handler) classified\n  `<script>`/`<link rel=stylesheet>` errors as fatal before checking mount state,\n  so an async chunk's stylesheet failing post-mount covered a working UI. Both\n  now gate on mount state first; tests added in both directions.\n\nAlso documented the `finalizeTimeoutMs` upper bound (`gladia.utils.ts`).\n\n## Deferred / out-of-band\n\n- Binary `Vec<u8>` IPC bodies → needs Rust toolchain + Specta regen (previously\n  deferred for the same reason).\n- `.ghtoken` credential in git history → rotation + history purge (maintainer\n  action; file already removed + ignored).\n- Gladia peer-stub build assertion, Gitleaks `useDefault` tradeoff → left open\n  with rationale in the audit doc.\n\n## Verification\n\nRust and JS toolchains (cargo/pnpm) are not available in this sandbox, so the\n`cargo test`/`check-types`/`vitest` runs are left to CI. Changes are narrow and\nself-contained (one classification change + tests, one ordering change + tests).\n\n## Summary by Sourcery\n\nPreserve user data across database downgrades and ensure post-mount asset failures are handled without obscuring the running application.\n\nBug Fixes:\n- Preserve readable databases during application downgrades by surfacing migration versions from newer releases instead of quarantining the database.\n- Prevent post-mount script and stylesheet load failures from covering a functioning UI with the fatal error overlay, while logging those failures for diagnostics.\n\nEnhancements:\n- Make global error overlay installation idempotent and document the upper bound applied to Gladia finalization timeouts.\n\nDocumentation:\n- Document the Gladia finalization timeout limit and its configuration implications.\n\nTests:\n- Add database coverage for downgrade preservation and upgrading existing databases to the latest migration.\n- Expand error-overlay coverage for pre- and post-mount resource failures, logging behavior, and repeated installation.\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated description by cubic. -->\n---\n## Summary by cubic\nPrevents downgrade-triggered data loss and stops the global error overlay from covering the UI after mount. Previously downgrades quarantined readable databases and post-mount asset errors could either paint or be dropped; now downgrades surface the error without quarantine and post-mount asset failures are logged as non-fatal, with the overlay installer made idempotent.\n\n- Bug Fixes\n  - Treat migration versions written by a newer release as Other so downgrades surface without quarantining; known-version checksum mismatches still quarantine.\n  - Check mount state before classifying resource targets so post-mount script/stylesheet failures log via console.warn instead of painting the fatal overlay.\n  - Make `installGlobalErrorOverlay` idempotent to avoid duplicate listeners on re-install.\n  - Document and clamp the finalize timeout ceiling in `packages/voice-ai`.\n\n- Tests\n  - Add coverage for upgrading an existing database to head without quarantine.\n  - Assert downgrades with multiple unknown recorded migration versions preserve the database.\n  - Verify pre- vs post-mount resource failures and add an early overlay test for post-mount resource load.\n  - Add an idempotency test to ensure a single pair of listeners is registered.\n\n<sup>Written for commit 79fc92d2a8661654b93d371322b877f2490ec0cb. Summary will update on new commits.</sup>\n\n<a href=\"https://cubic.dev/pr/maus-inc/mausVoice/pull/134?utm_source=github\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" data-no-image-dialog=\"true\"><picture><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\" srcset=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-dark.svg\"><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\" srcset=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-light.svg\"><img alt=\"Review in cubic\" src=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-dark.svg\"></picture></a>\n\n<!-- End of auto-generated description by cubic. -->\n\n"
