+      "description": "## Summary\n\nThe latest build could refuse to show a window in two ways:\n\n1. **SQLite migrations abort process startup.** `tauri-plugin-sql` runs sqlx during plugin init. After `SELECT version, checksum FROM _sqlx_migrations` (75 rows), a checksum mismatch or a half-applied migration fails plugin init. `run().expect(\"tauri runtime failure\")` then kills the process before any window exists.\n\n2. **The fatal overlay covers a running UI.** After the bundle loaded, `installGlobalErrorOverlay` treated every capture-phase `error` and every `unhandledrejection` as “mausVoice failed to start,” including image load failures and sidecar timeouts.\n\n## Changes\n\n- Apply migrations in setup instead of on the SQL plugin. On checksum mismatch, a failed prior migration, or a corrupt file, quarantine the DB as `mausvoice.broken-<timestamp>.db` and open a fresh one so the app still launches.\n- Paint the fatal overlay only for pre-mount failures and failed script/stylesheet loads. Ignore post-mount rejections and non-script resource errors.\n\n## Test plan\n\n- [ ] Launch against a healthy existing `mausvoice.db` (75 applied migrations, matching checksums). App opens as usual.\n- [ ] Tamper one `_sqlx_migrations.checksum` (or leave `success = false`). App still opens; a `mausvoice.broken-*` file appears next to the DB.\n- [ ] After the UI is up, trigger a failed image load or an unhandled rejection. The dashboard must stay visible (no full-screen “failed to start” overlay).\n- [ ] A missing JS/CSS asset before mount still shows the fatal overlay.\n\n## Summary by Sourcery\n\nKeep the desktop app launchable and usable when database integrity or frontend runtime failures occur.\n\nBug Fixes:\n- Recover from corrupt, inconsistent, or previously failed SQLite migration state by quarantining the broken database and opening a fresh one instead of aborting application startup.\n- Prevent runtime errors, unhandled rejections, and non-critical resource failures from hiding an already mounted interface with the fatal startup overlay.\n\nEnhancements:\n- Move database migration handling into application setup while preserving hard failures for non-integrity database errors.\n- Limit fatal startup reporting to pre-mount failures and failed JavaScript or stylesheet asset loads.\n- Allow legacy transcription-model migration errors to be logged without blocking startup.\n\nTests:\n- Add coverage for database corruption recovery, migration checksum and history validation, quarantine behavior, rollback failures, and overlay gating rules.\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated description by cubic. -->\n---\n## Summary by cubic\nKeeps the desktop app usable when `sqlx` migrations or runtime errors fail and prevents the startup overlay from hiding a mounted UI. Old: migrations ran at `tauri_plugin_sql` init and any checksum/failed migration aborted startup; the overlay treated any capture-phase error/unhandledrejection as “failed to start.” New: apply migrations during setup with recovery; only pre-mount errors and failed script/stylesheet loads show the overlay.\n\n- Database open and recovery: register `tauri_plugin_sql` without `.add_migrations`; open via `open_app_database` using `SqliteConnectOptions`. Apply each migration in a transaction, compute SHA‑384 checksums like `sqlx`, and reject recorded versions not in the current Up set. Classify integrity failures (checksum mismatch, prior failure, corrupt/not-a-DB, unknown recorded version) and quarantine `mausvoice.db` plus `-journal`/`-wal`/`-shm` into a unique `mausvoice.broken-<timestamp>` directory using a reversible rename; reopen a fresh DB. Keep non‑integrity errors (locks, permission issues, bad new migration) as hard failures. If rollback fails, still treat as Integrity so quarantine proceeds. Legacy transcription-model migration errors now log and do not block startup.\n- Startup overlay gating: name and remove the early capture-phase handler (`window.__mausVoiceEarlyError`). After React mounts, ignore runtime `error` events and `unhandledrejection`s and log them instead. Treat only failed `<script>` and stylesheet `<link>` loads as fatal (case-insensitive rel matching); ignore icon/other links and image/media load failures, and skip logging empty image-load errors.\n\n<sup>Written for commit 1ea428e09f33bdc956d8885c06596ecfb974c9cf. Summary will update on new commits.</sup>\n\n<a href=\"https://cubic.dev/pr/maus-inc/mausVoice/pull/128?utm_source=github\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" data-no-image-dialog=\"true\"><picture><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\" srcset=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-dark.svg\"><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\" srcset=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-light.svg\"><img alt=\"Review in cubic\" src=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-dark.svg\"></picture></a>\n\n<!-- End of auto-generated description by cubic. -->\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai -->\n## Summary by CodeRabbit\n\n- **Bug Fixes**\n  - Prevented startup error overlays from covering the app after the interface has loaded.\n  - Improved handling of startup asset failures while ignoring non-critical image and icon errors.\n  - Added recovery for corrupted or incomplete local databases, including automatic migration retries.\n  - Allowed app startup to continue when legacy migration encounters an error.\n\n- **Tests**\n  - Added coverage for startup errors, runtime failures, error overlays, database integrity issues, migration failures, and recovery behavior.\n<!-- end of auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai -->"
