uthoritative review entry point and external-reference model.\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated description by cubic. -->\n---\n## Summary by cubic\nMake Part I the only normative review process and replace embedded external skills with a pinned references table to eliminate conflicting guidance. Align local Rust checks with CI and add a fast path for low‑risk docs-only changes.\n\n- Old vs new:\n  - Part IV: embedded appendices → now a non‑normative references table with pinned source URLs; on conflict, Part I and `AGENTS.md` take precedence.\n  - Rust checks: relied on a comment about CI’s `TAURI_CONFIG` → commands now set `TAURI_CONFIG` inline to reproduce CI exactly.\n  - Process: no docs-only shortcut → new Section 12.1 fast path with explicit exclusions.\n\n**Review and rollout**\n- Validate the Part IV table entries and that external skills are used only as evidence, not as process; map imported severities to the protocol’s Critical–Nitpick scale.\n- Required: when running local Rust verification, use the documented commands with `TAURI_CONFIG='{\"bundle\":{\"externalBin\":[]}}'`.\n- Required: use the Section 12.1 fast path only when every changed file is truly docs-only and Low risk; otherwise run the full procedure.\n- Treat `FULL-REVIEW.md` Part I as authoritative; `REVIEW.md` now states this entry point and precedence explicitly.\n- Formatting: `prettier@3` applied; no behavioral impact.\n\n<sup>Written for commit 495c148200e5bf396271bd8434c284535edc934f. Summary will update on new commits.</sup>\n\n<a href=\"https://cubic.dev/pr/maus-inc/mausVoice/pull/130?utm_source=github\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" data-no-image-dialog=\"true\"><picture><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\" srcset=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-dark.svg\"><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\" srcset=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-light.svg\"><img alt=\"Review in cubic\" src=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-