ce the duplicated review handbook with an authoritative end-to-end review protocol and loader, while directing agents to use it for all reviews.\n\nNew Features:\n- Add a four-part end-to-end review protocol covering evidence tracking, risk-based review phases, boundary tracing, security, test validity, desktop scenarios, verification, and finding validation.\n- Include the project-specific risk catalog and verbatim imported review skills for CodeRabbit, standards/spec review, iterative review loops, and multi-axis quality review.\n- Add operational guidance for PR review metadata and a backlog for automated review-inventory collection.\n\nBug Fixes:\n- Replace the accidentally duplicated review handbook with a single authoritative protocol.\n\nEnhancements:\n- Make REVIEW.md a stable loader for the expanded protocol in FULL-REVIEW.md and direct agents to load it before reviews.\n- Clarify repository-confirmed verification commands, status reporting, generated-binding checks, and upstream resolution of imported skill references.\n\nDocumentation:\n- Expand the review documentation with explicit procedures, project risks, review report formats, completion rules, and verification requirements.\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated description by cubic. -->\n---\n## Summary by cubic\nConsolidates the duplicated review handbook into a single end-to-end protocol and keeps `REVIEW.md` as a stable loader to `FULL-REVIEW.md`, so existing “Load REVIEW.md” gates keep working.\n\n- Defines a four-part protocol: review procedure (evidence ledger E0–E5, change inventory, boundary traces, contracts, security records, verification matrix), project risk catalog, operational changes, and verbatim imported skills from `coderabbitai/skills`, `mattpocock/skills`, `2dmurali/review-loop-skill`, and `addyosmani/agent-skills`.\n- Verification matrix limits commands to those confirmed by `package.json` and `.github/workflows/*`; replaces mutating `pnpm format` with `pnpm exec prettier --check` 