+      "description": "## What this is\n\nAn end-to-end implementation pass answering **four independent assertive reviews** of the superfix state (`fix/superfix-review-findings` @ `3560b01` = PR #63 head): one PR-#109-vs-current comparison and three full-diff reviews of PR #63, all run in an assertive CodeRabbit-style profile against this repo's REVIEW.md handbook.\n\nEvery finding was verified against the code before being touched (no blind implementation). Findings were implemented where real, left alone where already correct, and pushed back with evidence where wrong. Full accounting:\n\n- **Research + verdict audit:** `docs/pr63-pr109-review-findings-audit.md`\n- **Two-axis self-review (Standards + Spec):** `docs/pr63-pr109-followup-review.md`\n\n## Headline fixes\n\n**Critical / blocking behavior**\n- `release.yml` Windows-matrix \"Build Tauri app\" step ran POSIX `if [ ... ]` on the default `pwsh`. Every Windows release build would fail at this step. *Delivered via the handoff patch in the comments — the agent bot token can't push `.github/workflows` edits; see the pinned handoff comment below.*\n- `humanizeScrub` no longer flattens newlines or rewrites words inside fenced/inline code; persisted assistant output keeps its Markdown/JSON structure.\n- Gemini: tool responses now pair by **function name** (was sending synthetic `gemini-tc-N` ids), permanent 4xx are no longer retried 3× with a rebuilt base64 audio upload, empty/non-SSE 200 stream responses fail loudly instead of faking success, the SSE reader is cancelled/released in `finally`, and abort signals/deadlines thread through.\n- Dictation backlog: one rejection-safe serial queue; finalize drains **inside** the queue (poll can no longer double-deliver); failed combined drains re-backlog the new segment; `cleanup()` advances the session nonce.\n\n**Major**\n- Real-time output and \"Review before insert\" are mutually exclusive at the action layer (the UI copy says so, and the switch happens in one persisted write).\n- Context menus portal to `document.body` (Framer Motion's transformed route wrapper no longer re-anchors/clips them), Escape is consumed in capture phase so a host dialog doesn't also close, and focus actually moves into the menu.\n- Right-click \"Delete\" on a style now goes through the shared `ConfirmDialog`; a rejected delete no longer silently unhandled-rejects.\n- Style switches restore the previous selection when persistence fails (the store snapshot was taken *after* the in-memory write, so rollback restored the new value).\n- Windows elevation preflight is bounded (15s prefs read / 5min relaunch watchdog), late relaunch results are ignored, and prefs seeding routes through `setUserPreferences` so derived settings apply — no more infinite loading screen.\n- Rust private/saved-endpoint HTTP: every request *and every redirect hop* is validated, DNS-resolved, policy-checked against the **resolved addresses**, and dialed pinned to them (string-only checks couldn't stop DNS rebinding). Plaintext policies bypass system proxies; link-local/unspecified resolutions are rejected for every policy.\n- `secret-scan.yml` can now actually scan PRs (`pull_request` trigger) — in the handoff patch.\n\n**Minor / nitpick** (still shipped)\n- whisper.cpp ggml model blobs: pinned to immutable Hugging Face revision `5359861c7…` + per-blob LFS SHA-256 (the exact checksums whisper.cpp's own download script enforces). Env-var URL overrides stay dev-only and intentionally skip the pin.\n- Composer-text reaper thread: condvar wake + join on `Drop`.\n- `unexpected_cfgs` back to `warn`; `rfd` minimal features on all three OSes.\n- Model pickers: single-flight polling, stale-response drops on unmount/config change, `/v1` path handling pinned by tests.\n- Bare `void` preference calls → shared `logOnRejection` wrapper.\n- Deterministic i18n sort; **all 86 new user-facing strings translated** into the 9 locales, plus a completeness contract test that fails when a multi-word message is English in every catalog.\n- Docs: OpenAI default model corrected to `whisper-1`; local `tauri build` without updater artifacts warns loudly; review-flagged formatting drift normalized.\n\n**Refuted with evidence** (no change; reasoning in the audit doc): the retranscription stuck-row scenario (duplicate-submit guard makes it unreachable), Gladia forced-ready handoff (SDK buffers per contract + warning recorded), ContextMenu `autoFocus` claim (retained and pinned by a new focus regression test), resampler 320,001 Hz comment (correct as written), and one review's suggested rfd features (`[\"macos\"]`/`[\"windows\"]` don't exist in rfd 0.15.4).\n\n**Deferred, documented:** binary IPC framing for private-HTTP bodies (needs regenerated Specta bindings), `.ghtoken` history rotation (out-of-band credential action).\n\n## Verification\n\n- 818/818 desktop unit+script tests, 59/59 voice-ai tests, 48/48 `node --test` script contracts (incl. new release-shell contract guard)\n- `tsc --noEmit`, oxlint (0 warnings across 474 files), Prettier clean on touched files, `git diff --check` clean\n- i18n extract+sync converges to a no-op; docs site builds (100 pages)\n- Rust changes are additive/mirror existing idioms with new `#[test]` coverage; the cargo matrix still owes a run (no toolchain in the authoring sandbox) — please let CI confirm `cargo build/test/clippy`.\n\n> **Note:** this PR intentionally excludes `.github/workflows/*` edits. They are delivered as an apply-ready patch in the handoff comment below (the Arena bot token lacks the `workflows` scope).\n\n## Summary by Sourcery\n\nHarden networking, AI transport, dictation, settings, UI behavior, release automation, and supply-chain verification across the desktop application.\n\nNew Features:\n- Add comprehensive safeguards for private and saved-endpoint HTTP requests, including redirect validation, DNS policy enforcement, and pinned connections.\n- Harden Gemini transport behavior with correct tool-result pairing, bounded retries, cancellation, deadlines, and strict stream validation.\n- Make dictation backlog delivery serialized and resilient across failures, polling races, and session cleanup.\n- Enforce mutual exclusivity between real-time output and review-before-insert preferences.\n- Improve context-menu positioning, keyboard handling, focus management, and destructive-action confirmation.\n\nBug Fixes:\n- Prevent Markdown and structured assistant output from being altered by humanization cleanup.\n- Bound Windows elevation startup operations and restore persisted derived settings correctly.\n- Restore writing-style selections when persistence fails.\n- Prevent model-picker polling races and stale responses.\n- Pin whisper.cpp model downloads and verify their integrity.\n\nEnhancements:\n- Improve localization consistency and add translation completeness checks.\n- Ensure fire-and-forget settings actions log rejected promises safely.\n- Clean up background reaper lifecycle and tighten Rust configuration defaults.\n- Regenerate native API bindings for updated command and type definitions.\n\nBuild:\n- Add release workflow shell contracts and warn when local builds cannot self-update.\n- Reduce unnecessary platform-specific Rust dependency features.\n\nCI:\n- Enable pull-request secret scanning and restore least-privilege permissions for desktop linting.\n- Run release workflow shell contract checks in documentation CI.\n\nDocumentation:\n- Document the review audit, Rust toolchain requirements, and updated model/release behavior.\n- Correct the documented OpenAI transcription model and normalize documentation formatting.\n\nTests:\n- Add regression coverage for HTTP redirect and DNS policy enforcement, Gemini transport, dictation lifecycle, UI interactions, preference normalization, model pickers, localization, model pinning, and promise rejection handling.\n\nChores:\n- Add repository attributes and apply formatting and generated-binding updates.\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated description by cubic. -->\n---\n## Summary by cubic\nHardens release/CI, desktop network egress, Gemini transport, dictation, and settings to close four assertive review rounds. Private/saved endpoints now return complete bodies (no SSE/token streaming), Gemini uses a single per‑operation deadline and stricter retry/validation, and real‑time output and review‑before‑insert are exclusive.\n\n- Network/private+saved HTTP: validate, DNS‑resolve, policy‑check, and pin every redirect hop; reject link‑local/unspecified results; latch credential stripping after any cross‑origin hop; refuse saved‑endpoint cross‑origin redirects up‑front; plaintext policies bypass proxies; saved HTTPS through a system proxy resolves at CONNECT but stays TLS‑hostname bound; `secureFetch` rejects relative URLs with a contextual error.\n- Gemini: pair tool results by function name; absolute per‑operation deadline with one AbortSignal reused across retries; no retries on 4xx (except 429) or AbortError/TimeoutError; treat empty/non‑SSE 200 streams as errors; expose `GeminiHttpError`; validate model IDs and block dot‑segments; propagate AbortSignal from repos.\n- Dictation: rejection‑safe serialized paste queue; finalize drains inside the queue; failed drains re‑backlog; cleanup advances the nonce.\n- UX/Settings: context menus portal to body with focus/Escape capture; “Delete style” confirms and rolls back on failure; style selection rolls back on persistence failure; Windows elevation preflight/relaunch are watchdog‑bounded; enforce and load‑time‑normalize real‑time vs review exclusivity; copy explains that review pauses streaming.\n- Supply chain/i18n: pin `whisper.cpp` ggml blobs to an immutable Hugging Face revision with per‑blob SHA‑256; deterministic i18n sync; localization completeness contract test.\n- Repos/Model pickers: OpenAI‑compatible repos expect a `/v1` base and append `/models` internally; picker probes single‑flight every 3s only while unavailable and stops when healt