ems\n- `REVIEW.md`: prose cleanup, no technical changes\n- `docs/RELEASE.md`, `docs/HANDOFF.md`, `docs/desktop-architecture.md`: updated and trimmed\n\n## Verification\n\nZero em dashes, zero curly quotes, zero AI vocabulary, zero filler words remain in any `.md` file across the entire repository. All 17 provider test mechanisms, all batch parameters, CSP coverage, model defaults, and recommendation tiers verified against source.\n\n## Summary by Sourcery\n\nOverhaul repository documentation to remove obsolete material, align maintained references with the current implementation, and improve consistency across Markdown content.\n\nNew Features:\n- Add Docker/Ollama setup guidance and document all nine current built-in writing styles in the Astro documentation site.\n\nBug Fixes:\n- Correct documentation errors about supported versions, providers, transcription behavior, model recommendations, settings, CI limits, release scope, and package APIs to match the current source code.\n\nEnhancements:\n- Consolidate maintained documentation under the Astro docs site and refresh repository architecture, development, configuration, provider, and usage references.\n- Remove obsolete handoff prompts, release plans, review artifacts, pointer stubs, and other superseded documentation.\n- Apply consistent prose and formatting cleanup across repository Markdown files, including removal of em dashes, curly quotes, filler, and stale AI-oriented wording.\n\nDocumentation:\n- Update contributor and user-facing reference documentation with current packages, providers, preferences, tools, feature gates, models, workflows, and release procedures.\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated description by cubic. -->\n---\n## Summary by cubic\nOverhauls repository docs to match current code and consolidate them on the Astro site. Removes stale files, adds missing topics, and corrects factual drift so contributors and users don’t follow outdated guidance; also applies review-driven fixes from the lat