+      "description": "## Summary\n\nThis PR completes the UI/Behavioral Issues Plan for mausVoice, implementing the remaining Wave 4 agents and stacking all changes on top of the `fix/superfix-review-findings` branch as the base.\n\n## What this PR contains\n\n### All previously merged agent PRs (Waves 1-3)\n- A01: Home double scrollbar fix\n- A02: ScrollListPage collapse glitch/leak fix\n- A03: UAC elevation helper + real quit command\n- A05: Dark mode selected outline visibility\n- A06: Dev surfaces gated to pre-release/CI\n- A07: Slider thumb hover stability\n- A08: Dictation backlog model (no clipboard spam)\n- A09: Mid-dictation style switch applies correctly\n- A10: Retranscribe loading/completion feedback\n- A13: Drop shadow behind silver long-press element\n- A14: Light-mode button inner shadow correction\n- A15: Style selectors gated on post-processing enablement\n- A16: Mirror inner/drop shadow design into light mode\n- A17: Embedded Satoshi + Drag To Move animation\n- A18: Tray dashboard visibility toggle\n- A20: Register App documentation\n- A22: Pill top style selector actually applies style\n- A24: AssemblyAI model selection\n\n### Wave 4 agents (NEW in this PR)\n- **A04** — Assistant pill popout raw markdown: `assistant-pill-text.utils.ts` strips markdown constructs (bold, headings, code blocks, links, lists, images) to plain text before sending to native pill\n- **A11** — Custom native-feeling right-click context menu: `ContextMenu.tsx` with keyboard navigation, dark/light theming, clipboard items for text inputs\n- **A19** — Em-dash sweep + humanize skill: `humanize.txt` prompt artifact + `humanize.utils.ts` post-hoc scrubber for AI slop markers\n- **A21** — Hotkey spam filtering: `hotkey-filter.utils.ts` debounces identical triggers while recording, release-before-refire, always-allows stop/cancel\n\n### Review findings addressed\n- Fixed REF_LINK_RE running after code block insertion (was stripping `[code]` markers)\n- Fixed MULTILINE regex flags (added `g` to block-level regexes)\n- Fixed logger.debug -> logger.verbose (TS API compat)\n- Fixed ContextMenu MUI v7 slotProps API\n\n## Verification\n- TypeScript check-types: PASS\n- Tests: 71/71 suites pass (701/755 tests; 54 failures are API-key dependent integration tests)\n- 27 new unit tests for Wave 4 implementations\n\n## Remaining (out of scope)\n- A12 (stability audit) — requires runtime memory profiling\n- A23 (thock haptics) — requires Rust pill crate changes + audio assets\n\n## Summary by Sourcery\n\nComplete the remaining desktop UI and behavioral fixes while hardening startup, dictation, pill rendering, provider configuration, and release surfaces.\n\nNew Features:\n- Add a native-feeling, keyboard-accessible context menu with clipboard actions and contextual actions across key desktop surfaces.\n- Add AssemblyAI batch transcription model selection with validation, fallback handling, and legacy model migration.\n- Add dictation backlog delivery, hotkey spam filtering, mid-dictation style switching, assistant-pill markdown cleanup, and humanized AI output processing.\n- Add startup elevation gating with a real process-quit action and synchronized dashboard tray visibility labels.\n- Add cross-platform pill label animation, embedded-font handling, long-press ring shadows, and interaction thock feedback.\n\nBug Fixes:\n- Prevent scroll-list header collapse oscillation and observer or animation-resource leaks.\n- Fix slider thumb centering during hover and drag states, selected outlines in dark mode, retranscription feedback, and dashboard nested scrolling.\n- Correct AssemblyAI request handling and preserve transcription behavior for supported and legacy model selections.\n\nEnhancements:\n- Centralize cross-platform pill rendering calculations and shadow behavior in shared Rust utilities.\n- Unify writing-style switching across pill, hotkey, arrow, and in-dictation paths.\n- Improve dictation output routing so text is retained until an editable target is available instead of repeatedly copying to the clipboard.\n\nBuild:\n- Gate Tauri DevTools behind the debug-assist feature so stable releases omit inspection support at compile time.\n- Update desktop development, CI, and prerelease build commands to opt into the debug-assist feature where appropriate.\n\nCI:\n- Add path-based workflow triggers, per-run concurrency, and debug-assist support for desktop CI artifacts.\n- Increase the Rust transcription workflow timeout to accommodate slow model downloads.\n\nDeployment:\n- Ensure stable release builds exclude DevTools while prerelease builds retain the QA inspection surface.\n\nDocumentation:\n- Add Register App user documentation and expand the UI and behavioral issue planning and handoff documentation.\n- Update AssemblyAI provider documentation to describe batch transcription model selection and fallback behavior.\n\nTests:\n- Add comprehensive unit and component coverage for context menus, scroll collapse behavior, retranscription state, style switching, humanization, AssemblyAI models, elevation gating, selected outlines, slider transforms, and pill rendering utilities.\n\nChores:\n- Normalize sorting behavior and harden resource cleanup, font registration, tray synchronization, and native event parsing across desktop and pill components.\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated description by cubic. -->\n---\n## Summary by cubic\nCompletes Wave 4 (A04, A11, A19, A21) and hardens startup, input, and build pipelines. Behavior changes: right‑click shows a native‑feeling menu with working clipboard on inputs; assistant output is humanized and pill text is plain; style‑switch hotkeys no longer wedge; Windows startup runs a UAC preflight that can quit or continue unelevated.\n\n- Context menu (A11): handles native mouse events, restores focus/selection to the right‑clicked editable, yields to the clipboard menu for inputs, supports keyboard nav and theming; wired into chats, conversations, transcriptions, dictionary, and styles.\n- Assistant output (A19, A04): loads a shared HUMANIZE skill and scrubs finalized text; strips markdown before syncing assistant messages to the native pill with streaming‑safe link/image/italics handling.\n- Style switching (A21, A09): debounces while recording and clears “held” per physical key; mid‑dictation style selection applies to the utterance’s final output; style controls hide when post‑processing is disabled.\n- Elevation: Windows UAC preflight blocks heavy init until resolved; “Launch normally” releases the gate; “Close mausVoice” actually quits via a new native command.\n- Haptics (A23): adds thock audio, honors the interaction‑chime preference, and rate‑limits; on Windows, WebView keepalive clears only after the window is visible.\n- UI polish: ScrollList header collapse no longer spasms or leaks observers; slider thumb stays centered on hover/drag; selected outlines remain visible in dark mode; retranscribe shows loading and completion toasts; TitleBar resize listener no longer leaks.\n- AssemblyAI: adds a model picker with Universal‑3.5 Pro + Universal‑2 fallback; plumbs through repos and tests; provider form and docs updated.\n- Build/CI: gates DevTools behind the `debug-assist` feature (enabled only for CI/prerelease); workflows use path filters and per‑PR concurrency; grant `actions: write` for caches/artifacts; raise Ubuntu Rust‑transcription timeout to 45 minutes; CSP contract allows `api-docs.deepseek.com`. Tests aligned to the AssemblyAI speech_models behavior.\n\n**Rollout/Migration**\n- CI/prerelease builds must pass `--features debug-assist`; stable releases must omit it.\n- Optional: set an AssemblyAI transcription model; legacy tiers transparently migrate to supported successors.\n- No manual data migrations.\n\n<sup>Written for commit 419cb45bbc60bc18b864de17c04c03757296a409. Summary will update on new commits.</sup>\n\n<a href=\"https://cubic.dev/pr/maus-inc/mausVoice/pull/105?utm_source=github\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" data-no-image-dialog=\"true\"><picture><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\" srcset=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-dark.svg\"><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\" srcset=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-light.svg\"><img alt=\"Review in cubic\" src=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-dark.svg\"></picture></a>\n\n<!-- End of auto-generated description by cubic. -->\n\n"
