+      "description": "## Summary\n\nStacked on `arena/01a01a61-mausvoice` (PR #105). This PR fixes the findings from a CodeRabbit-assertive audit of PR #105's Wave-4 deliverables, and completes the remaining unfinished items that a smaller follow-up model flagged as still open.\n\n## Fixes\n\n### Critical\n- **A11 — right-click crash:** the context-menu provider passed a *native* `contextmenu` `MouseEvent` into `handleContextMenu`, which dereferenced the React-only `e.nativeEvent` (undefined) — an uncaught `TypeError` on every right-click of a text input, after the default menu was already suppressed. The hook now accepts the native event throughout.\n- **A11 — clipboard menu couldn't work on inputs:** it read selection via `window.getSelection()` (always empty for `<input>`/`<textarea>`) and ran `document.execCommand` while the auto-focused *menu* held focus. Added `resolveEditableTarget`/`focusEditable` (selectionStart/End + Range snapshot, focus/selection restore before the command).\n\n### Major\n- **A19 — humanize skill was dead:** `humanize.txt` was referenced nowhere. Added a shared `HUMANIZE_SKILL_TEXT` artifact and wired it into the agent system prompt and every post-processing prompt.\n- **A21 — release-before-refire wedge:** style-switch \"held\" state only cleared on all-keys-up, which never fires during hold-to-talk dictation. Release is now keyed to the specific physical key (`getStyleSwitchActionNamesForKey`).\n- **A19 — em-dash sweep (final copy pass):** zero em-dashes remain in user-facing copy and all 10 locale catalogs (4 strings + 9 locales fixed with locale-correct punctuation).\n\n### Minor / nitpick\n- A11: i18n'd the clipboard labels (Cut/Copy/Paste/Select All) with real translations for all 9 non-English locales; focus restore only on Escape/item activation; removed the `stateRef` write-during-render; `navigator.userAgentData` over deprecated `navigator.platform`.\n- A04: removed dead/broken `isStreamingStable`; corrected the streaming-contract comment.\n- A19: case-insensitive \"utilize\" inflections; dropped the misleading en-dash \"removal\".\n\n## Tests\n- `ContextMenu.test.ts` (native-event regression, non-input passthrough, Escape close, item click, input-selection Copy enablement)\n- `keyboard.utils.test.ts` (`getStyleSwitchActionNamesForKey`)\n- extended `assistant-pill-text` / `humanize` / `prompt.utils` tests\n\n## Verification\n- `pnpm --filter desktop check-types` — PASS\n- `pnpm --filter desktop lint` — PASS (0 warnings / 0 errors)\n- `pnpm --filter desktop i18n` — no drift\n- `pnpm --filter desktop test:unit` — 73 files / 726 tests PASS\n\n## Remaining (documented in `docs/handoff/remaining-work.md` + `docs/wave-status.md`)\n- **A23** thock rate-limiter unit test (needs `cargo`; spec provided)\n- **A12** stability/memory audit report (needs a running prerelease build; protocol provided)\n- **A11** full surface wiring (transcriptions/dictionary/styles/chats; per-surface spec provided)\n- **CI workflow timeout 20→45 min** (`docs/handoff/workflow-timeout.patch` — blocked on `workflows` scope)\n\nThese are intentionally shipped as deterministic handoff docs so a device with the right permissions can execute them without re-deriving context.\n\n## Summary by Sourcery\n\nComplete the remaining Wave 4 audit fixes by hardening context menus, prompt humanization, hotkey release behavior, streaming guidance, and verification coverage.\n\nNew Features:\n- Add localized native context menus for editable controls and contextual actions across chats, transcripts, dictionary rows, and styles.\n- Load a shared humanization skill into agent and post-processing prompts. \n\nBug Fixes:\n- Prevent right-click crashes and restore clipboard operations on input and contenteditable selections.\n- Release style-switch hotkeys when their physical key is released during hold-to-talk dictation.\n- Fix asynchronous TitleBar resize-listener cleanup and remove incorrect streaming-stability logic.\n\nEnhancements:\n- Improve context-menu focus restoration, scrolling, empty-menu behavior, clipboard error handling, platform detection, and humanization coverage.\n- Clarify assistant-pill streaming behavior and add robust hotkey and clipboard handling.\n\nCI:\n- Increase the Rust transcription workflow timeout from 20 to 45 minutes.\n\nDocumentation:\n- Add handoff and wave-status documentation for remaining audits, verification, and environment setup.\n\nTests:\n- Add regression and component coverage for context menus, editable selections, surface actions, style-switch release behavior, humanization prompts, streaming output, and thock rate limiting.\n\nChores:\n- Update localized user-facing copy to remove em dashes and add translated clipboard labels.\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated description by cubic. -->\n---\n## Summary by cubic\nFixes Wave‑4 audit gaps and completes native context menus across chats, transcripts, dictionary, and styles. Old behavior: right‑clicking inputs crashed, editable targets were hijacked, long menus closed on scroll, and empty menus suppressed the OS menu; new behavior: stable, localized menus that respect editables, scroll internally, and only suppress the OS menu when items exist. Also fixes style‑switch release during hold‑to‑talk, loads the humanize skill into prompts, clarifies assistant‑pill streaming, tightens tests, and raises the CI timeout.\n\n- Context menus (A11): accept native `contextmenu` events; yield right‑clicks on inputs/`contenteditable` to the clipboard menu via `isEditableTarget`; capture/restore selection for Cut/Copy/Paste/Select All; suppress the OS menu only when items exist; allow internal scrolling without dismissing; restore focus to the right‑clicked element; remove the dead surface‑registration API; localize labels; guard clipboard read/write failures; wire `useContextMenu` into `ChatMessageBubble`, `ConversationListItem`, `DictionaryRow`, `ManualStylingRow`, and `TranscriptRow`.\n\n- Other fixes:\n  - A19 humanize: add `HUMANIZE_SKILL_TEXT`; load it into agent and post‑processing prompts; keep case‑insensitive “utilize” variants; reconcile `scripts/prompts/humanize.txt`.\n  - A21 style switching: release held state on the specific physical key via `getStyleSwitchActionNamesForKey`; share prefixes via `STYLE_SWITCH_ACTION_PREFIXES`.\n  - A04 assistant pill: remove dead `isStreamingStable`; document re‑converting accumulated text per sync.\n  - A12: fix `TitleBar` `onResized` listener leak with a cancellation guard.\n  - A23: extract pure `should_throttle_at` and add Rust unit tests.\n  - Copy/i18n: add real Cut/Copy/Paste/Select All translations; prefer `navigator.userAgentData`.\n  - CI/docs: raise Ubuntu Rust‑transcription timeout to 45 minutes; add handoff docs and Rust toolchain setup.\n\n<sup>Written for commit 05d5decf8bd6855b95fe110013faba9d40d6e20b. Summary will update on new commits.</sup>\n\n<a href=\"https://cubic.dev/pr/maus-inc/mausVoice/pull/118?utm_source=github\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" data-no-image-dialog=\"true\"><picture><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\" srcset=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-dark.svg\"><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\" srcset=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-light.svg\"><img alt=\"Review in cubic\" src=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-dark.svg\"></picture></a>\n\n<!-- End of auto-generated description by cubic. -->\n\n"
