+      "description": "## Summary\n\n- route provider API requests through Tauri's native HTTP transport so desktop credentials and transcription requests are not blocked by browser CORS\n- add live model discovery and preserve provider-returned model IDs across Cerebras, DeepSeek, Claude, Gemini, OpenAI-compatible providers, and related catalogs\n- refresh stale provider fallbacks/defaults and current transcription request shapes for xAI, ElevenLabs, AssemblyAI, OpenAI, OpenRouter, and Groq\n- add an accessible help tooltip explaining the OpenAI-compatible **Include /v1 path** setting\n- replace fixed-model credential probes where possible and update provider documentation\n\n## Validation\n\n- `corepack pnpm --filter desktop test:unit` — 53 files, 550 tests passed\n- `corepack pnpm --filter desktop check-types`\n- `corepack pnpm --filter @maus-inc/voice-ai build`\n- `corepack pnpm --filter @maus-inc/voice-ai test` — 4 files, 10 tests passed\n- `corepack pnpm --filter docs check-types`\n- `corepack pnpm --filter docs build`\n- desktop Oxlint, targeted Prettier, and `git diff --check`\n\n## Notes\n\n- production Deepgram, AssemblyAI, ElevenLabs, and xAI requests continue to default to native `secureFetch`; focused tests use explicit transport injection where necessary\n- the docs build completes with the repository's existing unresolved absolute-asset warnings\n\n## Summary by Sourcery\n\nRoute provider connectivity through secure native transport and refresh model discovery and provider contracts across desktop AI features.\n\nNew Features:\n- Add native desktop HTTP routing for hosted providers and authorized OpenAI-compatible endpoints.\n- Enable live model discovery while retaining provider-returned model IDs across supported catalogs.\n- Add shared OpenAI-compatible URL resolution and an accessible Include /v1 help tooltip.\n\nBug Fixes:\n- Prevent browser CORS and stale fixed-model connectivity checks from blocking provider credentials and requests.\n- Align Gemini, xAI, ElevenLabs, AssemblyAI, OpenAI, and related transcription requests with current provider contracts.\n- Constrain OpenAI-compatible redirects and endpoints to the saved origin and path while restricting plaintext HTTP to private networks.\n\nEnhancements:\n- Refresh provider fallback models and use model-list authentication checks instead of fixed inference requests where supported.\n- Require saved API-key records for OpenAI-compatible runtime requests and unify discovery, testing, and runtime URL handling.\n\nBuild:\n- Remove the Google GenAI SDK dependency after migrating Gemini to the native HTTP API.\n\nCI:\n- Update desktop, package, and documentation workflow triggers and synchronize desktop CI transport behavior.\n\nDocumentation:\n- Update provider documentation for native transport, live discovery, current model defaults, transcription contracts, and OpenAI-compatible endpoint requirements.\n\nTests:\n- Expand unit coverage for native provider transport, model discovery, URL construction, endpoint security, Gemini streaming, and updated transcription contracts.\n\nChores:\n- Refresh locale and lockfile outputs alongside the provider and transport updates.\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated description by cubic. -->\n---\n## Summary by cubic\nRoutes provider and OpenAI‑compatible requests through native HTTP with cancel and scoped redirects, and unifies tests/pickers/runtime on live model discovery and shared Include “/v1” URL resolution. Fixes Gemini transport by moving to native HTTP (no SDK) and aligning request contracts.\n\n- Add an authorized `openai_compatible_http_request` and `createOpenAICompatibleFetch(apiKeyId)` for saved HTTPS OpenAI‑compatible endpoints; keep plaintext HTTP confined to private/local hosts, block public IP literals, scope redirects to the saved origin/path, and propagate aborts to the native future.\n- Use `buildOpenAICompatibleUrl`/`appendOpenAICompatiblePath` to preserve reverse‑proxy prefixes and the Include “/v1” setting; pickers/tests now pass `apiKeyId` and `includeV1Path` and share runtime resolution.\n- Switch Gemini to native HTTP with injected transport; filter discovery to generation‑capable models. Accept discovered IDs across Groq, Anthropic, Gemini, Cerebras, DeepSeek, OpenAI, xAI, OpenRouter, and generic OpenAI‑compatible; refresh fallbacks (Gemini 3.x flash, Claude `claude-sonnet-5`, Cerebras `gpt-oss-120b`/`gemma-4-31b`, DeepSeek `deepseek-v4-flash`/`deepseek-v4-pro`), and change the OpenRouter default to `openai/gpt-oss-20b`.\n- Update transcription: AssemblyAI sets `speech_model: \"best\"`, xAI uses model‑less STT, ElevenLabs token and batch requests use the secure transport, and OpenAI’s default/fallback is `whisper-1`.\n- Add an Include “/v1” help tooltip; expand tests for routing, URL construction, catalogs, and provider contracts; run desktop/package/docs tests on pushes to `main` and fix desktop CI transport/locale sync.\n\n**Required migration**\n- Remove credentials from any saved OpenAI‑compatible Base URL; store keys in the API key record.\n- Set the Include “/v1” switch to match your server; Test, pickers, and runtime now share this resolution.\n- Ensure an API key record exists for OpenAI‑compatible tasks; repos now throw when missing.\n- Use HTTPS for public OpenAI‑compatible hosts; plaintext HTTP works only for local/private networks.\n\n<sup>Written for commit a63608cab666559098aaeaf2320d64300f3241e9. Summary will update on new commits.</sup>\n\n<a href=\"https://cubic.dev/pr/maus-inc/mausVoice/pull/109?utm_source=github\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" data-no-image-dialog=\"true\"><picture><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\" srcset=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-dark.svg\"><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\" srcset=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-light.svg\"><img alt=\"Review in cubic\" src=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-dark.svg\"></picture></a>\n\n<!-- End