+      "description": "## Summary\n\nImplements the full PR #118 change set and resolves the follow-up CodeRabbit-style review findings.\n\n- Prevents contextual destructive actions from bypassing managed/system style and global dictionary-term restrictions.\n- Routes dictionary input right-clicks to clipboard actions rather than the row Delete menu.\n- Handles nested `contenteditable=\"false\"` boundaries correctly.\n- Makes thock limiter tests safe under Cargo's parallel test runner by serializing and restoring process-global state.\n- Synchronizes the standalone humanize prompt artifact with `HUMANIZE_SKILL_TEXT`, with a regression test.\n\n## Verification\n\n- `corepack pnpm --filter desktop... build`\n- `corepack pnpm --filter desktop lint`\n- `corepack pnpm --filter desktop test:unit` — 77 files / 743 tests passing\n- `git diff --check`\n\nRust tests were not run locally because this sandbox does not provide `cargo`.\n\n## Summary by Sourcery\n\nHarden contextual menus, style hotkeys, and post-processing prompts against permission bypasses, right-click handling issues, and inconsistent humanization guidance.\n\nNew Features:\n- Improve contextual menus with clipboard actions for editable fields and prompt, deselection, and permission-aware style actions.\n\nBug Fixes:\n- Prevent destructive contextual actions from bypassing managed or system-item restrictions.\n- Respect nested contenteditable=false boundaries and preserve hotkey debounce behavior after key release.\n- Apply shared humanization guidance consistently to post-processing prompts.\n- Keep the standalone humanization prompt artifact synchronized with its source text.\n\nEnhancements:\n- Clarify streaming pill conversion requirements for accumulated messages.\n\nTests:\n- Add regression coverage for protected contextual menu actions, editable-field clipboard handling, hotkey debounce and custom style actions, prompt guidance inclusion, and prompt artifact synchronization.\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated description by cubic. -->\n---\n## Summary by cubic\nHarden context menus and hotkey release handling to prevent permission bypass and debounce leaks, and apply shared humanization to all post‑processing prompts. Previously we replaced native menus and exposed Delete on managed/system entries and key‑up could bypass the 300 ms debounce; now editable targets get clipboard actions, destructive items follow policy, and releases keep the last fire timestamp.\n\n- Context menus\n  - Respect `contenteditable=\"false\"` boundaries and preserve native menus when a row has no actions.\n  - `DictionaryRow`: hide Delete for organization‑managed terms; route right‑clicks on inputs/contenteditables to clipboard.\n  - `ManualStylingRow`: add “View full prompt”; hide Edit/Delete for managed/system styles; offer “Deselect style” when applicable.\n- Hotkeys, prompts, streaming\n  - Key‑up clears the held state only; debounce remains enforced. Release mappings derive from shared `STYLE_SWITCH_ACTION_PREFIXES` and configured/default combos, so custom style actions are releasable.\n  - Append `HUMANIZE_SKILL_TEXT` to all post‑processing system prompts and add a byte‑for‑byte sync test with `scripts/prompts/humanize.txt`.\n  - Migration: streaming clients must re‑convert the full accumulated message on each update.\n\n<sup>Written for commit f4256c0dc3a79d014196cdd83e6f9c218b307732. Summary will update on new commits.</sup>\n\n<a href=\"https://cubic.dev/pr/maus-inc/mausVoice/pull/120?utm_source=github\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" data-no-image-dialog=\"true\"><picture><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\" srcset=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-dark.svg\"><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\" srcset=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-light.svg\"><img alt=\"Review in cubic\" src=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-dark.svg\"></picture></a>\n\n<!-- End of auto-generated description by cubic. -->\n\n"
