+      "description": "## Summary\n\n- route Gemini generation, streaming, transcription, discovery, and integration tests through the injected desktop-native HTTP transport\n- replace the Gemini SDK-managed transport with direct REST/SSE handling, keep API keys out of URLs, and remove the unused SDK dependency\n- correct xAI STT multipart formatting and keep its model-less/file-last contract covered by tests\n- align provider defaults with their verified fallback catalogs and restore the current DeepSeek V4 IDs\n- add Gemini transport/SSE coverage and the missing HTTPS saved-endpoint domain/IP-literal policy test\n\nThis is stacked on #109 and targets its head branch so the diff contains only the review follow-up.\n\n## Verification\n\n- `pnpm --filter @maus-inc/voice-ai test` — 47 tests passed\n- `pnpm --filter desktop test:unit` — 581 tests passed\n- `pnpm --filter desktop check-types`\n- `pnpm --filter docs check-types`\n- focused desktop model-provider/transcription tests — 30 tests passed\n- Oxlint, Prettier, and `git diff --check`\n\nRust tooling is unavailable in the agent environment, so the added isolated Rust URL-policy test was not run locally and should run in CI.\n\n## Summary by Sourcery\n\nReplace Gemini SDK transport with native REST/SSE requests and align provider request contracts, defaults, and endpoint validation.\n\nNew Features:\n- Route Gemini generation, streaming, transcription, and model discovery through injectable native HTTP transport with direct REST and SSE support.\n\nBug Fixes:\n- Keep Gemini API keys out of request URLs by sending them through request headers.\n- Correct xAI speech-to-text multipart request formatting and model-less file-last behavior.\n- Restore verified DeepSeek V4 model identifiers and align provider defaults with fallback catalogs.\n- Harden saved HTTPS endpoint validation for public and link-local IP literals while allowing domains and private IPs.\n\nEnhancements:\n- Remove the unused Google Gemini SDK dependency in favor of native provider handling.\n\nDocumentation:\n- Document that Gemini operations use the desktop HTTP transport.\n\nTests:\n- Add Gemini native transport, request-header, transcription, streaming SSE, and model discovery coverage.\n- Expand xAI transcription contract coverage and add saved-endpoint URL policy coverage.\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated description by cubic. -->\n---\n## Summary by cubic\nRoute all Gemini operations through the desktop-native HTTP transport and drop the `@google/genai` SDK. Previously Gemini used the webview/SDK transport and put API keys in URLs; now we send keys in headers via native REST and parse SSE ourselves, preventing key leakage and stabilizing streaming.\n\n- Implement direct Gemini REST and native SSE handling in `packages/voice-ai` with `customFetch` injection (defaults to `fetch`); add tests for generate, transcribe, stream, and header-based model listing.\n- Integrate desktop-native transport: pass `tauriFetch` for generation/streaming and `secureFetch` for transcription; update docs to note desktop HTTP transport for Gemini.\n- Correct provider contracts and defaults: use fallback catalogs for defaults (`CLAUDE_MODELS[0]`, `CEREBRAS_MODELS[0]`, `DEEPSEEK_MODELS[0]`, `GEMINI_*_MODELS[0]`); restore DeepSeek V4 IDs; fix xAI STT multipart to append `format: \"true\"` and `language` only when a language is specified, omit `model`, and keep the file field last; tests cover both specified-language and auto-detect cases.\n- Harden saved-endpoint policy with a Rust test: allow HTTPS domains and private IP literals; reject public and link-local IP literals.\n- Remove dependency `@google/genai` and prune lockfile.\n\n<sup>Written for commit 2714145943846d53beb6ab1a3238e965431218df. Summary will update on new commits.</sup>\n\n<a href=\"https://cubic.dev/pr/maus-inc/mausVoice/pull/124?utm_source=github\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" data-no-image-dialog=\"true\"><picture><source media=\"(prefers-col