+      "description": "## Summary\n\nStacked on **PR #118** (`arena/01a01be4-mausvoice`). This is the implementation pass from the assertive CodeRabbit-style review of PR #118's Wave-4 deliverables — every finding, including non-blockers, is fixed and verified.\n\n## Changes\n\n### Context menu (`apps/desktop/src/components/common/ContextMenu.tsx`)\n- **Removed dead surface-registration API** — `registerSurface`, `useSurfaceContextMenu`, and `ContextMenuProviderContext` were exported but never imported, and the provider never dispatched to registered surfaces. Deleted along with the unused `ContextMenuState.open` / `surfaceKey` fields, `disabledReason`, and the `menuRef`.\n- **Scroll-inside-menu bug fixed** — scrolling a long menu (`overflowY: auto`) used to dismiss it. Only an *external* scroll now closes the menu. (+2 regression tests)\n- **Focus restore corrected** — now captures the actual right-clicked element (not just the last-focused one) and refreshes it on every open, so reopening on a different surface restores to the new surface, never the menu.\n- **Clipboard unhandled rejections guarded** — `navigator.clipboard.writeText/readText` now `.catch()`, since they reject on permission denial in some webviews.\n- **Empty-item ordering** — `handleContextMenu` now returns *before* `preventDefault()`, so an empty item list no longer suppresses the platform's native menu. (+regression test)\n- **Editable-yield fix** — wired surfaces containing text fields (e.g. `DictionaryRow`'s term/replacement inputs) were intercepting right-clicks and showing the row menu (Delete) instead of the provider's Cut/Copy/Paste/Select All clipboard menu. Exported `isEditableTarget()` and guarded all five surface handlers. (+`isEditableTarget` unit tests + a provider/surface-yield integration test)\n\n### A23 thock rate-limiter (`apps/desktop/src-tauri/src/system/audio_feedback.rs`)\n- **Flaky parallel-test fix** — the four unit tests shared the process-global `LAST_THOCK_MS` static and each `reset()`'d it, so cargo's parallel test threads could interleave assertions and fail nondeterministically (REVIEW.md \"parallel tests mutating statics\" anti-pattern). Refactored `should_throttle_at` into a **pure** `(now_ms, last_ms) -> (bool, next_last_ms)` with no shared state; the production `should_throttle()` manages the static. ⚠️ `cargo` is unavailable in this sandbox, so the crate was not compiled here — the change is a minimal, hand-traced pure refactor that needs `cargo test` in a Rust-capable environment.\n\n### Humanize prompt artifact (`scripts/prompts/humanize.txt`)\n- Reconciles the false \"must stay in sync\" claim: added the **verbatim** `HUMANIZE_SKILL_TEXT` as the authoritative runtime skill, and marked the longer prose as an expansion that must not contradict it (previously the file claimed it mirrored the code while carrying entirely different instructions).\n\n### Docs\n- `docs/handoff/remaining-work.md` and `docs/wave-status.md` now match the committed state: A23's `should_throttle_at` tests exist (cargo verification only), A11 surfaces A/C/D (transcriptions, styles, chats, dictionary) are wired with composer/home (E/F) explicitly descoped, and the `handleContextMenu` signature / editable-yield guard are documented. A12 remains the sole genuinely-open item (requires a running prerelease build + DevTools, impossible in this sandbox).\n\n## Verification\n- `pnpm --filter desktop check-types` — PASS\n- `pnpm --filter desktop lint` (prettier + oxlint) — PASS, 0 warnings / 0 errors\n- `pnpm --filter desktop i18n` — no drift\n- `pnpm --filter desktop test:unit` — 77 files / **744 tests PASS**\n- Rust (`cargo`) — not runnable in this sandbox; the A23 refactor is ready for CI verification\n\nBranch: `arena/01a01c89-mausvoice` → base `arena/01a01be4-mausvoice` (PR #118 head).\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated description by cubic. -->\n---\n## Summary by cubic\nResolves PR #118 review findings and SonarCloud notes: refactors the context menu for correct native fallthrough, scrolling, and focus, routes editable right‑clicks to the clipboard menu, and makes the A23 thock rate‑limiter testable without races. Updates docs and syncs the humanize prompt with the runtime skill.\n\n- Context menu\n  - Remove dead provider APIs (`registerSurface`, `useSurfaceContextMenu`, `ContextMenuProviderContext`) and unused state; export `isEditableTarget`.\n  - Do not suppress the native menu when no items are provided.\n  - Keep the menu open on internal scroll; close only on external scroll.\n  - Restore focus to the right‑clicked element on close, including reopen on a different surface; minor maintainability cleanup to the focus-restore logic.\n  - Guard `navigator.clipboard.writeText/readText` rejections.\n  - Wire surfaces to yield editable targets to the provider’s clipboard menu: `TranscriptRow`, `DictionaryRow`, `ManualStylingRow`, `ConversationListItem`, `ChatMessageBubble`. Add unit and integration tests.\n\n- A23 thock rate‑limiter (Rust)\n  - Make the decision pure: `should_throttle_at(now_ms, last_ms) -> (bool, next_last_ms)`; keep `should_throttle()` managing the static.\n  - Add four unit tests; requires CI `cargo test` to verify. Docs corrected to reference the two‑argument signature.\n\n- Docs and prompts\n  - `scripts/prompts/humanize.txt`: include a verbatim copy of the runtime `HUMANIZE_SKILL_TEXT` and state that expansions must not contradict it.\n  - Update `docs/handoff/remaining-work.md` and `docs/wave-status.md` to reflect A23 tests and A11 wiring status (A/C/D wired; E/F descoped).\n\n- Tests\n  - Expand `ContextMenu.test.ts` to cover native fallthrough on empty items, internal vs external scroll, `isEditableTarget`, and provider/surface yield.\n\n**Migration**\n- Update all `handleContextMenu` calls to `handleContextMenu(e.nativeEvent, items)`; the `surfaceKey` parameter no longer exists.\n- Remove any usage of `useSurfaceContextMenu` and `registerSurface` (deleted).\n\n<sup>Written for commit ed46e49dc8f26010c4e14cd8aa6801b60c4249b5. Summary will update on new commits.</sup>\n\n<a href=\"https://cubic.dev/pr/maus-inc/mausVoice/pull/121?utm_source=github\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" data-no-image-dialog=\"true\"><picture><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\" srcset=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-dark.svg\"><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\" srcset=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-light.svg\"><img alt=\"Review in cubic\" src=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-dark.svg\"></picture></a>\n\n<!-- End of auto-generated description by cubic. -->\n\n## Summary by Sourcery\n\nResolve review findings by correcting context-menu behavior, stabilizing the A23 rate-limiter tests, and aligning prompt and project-status documentation with the implemented work.\n\nBug Fixes:\n- Fix context-menu behavior so internal menu scrolling remains open, empty menus preserve the native browser menu, focus returns to the clicked surface, clipboard failures are handled safely, and editable targets use the provider clipboard menu.\n- Eliminate nondeterministic A23 rate-limiter tests caused by shared process-global state.\n\nEnhancements:\n- Simplify the context-menu API by removing unused surface-registration functionality and state.\n- Wire contextual menus for transcription, dictionary, styling, conversation, and chat-message surfaces while explicitly deferring composer and home menus.\n\nDocumentation:\n- Update handoff and wave-status documentation to reflect completed A23 testing, A11 surface wiring, and the remaining A12 work.\n- Clarify the authoritative humanize runtime prompt and reconcile its accompanying expansion.\n\nTests:\n- Add regression coverage for editable-target detection, native-menu preservation, scroll behavior, and provider/surface menu precedence.\n- Make the A23 rate-limiter tests deterministic through timestamp-injected pure-function testing."
