WebSocket endpoint in the production CSP.\n- Remove the unnecessary listener spread in Gladia streaming tests.\n\nDocumentation:\n- Clarify Windows NSIS installer output paths for native and explicitly targeted builds.\n\nTests:\n- Expand Gladia cleanup and secret-redaction coverage and update batching expectations.\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated description by cubic. -->\n---\n## Summary by cubic\nHardens Gladia transcription streaming and fixes a CodeFactor warning. Reduces false reconnects, guarantees cleanup, expands secret redaction, and tunes batching for reliability and lower API pressure.\n\n- Fire connection-interrupted only on abnormal WebSocket closes (was on every ended); fewer spurious reconnect flows.\n- Always release SDK resources after finalize; prevents leaks.\n- Preserve the startup buffer on overflow errors (was wiping it); improves reconnect audio continuity.\n- Log startup failures and provider transcription warnings; better support visibility.\n- Redact refresh_token, x-gladia-key, authorization, api_key, token, and key in Gladia error text; prevents secret leaks. Refactor redaction to sequential replacements to satisfy Sonar complexity limits.\n- Use 10-minute Gladia batch segments with concurrency 1 (was 60 minutes with 3) and persist `this.model` in metadata.\n- Assert `wss://api.gladia.io` in the CSP connect-src contract; required for `@gladiaio/sdk`.\n- Localize provider-duration-limit strings across non-English locales to remove English fallbacks.\n- Tests/Docs: update chunking expectations; assert cleanup after finalize; expand redaction coverage; clarify Windows NSIS artifact paths.\n\n<sup>Written for commit 7869bab43268497e77f128a3e7293c3039e7d319. Summary will update on new commits.</sup>\n\n<a href=\"https://cubic.dev/pr/maus-inc/mausVoice/pull/117?utm_source=github\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" data-no-image-dialog=\"true\"><picture><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\" srcset=\"https://www.cubic.dev/