+      "description": "## What\n\nRan two \"unslop\" skills ([asavvin-pixel/unslop](https://github.com/asavvin-pixel/unslop) and the pstack unslop from [cursor/plugins](https://github.com/cursor/plugins)) over `README.md` and all 97 pages under `apps/docs/src/content/docs/` (~27,000 words). Prose-only edits: 44 files, 73 lines changed.\n\n## Changes\n\n**Typography and mechanics**\n- Replaced all 45 em dashes, each rewritten by hand into real sentence structures rather than swapped for parentheses or connector colons (both of which are their own tells)\n- Normalized curly quotes to straight quotes across 14 files (the docs mixed both styles)\n- Bullet-list `**Term** — definition` headers switched to the colon form the rest of the site already uses\n\n**Rhetoric and repetition**\n- The sentence \"The capability filter and the transcription dispatcher agree: ...\" was stamped nearly verbatim across three provider pages; each instance now reads differently and two drop internal-architecture framing users don't need\n- Softened the clustered \"rather than assuming / rather than relying\" tic (6 instances)\n- Cut two chewed-conclusion openers (\"Understanding them makes configuration ... much simpler\") and the clipped fragment pairs in the README (\"Filler words out, structure in.\", \"That's it.\")\n\n**Plain speech**\n- Hidden-actor passives converted to active voice where the actor matters (\"API credentials are stored ... rows are cleared by this action\" → \"mausVoice stores ... this action clears\")\n- Split a 58-word sentence with nested parentheticals in the provider capability reference\n- README grammar fixes: run-on tagline, Title Case in the keys line, \"All documentation regarding development are here\"\n\n## Not changed\n\nEvery model name, path, port, cipher, version number, command, and link is untouched. Table cells and rigid reference formats were left alone. No page structure changed.\n\n## Validation\n\n- `pnpm build` in `apps/docs` passes: 96 pages,