+      "description": "## Summary\n\nFixes all 18 issues identified in the Kilo code review of commit `c3e9337`.\n\n### WARNING fixes (6)\n| File | Issue | Fix |\n|------|-------|-----|\n| `apps/desktop/src-tauri/src/commands.rs:678` | SSRF boundary gap — `https` saved endpoints skip private-network protection | Added host-level validation for HTTPS saved endpoints, extending the same loopback/RFC1918/unique-local checks that already exist for HTTP |\n| `apps/desktop/src/utils/secure-fetch.utils.ts:82` | `new Response(...)` throws on null-body statuses (204/205/304) | Pass null body for null-body status codes |\n| `packages/voice-ai/src/assemblyai.utils.ts:262` | Wrong AssemblyAI field `speech_models` + invalid model `universal-3-5-pro` | Changed to `speech_model: \\\"best\\\"` |\n| `packages/voice-ai/src/openai.utils.ts:100` | Invalid default transcription model `gpt-transcribe` | Replaced with `whisper-1` (the only known working default) |\n| `apps/desktop/src/repos/model-provider.repo.ts:339` | Gemini `getTranscriptionModels` returns unfiltered fetched list | Added `isGeminiTranscriptionModel` filter |\n| `apps/desktop/src/utils/openai-compatible-transcribe.utils.ts:80` | Too-broad `unsupported` matcher re-uploads full audio up to 3x | Narrowed regex to require proximity of format/unsupported keywords |\n\n### SUGGESTION fixes (12)\n| File | Issue | Fix |\n|------|-------|-----|\n| `secure-fetch.utils.ts:96` | Negative scheme check | Changed to positive allow-list |\n| `secure-fetch.utils.ts:74` | Conditional `apiKeyId` spread | Added explicit validation for required param |\n| `secure-fetch.utils.ts:76` | `invoke()` rejects raw string | Wrapped rejection in Error |\n| `openai-compatible-transcribe.utils.ts:112` | `data.segments` assumed array | Added `Array.isArray` guard |\n| `openai-compatible-transcribe.utils.ts:66` | Path join bypasses normalizer | Use shared `normalizeOpenAICompatibleBaseUrl` |\n| `spoken-commands.utils.ts:316` | `applyScratch` deletes entire transcript | Early return instead of clearing all text |\n| `StyleHotkeysDialog.tsx:143` | Missing close affordance | Added IconButton with Close icon |\n| `077_spoken_commands_enabled.sql:2` | Wrong migration comment | Removed incorrect PR references |\n| `downloads.rs:550` | Re-hashes artifact on every check | Cache mtime to skip re-hash when file unchanged |\n| `xai.utils.ts:63` | `format: \\\"true\\\"` non-standard | Use actual audio extension |\n| `gemini.utils.ts:382` | `customFetch` not threaded | Added to generation/streaming/transcription |\n| `deepseek.utils.ts:17` | Unverified model ids | Updated to known working DeepSeek model IDs |\n\n## Summary by Sourcery\n\nHarden endpoint and transcription handling while correcting provider integrations and improving related user experience and performance.\n\nBug Fixes:\n- Close the HTTPS saved-endpoint SSRF gap by validating public IP literals while preserving supported private and domain-based endpoints.\n- Prevent invalid response construction for null-body HTTP statuses and improve secure-fetch error handling and scheme validation.\n- Correct transcription provider request fields, defaults, model catalogs, Gemini filtering, xAI audio format reporting, and DeepSeek model identifiers.\n- Reduce unnecessary OpenAI-compatible transcription retries and guard against malformed segment data.\n\nEnhancements:\n- Improve OpenAI-compatible endpoint normalization and add an explicit close affordance to the style hotkeys dialog.\n- Avoid repeated artifact hashing when downloaded files have not changed.\n\nTests:\n- Update provider and AssemblyAI tests to reflect corrected transcription request and model behavior.\n\nChores:\n- Remove obsolete migration commentary.\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated description by cubic. -->\n---\n## Summary by cubic\nCloses an HTTPS SSRF gap, hardens `secureFetch`, and fixes provider/model defaults while reducing spurious transcription retries. Old behavior let HTTPS saved endpoints hit public IP literals and retried uploads on loosely matched 4xx; new behavior blocks public IP literals (still allows loopback/RFC1918/unique‑local/.local and all domain names) and only retries on clear unsupported‑format errors.\n\n- HTTPS saved endpoints: Apply the same host validation to HTTP and HTTPS with one predicate. Allow all domain names; block public IP literals unless loopback/RFC1918/unique‑local. Side effect: https://203.x.x.x fails; https://10.x.x.x and https://localhost work.\n- `secureFetch`: Positive scheme allow‑list (HTTP via private Tauri command, HTTPS via `tauriFetch`; other schemes throw). Treat 204/205/304 as null‑body. Require `apiKeyId` for the OpenAI‑compatible command. Wrap `invoke()` failures to preserve useful messages. Required action: callers of the OpenAI‑compatible command must pass `apiKeyId`.\n- OpenAI‑compatible transcription: Normalize base URLs; narrow the unsupported‑format check to avoid unrelated 4xx retries; guard `segments` with `Array.isArray`.\n- Providers/models: OpenAI default = `whisper-1` and remove `gpt-transcribe`; AssemblyAI uses `speech_model: \"best\"`; DeepSeek defaults to `deepseek-chat` and supports `deepseek-reasoner`; Gemini transcription list is filtered; xAI sends the actual audio format.\n- UX/tests: Add a Close button to the Style Hotkeys dialog; update provider and AssemblyAI tests; remove an incorrect migration comment.\n\n<sup>Written for commit 78141c8c6e18f5ba964794c46fb08cb1dacab726. Summary will update on new commits.</sup>\n\n<a href=\"https://cubic.dev/pr/maus-inc/mausVoice/pull/113?utm_source=github\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" data-no-image-dialog=\"true\"><picture><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\" srcset=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-dark.svg\"><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\" srcset=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-light.svg\"><img alt=\"Review in cubic\" src=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-dark.s