+      "description": "## Why\n\nStacked on top of #110 (base: `arena/01a01b11-mausvoice`).\n\nSonarCloud still reports **1 open issue on new code** for PR #110:\n\n| Rule | File | Message |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| `python:S8786` (Reliability, MEDIUM) | `scripts/translate.py:81` | Simplify this regular expression to reduce its runtime, as it has super-linear performance due to backtracking. |\n\n[Sonar issue list for #110](https://sonarcloud.io/project/issues?id=maus-inc_voquill&pullRequest=110&issueStatuses=OPEN,CONFIRMED&sinceLeakPeriod=true) (Quality Gate is already green; this clears the last remaining new-code issue.)\n\n## What changed\n\n`scripts/translate.py` only.\n\nThe flagged pattern was:\n\n```python\nr'(\\w+):\\s*(?:\\n\\s*)?(\"[^\"\\\\]*(?:\\\\.[^\"\\\\]*)*\")'\n```\n\n`\\s` already matches `\\n`, so `\\s*` and the optional `(?:\\n\\s*)` group overlap. On a whitespace run that is *not* followed by a string literal, the engine re-tries every possible split between the two — polynomial backtracking.\n\nNow:\n\n```python\nTS_STRING_RE = r'\"(?:[^\"\\\\]|\\\\.)*\"'\n\nTS_PAIR_RE = re.compile(rf\"(\\w+):\\s*({TS_STRING_RE})\", re.DOTALL)\n```\n\n- Dropped the redundant `(?:\\n\\s*)?` group — `\\s*` already covers wrapped values.\n- String-literal matching uses disjoint alternatives (`[^\"\\\\]` vs `\\\\.`) under a single quantifier instead of a nested-quantifier unrolled loop.\n- The same literal pattern in `write_ts_translation_values()` now reuses `TS_STRING_RE`, so parse and write stay in sync (that copy had the identical ambiguity).\n\n## Verification\n\n- Parse + substitution output is byte-identical to the old regexes on a fixture covering: values on the next line, escaped quotes, escaped backslashes, `\\n` escapes, unicode/emoji, and keys that are suffixes of other keys (`name` / `displayName`).\n- Round-tripped `parse_ts_translations()` → `write_ts_translation_values()` → re-parse via the real module; missing-key `RuntimeError` path still fires.\n- Pathological input (`\"k:\" + \" \\n\" * 8000`): **~960 ms → ~0.4 ms**; scaling is now linear instead of quadratic.\n- `python3 -m py_compile scripts/translate.py` clean.\n\n## Summary by Sourcery\n\nPrevent pathological regex performance in TypeScript translation handling while keeping parsing and rewriting behavior consistent.\n\nBug Fixes:\n- Eliminate super-linear regular-expression backtracking in translation parsing and writing, improving performance on pathological TypeScript translation input.\n\nEnhancements:\n- Centralize TypeScript string-literal matching so parsing and writing use the same unambiguous pattern while preserving existing translation behavior.\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated description by cubic. -->\n---\n## Summary by cubic\nRemoves super-linear backtracking in translation regexes to clear SonarCloud rule `python:S8786`. Old pattern overlapped `\\s*` with an optional `\\n\\s*` and used a nested-quantifier string; new pattern uses a shared linear-time `TS_STRING_RE` and drops the redundant group without changing behavior.\n\n- Touches only `scripts/translate.py`; both read and write paths now reuse `TS_STRING_RE`.\n- `TS_PAIR_RE` is now `rf\"(\\w+):\\s*({TS_STRING_RE})\"` with `re.DOTALL`; wrapped values remain supported.\n- String literal uses disjoint alternatives (`[^\"\\\\]` vs `\\\\.`) under one quantifier to avoid ambiguity.\n- Verified byte-identical parse/write on fixtures; pathological input improves from ~960 ms to ~0.4 ms.\n- No config changes or migrations; resolves the last open Sonar issue on this stack.\n\n<sup>Written for commit dd68323efe15a95d9d12c00e4fca7d98b8036264. Summary will update on new commits.</sup>\n\n<a href=\"https://cubic.dev/pr/maus-inc/mausVoice/pull/116?utm_source=github\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" data-no-image-dialog=\"true\"><picture><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\" srcset=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-dark.svg\"><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\" srcset=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-light.svg\"><img alt=\"Review in cubic\" src=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-dark.svg\"></picture></a>\n\n<!-- End of auto-generated description by cubic. -->\n\n"
