+      "description": "## Problem\n\nThe **Prompt** writing style produced a message *about* writing a prompt instead of the optimized prompt itself. For example, dictating:\n\n> Fix the prompt style. It just attributes a message that is telling the transcript is seen to write a prompt instead of actually optimizing and writing the prompt.\n\nyielded the final transcription:\n\n> Write a refined prompt that transcribes the given transcript and corrects its style, focusing on optimization rather than merely attributing the message.\n\n## Root cause\n\nThe Prompt tone's post-processing instructions (`tone.utils.ts`, delivered via `buildSystemPostProcessingTonePrompt`) said to *\"Condense the speaker's rambling or fragmented dictation into a concise, self-contained prompt\"*, and its only few-shot example output began with *\"Write a short email…\"*. Models generalized that pattern and emitted meta-instructions (\"Write a refined prompt that…\") describing the task of writing a prompt, rather than the finished prompt text — especially when the dictation was itself already an instruction.\n\n## Changes\n\n- **`apps/desktop/src/utils/tone.utils.ts`** — rewrote the `prompt` tone template to:\n  - return the finished, ready-to-paste prompt text itself, addressed directly to the AI that will execute it;\n  - explicitly forbid descriptions, instructions to write a prompt (e.g. \"Write a prompt that…\"), and explanations of edits;\n  - keep already-imperative dictations as direct commands (cleaned up), instead of wrapping them in prompt meta-instructions;\n  - preserve the existing constraints (intent/names/numbers, 1–3 sentences, no invented details, no em-dashes).\n- Replaced the single few-shot example with two, the second mirroring the reported case so the desired transformation is anchored:\n\n  > **Input:** Fix the prompt style, it, uh, just gives a message that says to write a prompt instead of, you know, actually writing the prompt.\n  > **Output:** Fix the Prompt style so it returns the finished, optimized prompt itself instead of a message that says to write a prompt.\n\n- **`apps/desktop/src/utils/prompt.utils.ts`** — drive-by fix: `buildLocalizedAgentPrompt` logged an undefined `prompt` variable; it now logs `base`.\n\n## Verification\n\n- Rendered the full system/user prompt for the Prompt tone through the real code path (`buildSystemPostProcessingTonePrompt` / `buildPostProcessingPrompt`) with the reported transcript to confirm the model now receives the corrected instructions.\n- `tsc --noEmit` clean; prettier clean.\n- All unit tests pass (541 tests / 51 files). The only failures are live-API eval/integration tests that require `GROQ_API_KEY` and are unavailable in the sandbox.\n\n## Notes\n\n- Stacked on `fix/superfix-review-findings` (#63) since this branch was cut from it; retarget to `main` once #63/#105 land. The diff here is exactly the one fix commit (`98529fe`).\n\n## Summary by Sourcery\n\nMake the Prompt writing style produce the optimized task directly instead of describing prompt creation.\n\nBug Fixes:\n- Ensure the Prompt writing style returns the finished, ready-to-use prompt rather than a meta-instruction describing how to write one.\n- Correct agent prompt logging to reference the defined base prompt value. To prevent meta-instructions, explicitly preserve already imperative dictations as direct commands and prohibit descriptions or explanations.\n\nEnhancements:\n- Strengthen Prompt style guidance and examples to preserve speaker intent while producing concise, direct task instructions.\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated description by cubic. -->\n---\n## Summary by cubic\nMakes Prompt style return the finished prompt text instead of a meta-instruction. Previously it emitted “Write a refined prompt that…”, now it outputs the cleaned task content itself and preserves imperative dictations.\n\n- apps/desktop/src/utils/tone.utils.ts: tighten the `prompt` tone to return only the task content (1–3 sentences); explicitly ban descriptions, instructions to write a prompt, and explanations of edits; forbid added references to the transcript/speaker/assistant/that this is a prompt, unless those words are in the dictated task; replace few-shot examples to remove the “Write a …” pattern and use two compliant examples (Q3 summary; login-bug fix).\n- apps/desktop/src/utils/prompt.utils.ts: fix logging to print `base` instead of an undefined `prompt`.\n\n<sup>Written for commit f0e44520e7dee0cf4f7266278cd58c62387710d4. Summary will update on new commits.</sup>\n\n<a href=\"https://cubic.dev/pr/maus-inc/mausVoice/pull/106?utm_source=github\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" data-no-image-dialog=\"true\"><picture><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\" srcset=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-dark.svg\"><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\" srcset=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-light.svg\"><img alt=\"Review in cubic\" src=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-dark.svg\"></picture></a>\n\n<!-- End of auto-generated description by cubic. -->\n\n"
