+      "description": "Reverts maus-inc/mausVoice#107\n\n## Summary by Sourcery\n\nRevert the broad SonarCloud cleanup and deduplication changes while restoring the previous implementations and platform-specific test harnesses.\n\nEnhancements:\n- Revert the prior SonarCloud cleanup and deduplication refactor across agent execution, transcription, provider integrations, UI components, utilities, scripts, and shared types.\n- Restore platform-specific pill test harnesses and inline implementations that had been consolidated into shared helpers.\n\nTests:\n- Restore the detailed desktop pill test scripts for macOS, Windows, and GTK scenarios.\n\nChores:\n- Revert associated cleanup changes, including helper extraction, stricter validation, modern API substitutions, and related naming and type adjustments.\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated description by cubic. -->\n---\n## Summary by cubic\nReverts the SonarCloud “cleanup + deduplication” refactor to restore prior desktop behavior and unblock regressions. Restores original audio streaming, transcription sessions, state shape, simpler sorting/encoding utilities, and reintroduces local `.env` Google OAuth client secrets for local builds.\n\n- Review focus\n  - Audio/transcription: removes shared `streaming-audio-buffer` module; reimplements chunking per provider (AssemblyAI, Deepgram, ElevenLabs). Verify interim results, finalize flows, and playback control (`activePlayback` is now a mutable export).\n  - Local sidecar: switches to `LocalSidecar*` types and updates call sites. Re-test local model status/download/delete and pause/resume flows.\n  - UI/components: simplifies keys, event handlers, and conditional rendering across lists/menus/dialogs. Check menu item keys, Breadcrumb keys, and Update dialog progress.\n  - Utilities: reverts to simpler `.sort()` and `charCodeAt`/regex usage and JSON/code block parsing. Expect minor differences in collation/Unicode handling.\n  - Repos/providers: restores pre-refactor access patterns and fallbacks across `Groq`, `OpenAI`, `OpenRouter`, `Ollama`, and OpenAI-compatible endpoints. Confirm model lists and transcription endpoints still resolve.\n\n- Rollout/Migration\n  - Verify `.env.*` Google OAuth client secrets align with CI expectations; rotate or remove committed secrets if required by your security posture.\n  - Re-run smoke tests for transcription (local, Azure, AssemblyAI, Deepgram, ElevenLabs) and for local model management.\n  - No data/schema migrations; perform a clean install/build to avoid stale cache from removed modules.\n\n<sup>Written for commit fa069627919fc2f922f056febb8a3a1bb66d3872. Summary will update on new commits.</sup>\n\n<a href=\"https://cubic.dev/pr/maus-inc/mausVoice/pull/108?utm_source=github\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" data-no-image-dialog=\"true\"><picture><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\" srcset=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-dark.svg\"><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\" srcset=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-light.svg\"><img alt=\"Review in cubic\" src=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-dark.svg\"></picture></a>\n\n<!-- End of auto-generated description by cubic. -->\n\n\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai -->\n\n## Summary by CodeRabbit\n\n* **Bug Fixes**\n  * Improved app-target registration and error feedback.\n  * Improved local transcription download cancellation and model-status refresh behavior.\n  * Preserved duplicate transcription warnings for clearer diagnostics.\n  * Improved Windows version detection and GPU-loading reliability.\n  * Improved transcription requests across supported AI providers with clearer error handling.\n\n* **Improvements**\n  * Refined login initialization, keyboard shortcuts, audio playback, locale matching, and transcript processing.\n  * Expanded pill and transcription test coverage across desktop platforms.\n\n* **Refactor**\n  * Simplified internal processing while preserving existing app behavior and interface presentation.\n\n<!-- end of auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai -->"
