+      "description": "Resolves the 329 open SonarCloud issues across all analyzed languages:\n\n**TS/JS (228+29):** all 86 active rules fixed — readonly members (S2933), optional chaining (S6582), replaceAll/codePointAt (S7781/S7758), nested ternaries (S3358), cognitive complexity (S3776), empty methods (S1186), regex backtracking (S8786), React keys/components (S6478/S6479), node: imports (S7772), and more.\n\n**Shell (37):** unified 3 duplicated test.sh into one shared script (S1192), [[ instead of [ (S7688), switch defaults (S131), stderr-safe messages (S7677), HTTPS enforcement (S6506), --ignore-scripts (S6505).\n\n**Python (20):** taint validation for path/shell sinks (S8707/S8705/S2083), constants (S1192), linear regexes (S8786), complexity + collapsible-if refactors.\n\n**PowerShell (7) / GitHub Actions (5) / Secrets (3):** $null-LHS, $matches rename, empty-catch handling, Write-Output; job-level permissions; rotated+removed committed OAuth secrets.\n\n**Duplication:** 1.3% → ~0 via extracted shared modules (streaming-audio-buffer, voice-ai shared.utils, provider schemas, transcription types).\n\nNote: 5 .github/workflows fixes (--ignore-scripts + job-level permissions) could not be pushed (GitHub App token lacks `workflows` permission) — patch saved at sonar_work/workflow-fixes.patch.\n\nVerified: pnpm check-types, pnpm lint, 370 unit tests all pass.\n\n## Summary by Sourcery\n\nResolve repository-wide static-analysis issues while consolidating duplicated functionality and improving runtime robustness.\n\nBug Fixes:\n- Resolve the broad set of SonarCloud-reported correctness, security, maintainability, and code-quality issues across TypeScript, JavaScript, Python, shell, PowerShell, and workflow-related code.\n- Improve agent event processing, transcription streaming finalization, keyboard shortcut handling, update messaging, and input/path validation.\n\nEnhancements:\n- Extract shared audio buffering, provider integration, transcription, schema, and test-script utilities to eliminate duplicated implementations.\n- Consolidate provider repositories, UI rendering logic, translation tooling, and session helpers for clearer and more maintainable code.\n- Strengthen platform portability, secure command and network handling, and consistency across APIs, types, and application state.\n\nBuild:\n- Update installation and build scripts for safer dependency installation, platform-specific command execution, and configurable Rust targets.\n\nTests:\n- Retain and streamline unit and integration test coverage while consolidating duplicated test fixtures and shared scripts.\n\nChores:\n- Remove committed environment and secret material and apply broad static-analysis cleanup throughout the repository.\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated description by cubic. -->\n---\n## Summary by cubic\nFixes all 329 open SonarCloud issues and removes duplicated logic, primarily by extracting a shared streaming audio buffer for transcription sessions. Rotates committed Google OAuth client secrets and moves them to CI, improving security.\n\n- Streaming transcription (AssemblyAI, Deepgram, ElevenLabs) now shares `src/sessions/streaming-audio-buffer.ts` for chunking and interim buffering; verify latency and finalization across providers.\n- Local transcription sidecar types are renamed (`SidecarDownloadSnapshot`, `SidecarModelStatusResponse`) and a facade is exported from `sidecars/index.ts`; test model status/download/pause/delete and settings screens.\n- Repos and providers are refactored for clarity and safety; confirm Groq/OpenAI/OpenRouter/Ollama model listing, selection, and generation/transcription, and note lists now sort with `localeCompare`.\n- UI adjustments (Update dialog, API key list, microphone selector, table/list keys) reduce React key warnings and improve stability; behavior should be unchanged.\n- `activePlayback` is now accessed via `getActivePlayback()`; internal callers updated.\n\n**Rollout/Migration**\n- Set `MAUSVOICE_GOOGLE_CLIENT_SECRET` in CI for prod/enterprise builds and in local developer `.env`; the previously committed values were rotated and removed.\n- A maintainer with workflow permissions must apply `sonar_work/workflow-fixes.patch` to update `.github/workflows` (`--ignore-scripts` and job-level permissions).\n\n<sup>Written for commit 78745f29f1677a012390c1875fb22865cf2fed83. Summary will update on new commits.</sup>\n\n<a href=\"https://cubic.dev/pr/maus-inc/mausVoice/pull/107?utm_source=github\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" data-no-image-dialog=\"true\"><picture><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\" srcset=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-dark.svg\"><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\" srcset=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-light.svg\"><img alt=\"Review in cubic\" src=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-dark.svg\"></picture></a>\n\n<!-- End of auto-generated description by cubic. -->\n\n"
