+      "description": "## Summary\n\nResumes **#98** and addresses the two kilo-review suggestions on `tone.actions.ts`:\n\n1. **Queue never resets (unbounded promise-chain growth)** — `enqueueStyleSwitch` now detaches from the settled chain once the queue drains, resetting `styleSwitchQueue` to a fresh `Promise.resolve()` instead of chaining onto an ever-growing tail that retained every prior task closure for the app's lifetime.\n2. **`selectToneByHotkey` bypasses the serialization queue** — the global style shortcut now runs through `enqueueStyleSwitch`, so a hotkey selection can no longer race an in-flight style cycle.\n\n## Test plan\n- [x] `pnpm --filter desktop check-types`\n- [x] `oxlint` + `prettier --check` on touched files\n- [x] `pnpm --filter desktop test:unit` (612 passed, incl. new serialization test)\n- [ ] Manual: rapid chevron clicks + hotkey select stay consistent; tooltip name matches applied style\n\nBase: `arena/01a01761-mausvoice` (same base as #98). Branch is forked from #98's head commit `0257421`.\n\n## Summary by Sourcery\n\nSerialize all writing-style changes and harden pill event handling so style selections remain consistent without unbounded queue growth.\n\nBug Fixes:\n- Prevent style-switch events from bypassing serialization, ensuring rapid chevron, hotkey, and in-app style changes are applied consistently.\n- Prevent the style-switch promise queue from retaining completed task chains indefinitely.\n- Improve pill style-switch event handling by validating JSON payloads, accepting direction casing variations, and reporting malformed or unsupported events clearly.\n\nEnhancements:\n- Centralize pill style-switch direction handling and event emission across desktop and macOS overlay paths, with a main-window emission fallback.\n\nTests:\n- Add coverage for canonical, mixed-case, malformed, and unrelated pill style-switch payloads.\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated description by cubic. -->\n---\n## Summary by cubic\nHardens pill style-switch handling in Rust without changing the webview contract. Previously we matched stdout with substring checks and emitted directly; now we parse JSON style_switch messages case-insensitively and emit via a centralized helper with a broadcast fallback.\n\n- Add `PillStyleSwitchDirection` and `parse_style_switch_direction` to accept `{\"type\":\"style_switch\",\"direction\":...}`, ignore unrelated/malformed lines, and log targeted warnings.\n- Centralize event names in `PILL_STYLE_SWITCH_FORWARD_EVENT`/`PILL_STYLE_SWITCH_BACKWARD_EVENT` and emit via `emit_pill_style_switch`, preferring `\"main\"` then broadcasting; log at `debug`/`warn`/`error` as appropriate.\n- Update macOS overlay to reuse the shared parser/emitter.\n- Keep event names (`tone-switch-forward`/`tone-switch-backward`) and `DictationSideEffects` listeners working as-is; no TypeScript changes.\n- Add Rust tests for parsing, case-insensitive directions, and rejection paths.\n\n<sup>Written for commit aa4ac8529f133efc747208435cf36131e3fdbe22. Summary will update on new commits.</sup>\n\n<a href=\"https://cubic.dev/pr/maus-inc/mausVoice/pull/101?utm_source=github\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" data-no-image-dialog=\"true\"><picture><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\" srcset=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-dark.svg\"><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\" srcset=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-light.svg\"><img alt=\"Review in cubic\" src=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-dark.svg\"></picture></a>\n\n<!-- End of auto-generated description by cubic. -->\n\n"
