+      "description": "## Summary\n\nWhen \"switch style while dictating\" is on, switching mid-utterance now produces final output in the **newly selected** profile.\n\n**Root cause:** `finalizeAndPostProcess` always post-processed with `segmentStartToneIdRef` (captured at recording start). All three switch channels already wrote `user.selectedToneId`, but finalize ignored that live selection.\n\n**Semantics:**\n- **Manual mode:** final output uses the tone selected at **stop**. Mid-utterance switches (pill chevrons, style hotkeys, Left/Right while holding dictate) apply to this utterance.\n- **Race:** a switch that arrives *after* stop has snapshotted the tone loses for this utterance (it still updates the selection for the next one).\n- **Realtime:** already-inserted interim text is never restyled; a mid-stream switch applies from the next segment only.\n- **Automatic mode:** unchanged (app-target tone captured at stop).\n\nAll three channels go through `applyInDictationStyleSwitch` → `applyWritingStyleSelection` → `setSelectedToneId`, so the pill label and the applied tone cannot drift.\n\n## Test plan\n\n- [x] Unit: `getEffectiveToneIdAtFinalize` (switch before stop / during realtime / after stop / automatic)\n- [x] Unit: all three channels share the same state transition\n- [x] Unit: Left/Right arrow resolver (enabled, activation held, disabled cases)\n- [x] `pnpm --filter desktop check-types`\n- [x] `pnpm --filter desktop test:unit` (620 passed)\n- [ ] Manual: enable in-dictation style switching, start dictating, switch via (a) pill, (b) style hotkey, (c) Left/Right while holding dictate; stop; confirm output matches the new profile\n- [ ] Manual: automatic styling mode still uses the app-target tone\n\n## Summary by Sourcery\n\nApply the style selected at dictation stop to manually styled final output while keeping realtime text and automatic styling semantics unchanged.\n\nNew Features:\n- Apply manual writing-style changes made during dictation to the utterance’s final output based on the selection at stop time.\n- Support consistent in-dictation style switching through the pill controls, style hotkeys, and Left/Right arrows while holding the dictate activation key.\n\nBug Fixes:\n- Prevent finalized dictation from using the style captured at segment start when the user switched styles during the utterance.\n- Preserve automatic styling behavior by prioritizing the focused app’s assigned tone.\n\nEnhancements:\n- Centralize writing-style switch state transitions and add snapshot lifecycle handling to avoid races and tone carryover between utterances.\n\nTests:\n- Add unit coverage for finalize-time tone selection, switch-channel consistency, arrow-key resolution, snapshot handling, and user-state persistence behavior.\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated description by cubic. -->\n---\n## Summary by cubic\nApplies mid‑dictation style switches to the utterance finalized at stop in manual mode. Previously we froze the style at segment start; now the stop‑time selection styles the final output, so pill, cycle/select hotkeys, and Left/Right (while holding dictate) affect the current utterance. Realtime interim text is never restyled.\n\n- Behavior: Manual uses stop → start → live selection; automatic uses the app‑target tone captured at stop, falling back to the live selection when the app has no tone.\n- Switching path and races: All channels route through applyInDictationStyleSwitch → toWritingStyleTransition → applyWritingStyleSelection. We write the selection in memory before persist so a same‑turn stop snapshots it; we skip persist when no user exists.\n- Snapshot lifecycle: `createUtteranceToneSnapshots` seeds at start, overwrites at stop, and clears on abort, on stop completion/errors, and when switching to type mode to prevent carryover.\n- Arrow keys: Left/Right cycling requires an active manual dictate session with the activation key held and triggers only on the first press edge. Dictate combos are memoized and checked via isActivationComboHeld; edge detection uses resolveNewlyPressedDictationArrow.\n- No migrations. New switch channels must call applyInDictationStyleSwitch.\n\n<sup>Written for commit e8c92b2a551d2dd74325d1ff533f3f587ee26d05. Summary will update on new commits.</sup>\n\n<a href=\"https://cubic.dev/pr/maus-inc/mausVoice/pull/102?utm_source=github\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" data-no-image-dialog=\"true\"><picture><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\" srcset=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-dark.svg\"><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\" srcset=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-light.svg\"><img alt=\"Review in cubic\" src=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-dark.svg\"></picture></a>\n\n<!-- End of auto-generated description by cubic. -->\n\n"
