+      "description": "## Agent A16 — Mirror the inner/drop shadow design into light mode\n\nPorts the layered inner-highlight + soft drop-shadow design (as refined in dark mode) into light mode, applied consistently across buttons, cards, list items and the title bar, so both modes share one visual language with mode-appropriate values.\n\n### Changes\n\n**`apps/desktop/src/styles/shadows.ts`**\n- `premiumSurface.light.*` drops now mirror dark's stop geometry 1:1 — contact `0 1px 2px`, mid `0 8px 20px`, ambient `0 18px 40px` (hover `2/4 · 12/28 · 28/56`; selected `1/2 · 10/24`) — with warm `ink()` at roughly a third of dark's alpha, so light surfaces carry the same layered lift without greying the cream. The state ramp tracks dark's: hover > rest, active collapses to contact-only, selected heaviest.\n- A14's light emboss alphas are kept verbatim (rest 0.42/0.14, hover 0.58/0.20, active 0.07+0.18, selected 0.18/0.06) and dark mode is untouched.\n- `titleBarShadow.light` now shares dark's structure: a machined inset rim on the bottom edge (`inset 0 -1px 0 highlight(0.3)`) + one soft warm drop at dark's `0 10px 28px` geometry, replacing the flat outer highlight line + faint `0 8px 24px` drop.\n- New `accentSurface` token: the accent CTA's ad-hoc box-shadow moves out of `theme.ts` into `shadows.ts` (values unchanged), so `theme.ts` references tokens only.\n\n**`apps/desktop/src/theme.ts`**\n- `variant: \"blue\"` button consumes `accentSurface.light/dark` instead of inline shadow strings (the only ad-hoc shadow string in theme.ts).\n\n**`apps/desktop/src/styles/shadows.test.ts`** (new, 19 contract tests)\n- Stop-geometry parity between light/dark per state; scheme ink tinting (warm `rgb(26,23,18)` light vs neutral black dark, white emboss).\n- Pinned A14 light emboss alphas and dark emboss alphas (regression guards).\n- Pinned A16 light drop alphas + the per-state ramp (hover > rest, active collapse, selected heaviest).\n- Title bar structure parity; accentSurface per-mode accent tint.\n- Guard: `theme.ts` contains no literal `boxShadow:` strings.\n\n### Verification\n- `pnpm --filter desktop check-types` ✅\n- `pnpm --filter desktop test:unit` ✅ 63 files / 621 tests (19 new)\n- `pnpm --filter desktop lint`: prettier+oxlint clean on all touched files ✅ (full `lint` still flags 3 pre-existing files outside this lane: `DictationSideEffects.tsx`, `dictation.strategy.ts`, `output-routing.utils.ts` — out-of-lane finding)\n- `pnpm run build` (root) ✅ 10/10 tasks\n- Offline pixel renderer (CSS box-shadow model, supersampled): dark mode byte-identical before/after across all 10 surface renders; light mode before→after near-band ΔL: rest 15→27, hover 30→41, selected 24→32, title bar 6.5→17 (Weber ratios move from ~1.07 toward dark's ~1.5–1.8 without muddying the cream).\n\nNo i18n strings, Rust, or bindings touched.\n\n## Summary by Sourcery\n\nMirror the layered shadow language across light and dark desktop themes while preserving appropriate visual tuning for each mode.\n\nNew Features:\n- Add shared accent surface shadow tokens for blue CTA buttons in light and dark modes.\n\nEnhancements:\n- Align light-mode surface shadows with dark-mode layered geometry while preserving mode-specific emboss and tint values.\n- Update light title-bar shadows to use the shared inset-rim and soft-drop structure.\n- Centralize theme shadow definitions and remove ad-hoc box-shadow values from theme configuration.\n\nTests:\n- Add contract tests covering shadow geometry, state ramps, color tints, title-bar structure, accent tokens, parser validation, and theme token usage.\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated description by cubic. -->\n---\n## Summary by cubic\nMirrors the dark-mode layered inner highlight + soft drop-shadow design in light mode so both schemes share one shadow language. Dark remains unchanged; light gains clearer lift without greying the cream.\n\n- Aligns `premiumSurface.light` to dark’s stop geometry (contact 0/1/2, mid 0/8/20, ambient 0/18/40; hover 2/4·12/28·28/56; selected 1/2·10/24) with warm `ink()` alphas; state ramp matches dark (hover > rest; active collapses; selected heaviest).\n- Updates `titleBarShadow.light` to an inset bottom rim plus a single soft drop at 10/28, warm‑tinted.\n- Extracts the CTA shadow into `accentSurface` and switches `theme.ts` to it; a resolved-theme walk enforces that no literal `boxShadow:` strings remain.\n- Adds contract tests pinning geometry parity, scheme tints, A14 emboss alphas, A16 drop alphas and ramps, and title bar structure. Centralizes shadow parsing as `parseShadowLayers()` in `shadows.ts` (tests reuse it; only `rgba()` tokens are supported and invalid formats fail loudly).\n\nVisual impact: light-mode surfaces and the title bar lift more clearly; dark mode is byte-identical. No API or theme-token migrations required.\n\n<sup>Written for commit 31805a0d69fcce0f6c801c8d90eff00b92f9b6c2. Summary will update on new commits.</sup>\n\n<a href=\"https://cubic.dev/pr/maus-inc/mausVoice/pull/104?utm_source=github\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" data-no-image-dialog=\"true\"><picture><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\" srcset=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-dark.svg\"><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\" srcset=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-light.svg\"><img alt=\"Review in cubic\" src=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-dark.svg\"></picture></a>\n\n<!-- End of auto-generated description by cubic. -->\n\n"
