+      "description": "Continues #96 (branched from its head, `4ef39c7`) and addresses the review feedback left there.\n\n## Review comments addressed\n\n**1. `ring_head_disc_fractions_and_falloff` asserted the wrong direction**\n\nThe test walked `k` from 1 (innermost) to `steps` (outermost) but seeded `prev_radius = f64::INFINITY` and asserted `radius_frac < prev_radius` — i.e. \"radius shrinks inward\" — which contradicts the implementation (`radius_frac = k / steps`, growing with `k`) and the doc comment. It would have failed at `k = 2` (0.5 < 0.25).\n\nCorrected to match the documented behaviour: walking `k` upward walks *outward*, so radius grows (`0.25 → 0.5 → 0.75 → 1.0`) while the falloff dims (`1.0 → 0.531 → 0.218 → 0.047`) — which is the same statement as \"brightness increases inward\". Added an assertion that the outermost disc spans the full head radius (`radius_frac == 1.0`), so the stack covers the head instead of stopping short of the rim. The existing exponent checks are unchanged and still hold.\n\n**2. `Gfx::stroke_polyline` unwrapped Direct2D calls on the render hot path**\n\n`CreatePathGeometry()` and `Open()` are now `let Ok(..) else { return }` early-returns, and `sink.Close()` failure also returns before `DrawGeometry` (an unclosed sink leaves the geometry unusable). Brush creation moved after geometry construction so the failure paths do nothing at all. Dropping one shadow pass on a frame is imperceptible; a panic would take the overlay process down. This runs once per shadow layer per frame while the ring is held, so device loss or resource exhaustion is a realistic failure mode.\n\n## Verification\n\n- tree-sitter Rust parse of both touched files: clean.\n- Falloff/radius sequence re-checked numerically against the corrected assertions.\n- No Rust toolchain in this sandbox (crates.io / static.rust-lang.org are network-blocked), so `cargo fmt --check`, `cargo clippy` and `cargo test` still need to run in CI. Lines kept ≤100 cols; `let ... else` is already used elsewhere in `rust_windows_pill` (`src/ipc.rs`), so the edition/MSRV supports it.\n\n## i18n updated\n\nNone (no user-facing strings).\n\n## Summary by Sourcery\n\nImprove long-press ring readability with coordinated shadow and head layers while making rendering robust to backend failures.\n\nNew Features:\n- Add a soft layered shadow and dark head underlay to improve long-press ring visibility across light backgrounds.\n\nBug Fixes:\n- Prevent rendering failures and degenerate geometry from crashing or producing invalid long-press ring output.\n\nEnhancements:\n- Centralize ring shadow, head placement, disc falloff, alpha cutoffs, and layer planning across all platform renderers.\n- Reduce unnecessary low-alpha comet segment draws while preserving existing timing and geometry.\n\nTests:\n- Add shared tests covering ring head placement, disc falloff, shadow layers, cutoffs, and degenerate inputs.\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated description by cubic. -->\n---\n## Summary by cubic\nImproves long‑press readability by adding a soft shadow behind the silver ring and a dark underlay beneath the comet head. Previously there was no shadow and the ring could disappear on light backdrops; now shared layer planning keeps platforms in sync without changing timings or geometry, and low alphas leave dark backdrops unaffected.\n\n- Changes\n  - Shared (`packages/rust_pill_shared`): add `RingLayers` to plan the shadow arc, head placement, and concentric discs once per frame; new constants `RING_SHADOW_LAYERS`, `RING_SHADOW_HEAD_ALPHA`, `RING_HEAD_FALLOFF_EXP`, `RING_HEAD_DISC_ALPHA_SCALE`, `RING_HEAD_FADE_CUTOFF`, `RING_SEGMENT_ALPHA_CUTOFF`, `RING_PATH_LEN_EPSILON`; helpers `ring_head_disc()` and `ring_head_index()`. Tests cover head index bounds/monotonicity, disc falloff ordering, shadow-layer falloff, cutoffs, and degenerate inputs.\n  - Renderers (`packages/rust_macos_pill`, `packages/rust_gtk_pill`, `packages/rust_windows_pill`): resample the perimeter once; draw `RingLayers::shadow_passes()` up to `head_index`, then `underlay_discs()` and `head_discs()`. Skip comet segments below `RING_SEGMENT_ALPHA_CUTOFF` and guard degenerate buffers. Windows adds `Gfx::stroke_polyline()` to batch shadow strokes and early-returns on Direct2D geometry/sink failures; create the brush after geometry.\n\n- Rollout\n  - No migrations or public API changes. Unit tests added/updated; run fmt/clippy/tests in CI.\n\n<sup>Written for commit b63a6f90d769dec2dca99d6b9d762f3be5f86c9b. Summary will update on new commits.</sup>\n\n<a href=\"https://cubic.dev/pr/maus-inc/mausVoice/pull/99?utm_source=github\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" data-no-image-dialog=\"true\"><picture><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\" srcset=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-dark.svg\"><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\" srcset=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-light.svg\"><img alt=\"Review in cubic\" src=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-dark.svg\"></picture></a>\n\n<!-- End of auto-generated description by cubic. -->\n\n"
