+      "description": "## Summary\nContinues #97 and addresses Sourcery's review on that PR.\n\n- **Single write-site for the elevation gate.** `releaseElevationStartupGate` is the only place that clears `settings.elevationStartupPending`. `AppSideEffects` (pre-flight) and `ElevationDeclinedDialog` (\"Launch normally\") both go through `elevation.actions` so the gate cannot drift if the behavior changes.\n- **Pre-flight extracted to an exported action.** `runStartupElevationPreflight` owns the prefs read, UAC call, and hold-vs-release policy (`cancelled` / `require-restart` keep the gate closed; everything else releases).\n- **Contract tests pin APIs and state transitions**, not source snippets. `elevation.actions.test.ts` covers gate release, launch-normally, quit, platform policy, and the full pre-flight matrix. The old string-matching checks in `elevation-startup.test.ts` / `startup-elevation.test.ts` are gone except for rust-only setup/close-handler pins (no TS surface).\n\n## Test plan\n- [x] `pnpm --filter desktop exec tsc --noEmit`\n- [x] Prettier + oxlint on touched files\n- [x] Vitest: elevation + native + startup contracts (28/28)\n- [ ] Windows manual from #97 still applies (enable pref → helper before full app; decline → Launch normally / Close mausVoice)\n\n## Summary by Sourcery\n\nGate Windows startup behind an early elevation pre-flight and provide consistent normal-launch or process-quit behavior after a declined UAC prompt.\n\nNew Features:\n- Add an early Windows startup elevation pre-flight that gates full application initialization until the UAC decision is resolved.\n- Add an explicit native quit command for closing the application from the elevation-declined flow.\n\nBug Fixes:\n- Ensure declining elevation can launch the app normally without allowing initialization to race ahead of the elevation decision.\n- Preserve hide-to-tray behavior for the main-window close action while making the decline dialog’s close action terminate the process.\n\nEnhancements:\n- Centralize elevation gate transitions and route both pre-flight and decline-dialog actions through shared elevation actions.\n- Mount the decline dialog during the pre-initialization surface and keep authentication, background services, and routing behind the startup gate.\n\nTests:\n- Replace source-string elevation checks with contract tests covering elevation policy, gate transitions, native actions, startup gating, and quit behavior.\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated description by cubic. -->\n---\n## Summary by cubic\nGates Windows startup on an early UAC pre-flight and centralizes the elevation gate. Previously UAC ran after the frontend started and “Close mausVoice” hid to tray; now full init waits behind a single gate and “Close mausVoice” quits the process.\n\n- Single readiness flow: `useElevationStartupReady`, `canRunPostElevationInit`, and `isReadyForFullApp` gate auth/router/Mixpanel/receivers; removed scattered elevation checks.\n- One write-site for clearing the gate via `releaseElevationStartupGate`; `runStartupElevationPreflight` owns prefs read, UAC call, and hold/release; `elevationStartupPending` defaults true and clears off non‑Windows or after the UAC decision.\n- Elevation decline UX during pre-init: moved `ElevationDeclinedDialog` to `AppWithLoading`; actions route through `launchNormallyAfterElevationDecline` and `quitAfterElevationDecline`.\n- Adds native quit: `quit_app` command wired through `commands.quitApp` in `@maus-inc/desktop-native-apis` and `native.repo`; decline dialog’s “Close mausVoice” exits the process; main-window close still hides to tray.\n- Tests focus on contracts: elevation and native action state transitions, startup gating, and Rust-only setup/close-handler pins (including `quit_app` exposure).\n\n<sup>Written for commit 54a7171a206f5d069abf4a3b11a5fe46c88f2b5f. Summary will update on new commits.</sup>\n\n<a href=\"https://cubic.dev/pr/maus-inc/mausVoice/pull/100?utm_source=github\" target=\"_blank\