+      "description": "Draft validation branch for the PR #63 review follow-ups. Implementation and final verification are in progress.\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated description by cubic. -->\n---\n## Summary by cubic\nRoutes plaintext HTTP through a validated, cancellable Rust client and moves audio import to a Rust‑owned picker. Unifies pill geometry coordinate spaces to fix composer anchoring and restores tight resample checks while pinning all ONNX artifacts by SHA‑256.\n\n- Security/Networking\n  - Adds `private_http_request`/`cancel_private_http_request`: allow loopback/RFC1918/IPv6 unique‑local/.local only, reject credentials, validate each redirect (max 5), disable proxies, cap body/response (128 MiB/32 MiB). AbortSignal cancels native requests, pre‑start aborts are preserved via a TTL’d queue, cleanup is per‑request, and active/pre‑start capacities are isolated. Tests cover host policy and cancellation ordering.\n  - Introduces `secureFetch` (`src/utils/secure-fetch.utils.ts`): keep curated HTTPS in `@tauri-apps/plugin-http`; route all plaintext HTTP to the Rust validator. Replaces direct plugin usage across Ollama/Speaches/OpenRouter/model‑provider/sidecars. Removes plaintext `http://` globs from `http:default`; CSP `connect-src` stays a curated HTTPS allow‑list with updated contract tests.\n\n- Product/Models/CI/Geometry/Updater\n  - Audio import: Rust owns the OS picker and may return null; `TranscriptionRepo.importAudioFile()` takes no path. UI retains dialog state on cancel and disables buttons during import.\n  - Transcription: apply `noSpeechProb` gating whenever segments exist (language‑agnostic), keep English phrase filter off for non‑English, and treat `auto` as English for spoken commands. Adds `aria-describedby` to the disabled mic and prevents the post‑mount fatal overlay.\n  - Models/CI: require SHA‑256 for every ONNX runtime artifact (graphs and tokenizer/vocabulary) with tests; enable `reqwest` `\"stream\"` and `tokio` `\"macros\"`.\n  - Updater: use `pathToFileURL` via `isDirectInvocation`; supports spaces and Windows drive‑letter paths with tests.\n  - Desktop geometry: report pill rect and monitor work area in the same physical‑pixel space and centralize logical→physical conversion; add epsilon‑based geometry tests. Restore a tight long‑resample timing check as an opt‑in test.\n  - Migration: route private HTTP through `secureFetch`/`private_http_request` and do not add plaintext `http://` capability globs. Update callers to `TranscriptionRepo.importAudioFile()` (no args, handle null). No DB changes.\n\n<sup>Written for commit 0649df61b0b9cce543e8ca637f1964b67de544d7. Summary will update on new commits.</sup>\n\n<a href=\"https://cubic.dev/pr/maus-inc/mausVoice/pull/73?utm_source=github\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" data-no-image-dialog=\"true\"><picture><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\" srcset=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-dark.svg\"><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\" srcset=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-light.svg\"><img alt=\"Review in cubic\" src=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-dark.svg\"></picture></a>\n\n<!-- End of auto-generated description by cubic. -->\n\n## Summary by Sourcery\n\nHarden private-network access and audio importing while tightening transcription behavior, model integrity checks, updater invocation, and related validation coverage.\n\nNew Features:\n- Route plaintext HTTP requests through a validated, cancellable Rust client while retaining curated HTTPS provider access.\n- Move audio-file selection into the Rust-owned native picker with cancellation-aware import UI behavior.\n\nBug Fixes:\n- Apply silence-probability filtering consistently across languages and treat auto-detected dictation as English for spoken commands.\n- Prevent fatal error overlays after the application has mounted.\n- Correct updater direct-invocation detection for paths containing spaces and Windows drive