+      "description": "## Purpose\n\nResumes PR #73 (based on its head `01a25de`) and addresses the two kilo-code-bot superfix review findings.\n\n## Changes\n\n### 1. `packages/rust_gtk_pill/src/pill.rs` — split coordinate spaces in `pill_geometry`\n\n**Finding:** `rect` was reported in physical pixels (`w as f64 * scale`, with `saved_x`/`saved_y` being X11 root coordinates), while `monitor_rect` came from `monitor.workarea()` unscaled (logical). The desktop's composer-anchoring math (`computeComposerRect`) compares the two rects directly, so on any display with `scale != 1` the comparison was off by the scale factor.\n\n**Fix:** scale the workarea by its monitor's own `scale_factor()` into the same physical space — the same logical→physical conversion the X11 placement math already applies (`x11.rs:383-387`). This also matches the other platform pills: Windows reports both rects physical (`GetWindowRect`/`rcWork`), macOS reports both in points, and Tauri window positions on X11 are physical. The conversion is extracted into `workarea_to_physical` and locked in with display-free unit tests (scale 2x, scale 1x, and a regression guard that pill + monitor rects share one space).\n\n### 2. `packages/rust_transcription/src/audio.rs` — relaxed resample timing budget\n\n**Finding:** the 5-min/48 kHz resample test's budget was relaxed 15 s → 60 s (4x looser) in the PR #73 merge, letting a genuine `resample_to_rate` regression pass CI silently. (The relaxation originated in #77 to stop `cargo test --lib` flaking on shared runners — restoring 15 s outright would reintroduce that flake.)\n\n**Fix:** split the test — the default `resampling_handles_long_input_without_panic` keeps the deterministic length check so CI never flakes on wall-clock, and a new `#[ignore]`d `resampling_long_input_stays_within_time_budget` enforces the original tight `< 15_000 ms` budget when run explicitly (`cargo test -- --ignored`). Real slowdowns stay detectable without making default CI flaky.\n\n## Verification\n\n- No Rust toolchain is reachable from this sandbox (rust-lang.org, GitHub release assets, and Debian mirrors all blocked), so compile/test verification relies on CI: `lint-desktop.yml` runs `cargo clippy --all-targets -- -D warnings` + `cargo test` on `rust_gtk_pill` (ubuntu) and the unit workflows run `rust_transcription --lib`.\n- New gtk pill tests are pure arithmetic (no display needed) and follow the existing `visibility_tests` glob-import pattern; `Rect` resolves via `crate::ipc`.\n\n## Summary by Sourcery\n\nEnsure GTK pill geometry uses consistent physical coordinates and preserve reliable resampling performance checks without flaky default tests.\n\nBug Fixes:\n- Align GTK pill and monitor rectangles in the same physical coordinate space, fixing HiDPI composer anchoring and X11 monitor placement.\n- Restore detection of long-input resampling performance regressions with an opt-in 15-second timing test while keeping default CI deterministic.\n\nEnhancements:\n- Centralize logical-to-physical monitor geometry conversion and add regression coverage for scaled and unscaled displays.\n\nTests:\n- Split long-input resampling coverage into a deterministic output-length test and an ignored wall-clock budget test.\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated description by cubic. -->\n---\n## Summary by cubic\nAligns GTK pill and monitor geometry to the same physical pixel space and restores the original 15 s resample budget via an opt-in test, fixing HiDPI composer anchoring while keeping CI deterministic.\n\n- `rust_gtk_pill`: Adds `logical_rect_to_physical` and uses it for pill geometry reporting, X11 monitor hit-testing, and primary-monitor anchoring so pill and monitor rects match in physical pixels. Updates `ipc::Rect` docs to reflect platform-specific units. Adds unit tests with epsilon-based float assertions. No behavior change on scale=1 or Wayland.\n- `rust_transcription`: Splits the long-input resample test. The default test asserts output length only; a new `#[ignore]`d test enforces the original < 15_000 ms budget. Shares constants/helpers between the two to prevent drift.\n\n<sup>Written for commit 1c4b00b05f2b6cc6922cb86f008e6c2e62d52026. Summary will update on new commits.</sup>\n\n<a href=\"https://cubic.dev/pr/maus-inc/mausVoice/pull/103?utm_source=github\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" data-no-image-dialog=\"true\"><picture><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\" srcset=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-dark.svg\"><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\" srcset=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-light.svg\"><img alt=\"Review in cubic\" src=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-dark.svg\"></picture></a>\n\n<!-- End of auto-generated description by cubic. -->\n\n"
