+      "description": "## Purpose\n\nFixes failing Desktop Rust lint/unit jobs on the current superfix head and the remaining assertive review findings from PR #63.\n\n## Changes\n- IPv6 loopback host matching (`::1` as `url::Url::host_str()` emits it)\n- Windows-safe empty-args terminal allow-list test\n- Percent-decode leftover `%` treated as a terminal value (with tests)\n- Relax long resample timing budget for `cargo test --lib`\n- Doc/toolchain drift: pnpm 10.34.5, flavors, installer paths, sidecar env names, SenseVoice, architecture split, eval coverage, bindings example path\n\n## Verification\nCI: `cargo clippy -D warnings`, `cargo test --lib`, desktop lint/tests.\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated description by cubic. -->\n---\n## Summary by cubic\nFixes CI Rust failures and closes remaining PR #63 review items. Tightens network/CSP, hardens transcription and sanitize (spoken commands + silence-hallucination filter), stabilizes startup/updater, and adds a reviewable composer and style‑hotkey management.\n\n- Network/CSP: restrict `http:default` (`@tauri-apps/plugin-http`) to loopback/RFC1918/link‑local/`*.local`; keep `remote.urls` loopback‑only; accept IPv6 `::1`; contract tests cover CSP `connect-src` and plugin scope.\n- Startup/build: keep `react-intl`/`@formatjs` in the React vendor chunk; early overlay also catches vendor init failures; copy Windows Sherpa DLLs by on‑disk names.\n- Updater: publish a signed `latest.json` only when `UPDATER_*` minisign secrets exist; verify macOS manual installer signatures; handle read‑only installs; status‑aware UI and tests.\n- Transcription/import: preserve overlap‑merged transcripts; apply replacements to segments; add spoken formatting commands and a silence‑hallucination filter (prefs‑gated); new `transcription_import_audio`; store sanitized text.\n- Backend/pill: app routes keep incomplete “%” literal (incl. decode‑once path); WAV loader reads from an open file; Windows import validates file identity (TOCTOU); add `@tauri-apps/plugin-dialog`; declare `desktop`/`mobile` cfgs; forward pill geometry (physical pixels) to the UI.\n- Commands/UI: add `transcription_import_audio`, `hotkey_replace_style_hotkeys`, composer page and voice instruction recorder; scope `keys_held` and assistant sync to the main window; reject empty style‑hotkey prefixes, snapshot edits, and revoke legacy always‑allow keys; improve remote output review and guard NaN tenure.\n- Data model: migrations 075–077 add tone structured fields and feature prefs (style cycling, hallucination filter flag, review‑before‑insert, agent tool/timeouts, `spoken_commands_enabled`); defaults keep previous behavior.\n- CI/docs: least‑privilege workflows; expanded native test matrix; secret history scans with pinned `gitleaks`; updater/CSP contract tests; docs updated (tool registry IDs, SenseVoice, architecture/setup). Dev Node from `.nvmrc` (v24), `pnpm` 10.34.5, Rust 1.88.0.\n\n- Rollout and migration\n  - Releases publish stable `latest.json` only when `UPDATER_*` signing secrets are configured.\n  - When adding a provider host, update CSP `connect-src` in `apps/desktop/src-tauri/tauri.conf.json` and the `http:default` allow‑list in `apps/desktop/src-tauri/capabilities/default.json`.\n  - Replace style shortcuts via the atomic `hotkey_replace_style_hotkeys` command (empty prefixes are rejected).\n  - Developer setup: Node v24 from `.nvmrc`, `pnpm` 10.34.5, and Rust 1.88.0; database migrations run on startup.\n\n<sup>Written for commit 43786f86fa878bb977c164cd563e2dcd06aa82b3. Summary will update on new commits.</sup>\n\n<a href=\"https://cubic.dev/pr/maus-inc/mausVoice/pull/77?utm_source=github\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" data-no-image-dialog=\"true\"><picture><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\" srcset=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-dark.svg\"><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\" srcset=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-light.svg\"><img alt=\"Review in cubic\" src=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-dark.svg\"></picture></a>\n\n<!-- End of auto-generated description by cubic. -->\n\n## Summary by Sourcery\n\nHarden desktop security and reliability while resolving Rust CI failures and aligning tooling, transcription, updater, composer, and documentation behavior with the current application.\n\nNew Features:\n- Add composer floating-window commands and support for recording and exchanging composer text.\n- Add SenseVoice as a supported local transcription model and document its setup and runtime behavior.\n\nBug Fixes:\n- Fix loopback URL validation for IPv6, preserve literal percent characters in routes, retain transcript formatting when no sanitization is needed, and preserve spacing after partial spoken-command edits.\n- Harden manual installer downloads with trusted redirect validation, size limits, and detached signature verification before opening.\n- Prevent invalid empty style-hotkey prefixes, stale always-allow permissions, invalid analytics tenure values, and unsafe filesystem or terminal-command access.\n\nEnhancements:\n- Improve floating-window geometry reporting across display scale factors and make platform-specific dependencies and toolchain configuration compatible with CI.\n- Stabilize composer editing, transcription imports, hallucination filtering, remote output review, and native pill behavior.\n\nBuild:\n- Pin Rust 1.88.0, update pnpm documentation to 10.34.5, declare platform cfgs, and adjust platform-specific dependency configuration.\n\nCI:\n- Relax the long resampling test budget and address current clippy and cross-platform Rust CI failures.\n\nDocumentation:\n- Refresh development, release, architecture, local-model, testing, installer, and native API documentation to match current workflows, models, environment names, and build paths.\n\nTests:\n- Extend coverage for IPv6 loopback handling, literal percent routes, Windows-safe terminal validation, installer security lim