+      "description": "Agent A17 mission complete. See commit message for details. Fixes embedded font fallback on all three pill platforms and adds crossfade/slide animation from 'Click to dictate' to 'Drag To Move' keyed to drag/long-press state.\n\n## Summary by Sourcery\n\nImprove pill typography and provide animated visual feedback for drag interactions across all desktop platforms.\n\nNew Features:\n- Animate the pill’s idle prompt between “Click to dictate” and “Drag To Move” during dragging and long-press gestures.\n\nBug Fixes:\n- Ensure embedded Satoshi font resolution is reliable across GTK, macOS, and Windows instead of silently falling back to system fonts.\n\nEnhancements:\n- Render pill labels and tooltips at the intended normal/medium Satoshi weight and share crossfade, slide, and font-error handling across platforms.\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated description by cubic. -->\n---\n## Summary by cubic\nEmbeds and reliably resolves the Satoshi font across GTK, macOS, and Windows, and animates the idle pill label between “Click to dictate” and “Drag To Move” on drag/long‑press. Previously labels could fall back to system fonts and stayed bold/static; now they render in Satoshi at normal weight with a crossfade/slide, improving clarity and drag affordance.\n\n- GTK (`packages/rust_gtk_pill`): registers the embedded TTF via fontconfig FFI (FcInitLoadConfigAndFonts + FcConfigAppFontAddFile) and prepends `FONTCONFIG_PATH`; draw and tooltip paths use normal weight.\n- macOS (`packages/rust_macos_pill`): writes the font to a temp file and atomically renames before CoreText registration; logs if NSFont cannot resolve; draw/tooltips use normal weight.\n- Windows (`packages/rust_windows_pill`): registers with GDI, refreshes the DirectWrite collection once, and passes it to `create_text_format`; uses weight 500 (Medium) to avoid synthesized bold; logs and panics on unrecoverable resolve failures; tooltip uses non‑bold.\n- Shared (`packages/rust_pill_shared`): adds label text/constants and helpers (`LABEL_*`, `label_crossfade_alpha`, `label_slide_y`, `LABEL_SPRING_STIFFNESS`) and `log_font_error`; adds `drag_label_t`/`drag_label_velocity` to `PillState` and wires tick/draw across platforms.\n- Rendering: all platforms crossfade/slide between idle and drag labels keyed to drag/long‑press; idle label shows only when expanded and hovered/assistant_active; tooltips render at normal weight. No public API changes.\n\n<sup>Written for commit 2756c4af3c0819180ffe83103e70f2a8e7b676e0. Summary will update on new commits.</sup>\n\n<a href=\"https://cubic.dev/pr/maus-inc/mausVoice/pull/95?utm_source=github\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" data-no-image-dialog=\"true\"><picture><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\" srcset=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-dark.svg\"><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\" srcset=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-light.svg\"><img alt=\"Review in cubic\" src=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-dark.svg\"></picture></a>\n\n<!-- End of auto-generated description by cubic. -->\n\n"
