+      "description": "## Summary\n\nReplaces the per-segment paste-and-flash model with a backlog model for dictation output routing. When no editable target is focused, segments are silently accumulated in a Zustand-backed backlog. The entire backlog is delivered in one shot on the first of: (a) user focuses an editable input, or (b) transcription completes.\n\n## Changes\n\n### `apps/desktop/src/state/app.state.ts`\n- Added `dictationBacklog: string[]` and `dictationBacklogNonce: number` to `AppState` / `INITIAL_APP_STATE`.\n\n### `apps/desktop/src/utils/output-routing.utils.ts`\n- `insertLocalTranscriptOutputViaPaste` now accepts optional `suppressClipboardFlash` param (default `true` for backward compat). When `false` the pill flash is suppressed — the key lever for eliminating per-segment spam.\n- New exports: `getDictationBacklog`, `hasDictationBacklog`, `appendToDictationBacklog`, `clearDictationBacklog`, `incrementDictationBacklogNonce`, `drainDictationBacklog`.\n- `drainDictationBacklog` joins backlog + optional new segment, delivers via paste, clears backlog on success. Uses `suppressClipboardFlash=false` so the one permitted flash fires. Protects against cross-session contamination via nonce comparison.\n\n### `apps/desktop/src/strategies/dictation.strategy.ts`\n- `checkFocusedPasteTarget()` helper wrapping the existing Tauri command.\n- `backlogActive` field + `hasBacklog` getter.\n- `checkAndDrainBacklog()` public method (serialized on pasteQueue) for external polling.\n- **`handleInterimSegment`** refactored: remote mode unchanged; non-editable → backlog append (no flash); editable+drain drain backlog+paste current; editable+empty paste live.\n- `onBeforeStart` now also clears backlog and increments session nonce.\n- `handleFinalStreamedTranscript` drains any remaining backlog before returning.\n- `cleanup` resets `backlogActive` and clears backlog.\n\n### `apps/desktop/src/components/root/DictationSideEffects.tsx`\n- New 1-second polling interval that calls `strategy.checkAndDrainBacklog()` while the strategy reports `hasBacklog`. Covers the \"user clicks an input while not speaking\" case.\n\n## Key behaviours\n- **Zero** clipboard writes and **zero** pill flashes during dictation with no editable target.\n- At most **one** clipboard write + **one** pill flash per delivery event.\n- Real-time into a focused field keeps working with same latency.\n- Button/timer activation paths drain backlog once on finalize.\n- Remote output mode bypasses backlog (unchanged).\n\nCloses #(dictation clipboard spam issue)\n\n## Summary by Sourcery\n\nAdopt backlog-based dictation output routing to consolidate unfocused segments into a single delivery and prevent clipboard notification spam.\n\nNew Features:\n- Buffer dictation output when no editable target is focused and deliver the accumulated text when an input is focused or transcription completes.\n\nBug Fixes:\n- Eliminate repeated clipboard writes and notification flashes for dictation segments produced without an editable target.\n\nEnhancements:\n- Preserve live insertion for focused editable targets and keep remote output routing unchanged.\n- Protect backlog delivery across dictation sessions and serialize focus polling and backlog draining.\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated description by cubic. -->\n---\n## Summary by cubic\nBuffers dictation segments when no editable target is focused and delivers them in one insertion, eliminating repeated “Copied to clipboard” flashes. Previously each interim segment pasted and flashed; now we backlog while unfocused and drain on focus or finalize, preserving live insertion and leaving remote delivery unchanged.\n\n- Adds `dictationBacklog` plus a session `dictationBacklogNonce`; clear/increment on session start and clear on cleanup.\n- Drains via `insertLocalOutput`, honoring per‑app insertion method and paste keybinds; returns `{ delivered, copiedToClipboard }` with pre/post nonce checks and preserves backlog on failure.\n- Adds `checkFocusedPasteTarget()` and a 1s poll during active sessions to drain when an input becomes focused; all drains serialize on the paste queue and log probe errors.\n- Aligns spacing with the live path and avoids double‑spacing when draining alongside a new segment.\n- Clipboard behavior: zero writes/flashes while backlogging; at most one per delivery event; remote output bypasses backlog.\n\n- Migration:\n  - Update callers of `insertLocalTranscriptOutputViaPaste(text, keybind)` to handle the returned `PasteOutcome` and remove the third argument.\n  - If you call `insertLocalOutput`, handle its new `PasteOutcome | undefined` return type.\n\n<sup>Written for commit 5ab4e0f2f25c8f29f74eae78b5de49d8153c83a0. Summary will update on new commits.</sup>\n\n<a href=\"https://cubic.dev/pr/maus-inc/mausVoice/pull/94?utm_source=github\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" data-no-image-dialog=\"true\"><picture><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\" srcset=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-dark.svg\"><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\" srcset=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-light.svg\"><img alt=\"Review in cubic\" src=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-dark.svg\"></picture></a>\n\n<!-- End of auto-generated description by cubic. -->\n\n"
