+      "description": "Agent A14 — Light-mode inner shadow on buttons is too heavy\n\n## What I changed (file:line level)\n- **apps/desktop/src/styles/shadows.ts:12-33** — reduced `premiumSurface.light` inset highlight alphas for all states to a light, crisp top emboss:\n  - `rest`: `highlight(0.72) → 0.42`, `highlight(0.28) → 0.14` (kept outer shadows `ink(0.04/0.08/0.06)`)\n  - `hover`: `0.85 → 0.58`, `0.35 → 0.20` (outer shadows unchanged)\n  - `active`: `ink(0.12) → 0.07`, `highlight(0.35) → 0.18` (outer `ink(0.06)` unchanged)\n  - `selected`: `0.20 → 0.18`, `0.08 → 0.06` (outer `0.18/0.22` unchanged)\n  - `premiumSurface.dark` left pixel-identical\n- **apps/desktop/src/components/dashboard/DashboardEntryLayout.test.ts:52-55** — fix type error (`children` required) to unblock `check-types`/`lint` (out-of-lane, minimal)\n\n## Root cause found\nLight-mode `premiumSurface.light` used high-opacity white insets (0.72/0.85 at 1px, 0.28/0.35 at 2px) that rendered as a thick bright band on both light flat surfaces (`level1 #FDFBF8`) and dark contained surfaces (`inkSolid.base #1A1712`). On dark contained, 0.72 white produced `rgb(191,190,189)` vs dark's refined `rgb(44,44,46)` at 0.08 — 4× brighter, reading as heavy engraved edge rather than subtle machined-keycap emboss. The 2px blur alphas were also 2× dark's effective contrast. Active's dark inset `ink(0.12)` was too strong for a pressed inner shadow on cream, creating muddy interior vs dark's intentional heavier `darkInk(0.45)` on near-black. Selected was slightly high at 0.20. Drop shadows were intentionally left unchanged per A16 boundary.\n\n## Tests added\nNo new unit tests (shadow tokens are visual). Verified via existing `test:unit` (569 tests pass) and manual visual matrix covering rest/hover/active/selected/disabled × light/dark (see Verification).\n\n## i18n updated\nNone — no user-facing strings changed.\n\n## Out-of-lane findings (for other agents)\n- **DashboardEntryLayout.test.ts** was failing `tsc --noEmit` due to missing required `children` prop in `createElement(DashboardEntryLayout, {maxWidth})` calls; fixed minimally.\n- **premiumSurface.light** is shared with `MuiCard`/`MuiPaper`/`MuiFab`/`MuiDialog`/`MuiTooltip` (A16 scope). Verified lighter emboss remains appropriate for those surfaces: on `level1 #FDFBF8` the new 0.42/0.14 produces a subtle near-white edge (~~253.8 vs 254.4 previously, Δ ~0.6 rgb) still visible but not heavy; on dark contained the drop from 191→122 rgb is significantly lighter. Cards with `hairline` + premiumSurface will appear more refined; A16 should confirm drop-shadow evolution doesn't need adjustment.\n- **MuiToggleButton** has no `boxShadow` — consistent with not being a premiumSurface consumer, but if toggles should mirror flat button emboss when selected, A16 may want to add `premiumSurface.*.selected` there (would affect dark mode).\n- **pnpm-lock.yaml** transiently showed `smol-toml` addition after `pnpm install`; reverted.\n\n## Verification commands run and results\n- `pnpm --filter desktop check-types` → pass (after test fix)\n- `pnpm --filter desktop lint` → pass (0 warnings, prettier + oxlint)\n- `pnpm --filter desktop run test:unit` → 57 passed, 569 tests, 0 failures\n- `pnpm --filter desktop run build` (tsc + vite) → built in 26s, no errors\n- `pnpm run build` (turbo) → 10 tasks successful, cached 9, desktop rebuilt successfully\n- Visual matrix: compared light rest/hover/active/selected and dark equivalents; dark unchanged (pixel diff 0). Light buttons now show subtle 1px white edge + softer 2px halo, no muddy dark inset at rest/hover; active shows light inset dark at 0.07 (subtle press) vs previous 0.12 (heavy).\n\n## Summary by Sourcery\n\nRefine light-mode button embossing while preserving dark-mode shadows and outer shadow behavior.\n\nBug Fixes:\n- Lighten light-mode button inner shadows across rest, hover, active, and selected states to prevent heavy highlights and muddy pressed styling.\n\nTests:\n- Fix DashboardEntryLayout test fixtures so type checking and linting complete successfully.\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated description by cubic. -->\n---\n## Summary by cubic\nLightens light‑mode button inner highlights for a crisper top emboss. Old behavior: thick white insets that read engraved; new behavior: a subtle 1px highlight with a softer halo; dark mode and outer drop shadows are unchanged.\n\n- Lowers `premiumSurface.light` inset alphas across rest/hover/active/selected; active from `ink(0.12)`/`highlight(0.35)` to `ink(0.07)`/`highlight(0.18)`.\n- Leaves outer drop shadows unchanged and `premiumSurface.dark` pixel-identical; documents light‑mode shadow rationale inline for future tuning.\n- Keeps `DashboardEntryLayout` `children` required; updates its test to pass an explicit child to satisfy type checks.\n\n<sup>Written for commit 3c4b6af812ad9e7fd8006f2c9cf3bf51b8eed895. Summary will update on new commits.</sup>\n\n<a href=\"https://cubic.dev/pr/maus-inc/mausVoice/pull/91?utm_source=github\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" data-no-image-dialog=\"true\"><picture><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\" srcset=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-dark.svg\"><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\" srcset=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-light.svg\"><img alt=\"Review in cubic\" src=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-dark.svg\"></picture></a>\n\n<!-- End of auto-generated description by cubic. -->\n\n"
