+      "description": "## Summary\n\nFixes [Agent A05] — in dark mode the \"selected\" outline on provider/API-key cards and model rows was invisible (reported for the Personal Deepgram card). Light mode was unaffected.\n\n## Root cause\n\nTwo compounding defects in `ApiKeyCard` (`apps/desktop/src/components/settings/ApiKeyList.tsx`):\n\n1. **Ring color frozen to the light value.** The selected `boxShadow` ring used an sx callback reading `theme.palette.primary.main`. With MUI CSS variables enabled, `theme.palette` on the callback theme always holds the **light** scheme values, so the ring rendered as `0 0 0 1px #1A1712` (dark ink) **in both schemes** — invisible against the `#161617` onyx card.\n2. **MUI's dark-scheme Paper override resets the border.** For outlined `Paper`, MUI emits `*:where([data-mui-color-scheme=\"dark\"]) .css-… { border: 1px solid <dark divider> }` which — same specificity, later in the cascade — clobbers the sx `borderColor` in dark mode. So the border alone can't carry the selection signal either.\n\n## Fix\n\n- Added one shared, theme-aware selected outline — `selectedOutlineSx(theme)` in `apps/desktop/src/styles/selection.ts` — consumed by every selected-card/row pattern:\n  - stroke = `text.primary` (dark ink on cream in light mode, light text on onyx in dark mode) — same token the AI-menu `activeRowSx` already uses for its rail, so no new color language;\n  - the crisp `0 0 0 1px` ring is emitted via `theme.vars.palette.text.primary` — a CSS variable that resolves per active color scheme at runtime, and lives in `box-shadow` so MUI's dark border override can't touch it;\n  - selected hover keeps the stroke; global `:focus-visible` outline untouched.\n- Applied to: `ApiKeyCard` (selected), `EditApiKeyCard` (active editing state), and the active model **download row** in `AITranscriptionConfiguration.tsx`. Agent-mode / post-processing provider lists reuse `ApiKeyList`, so they inherit the fix.\n\nContrast (WCAG non-text, ≥ 3:1 required): light stroke `#1A1712` vs card `#FDFBF8` ≈ **16:1**; dark stroke `rgb(242,241,238)` vs card `#161617` ≈ **16:1**.\n\n## Verification\n\n- `pnpm --filter desktop check-types` — only **pre-existing** errors remain (see below; none in touched files)\n- `pnpm --filter desktop lint` — touched files prettier + oxlint clean\n- `pnpm --filter desktop test` — all 57 unit files pass incl. new `src/styles/selection.test.ts` (3 tests: var-based ring, per-scheme contrast ≥ 3:1, hover keeps stroke); integration/evals failures are missing-API-key env failures\n- `pnpm run build` — desktop blocked by pre-existing `DashboardEntryLayout.test.ts` TS errors; `run-vite-with-flavor.mjs build` (the actual bundle) succeeds\n- jsdom render of the exact card sx confirmed the generated CSS emits `border-color`/`box-shadow: … var(--app-palette-text-primary)` in both schemes\n\n## Out-of-lane findings (for other agents)\n\n- **AssemblyAI commit `302b3e8` (#85) does not type-check / test green on `arena/01a01761-mausvoice`:** `'model' does not exist in type 'AssemblyAITestIntegrationArgs'/'AssemblyAITranscriptionArgs'` in `src/settings/api-key-provider-config.tsx:126` and `src/repos/assemblyai-transcribe-audio.test.ts` (multiple lines); `'@maus-inc/voice-ai' has no exported member 'ASSEMBLYAI_TRANSCRIPTION_MODELS'` in `src/repos/model-provider.repo.ts:2` and `src/repos/transcribe-audio.repo.ts`. Likely missing `pnpm gen:bindings` + a rebuild of `@maus-inc/voice-ai` — those tests also fail at runtime in the unit suite. This blocks `pnpm run build` for everyone until fixed.\n- `src/components/dashboard/DashboardEntryLayout.test.ts:52,55` — pre-existing TS errors (`maxWidth` overload; missing `children`), also blocks `tsc`.\n- `src/components/common/ToolPermissionPrompt.tsx:109` and `src/components/onboarding/KeybindingsForm.tsx:202` — remaining `borderColor: \"primary.main\"` uses (string form, so they flip to white in dark and are visible — not the same bug), candidates for the shared helper if those lanes want consistency.\n- `pnpm-lock.yaml` — was stale (root `package.json` declares `smol-toml@^1.3.0`, lockfile missing it); synced it so `pnpm install --frozen-lockfile` works. Pure lockfile addition, no dependency changes.\n\n## Summary by Sourcery\n\nMake selected provider, API-key, and model rows visibly distinguishable across color schemes.\n\nBug Fixes:\n- Restore visible selected-state outlines for provider/API-key cards and active model download rows in both light and dark modes.\n\nEnhancements:\n- Centralize scheme-aware selection styling and preserve selected strokes during hover while keeping focus-visible behavior unchanged.\n\nBuild:\n- Sync the pnpm lockfile with the declared smol-toml dependency.\n\nTests:\n- Add coverage for CSS-variable-based outline rendering, configurable ring width, and WCAG contrast across color schemes.\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated description by cubic. -->\n---\n## Summary by cubic\nFixes invisible selected outlines in dark mode on provider/API-key cards and model download rows by using a scheme-aware ring; also centralizes hover handling and makes the ring width configurable.\n\n- Adds selectedOutlineSx(theme, ringWidth=1) that draws a crisp 0 0 0 Npx ring via theme vars (text.primary) in box-shadow, so it remains visible in both color schemes and ignores Paper border overrides.\n- Applies the helper to ApiKeyCard (selection + hover), EditApiKeyCard (selection), and active model download rows.\n- ApiKeyCard now owns hover: selected keeps its stroke; unselected uses action.active. The helper is a pure selected-state style.\n- Adds tests for CSS-var ring generation, configurable ring width, and ≥3:1 contrast in both schemes.\n- Syncs lockfile to include `smol-toml`; no app behavior changes.\n\n<sup>Written for commit c5ef04b9c1cc0f298008d07bcf6451ec84ae25c1. Summary will update on new commits.</sup>\n\n<a href=\"https://cubic.dev/pr/maus-inc/mausVoice/pull/92?utm_source=github\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" data-no-image-dialog=\"true\"><picture><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\" srcset=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-dark.svg\"><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\" srcset=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-light.svg\"><img alt=\"Review in cubic\" src=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-dark.svg\"></picture></a>\n\n<!-- End of auto-generated description by cubic. -->\n\n"
