+      "description": "## Summary\n\nCloses the \"AssemblyAI transcription doesn't let you pick a model to actually transcribe with\" finding (Agent A24).\n\nAssemblyAI transcription previously had no model field and always used the provider default. This adds a working model picker, persists the choice in the existing per-key `transcriptionModel` column (no migration), and passes it through the batch transcription pipeline as `speech_models`.\n\n## Model IDs (verified against current AssemblyAI docs)\n\n- `universal-3-5-pro` — flagship, 18 languages (AssemblyAI recommended)\n- `universal-2` — 99 languages\n- Unset ⇒ omit `speech_models` ⇒ AssemblyAI default (`[\"universal-3-5-pro\", \"universal-2\"]`), preserving today's behavior.\n\nLegacy `best`/`nano` tiers are no longer exposed: the singular `speech_model` parameter is deprecated (ignored by the API), and `nano` has been removed.\n\n## What changed\n\n- `packages/voice-ai/src/assemblyai.utils.ts` — `ASSEMBLYAI_TRANSCRIPTION_MODELS`, `resolveSpeechModel` validation (unknown id → clear error, no silent fallback), `speech_models` in the transcript payload, model-aware `assemblyaiTestIntegration`.\n- `apps/desktop/src/components/settings/api-key-provider-config.tsx` — dedicated AssemblyAI config with a `transcriptionModel` field + helper text; Test validates key **and** model.\n- `apps/desktop/src/repos/model-provider.repo.ts` — `AssemblyAIModelProviderRepo.getTranscriptionModels()` returns the allowlist so the card shows the free-solo autocomplete (same UX as Deepgram/xAI).\n- `apps/desktop/src/repos/transcribe-audio.repo.ts` + `repos/index.ts` — `AssemblyAITranscribeAudioRepo` takes the stored model and forwards it; metadata now reports the chosen model.\n- Docs + i18n catalogs updated.\n\nNo Rust / command / bindings changes, no DB migration, no CSP change (AssemblyAI host already allowlisted).\n\n## Verification\n\n- `pnpm --filter @maus-inc/voice-ai build` + `test` ✅\n- `pnpm --filter desktop check-types` ✅\n- `pnpm --filter desktop lint` ✅\n- `pnpm --filter desktop test:unit` — 542 passed ✅ (integration/evals need `GROQ_API_KEY`, unchanged)\n- `pnpm --filter desktop build` ✅\n\n## Summary by Sourcery\n\nEnable configurable speech-model selection for AssemblyAI batch transcription while preserving default behavior and legacy settings compatibility.\n\nNew Features:\n- Add an optional AssemblyAI speech-model picker for batch transcription, supporting Universal-3.5 Pro and Universal-2.\n- Persist the selected model with provider settings and expose it through transcription metadata.\n\nBug Fixes:\n- Preserve compatibility with legacy AssemblyAI model values by migrating them to current successors and reject unknown models before making network requests.\n\nEnhancements:\n- Send model-specific AssemblyAI batch transcription requests while retaining provider defaults when no model is selected.\n- Validate the selected model during integration tests and expose AssemblyAI's supported models in provider configuration.\n\nDocumentation:\n- Document AssemblyAI batch transcription model selection, fallback behavior, legacy model migration, and validation.\n\nTests:\n- Add coverage for model payloads, default behavior, legacy migration, invalid models, integration validation, settings configuration, and transcription metadata.\n\nChores:\n- Update localized settings catalogs for the new AssemblyAI model configuration."
