+      "description": "## Purpose\n\nRetranscribe on History/Home had almost no user-visible feedback: the row tooltip changed, the dialog closed, and errors used a snackbar, but there was no loading toast, no success toast, and no durable completed signal on the row. The success-ID `setTimeout` in the dialog could also race if the same row was retranscribed again before the previous timer fired.\n\nThis PR gives the flow a single owner for in-flight / completed / error, and renders that state on every surface that already shares `TranscriptionRow` (History and Home).\n\n## What changed\n\n- **Row button (`TranscriptRow`)**: spinner + `disabled` + `aria-busy` while `retranscribingIds` contains the row; checkmark while `retranscriptionSuccessIds` contains it; state-aware tooltip/`aria-label`. Disabled tooltip works via a `<span>` wrapper. `prefers-reduced-motion` uses a determinate spinner (no pulse).\n- **Dialog (`RetranscribeDialog`)**: still closes on submit so work continues in the background. Submit is idempotent and disabled while that id is in flight. Lifecycle (IDs, toasts, success timer) moved out of the dialog.\n- **Action (`retranscribeTranscription`)**: owns begin → work → success/error → generation-scoped success clear. A second submit for an already in-flight row is a no-op. Parallel rows do not share timers. One loading toast when the first job starts; one success toast when the last job finishes.\n- **Toasts**: in-app snackbar (same channel as the existing error path) plus additive `showPersistentToast` / `showCompletionToast` on the native pill.\n- **Tests**: pure state transitions; action races (double submit, parallel rows, stale timer); component states (spinner / check / idle).\n\n## i18n\n\n- Added `Retranscription complete`.\n- Dropped unused `Retranscribe audio` (aria-label now reuses the existing clip strings).\n- Ran `pnpm --filter desktop i18n`.\n\n## Verification\n\n- `pnpm --filter desktop check-types`\n- `pnpm --filter desktop lint`\n- `pnpm --filter desktop test:unit` — 545 passed\n- `pnpm --filter desktop run build`\n\nHand verification of History/Home UI is left to review (this sandbox has no signed desktop binary).\n\n## Out-of-lane notes\n\n- `TranscriptionDetailsDialog` already reads `retranscribingIds` / `retranscriptionSuccessIds` for its Retranscribe button; it picks up the shared state without edits (A15 owns later dialog style-select work).\n- `SnackbarEmitter` still always shows a close button, so the in-app loading snackbar is long-lived but not strictly non-dismissible.\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated description by cubic. -->\n---\n## Summary by cubic\nImproves retranscribe feedback and lifecycle ownership: rows show a spinner or static hourglass under reduced motion while in flight, a transient checkmark on success, and coordinated loading/success toasts. Previously the dialog owned a success timer and only errors showed a snackbar; now the action manages per‑row generations, dedupes submits, and syncs toasts safely.\n\n- Centralizes lifecycle in `retranscribeTranscription` with generation guards: skips duplicate submits, isolates timers per row, prunes generation ids after success/error, shows one loading toast when the first job starts and one success toast when the last job finishes; dismisses on error and swallows toast invoke failures.\n- `TranscriptRow`: disabled button with `aria-busy`, state-aware tooltip/`aria-label`, checkmark on completion, and spinner replaced by a static hourglass under reduced motion; flattens icon selection to satisfy Sonar; disabled tooltip works via a span wrapper.\n- `RetranscribeDialog`: still closes on submit; submit is disabled while in flight; opening is skipped for a row already retranscribing.\n- Toasts + i18n: adds `showPersistentToast(message, duration)` and `showCompletionToast` with an explicit 2m loading duration; translates “Retranscription complete” across locales and removes unused “Retranscribe audio”.\n- Tests cover state helpers, action races (double submit, parallel rows, stale timers), error recovery, and row UI states.\n\n<sup>Written for commit c6ad2b6b15d0493f4834984dcd572591e8967ff0. Summary will update on new commits.</sup>\n\n<a href=\"https://cubic.dev/pr/maus-inc/mausVoice/pull/84?utm_source=github\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" data-no-image-dialog=\"true\"><picture><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\" srcset=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-dark.svg\"><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\" srcset=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-light.svg\"><img alt=\"Review in cubic\" src=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-dark.svg\"></picture></a>\n\n<!-- End of auto-generated description by cubic. -->\n\n## Summary by Sourcery\n\nCentralize retranscription lifecycle handling to provide reliable progress, completion, and error feedback across History and Home.\n\nNew Features:\n- Provide visible retranscription progress and completion feedback across transcript rows with loading and success toasts.\n\nBug Fixes:\n- Prevent duplicate retranscription submissions and stale completion timers from corrupting row state or feedback.\n\nEnhancements:\n- Centralize retranscription lifecycle state and coordinate feedback across concurrent jobs.\n- Improve retranscription controls with state-aware accessibility labels, disabled behavior, and reduced-motion support.\n\nTests:\n- Add coverage for retranscription state transitions, concurrent and duplicate actions, stale timers, error recovery, and row UI states.\n\nChores:\n- Add and update retranscription translations across supported locales."
