+      "description": "## Summary\n\nFixes the dictation audio dim slider's thumb visually dipping downward on hover (and during drag).\n\n## Root cause\n\nMUI centers the horizontal slider thumb with `top: '50%'; transform: 'translate(-50%, -50%)'`. `ElasticSlider`'s `&:hover` / `&.Mui-active` overrides replaced that transform with a bare `scale(...)`. Because CSS `transform` is a single property, the bare scale **replaced** the centering translate, re-anchoring the thumb at its top-left corner and dropping its visual center ~8px down-right.\n\n## Change\n\n- Re-compose the centering translate into every thumb state transform (`translate(-50%, -50%) scale(...)`), keeping the geometric center fixed through hover, drag, and keyboard focus.\n- Extracted the inline `sx` into an exported `buildElasticSliderSx(blue, rail)` builder (identical styles) so the fix is unit-testable.\n- Added `THUMB_CENTER_TRANSFORM` constant documenting why the translate must be preserved.\n\n## Tests\n\n- New `ElasticSlider.test.ts` (3 assertions) pinning the rendered `sx` thumb transforms for hover and active states, plus a no-vertical-only-translation guard.\n\n## Verification\n\n- `vitest run` (new test) — 3 passed\n- `tsc --noEmit` — clean\n- `prettier --check` / `oxlint` on touched files — clean\n\nNo i18n strings changed. No Rust changes.\n\n## Summary by Sourcery\n\nPreserve the slider thumb’s geometric centering across interactive states to prevent it from visually dipping when hovered or dragged.\n\nBug Fixes:\n- Keep the ElasticSlider thumb vertically centered during hover and drag scaling.\n\nEnhancements:\n- Extract ElasticSlider styling into a reusable, testable style builder.\n\nTests:\n- Add coverage verifying centered thumb transforms for hover and active states.\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated description by cubic. -->\n---\n## Summary by cubic\nKeeps the desktop `ElasticSlider` thumb centered on hover/drag by preserving the centering translate in state transforms. Previously, a bare `scale(...)` replaced MUI’s translate and re-anchored the thumb down-right; now transforms use `translate(-50%, -50%) scale(...)` to keep the geometric center stable across hover, drag, and focus.\n\n**Review notes**\n- Re-composes the centering translate via `THUMB_CENTER_TRANSFORM` in `ElasticSlider.tsx`.\n- Extracts inline `sx` to `buildElasticSliderSx(blue, rail)` for testability; `ElasticSlider.test.ts` pins hover/active transforms and guards against vertical-only translation.\n- No prop or API changes. Visual-only change; `@mui/material` usage unchanged.\n\n<sup>Written for commit 3645745184d0d619ea2e799665562748a6354c64. Summary will update on new commits.</sup>\n\n<a href=\"https://cubic.dev/pr/maus-inc/mausVoice/pull/86?utm_source=github\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" data-no-image-dialog=\"true\"><picture><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\" srcset=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-dark.svg\"><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\" srcset=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-light.svg\"><img alt=\"Review in cubic\" src=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-dark.svg\"></picture></a>\n\n<!-- End of auto-generated description by cubic. -->\n\n"
