+      "description": "## Summary\n\nFixes the mid-transition header “glitch spasm” and observer/rAF leak on History, Dictionary, Styles, and every other `ScrollListPage` consumer.\n\nThe sticky header’s layout height was driven by `--p = scrollTop / collapseDistance`. Shrinking the header reduced `scrollHeight`, the browser re-clamped `scrollTop` (and overflow-anchor fought the change), which wrote a new `--p` and oscillated exactly in the collapse zone. A `ResizeObserver` on the scroller plus dual `--p` writers and `items.length` in both effect deps amplified the loop and leaked listeners across list mutations.\n\n## What changed\n\n- Single rAF-coalesced writer of `--p` (`attachScrollListCollapse`).\n- Measure only the hidden expanded/collapsed clones — never the scroller or the visible header.\n- Compensating spacer so `headerHeight + spacer === expandedHeight` for every progress (scrollHeight stays constant).\n- `overflow-anchor: none` so the browser cannot retarget scrollTop when the header interpolates.\n- Effects no longer re-subscribe on `items.length`; only `hasItems` (empty ↔ list).\n- `willChange` only while `0 < p < 1`.\n- `prefers-reduced-motion`: instant snap (expanded at top, collapsed otherwise).\n- Empty-state appearance and public props are unchanged. Consumers were not edited.\n\n## Tests\n\n- Pure geometry: progress clamp, title scale direction, header+spacer invariant.\n- Mocked `ResizeObserver` / scroll / matchMedia: cleanup on unmount, no listener growth across 20 remount+refresh cycles, `--p` stays at 0.5 when metrics are re-read mid-scroll.\n\n## Verification\n\n- `pnpm --filter desktop check-types`\n- `pnpm --filter desktop lint`\n- `pnpm --filter desktop test:unit` (544 passed, including 13 new)\n- `pnpm --filter desktop build`\n- `pnpm run build`\n\nCloses the A02 scroll-collapse item against #63.\n\n## Summary by Sourcery\n\nStabilize ScrollListPage sticky-header collapse behavior and clean up its observers, listeners, and animation frames.\n\nBug Fixes:\n- Prevent sticky ScrollListPage headers from oscillating during collapse transitions by stabilizing scroll geometry and scroll anchoring.\n- Eliminate observer, animation-frame, and event-listener leaks across list updates and component remounts.\n- Honor reduced-motion preferences by snapping the header between expanded and collapsed states.\n\nEnhancements:\n- Centralize collapse progress, header measurement, and side-effect lifecycle management in a reusable scroll-collapse utility.\n- Limit measurement to hidden header clones, coalesce progress updates, and apply animation hints only during active transitions.\n\nTests:\n- Add unit coverage for collapse geometry, progress clamping, reduced-motion behavior, mid-scroll remeasurement, and cleanup across repeated remounts and refreshes.\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated description by cubic. -->\n---\n## Summary by cubic\nStops `ScrollListPage` sticky header oscillation and fixes observer/rAF leaks. Old: `--p` updated from `scrollTop` while the header resized, shifting `scrollHeight` and fighting overflow-anchor; effects re-subscribed on item count changes. New: a single rAF writer owns `--p`, geometry comes from hidden clones, and a spacer keeps `scrollHeight` constant, with scoped side effects.\n\n- Extracts `attachScrollListCollapse`: writes `--p`, sets `data-collapsing=\"true\"` only while 0 < p < 1.\n- Measures only hidden expanded/collapsed clones; computes once per frame and uses `sameHeaderMetrics` to avoid state churn.\n- Adds a spacer so header + spacer always equals the expanded height; scopes `overflow-anchor: none` to the header/spacer and to the scroller only while collapsing; applies `will-change` only under `[data-scroll-list-collapse-anim]` during collapse.\n- Updates `ScrollListPage` to subscribe when `hasItems`, tear down on unmount, and expose `refresh()`. Without `ResizeObserver`, re-measures after commit/window resize without rebinding the scroll listener, and skips redundant refresh by checking the handle generation.\n- Honors reduced motion with snap behavior. Flattens `resolveResizeObserver` for Sonar. Adds unit tests for geometry, progress clamping, reduced-motion snapping, mid-scroll re-measure invariants, cleanup across remount/refresh cycles, and generation increments.\n\n<sup>Written for commit 88865b3c8aa9bd47b2ae486653c164403bff9ef8. Summary will update on new commits.</sup>\n\n<a href=\"https://cubic.dev/pr/maus-inc/mausVoice/pull/81?utm_source=github\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" data-no-image-dialog=\"true\"><picture><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\" srcset=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-dark.svg\"><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\" srcset=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-light.svg\"><img alt=\"Review in cubic\" src=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-dark.svg\"></picture></a>\n\n<!-- End of auto-generated description by cubic. -->\n\n"
