+      "description": "## Root cause\n\nThree nested scrollable containers in the Home page layout chain produced two visible scrollbars (and occasional horizontal overflow):\n\n1. `PageLayout.tsx` outer Stack — `overflowY: auto, flexGrow: 1, minHeight: 0`\n2. `DashboardPage.tsx` motion Box — `overflow: auto, flexGrow: 1, minHeight: 0`\n3. `DashboardEntryLayout.tsx` Stack — `overflowY: auto, flexGrow: 1, pr: 2`\n\nHome and Settings pages compose `DashboardEntryLayout` inside the already-scrolling `DashboardPage` motion Box.\n\n## Fix\n\nRemove scrolling from `DashboardEntryLayout` (the innermost container). The `DashboardPage` motion Box now owns the scroll axis for both Home and Settings pages.\n\n**`DashboardEntryLayout.tsx` changes:**\n- Removed `overflowY: \"auto\"` — eliminates the nested scroll container\n- Removed `pr: 2` — scrollbar gutter no longer needed\n- Added `minHeight: 0` — robust flex shrinking\n\n**No changes needed in:**\n- `PageLayout.tsx` — unaffected; continues scrolling non-dashboard pages\n- `HomePage.tsx` — unchanged; benefits from parent scroll\n- `SettingsPage.tsx` — unchanged; benefits from parent scroll\n- `ScrollListPage.tsx` — owned by Agent A02; unaffected\n\n## Tests added\n\n`DashboardEntryLayout.test.ts` — 4 SSR static-markup tests verifying:\n- Children render inside the layout\n- Default `maxWidth=\"sm\"` is applied\n- No `overflow-y` in rendered markup (no nested scroll container)\n- Correct `<Stack> > <Container> > children` structure\n\n## Verification\n\n| Check | Result |\n|---|---|\n| `vitest run` (component tests) | 7/7 passed (4 new + 3 existing) |\n| `tsc --noEmit` | 0 errors in changed files |\n| `prettier --check` | All matched files use Prettier code style\n\n## Summary by Sourcery\n\nRemove the nested dashboard layout scroll container so Home and Settings use a single parent-owned scrollbar.\n\nBug Fixes:\n- Eliminate the duplicate scrollbar and related horizontal overflow on dashboard pages by removing nested scrolling from DashboardEntryLayout.\n\nEnhancements:\n- Allow the parent DashboardPage container to own scrolling for Home and Settings while preserving reliable flex layout behavior.\n\nTests:\n- Add SSR component tests covering child rendering, container configuration, and the expected non-nested layout structure.\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated description by cubic. -->\n---\n## Summary by cubic\nEliminates the double scrollbar on Home by removing the nested scroll container in `DashboardEntryLayout`. Previously Home/Settings scrolled in both `DashboardPage` and `DashboardEntryLayout`; now `DashboardPage` owns scrolling, removing the extra gutter and preventing horizontal overflow.\n\n- Review notes\n  - `DashboardEntryLayout.tsx`: removed `overflowY: \"auto\"` and `pr: 2`; added `minHeight: 0` for reliable flex shrinking.\n  - No changes to `PageLayout`, `HomePage`, or `SettingsPage`; both pages now use the parent scroll only.\n  - Validate: single vertical scrollbar on Home/Settings and no horizontal overflow.\n  - Tests: added `DashboardEntryLayout.test.ts` with SSR structural assertions (children render, `maxWidth` prop propagates, `Stack > Container > children` structure, no extra wrapper indicating nested scroll).\n\n<sup>Written for commit df8ad04db36b19bb38057095f0db92097730871b. Summary will update on new commits.</sup>\n\n<a href=\"https://cubic.dev/pr/maus-inc/mausVoice/pull/78?utm_source=github\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" data-no-image-dialog=\"true\"><picture><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\" srcset=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-dark.svg\"><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\" srcset=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-light.svg\"><img alt=\"Review in cubic\" src=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-dark.svg\"></picture></a>\n\n<!-- End of auto-generated description by cubic. -->\n\n"
