+      "description": "## Summary\n\nValidates the unresolved PR #63 findings plus the inline comments accidentally posted on review https://github.com/maus-inc/mausVoice/pull/70#pullrequestreview-4962367814 against the current PR #63 head.\n\n### Fixed from the misplaced PR #70 review\n\n- close both audio-file TOCTOU windows by re-resolving confinement after open and matching the resolved target to the opened handle\n- reject double-encoded local-route traversal\n- validate initial model download URLs with the same HTTPS/Hugging Face policy as redirects (retaining debug-only loopback support)\n- refresh style-hotkey rows when tones change without using an unstable store selector\n- disable Composer Insert while a voice edit is in flight\n- allow benign `..` substrings in terminal arguments while continuing to reject a standalone parent segment\n- broaden the HTTP capability contract scan to all desktop/workspace-package source trees\n\n### Verified as already fixed on PR #63\n\nAll eleven pasted PR #63 findings are already addressed at the current head, including chunk-level hallucination gating/overlap merge behavior, replacement preservation, finalized/link test coverage, hotkey failure propagation, newline preservation, and the corrected test name. The dictation newline guard and ASCII-only English command boundary are explicitly documented.\n\n### Reviewed but not changed\n\n- `ToolPermission.conversationId` is required and populated by the only constructor; `conversation:undefined` is not representable in the current flow.\n- the documented `bullet point` command/file does not exist on PR #63.\n- both currently supported Groq Whisper models support `verbose_json` and the code documents that requirement.\n- missing manual-installer signatures are represented and rejected before the lower-level Rust call; the lower-level function correctly requires a signature URL.\n- the signer CLI accepts the private key through its required key option, and GitHub-hosted job runners are isolated; changing password/key transport without a supported stdin interface would risk breaking release signing.\n\n## Verification\n\n- `pnpm build` (all 10 build tasks passed)\n- desktop `check-types`\n- desktop lint (Prettier + oxlint)\n- 63 focused desktop tests passed\n- `git diff --check`\n\nRust tests/format could not be run locally because this sandbox image has no Rust toolchain; CI should run the repository's Rust gates.\n\n## Summary by Sourcery\n\nHarden file, route, command, and model-download validation while keeping related desktop UI state consistent.\n\nBug Fixes:\n- Close audio-file time-of-check/time-of-use races by validating the opened file against its resolved target and allowed locations.\n- Reject double-encoded local-route traversal and preserve safe handling of benign double dots in terminal arguments.\n- Apply the approved HTTPS and Hugging Face host policy to initial model downloads, while retaining debug/test loopback support.\n- Keep Composer and style-hotkey UI state synchronized during edits and tone changes.\n\nEnhancements:\n- Expand the HTTP capability contract scan across desktop and workspace-package source trees.\n\nTests:\n- Add coverage for terminal argument handling, double-encoded route traversal, and initial model URL validation.\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated description by cubic. -->\n---\n## Summary by cubic\nCloses audio import and managed-audio TOCTOU races, tightens app-route and command validation with clearer percent-decode errors, and enforces the initial model download URL policy. Keeps Composer and style-hotkey UI state consistent during edits and tone changes.\n\n- Audio files: open first, then canonicalize and verify identity (inode/device or Windows handle) against the opened path; reject files outside allowed roots or if the target changes during import/read.\n- Local routes: percent-decode iteratively with a small bound; after the first successful decode, treat a bare “%” as terminal and return the specific decode error on failure; reject double-encoded traversal.\n- Terminal args: allow benign “..” inside a token; still reject a standalone “..”.\n- Model downloads in `packages/rust_transcription`: validate the initial URL with the same HTTPS/Hugging Face allowlist as redirects; allow loopback HTTP only in debug or test builds, including IPv6 `::1`. Migration: move to approved HTTPS hosts or run in a debug/test loopback setup.\n- CSP capability contract test: scan desktop and all workspace-package sources, excluding tests.\n- UI: disable Composer Insert while `isEditing` is true; compute tones from `toneById` with `useMemo` and rebuild rows when the dialog opens, shortcuts change, or tones change.\n\n<sup>Written for commit 361938d1c27f9adf0b924114cfb9396d2868fc55. Summary will update on new commits.</sup>\n\n<a href=\"https://cubic.dev/pr/maus-inc/mausVoice/pull/72?utm_source=github\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" data-no-image-dialog=\"true\"><picture><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\" srcset=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-dark.svg\"><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\" srcset=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-light.svg\"><img alt=\"Review in cubic\" src=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-dark.svg\"></picture></a>\n\n<!-- End of auto-generated description by cubic. -->\n\n"
