+      "description": "## Purpose\n\nAddresses the open inline reviews on #63 (cubic review 4961422605, kilo review 4961451655, plus the pasted cubic/kilo round) and the failing **Lint Desktop (Windows)** job. Merge this **into `fix/superfix-review-findings`** (PR #63 head) — merging to `main` directly would bypass #63.\n\n## Failing CI job — fixed\n\n`Lint Desktop (Windows)` failed `cargo clippy --manifest-path packages/rust_windows_pill/Cargo.toml --all-targets -- -D warnings` (clippy 1.97) with:\n\n```\nerror: empty line after doc comment   (clippy::empty-line-after-doc-comments)\n   --> src\\pill.rs:1246\n1246 | /// released — a leaked capture would swallow mouse input system-wide.\n1251 |   fn current_pill_geometry(...)\n```\n\nThe `end_drag` doc comment was stranded above the newly inserted `current_pill_geometry`. This PR moves the comment back onto `end_drag`. That was the job's **only** error (verified from the run log). Note `Build Desktop (Windows)` already passed at 8657795.\n\n## Review comments — fixed here\n\n| Comment | Fix |\n| --- | --- |\n| **P2 ×2** cubic `keyboard.utils.ts:272` — `return run` | Restored `return run` (bot commit 8657795 had swapped in the caught `syncQueue`, swallowing native-grab failures). `syncQueue = run.catch(...)` still keeps the chain alive for later callers. Regression test added: failure rejects to the caller *and* the next sync still runs. |\n| **P2** cubic `StyleHotkeysDialog.tsx:120` | No code change needed — the dialog already `return`s before `close()` on sync failure; the error path was unreachable only because of the `syncQueue` regression above. Now reachable again. |\n| **WARNING** kilo `transcription.rs:122` — near-silent early return can hard-fail on device resolution | Applied the suggested fix: ONNX reports `CPU` without resolving; whisper path resolves but falls back to `mode.as_str().to_ascii_uppercase()` on failure. Non-silent inference paths still resolve strictly. |\n| **SUGGESTION** kilo `index.html:155` — early `unhandledrejection` listener never removed, duplicates the TS installer | Handler is now a stable named global (`window.__mausVoiceEarlyUnhandledRejection`) that `installGlobalErrorOverlay` removes (and deletes) once the bundle mounts. Root-children guard kept as a fallback. |\n| **SUGGESTION** kilo `spoken-commands.utils.ts:151` — ASCII-only word boundaries | Documented the assumption on `isAsciiAlnum` (pipeline is English-gated; normalizing note for multilingual future). |\n\n## Review comments — already fixed on the branch (verified + regression-tested now)\n\n- **P1 ×2** cubic `transcribe.actions.ts:187` / `hallucination.utils.ts:134` — overlap dupes: the repo gates each chunk's `no_speech_prob` segments *before* `mergeTranscriptions` and **omits `segments` on the merged output**, so the action layer never re-derives text from flattened multi-chunk segments. Single-chunk outputs keep their segments.\n- **WARNING** kilo `sanitize-transcript.utils.ts:44` — user-dictionary replacements dropped on `verbose_json`: gate now runs on replacement-processed segments. Added regression test (`k8s → Kubernetes` survives segment gating).\n- **WARNING** kilo `spoken-commands.utils.ts:358` — explicit newline dropped before attach-left: `trimTrailingSpace` only pops horizontal-whitespace entries. Added regression tests (`new line comma` → `\"\\n,\"`, `open paren new line close paren` → `\"(\\n)\"`).\n- **SUGGESTION** kilo `dictation.strategy.ts:69` — dead `endsWith(\"\\n\")` branch: already documented as guarding replacement/symbol-conversion newlines.\n\n## Verification (local, sandbox)\n\n- `test:unit` desktop: **532 passed** (incl. 3 new/updated regression tests)\n- `check-types`, `lint` (prettier + oxlint), `i18n` sync (0 added), voice-ai tests: **all green**\n- `vite build`: **no `intl-*.js` chunk is emitted** — react-intl/@formatjs/intl-messageformat are folded into `react-*.js` (confirms the white-window `intl-Bo580dMd.js` crash cannot recur on this branch; the tested build predated c434829a)\n- Rust: clippy failure root-caused from the Actions log; fix is a pure comment move. `Test Rust Transcription` / `Lint native pill` re-verified by CI after this merges into the #63 head branch.\n\n## Summary by Sourcery\n\nHarden hotkey synchronization, transcription edge cases, error-overlay handoff, and transcript command processing while restoring a clean Windows lint build.\n\nBug Fixes:\n- Restore caller-visible hotkey synchronization failures while keeping subsequent synchronization attempts operational.\n- Allow near-silent transcription results to complete without failing on device-resolution errors.\n- Prevent the early startup error overlay from remaining active after the application mounts.\n- Preserve transcript dictionary replacements and explicit newline commands during transcript sanitization and spoken-command processing.\n- Resolve the Windows pill documentation placement that caused Clippy to fail.\n\nEnhancements:\n- Document the English-only assumptions behind spoken-command word-boundary handling.\n\nTests:\n- Add regression coverage for hotkey failure propagation, dictionary replacements in verbose segments, and newline punctuation handling.\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated description by cubic. -->\n---\n## Summary by cubic\nFixes hotkey sync error propagation, prevents duplicate early error overlays after app mount, softens near-silent transcription device resolution, and keeps the Windows lint job green. Also types the bootstrap error handler on `window` to keep its name in sync and ensure safe removal.\n\n**Review notes**\n- Hotkeys: `syncHotkeyCombosToNative` now returns the run promise (old: returned the caught queue, swallowing rejections). The queue still catches to keep later syncs chained. A test verifies rejection reaches callers and the next sync proceeds.\n- Error overlay: the inline `unhandledrejection` listener in `index.html` is a named global that `installGlobalErrorOverlay` removes on mount (old: listener stayed attached and could repaint a fatal overlay over a running app). The handler is declared on `Window` in `vite-env.d.ts` to type it and keep the identifier in sync across `index.html` and the installer.\n- Transcription: the near-silent early return tolerates device resolution failures (ONNX reports CPU; whisper falls back to the compute mode string). Non-silent paths still resolve devices strictly and reject invalid IDs.\n- Windows pill: move a stranded doc comment back onto `end_drag` to satisfy `clippy::empty-line-after-doc-comments`. No runtime change.\n\n<sup>Written for commit 7e264dd39e2231247d81e09736e6c1d652a7def8. Summary will update on new commits.</sup>\n\n<a href=\"https://cubic.dev/pr/maus-inc/mausVoice/pull/69?utm_source=github\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" data-no-image-dialog=\"true\"><picture><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\" srcset=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-dark.svg\"><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\" srcset=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-light.svg\"><img alt=\"Review in cubic\" src=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-dark.svg\"></picture></a>\n\n<!-- End of auto-generated description by cubic. -->\n\n"
