+      "description": "## Purpose\nFollow-up on [PR #63](https://github.com/maus-inc/mausVoice/pull/63) addressing Cubic review 4960748801, Kilo review 4960575309, and Cubic’s proposed patches in comment 5327918333.\n\n## Fixes\n- Restrict `plugin-http` plaintext scope to loopback/RFC1918/link-local/`*.local` instead of `http://*:*`\n- Omit multi-chunk `segments` so overlap-merged transcripts are not flattened again\n- Classify SenseVoice `load_model` failures as `Runtime` (do not delete valid bundles)\n- Always emit a terminal `isLastChunk` signal on forced empty flush\n- Import/retranscribe uses `sanitizedTranscript`; replacements applied to segments\n- Dictation keeps newline-only output; agent skips empty hallucination-filtered messages\n- `keyboard-layout` maps to `AUTO_LANGUAGE` on audio import\n- Voice recorder only marks listening after `recognition.start()` succeeds\n- Composer apply can clear text; tutorial same-step dots no longer wipe drafts\n- Style snapshot after `loadManualStyleForCurrentApp`; hotkey sync errors propagate\n- Locale regressions restored (pt/de/es/fr/it)\n- Updater docs fail-closed for stable; gitleaks history-scan + config-id matching\n- TOCTOU metadata-before-open, resample zero-rate error, GTK monitor from live surface, Windows reset geometry after move\n\n## Notes\nGitHub App cannot update `.github/workflows/*` from this session, so the i18n untracked-file CI check was not included. Remaining workflow change can be applied in a privileged follow-up.\n\n## Summary by Sourcery\n\nHarden local transcription, dictation, security checks, updater publishing, and desktop behavior against review findings.\n\nBug Fixes:\n- Restrict plaintext HTTP access to local and private network destinations.\n- Preserve overlap-merged transcripts and sanitized segment replacements during transcription and import.\n- Prevent valid SenseVoice model bundles from being removed after runtime loading failures.\n- Ensure forced audio flushes emit a terminal signal and skip empty hallucination-filtered agent messages.\n- Correct dictation, voice recorder, composer, tutorial, keyboard-layout, style-loading, and hotkey error-handling behavior.\n- Restore locale catalog updates and improve Windows recorder/runtime and floating-window behavior.\n\nEnhancements:\n- Remove repeated model digest scans from the inference path after verified download admission.\n- Harden file import validation, model alias parsing, resampling errors, monitor detection, and startup error handling.\n- Improve secret-history scanning and require gitleaks checks to target the updater key rule.\n- Make stable updater publication fail closed when signing credentials are unavailable and clarify installer selection.\n\nBuild:\n- Update Linux personal-fork builds to include AppImage bundles.\n\nCI:\n- Fail desktop CI when locale files are untracked or catalogs are out of sync, and strengthen gitleaks binary and exit-status validation.\n\nDocumentation:\n- Document MSI preference for the default Windows updater target and fail-closed stable manifest publishing.\n\nTests:\n- Update the CSP capability contract to verify restricted plaintext HTTP ranges.\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated description by cubic. -->\n---\n## Summary by cubic\nTightens network scope and transcription paths and fixes regressions from #63. Plaintext `http:default` now only allows loopback, RFC1918, link‑local, and `*.local`; overlap‑merged transcripts are preserved across import and chat; request‑time model digest scans are removed; SenseVoice ONNX load failures are treated as runtime; empty finalize always emits a terminal chunk; and ONNX model `download_url` handling is exhaustive. Composer mounts correctly across recorder rebuilds, voice edit mode handles start failures, dictation preserves structural whitespace, the agent skips empty messages, the startup error overlay only paints before React mounts, and Windows Sherpa DLLs copy from on‑disk names while loading lowercase. CI enforces locale sync (including untracked files) and stricter `gitleaks` rule/binary checks; docs clarify MSI as the Windows default and fail‑closed stable manifest publishing.\n\n- Migration: Plain HTTP to public hosts is blocked. When adding a hosted provider, add its HTTPS host to both `apps/desktop/src-tauri/capabilities/default.json` and CSP `connect-src`.\n\n<sup>Written for commit 3f860394300a54fdfc351bd9abbd89acbc2c2807. Summary will update on new commits.</sup>\n\n<a href=\"https://cubic.dev/pr/maus-inc/mausVoice/pull/68?utm_source=github\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" data-no-image-dialog=\"true\"><picture><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\" srcset=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-dark.svg\"><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\" srcset=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-light.svg\"><img alt=\"Review in cubic\" src=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-dark.svg\"></picture></a>\n\n<!-- End of auto-generated description by cubic. -->\n\n"
