+      "description": "## Problem\n\nWindows release builds opened a plain white, unresponsive main window. The webview console showed:\n\n```\nintl-Bo580dMd.js:22 Uncaught TypeError: Cannot read properties of undefined (reading 'Fragment')\n```\n\nTauri, SQLite migrations, and the native pill all started normally. The window then sat at `(133, 10)` with no React tree.\n\n## Cause\n\n`vite.config.ts` forced `react-intl` / `@formatjs` into a dedicated `intl` chunk, separate from React. `react-intl` reads `React.Fragment` at module-init time (`textComponent: React.Fragment`). Across that chunk boundary Rollup's namespace interop left `React` uninitialized, so the vendor chunk threw before `main.tsx` could mount — or even install the in-app error overlay.\n\n## Fix\n\n- Put React and the formatjs/react-intl packages in the same `react` vendor chunk.\n- Teach the pre-bundle error overlay in `index.html` to paint module-evaluation failures and unhandled rejections, not just failed `<script>`/`<link>` fetches. A future import-time crash should show the error instead of a blank window.\n\n## Test plan\n\n- [x] Unit tests for the chunk helper (React and react-intl share a chunk; no `intl` chunk; Windows paths).\n- [x] Early overlay paints a synthetic `Fragment` module-evaluation error.\n- [ ] Rebuild the Windows desktop app and confirm the main window renders instead of staying white.\n- [ ] If anything still fails at import time, the dark overlay should show the stack rather than a blank page.\n\n## Summary by Sourcery\n\nKeep React-dependent internationalization packages with React and surface pre-mount startup failures through the early error overlay.\n\nBug Fixes:\n- Prevent Windows desktop builds from failing during startup when react-intl or FormatJS modules access React exports before the app mounts.\n- Display an early startup error overlay for module-evaluation failures and unhandled promise rejections instead of leaving a blank window.\n\nEnhancements:\n- Centralize vendor chunk selection and keep React, react-intl, and FormatJS packages in the same React chunk while preserving unrelated vendor splitting.\n\nTests:\n- Add coverage for vendor chunk assignment, Windows path normalization, removal of the separate intl chunk, and early overlay error handling."
