+      "description": "## Summary\n\nRemediates all findings from the deep pre-release audit of `main` (`e700728`) against `c7efd6f` (#28), reviewed per the REVIEW.md protocol.\n\n### Major\n- **CSP `connect-src` blocks four shipped providers in release builds.** Dev builds and CI never enforce `security.csp`, so the PR #49 CSP silently broke providers that use bare webview `fetch`/`WebSocket`. Added: `api.assemblyai.com` (batch path from #43), `api.x.ai`, `api.aldea.ai`, and `*.stt.speech.microsoft.com` (https+wss — Azure Speech SDK region-prefixed endpoints).\n- **`http:default` capability lockdown broke user-configured endpoints.** Ollama / OpenAI-compatible / Speaches base URLs are user-configured (LAN boxes, reverse proxies) and cannot be enumerated statically; restored `http://*:*` / `https://*` scope with the rationale documented in the capability description. The webview CSP remains the strict boundary for in-page fetches.\n\n### Minor\n- **`REVIEW.md` deduplicated** — the compaction commit (`d6de100`) left five concatenated drafts of the handbook separated by stray workspace path lines; only the final copy remains.\n- **`release.yml` `publish-cask`** now fails fast with an actionable error when `RELEASE_TOKEN` is unset, instead of 403-ing on the cross-repo tap push at the very end of a release; dropped the misleading `GITHUB_TOKEN` fallback (it can never push to `maus-inc/homebrew-mausvoice`).\n- **`release.yml` `verify-rust` gate widened** beyond `src-tauri --lib` to `rust_transcription` (`--lib`), `rust_pill_shared`, and `rust_gtk_pill` — crates that ship in the artifact are now tested before any platform build starts.\n\n### Test coverage\n- **New contract test** (`apps/desktop/src/csp-connect-src.contract.test.ts`): mechanically scans provider sources for `https`/`wss` host literals used with bare `fetch` (files importing `@tauri-apps/plugin-http` are exempt — that traffic bypasses the CSP) and asserts each host is allowed by `connect-src`, plus curated checks for dynamically-constructed endpoints (Azure region websockets, Firebase token refresh). Mutation-verified: removing `api.assemblyai.com` from the CSP fails with a pointed message. Runs in the existing vitest `src` suite, so `test-desktop-unit` and the release `verify-ts` gate both enforce it.\n\n### Nitpicks\n- CSP: `https://asset:` → `https://asset.localhost` (valid source expression).\n- `release.yml`: trailing newline at EOF.\n\n## Verification\n- prettier clean · oxlint 0 warnings/0 errors · `tsc --noEmit` clean\n- Desktop unit tests: **363/363** across 26 files (incl. the new contract test)\n- pr28+pr37 contract suites: 24/24 · both JSON configs parse · release.yml parses as YAML\n\n## Remaining manual step before tagging 0.1.6\nA bundled-build smoke test of AssemblyAI / Azure / xAI / Aldea — the contract test closes the mechanical gap, but only a release-webview pass definitively confirms the CSP fix (this class of breakage is invisible to `pnpm dev` and to all CI workflows)."
