+      "description": "## Summary\n\nHardens the local transcription sidecar's model artifact download path.\n\n- Caps every artifact at 4 GiB, enforced both from the declared `Content-Length` (including ranged-resume remaining-byte logic) and during streaming of chunked responses; oversized/breached partials and their resume validators are removed.\n- Verifies SHA-256 digests of the executable ONNX graph/weights after durable write via `spawn_blocking`; mismatches are removed and never renamed into place.\n- Restricts redirects to HTTPS, an allow-list of Hugging Face delivery hosts, and a five-hop limit via a custom `reqwest` policy.\n- Pins ONNX artifacts to immutable Hugging Face revisions (no `/resolve/main/`) with expected digests; runtime URL overrides are no longer accepted for ONNX.\n- Extends the Desktop Build PR filter to shared packages and lock/build configuration so dependency changes trigger the build.\n\n## Verification\n\nBranch is pushed; CI builds/checks are running on the PR.\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai -->\n## Summary by CodeRabbit\n\n* **New Features**\n  * Model downloads now verify SHA-256 checksums.\n  * Downloads enforce a 4 GiB size limit and safer HTTPS redirect rules.\n  * Model artifacts use pinned, immutable sources for reliable downloads.\n  * Text generation supports cancellation signals.\n\n* **Bug Fixes**\n  * Improved handling of oversized, incomplete, or invalid downloads.\n  * Stability checks now time out gracefully and classify transient provider failures.\n  * Canceled requests no longer trigger unnecessary fallback attempts.\n\n* **Documentation**\n  * Clarified model sources, checksums, pinning, and development overrides.\n\n* **Chores**\n  * Expanded build workflow coverage for relevant project changes.\n<!-- end of auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai -->"
