+      "description": "## What changed?\n\n**Production builds showed a plain white, unresponsive window:**\n\n```\nintl-Bo580dMd.js:22 Uncaught TypeError: Cannot read properties of undefined (reading 'Fragment')\n```\n\nRoot cause was a circular chunk graph in `apps/desktop/vite.config.ts`. `manualChunks` split `react-intl` / `@formatjs` / `intl-messageformat` into a separate `intl` chunk while those modules `import { Fragment } from \"react\"`. Vite emitted a warning `Circular chunk: intl -> react -> intl` and at runtime one ES namespace was still uninitialised, so `Fragment` was `undefined` and the app never mounted.\n\nThis PR merges `react-intl`/`@formatjs`/`intl-messageformat` back into the `react` chunk so the vendor graph stays acyclic. This branch also carries `fix(pill): include window rect and monitor geometry` (d8dedf4) from the parent `fix/superfix-review-findings`.\n\n**Changes:**\n- `apps/desktop/vite.config.ts`: map `react-intl` / `@formatjs` / `intl-messageformat` to `react` instead of `intl` (with explanatory comment). Verified: `vite build` no longer emits circular warning, no separate `intl-*.js` chunk, `react-C6PvueTV.js` is now 277 kB and does not import `intl`.\n\n## How is it tested?\n\n- [x] Automated tests — `pnpm exec turbo run build --filter=desktop^...` (6/6), `pnpm --filter desktop exec tsc --noEmit` (0 errors), `pnpm --filter desktop exec vitest run src` (43 files, 480 passed)\n- [x] Manual verification — `pnpm --filter desktop run build` (vite 7.3.6, 16463 modules, no circular warning, `dist/index.html` has `src=\"./assets/react-*.js\"` and no `crossorigin`)\n- [x] Code inspection\n\nFixes white-window reported on recent build.\n\n## Demo video/screenshots\n\nn/a — build artifact fix. `dist/assets/` before had `react-8u9IrfG0.js` + `intl-Bo580dMd.js` with mutual imports; after has single `react-C6PvueTV.js`."
