+      "description": "## Summary\n\nAddresses the 10 actionable CodeRabbit review comments on PR #59, plus a follow-up deep review against `REVIEW.md` (CodeRabbit assertive persona) that caught one additional least-privilege regression.\n\n### Inline CodeRabbit fixes (commit `edc7d2f`)\n\n- **Updater concurrent-check coalescing** (`apps/desktop/src/actions/updater.actions.ts`): a module-level `checkingUserInitiated` flag now accumulates `userInitiated` intent when a caller joins an in-flight `checkingPromise`, so a manual \"Check now\" that joins a pending background check opens the update dialog despite an active snooze and suppresses the background toast. The flag resets in the shared check's `finally`. Added a mixed-caller regression test.\n- **`AppSideEffects.tsx`**: removed stale `// 10 minutes` / `// 60 seconds` comments; `UPDATE_CHECK_INTERVAL_MS` and its 6-hour value unchanged.\n- **`SettingSection` / `UpdateSettingSection`**: added an optional `descriptionSlot` rendered without an enclosing `Typography`, and routed the version/status `Stack` through it (preserves the `role=\"status\"` and styling).\n- **`analytics-equivalence.test.ts`**: `Inputs` now derives `member`/`localUser`/`prefs` from the production `AnalyticsIdentitySources` type, keeping only the test-specific field-name mapping and local auth contact.\n- **Trust-boundary docs**: corrected wording across `auto-update.md`, `updates.md`, `RELEASE.md`, `releases.md`, `auto-update-pipeline-plan.md`, and `getting-started.md` — the minisign public key verifies the signed updater *bundles* referenced by `latest.json`; the manifest itself is not signed. Named `UPDATER_PUBLIC_KEY` as the release secret and removed the stale `TAURI_UPDATER_PUBLIC_KEY` reference; distinguished prerelease exclusion from signing and qualified \"unsigned test build\" as \"not OS-code-signed.\"\n- **`personal-fork-ci/workflows/build-desktop.yml`**: synchronized the `pull_request` path filter with `push` paths via a YAML anchor; 