+      "description": "## What changed?\n\n- configure MUI to use `data-mui-color-scheme` instead of its default media-only selector, allowing the in-app theme control to override the OS scheme\n- keep MUI's established `mui-mode` storage key as the source of truth and non-destructively migrate the temporary `mode` fallback when needed, preserving upgrade and rollback compatibility\n- resolve and apply the persisted scheme before first paint while using MUI palette variables after mount\n- add regression coverage for light, dark, system, selector, persistence, migration, and storage-precedence behavior\n- defer Windows startup UAC until the React frontend is mounted, preventing the pre-event-loop relaunch deadlock that left a blank canvas and no pill\n\n## How is it tested?\n\n- [x] Automated tests\n- [ ] Manual verification\n- [x] Code inspection\n\nValidation completed:\n\n- `pnpm --filter desktop check-types`\n- `pnpm --filter desktop test:unit` (359 tests passed)\n- `pnpm --filter desktop build`\n- browser-level MUI provider debug for stored-mode switching and live system-theme changes\n- Prettier and oxlint checks for changed source files\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai -->\n## Summary by CodeRabbit\n\n* **New Features**\n  * Added explicit administrator relaunch handling on Windows when startup elevation is enabled.\n  * Added clearer feedback when elevation is cancelled or fails.\n  * Added a visible fatal-error screen for startup and resource-loading failures.\n* **Bug Fixes**\n  * Improved theme initialization to prevent visual flashes during startup.\n  * Improved light, dark, and system theme handling, including migration of existing preferences.\n  * Improved loading of release assets in desktop builds.\n* **Tests**\n  * Added coverage for theme persistence, startup behavior, and administrator elevation flows.\n<!-- end of auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai -->"
