+      "description": "## Summary\n\nFollow-up on the SonarCloud code smell left OPEN by #44.\n\n[SonarCloud issue list for PR #44](https://sonarcloud.io/project/issues?id=maus-inc_voquill&issueStatuses=OPEN%2CCONFIRMED&pullRequest=44&sinceLeakPeriod=true) reports one OPEN issue:\n\n| Rule | Severity | Location | Message |\n|------|----------|----------|---------|\n| [typescript:S7741](https://sonarcloud.io/organizations/maus-inc/rules?open=typescript%3AS7741&rule_key=typescript%3AS7741) | Minor (LOW maintainability) | `apps/desktop/src/components/common/TypographyWithMore.tsx:154` | Compare with `undefined` directly instead of using `typeof`. |\n\n## Fix\n\nIn `TypographyWithMore`, `fontSize` and `lineHeight` are declared optional props, so `x !== undefined` is exactly equivalent to the previous `typeof x !== \"undefined\"` checks. Both occurrences in the block (lines 152 and 154) were updated so the pattern doesn't reappear on the next analysis.\n\nThe `typeof` guards for `window` and `ResizeObserver` elsewhere in the file are left untouched — those identifiers can be undeclared at runtime, which is the case where `typeof` is required.\n\n## Verification\n\n- `pnpm --filter desktop lint` — 0 warnings, 0 errors\n- `pnpm --filter desktop check-types` — clean (after building workspace packages per repo conventions)\n- `pnpm --filter desktop test:unit` — 353 passed\n- The 54 failing eval/integration tests also fail identically on `main` (they require API keys unavailable in CI-less environments); no new failures introduced.\n\n### `strict-peer-dependencies` + `peerDependencyRules` (follow-up commit)\n\nThis PR additionally enables `strict-peer-dependencies=true` in `.npmrc` with bounded `peerDependencyRules.allowedVersions` for `vite` and `zod`. These rules were relocated to `pnpm-workspace.yaml` because pnpm 10 no longer reads the `pnpm` field from `package.json` (it was being silently ignored there).\n\nTo confirm this does **not** break installs/CI, a clean from-scratch install was performed:\n\n```sh\n$ rm -rf node_modules\n$ pnpm install --frozen-lockfile\n... resolved 1430, reused 1425, downloaded 0, added 1430, done\nDone in 5.3s using pnpm v10.34.5   (exit 0)\n```\n\nWith `strict-peer-dependencies=true` active, any unmet peer dependency would have hard-failed the install. None did — the monorepo's lockfile currently resolves all peers cleanly, so the only exempted peers (`vite`, `zod`) are intentional allowances and no other peer mismatches exist. CI uses the same frozen lockfile, so it is likewise safe.\n\nCloses the single OPEN/CONFIRMED issue on the PR #44 SonarCloud analysis.\n"
