+      "description": "## Summary\n\nCorrects stale documentation that described removed code/features and adds a new page for the recently-shipped local ONNX speech models.\n\nVerified every claim against the current tree (`main` at `bf2c825`, Parakeet/Canary PR #36). Root and loose `docs/` files had drifted after the 0.1.6 Cloud/Enterprise removal; the Astro docs site under `apps/docs/` was mostly accurate but missed the new models.\n\n## Changes\n\n**Fixed wrong claims**\n\n- `AGENTS.md`, `llms.txt`, `README.md`, `docs/ARCHITECTURE.md`, `docs/getting-started.md`\n  - Removed references to deleted `enterprise/gateway`, `enterprise/admin`, `packages/functions`, `packages/pricing`, and non-existent `ui`/`config` packages.\n  - Removed fake `CloudAuthRepo`/`EnterpriseAuthRepo`/`isEnterpriseFlavor()`/`getIsEnterpriseEnabled()` code samples; repo factories now all return local implementations.\n  - Fixed Linux packaging: releases ship `.deb` + AppImage, not RPM.\n  - Added the `pnpm dev:linux` script (was only listing mac/windows).\n- `docs/docker.md` — Compose files live in `config/`, so every command now passes `-f config/docker-compose.yml` (the root-level commands failed as written).\n- `docs/RELEASE.md` — `tauri.prod.conf.json` has no committed `version` field; the release workflow injects it at build time.\n- `docs/local-model-integration.md` — added a prominent \"partially outdated\" banner and inline notes. Local inference runs in the `packages/rust_transcription` sidecar (whisper.cpp for GGML, ONNX Runtime for Parakeet/Canary). There is no `src-tauri/src/platform/whisper.rs`, no in-process `WhisperTranscriber`, and no model download at startup.\n- `configuration/clear-local-data.md` + `configuration/settings-map.md` — `clear_local_data` empties **11** tables (not 8), including `tones`, `app_targets`, and `paired_remote_devices`, and it deletes referenced audio files then vacuums.\n- `REVIEW.md` — removed the Electron `ipcMain.handle` reference and claims about ESLint/Markdownlint gates. The actual stack is Oxlint + Prettier on the frontend and Clippy on Rust.\n\n**Brought docs up to date for Parakeet/Canary (#36)**\n\n- `configuration/local-models.md`, `reference/local-models.md`, `reference/data-locations.md`, `reference/terminology.md`, `configuration/transcription-modes.md`, `configuration/model-and-device-selection.md`, `getting-started/system-requirements.md`, `development/repository-overview.md`, `development/transcription-sidecar.md`, `troubleshooting/local-models.md`, `apps/docs/public/llms.txt` — list the six whisper.cpp GGML models plus the three ONNX models (`parakeet-ctc-0.6b`, `parakeet-tdt-0.6b`, `canary-1b`), their artifacts (`model_int8.onnx_data`, `encoder-model.int8.onnx`, companions), the `transcription-models/` directory, and the corrected RAM tiers.\n- `packages/rust_transcription/README.md` — supported models and both runtimes.\n\n**New page**\n\n- `configuration/local-speech-models.md` — human-focused guide comparing the Whisper and ONNX families, including **pause / resume / cancel** during downloads (the new controls added in #36), per-model storage layout, and guidance on picking a model.\n\n## Verification\n\n- Prettier clean on every changed Markdown file.\n- `node --test scripts/ci/pr28-contracts.test.mjs` — 19/19 pass.\n- Model IDs, filenames, and artifact sets cross-checked against `packages/rust_transcription/src/models.rs` on `main`.\n- Table count and audio-deletion behavior cross-checked against `USER_DATA_TABLES_TO_CLEAR` and `clear_local_data` in `commands.rs`.\n\nNo code changes.\n"
