+      "description": "## Summary\n\nTwo rendering regressions introduced with the #36 changes, both root-caused and fixed with regression tests.\n\n### 1. Release builds rendered with no styling at all (CSP vs emotion)\n\n`#36` flipped `app.security.csp` from `null` to a strict policy. Tauri rewrites the served policy by appending nonces/hashes for the static `<script>`/`<style>` tags in `index.html`; per the CSP spec the presence of a nonce or hash makes browsers **ignore** `'unsafe-inline'`. Every MUI/emotion component style is injected at runtime as a nonce-less `<style>` tag, so release builds rendered as bare HTML: stacked layout, full-size logo, duplicated nav labels (icon rail + expanded menu both visible), default serif type. Dev builds were unaffected, which is why this only surfaced in shipped builds.\n\n**Fix:** `dangerousDisableAssetCspModification: [\"style-src\"]` — the Tauri-documented escape hatch for CSS-in-JS. `style-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline'` stays effective for emotion while `script-src` keeps its hash protection (the boot-theme inline script in `index.html` still runs via its injected hash).\n\n### 2. Blank AI settings panels for upgraders (legacy \"cloud\" modes)\n\nBuilds prior to #36 persisted `\"cloud\"` for `transcriptionMode`/`agentMode`. The cloud removal normalized only `postProcessingMode` at the Tauri boundary, so a stored `\"cloud\"` reached the store untouched: the AI transcription and assistant-mode dialogs rendered a `SegmentedControl` with no matching tab (first tab falsely highlighted) and `AnimateSwitch` matched no content branch — blank panel body.\n\n**Fix:** normalize all three modes in `fromLocalPreferences` (the repo boundary), mapping removed values onto the closest valid mode (transcription → `local`, agent/post-processing → `none`). `LocalUserPreferences` boundary fields for the raw modes are loosened to `Nullable<string>` to match what SQLite actually stores.\n\n## Tests\n\n- `src/tauri-conf.test.ts` — contract tests pinning the CSP invariants (`style-src` keeps `'unsafe-inline'`, `style-src` excluded from asset CSP modification, `script-src` stays strict).\n- `src/repos/preferences.repo.test.ts` — regression tests for legacy `cloud` transcription/agent/post-processing modes and pass-through of valid/unset modes.\n- `pnpm --filter desktop run test:unit`: 353/353 pass. `tsc --noEmit`, prettier, and oxlint clean.\n\n## Manual verification needed\n\nRebuild the desktop app (`scripts/build-desktop.ps1` / `pnpm tauri build`) and confirm the release window renders with full styling and that upgrading an install with persisted `cloud` preferences shows the local transcription panel instead of a blank body."
