+      "description": "## Description\nThis pull request adds support for NVIDIA Parakeet and Canary local speech models alongside interactive Pause, Resume, and Cancel download controls in the mausVoice local transcription settings.\n\n### Key Changes\n1. **Local Model Expansion**:\n   - Registered `parakeet-ctc-0.6b`, `parakeet-tdt-0.6b`, and `canary-1b` in `packages/rust_transcription` and desktop utilities.\n   - Updated hardware tier recommendations in `model-recommendation.utils.ts`.\n2. **Resumable HTTP Downloads & Task Lifecycle**:\n   - Implemented `DownloadJobStatus::{Pending, Running, Paused, Completed, Failed, Canceled}` using `tokio::sync::watch` control channels.\n   - Resumable downloads via HTTP `Range: bytes={existing_bytes}-` requests with fallback.\n   - Safe cancellation and cleanup of partial `.download` scratch files.\n   - Added REST endpoints:\n     - `POST /v1/models/:model/download/pause` / `POST /v1/models/:model/download/:job_id/pause`\n     - `POST /v1/models/:model/download/cancel` / `POST /v1/models/:model/download/:job_id/cancel`\n3. **UI / UX Craftsmanship (`AITranscriptionConfiguration.tsx`)**:\n   - Added **Pause**, **Resume**, and **Cancel** controls with semantic colors and icons (`PauseRounded`, `PlayArrowRounded`, `CloseRounded`).\n   - Grouped model selection menu into `NVIDIA NeMo / Sherpa-ONNX` and `OpenAI Whisper` categories.\n   - Polished inline action bar when the dropdown is closed, displaying live compact progress badges (`45%`).\n   - Added Emil Kowalski–style micro-interaction press feedback (`scale(0.97)`) and `tabular-nums` to prevent numeric jitter during downloads.\n\n### Verification\n- All 10 Turborepo workspace packages compiled successfully (`pnpm run build`).\n- 100% of unit test suites passed (`18/18 test suites, 308/308 unit tests`).\n- Passed Oxlint and Prettier formatting checks.\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai -->\n## Summary by CodeRabbit\n\n- **New Features**\