+      "description": "## Summary\n\nFixes the provider capability/dispatch mismatch identified during a production audit, and hardens the new AssemblyAI batch transcription path.\n\n### Context\nThe model-capability class marked Ollama as supporting transcription, so it appeared in the **AI transcription** selector — but `getTranscribeAudioRepo()` had no Ollama branch, and its catch-all silently created a **Groq** repository. Selecting Ollama for transcription therefore uploaded audio to Groq with an empty/invalid key. A second, undocumented case: **AssemblyAI** had the same mismatch on the retranscribe/batch path.\n\nOllama cannot be given a real transcription branch: stock Ollama has no speech-to-text endpoint (its OpenAI-compatible surface covers chat/completions/models/embeddings/responses only; the whisper/STT PR [ollama/ollama#13475](https://github.com/ollama/ollama/pull/13475) was declined upstream). So the fix makes capability filtering and dispatch agree.\n\n## Changes\n\n**Dispatch (AssemblyAI gets a real branch)**\n- `packages/voice-ai/src/assemblyai.utils.ts`: new `assemblyaiTranscribeAudio` — uploads each WAV segment to `/v2/upload`, creates a `/v2/transcript`, polls until `completed` (language detection for auto, `language_code` otherwise; retry on transient upload/create/status failures; bounded polling with tunable `timeoutMs`/`pollIntervalMs`).\n- `apps/desktop/src/repos/transcribe-audio.repo.ts`: new `AssemblyAITranscribeAudioRepo` (60s segments, batch 3, metadata `API • AssemblyAI`).\n- `apps/desktop/src/repos/index.ts`: explicit `assemblyai` and `groq` branches; the catch-all now pushes an explicit warning for stale/unhandled provider selections instead of failing silently.\n\n**Capability (Ollama is generative-only)**\n- `apps/desktop/src/repos/model-provider.repo.ts`: `OllamaModelProviderRepo.supportsTranscriptionModels()` → `false`, `getTranscriptionModels()` → `[]`, with a comment citing the upstream reality. Ollama no longer appears in the transcription picker (add-key dropdown, existing-key list, onboarding).\n\n**Failure-path warning surfacing**\n- `apps/desktop/src/actions/transcribe.actions.ts`: dispatch warnings are logged before the provider call and appended to the error thrown when transcription fails, so the \"no transcription implementation for provider X\" guidance reaches the log/user instead of being abandoned on the throw path.\n\n**Docs**\n- `transcription-modes.md`, `reference/providers.md`, `providers/ollama.md`, `providers/overview.md`, `providers/other-providers.md` updated to describe the resolved state.\n\n## Tests\n- `assemblyai-transcribe-audio.test.ts` (9): explicit-language payload, upload/create/status HTTP failures, missing upload URL, transcript errors, poll timeout, transient upload and status-poll retries, raw-bytes upload headers (Buffer payload).\n- `transcribe.actions.test.ts` (1): end-to-end failure-path test proving the dispatch warning reaches the log and the thrown error when the fallback Groq repo fails.\n- `transcribe-audio.repo.test.ts` (extended): AssemblyAI dispatch selection, mocked upload→create→poll flow, Ollama capability `false`, stale-Ollama-selection warning.\n- Full suite: **21 files / 327 tests pass**; `tsc --noEmit`, oxlint, prettier, docs build (`astro`), and PR28/PR37 contract tests all clean.\n\n## Notes\n- No dependencies added, no lockfile change, no Rust/IPC/persistence changes.\n- The scratch verification doc referenced in earlier turns was removed; it is not part of this PR.\n\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai -->\n## Summary by CodeRabbit\n\n- **New Features**\n  - Added AssemblyAI batch transcription with explicit language selection or automatic detection.\n  - Supports long audio through segmented processing, retries, polling, and timeout handling.\n  - Added stored-audio retranscription through AssemblyAI.\n\n- **Bug Fixes**\n  - Improved warnings and error details when a saved transcription provider is unavailable.\n  - Ollama is no longer offered for speech-to-text; previous Ollama selections fall back to Local transcription.\n\n- **Documentation**\n  - Updated provider capabilities, transcription modes, AssemblyAI workflows, and fallback behavior.\n<!-- end of auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai -->"
