+      "description": "Continues #35 (same work, rebased onto `main` via merge).\r\n\r\nThis branch = PR #35's commits + a merge of `main` (f7f425a) resolving the two conflicts:\r\n- `system/oauth_callback_page.rs` — took main's deletion (whole cloud-auth stack removed as dead code).\r\n- `packages/desktop-native-apis/src/bindings.ts` — took main's removal of the 6 auth wrappers, kept this branch's `cancelTyping(typingId?)` signature.\r\n\r\nVerified command-surface consistency after the merge: `app.rs` = `gen_bindings.rs` = `bindings.ts` = **115/115** commands, no drift.\r\n\r\nOpened from `arena/019ffcf1-mausvoice` because this agent session is pinned to that branch and cannot push to #35's head. Purpose: run CI to green (cargo check/clippy/test could not be run in the previous sandbox — no Rust toolchain).\r\n\r\n## Summary\r\n\r\nThis PR fixes every finding from the v0.1.6 pre-release production audit (commit af92fc0). No band-aids — every change goes to the root cause. All TS checks, lints, and unit tests pass.\r\n\r\n## Major (M1–M4)\r\n\r\n- **M1 `run_terminal_command` shell escape** — Rewrote the command to be fully shell-free: argv is whitespace-tokenized, binaries come from a strict per-platform allow-list (no sh/bash/cmd/powershell), path separators and shell metacharacters are rejected, the environment is cleared, output is capped at 128 KiB/stream with a 15s wall-clock timeout, and Windows sets CREATE_NO_WINDOW.\r\n- **M2 `clear_local_data` privacy leak** — Wipes all 11 user-data tables (added missing `tones`, `app_targets`, `paired_remote_devices`), collects transcription audio paths before the transaction, deletes each referenced WAV after commit with a `starts_with(audio_dir)` guard, sweeps the audio directory for orphan `.wav`s, then runs VACUUM. Also fixed the two TS callers (Clear Local Data dialog + Delete Account) to stop the recorder and key listener before wiping and reloading so in-flight native callbacks don't race an empty DB.\r\n- **M3 `useAsyncData` stale-promise race** — Added a monotonic generation counter: every refresh allocates a new generation, and promise resolution, catch, and the 30s safety timeout only mutate state when their generation still matches the latest one. The timeout is per-call and is cleared on cancel/unmount. Added Vitest coverage for resolve / error / timeout / stale-supersession / cancel.\r\n- **M4 `download_and_open_mac_installer` hardening** — HTTPS-only, host allow-list (github.com + objects.githubusercontent.com), path must end in `.pkg`, 250 MiB response cap, unique nanos+pid temp filename (no URL-derived basename that could escape `$TMPDIR`).\r\n\r\n## Minor / Nitpick / UI\r\n\r\n- **m1** Removed `https://maus-inc.github.io/mausVoice/*` from `remote.urls` IPC grant and replaced the HTTP plugin's wildcard allow-list with an explicit host list (LLM endpoints, Firebase, Deepgram/ElevenLabs/AssemblyAI, GitHub, Sentry, localhost).\r\n- **m2** Per-session typing ids — `simulate_type` returns `{ typingId }` and `cancel_typing(typingId?)` only cancels the matching session so blur/Escape from an older dictation can't cancel a newer typing run. Output router plumbs the id.\r\n- **m3** Added a comment in `db/mod.rs` explaining that migration \"version\" numbers (not filenames) are what tauri_plugin_sql keys off of and that 021/069/070 are intentionally absent.\r\n- **m4** `set_pill_visibility` now validates against `hidden|persistent|while_active` and returns `Result<(), String>`.\r\n- **m6** Replaced `\"csp\": null` with an explicit strict CSP (default-src self; connect-src allow-list of every host the app actually talks to; frame-src limited to YouTube; no object-src; frame-ancestors 'none').\r\n- **m7** Added `AtomicBool` re-entry guards + RAII `ReentryGuard` for `paste`, `simulate_type`, and `play_audio` so rapid-fire invocations return a clear error instead of interleaving clipboard/keystrokes/chimes.\r\n- **m8** `current_timestamp_millis` returns `Err` on clock-before-epoch or overflow instead of `Ok(i64::MAX)`.\r\n- **u6** Removed the Google Fonts `@import` from the local-loopback OAuth callback page; switched to a system sans-serif stack (required by the new CSP, and keeps the page offline-friendly).\r\n- **n3** Added an explanatory doc comment on `detect_connect_address` (RFC 5737 TEST-NET UDP trick — no packet is sent).\r\n- **n4** `set_tray_title` is now `#[cfg(target_os = \"macos\")]`; other platforms early-return Ok (tray titles are AppKit-only).\r\n- **n5** Removed the duplicate `rate <= 0 || samples.length === 0` short-circuit in `storeTranscription` (same check already ran 40 lines above).\r\n- **n6** Replaced the `run_on_main_thread` trampoline's `.unwrap()` calls with descriptive `.expect()`s, and added a `crate::utils::sync::lock` poison-recovering Mutex helper for future use.\r\n- **n7** Added a comment in `main.tsx` noting that the Firebase `apiKey` is a public client-side identifier (per Firebase's own guidance), not a secret.\r\n- **floating_window_create** now validates URL scheme/host (localhost + `/mausVoice/` docs origin only; `tauri:`/`asset:`/`data:` allowed; everything else rejected).\r\n- **bridge_server** Hotkey path segment is validated against a tight charset (`[A-Za-z0-9-_.]`) and length cap (1–64) before being dispatched.\r\n- Updated the power-mode `run_terminal_command` tool description in TS to match the new shell-free reality so the LLM doesn't try to compose pipes/redirections.\r\n\r\n## Tests\r\n\r\n- **Rust** `#[cfg(test)]` modules:\r\n  - `system::storage_repo` — empty path, absolute paths, parent traversal (`../`, `a/../../b`), nested-path acceptance, single-segment acceptance.\r\n  - `system::bridge_server` — `is_valid_hotkey_name` rejects empty, path traversal, spaces/metachars/query-strings; accepts normal ids.\r\n  - `commands` — terminal-command allow-list enforcement (empty, absolute paths, shells, metachars rejected; allow-listed binaries accepted); floating-window URL validation (localhost/docs allowed, evil origins / file:// / javascript: rejected); current_timestamp smoke check.\r\n- **TypeScript** `apps/desktop/src/hooks/async.hooks.test.ts` — 5 tests covering resolve, reject, timeout, stale-promise supersession, and cancel-clears-timeout.\r\n\r\n## Verification\r\n\r\n- `pnpm -F desktop tsc --noEmit` — 0 errors\r\n- `pnpm -F desktop oxlint src` — 0 warnings / 0 errors\r\n- `pnpm -F desktop vitest run src` — 313/313 unit tests pass (including the 5 new for `useAsyncData`)\r\n- `cargo check` was not run because the Rust toolchain is not installed in this sandbox; the code has been carefully reviewed for import/cfg/mutability correctness.\r\n\r\nBreaking changes for clients:\r\n\r\n- `simulate_type` now returns `{ typingId: number }` instead of `null`.\r\n- `set_pill_visibility` now returns `Result<null, string>` instead of `void`; existing call sites already `.catch()` it.\r\n- `cancel_typing` accepts an optional `typingId` parameter; calling it with no argument preserves the prior \"cancel active session\" semantics.\r\n"
