+      "description": "## Summary\n\nDocs site fixes + a working Homebrew tap that auto-publishes on every release.\n\n### Docs\n- Logo + favicon swapped to canonical mausVoice branding; deleted stray `favicon.svg` / `houston.webp` / `icon.svg`.\n- Starlight theme switched to monochrome black/white (was teal) and un-locked from force-dark; proper light theme added.\n- Hero button variants restored (removed overriding `.sl-link-button` rules).\n- Factual fixes: local default model is `tiny` (~77 MB) in `transcription-models/`; API mode is provider-agnostic; post-processing is **API / Off**; dictionary example row uses Deepgram.\n- **Linux install docs fixed**: removed the fake `mausvoice.github.io` apt/rpm repos (no such infra exists) and pointed Debian/Ubuntu users at the real `.deb` + AppImage.\n\n### Homebrew tap (real, auto-publishing)\n- `homebrew-mausvoice/Casks/mausvoice-desktop.rb` — cask template (source of truth in this repo), pins latest release `0.1.5`, `sha256 :no_check` until first automated publish pins it.\n- `scripts/ci/render-cask.mjs` — stamps version + SHA-256 into the cask.\n- `release.yml` gains a `publish-cask` job: on every release it downloads the DMG, computes the checksum, renders the cask, and pushes to `maus-inc/homebrew-mausvoice`.\n\nMirror of this work: PR was authored via handoff doc from a prior agent session; verified against live remote before execution.\n\n## Test plan\n- [x] `pnpm run build` + `pnpm run check-types` in `apps/docs` (passed on branch)\n- [x] `release.yml` valid YAML; `publish-cask` job present\n- [x] `render-cask.mjs` stamps version + sha256 correctly\n- [x] Tap repo `maus-inc/homebrew-mausvoice` seeded on `main` with the `0.1.5` cask\n\n## Outstanding (requires maintainer, not agent)\n- D.3: grant `RELEASE_TOKEN` **Contents: write** on `maus-inc/homebrew-mausvoice` so `publish-cask` can push.\n- D.4: revoke the PATs pasted in the original chat (treat as compromised).\n- D.5: `brew tap maus-inc/mausvoice && brew install --cask mausvoice-desktop && brew audit --cask mausvoice-desktop` end-to-end (needs a macOS runner).\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai -->\n## Summary by CodeRabbit\n\n* **New Features**\n  * Linux releases now include downloadable AppImage and `.deb` packages.\n  * macOS users can install the universal app through Homebrew.\n  * Release downloads now show clearer platform-specific formats.\n\n* **Documentation**\n  * Updated Linux and macOS installation instructions.\n  * Expanded transcription guidance for local Whisper and hosted or self-hosted providers.\n  * Clarified independent post-processing configuration and model options.\n  * Refreshed documentation styling, branding, examples, favicon, and download guidance.\n<!-- end of auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai -->"
