+      "description": "## Summary\n\nThis PR follows up on PR #17 with documentation site work and CI hardening for `mausVoice`:\n\n- **Removed the Enterprise documentation tree** (`apps/docs/src/content/docs/enterprise/`, 28 files) and stripped its sidebar + dead links from `apps/docs/astro.config.mjs`, `apps/docs/public/llms.txt`, and the `getting-started/introduction.md` nav.\n- **Restyle the docs site to match the product landing page** (`index.html`): dark base, teal accent (`--sl-color-accent: hsl(170 15% 45%)`), Satoshi/Inter/JetBrains Mono/TAN-PARADISO fonts, 4px radius, liquid-glass buttons/cards, forced dark mode.\n- **Added the four brand fonts** to `apps/docs/public/docs/assets/fonts/` so the docs build serves them at `/mausVoice/docs/assets/fonts/` (the CSS `@font-face` URLs are base-aware).\n- **Added a hero** to the introduction page mirroring the landing page hero.\n- **Pointed the landing page \"Documentation\" nav** at the live docs site instead of the GitHub source tree.\n- **Expanded PR #28 contract tests** (13 passing) covering reset IPC execution, frontend reset event emission, ring-alpha zero-crossing invalidation, and fork secret isolation.\n- **Hardened the Windows desktop build** against OOM (`--max-old-space-size=4096` + `--concurrency=1` on `windows-latest` only).\n- **Added a Pages deployment job** (`test-docs.yml`) — Option B: keeps `index.html` at the site root and publishes the built docs under `/mausVoice/`, assembling landing-page assets (marketing, docs, sitemap, robots) plus an artifact smoke test.\n\n## Validation\n\n- `apps/docs` Prettier, Oxlint, `check-types`, and `build` all pass locally (15 pages, sitemap created).\n- Contract test `scripts/ci/pr28-contracts.test.mjs`: 13/13 pass.\n- Font files verified to land at `dist/docs/assets/fonts/`; artifact assembly + smoke test verified locally.\n- **Action required to publish**: repo **Settings → Pages → Build & deployment → Source = \"GitHub Actions\"** (currently `legacy`/`main`/`/`). Until flipped, the `deploy` job cannot publish.\n\n## Notes\n\n- PR #17's GTK/X11 drop-position bug and its stale Enterprise `llms.txt` links are tracked on PR #17, not here.\n- SonarCloud `S8233` (workflow-level write permissions) was resolved by scoping `pages`/`id-token` to the `deploy` job.\n"
