+      "description": "## What this is\n\nCodeRabbit's review on **PR #22** ran against PR22's old `main` base and scanned 56 files — but 9 of the 10 findings point at code that belongs to **PR #17** (theme/pill/animation/dom-guard work), not PR22. PR22 is a revert + CI + branding-URL PR; none of the flagged files are in its diff.\n\nThis PR carries those findings as fixes, branched from PR17's head so they land in the right place.\n\n## Changes (10 findings, all verified against PR17's tree)\n\n**Rust — pill crates**\n- `pill_process.rs` — log a warning when `notify_reset_position` finds no managed pill process (was silent `Ok`)\n- `rust_gtk_pill/draw.rs` — **Critical**: remove unbalanced `cr.restore()` on the zero-progress early return (it popped a state `draw_all` had pushed)\n- `rust_gtk_pill/x11.rs` — idle anchor now uses `draw_width`/`draw_height` (draw canvas) instead of toplevel allocation, matching the other `pill_pos_on_monitor` call sites\n- `rust_gtk_pill/constants.rs` + `rust_windows_pill/constants.rs` — dedupe the 11 ring/drag tuning constants into `rust_pill_shared` (single source of truth)\n- `rust_macos_pill/app.rs` + `rust_windows_pill/pill.rs` — normalize clamp bounds (`max >= min`) so a small visible frame can't push the pill off screen\n\n**TypeScript**\n- `Root.tsx` — **Major/security**: stop rendering raw `error.message` to the UI; use a generic localized `FormattedMessage` (logger category entry preserved)\n- `dom-guard.utils.ts` — **Major**: gate the `Node` prototype patch to Windows only (`isWindows()`) so other platforms keep native prototypes; wrap the `appendChild` fallback so it can't throw uncaught\n- `AnimateIn.tsx` — add a stable `key` to the animated `motion.div` so `AnimatePresence` runs the exit animation; move the `AnimateSwitch` doc block above its declaration\n\n## Verification\n- `rust_pill_shared` + `rust_windows_pill` clippy: **pass** (GTK crate can't compile on this Windows box — missing Linux `gio-2.0` system lib — but the