+      "description": "## Summary\nImplements the issue #10 / CodeRabbit coding plan for the desktop app (8 phases).\n\n- **Pill overlays** (all three native crates — `rust_macos_pill`, `rust_gtk_pill`, `rust_windows_pill`, duplicated per platform): silver-white long-press outline; capsule-true corner radius derived from live geometry (no more morph into a squircle); spring-driven waveform→paused crossfade with no bounce; Pause/Cancel now hide during `Loading`/`Idle` and fade out.\n- **Title bar**: grants the missing `core:window:*` permissions so controls actually fire; adds invisible resize grips for the frameless window; swaps control glyphs to lucide via `MorphNavIcon` with a minimize/maximize morph; instruments `WindowEvent::Moved` to triage the \"can't drag past a point\" report.\n- **Theme**: cream-paper light + neutral onyx dark ladders on shared tokens; removes hardcoded blue-tinted literals; brand logo/wordmark invert correctly; pre-hydration canvas matches `level0` (no launch flash).\n- **Dashboard/home**: flattens the dashboard surface, drops the orange/blue promo gradients, wires the home header via `useSetHeaderContent`.\n- **Microphone enumeration**: stops merging distinct devices that report the same name (cpal has no stable identity). Disambiguates with an ordinal suffix; the first keeps its bare name so existing preferences still resolve; the device cache stores the same label the UI selects. Also exposes the descriptor as `camelCase` so `isDefault` is no longer silently `undefined`.\n- **AI settings menus**: `SegmentedControl` gains an opt-in `align=\"center\"` prop; the three AI menus centre the mode selector without centring the controls below. Shared active-row treatment (accent rail + blue tint + check glyph) for the OpenRouter and local Whisper model lists.\n- **Icons**: `icon.icns` was a 16×16 PNG renamed to `.icns` (the blurry macOS icon). The container is now assembled directly with the full `iconutil` frame set including Retina slots; `verify()` parses it back and the existing `--check` CI gate fails on any fake ICNS. Regenerated icons are pixel-identical, so only `icon.icns` changed.\n\n## Verification\n- `apps/desktop` `tsc --noEmit`, `oxlint`, and `prettier --check` all pass.\n- `node scripts/generate-app-icons.mjs --check` passes and fails on a renamed-PNG icns (gate confirmed).\n- Rust could not be compiled in-sandbox (no `cargo`/`rustup`); changes are source-correct by inspection and brace-balanced across all touched crates.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude](https://claude.com/)\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai -->\n## Summary by CodeRabbit\n\n* **New Features**\n  * Added frameless-window resizing and improved title-bar controls, including localized labels and animated icons.\n  * Added clearer microphone device names and more reliable device selection.\n  * Added smoother recording-to-paused transitions across desktop platforms.\n  * Hidden dictation controls now reappear automatically when activity starts.\n\n* **Improvements**\n  * Introduced refreshed warm light and neutral dark themes.\n  * Improved selected-item indicators and segmented-control alignment.\n  * Added reduced-motion support for onboarding animations.\n  * Updated translations and accessibility-related messaging across supported languages.\n\n* **Bug Fixes**\n  * Prevented theme flashes during startup.\n  * Improved pill sizing, outlines, and control visibility during state changes.\n<!-- end of auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai -->"
