+      "description": "## What changed?\n\nFollow-up to `71b40ec`. That commit's pill changes **never reached users, because the Windows pill crate did not compile.**\n\n`draw_paused()` was declared `gfx: &Gfx` but calls `save()`, `clip_rounded_rect()` and `restore()` — all of which need `&mut Gfx`. `prepare-sidecars.mjs` builds the pill with `allowFailure: true`, so the build stayed green and the app packaged a **stale pill binary**. That single defect explains four separate bug reports at once: long-press unchanged, drag not working, pause control not moved, and pill-driven dictation controls misbehaving.\n\n### Release blockers\n\n| Report | Root cause | Fix |\n|---|---|---|\n| Long-press / drag / pause \"unchanged\" | Windows pill crate failed to compile; failure was swallowed | Fix the `&Gfx`/`&mut Gfx` error; fail the sidecar build loudly on release/CI |\n| Pill keeps moving after mouse release | No OS pointer capture anywhere | `SetCapture` on arm, released on mouse-up + `WM_CAPTURECHANGED`, plus a `GetAsyncKeyState` fallback each tick |\n| Audio / dictation controls unreliable | Pause + cancel overlapped the pill body by 7px, so their click regions swallowed presses meant for the pill | Shared layout helpers place both controls fully outside the pill |\n| Light mode not applied | 18 `theme.palette.mode` branches in `styleOverrides` resolve once at theme build | All converted to `theme.applyStyles(\"dark\", ...)` |\n| Bluish tints | Hard-coded literals, incl. a literal `backgroundColor: \"blue\"` | Replaced with palette tokens |\n| Title-bar double-click dead | No handler existed in either revision | Explicit `onDoubleClick` (frameless windows don't synthesise it) |\n| Taskbar icon black background | `icon.ico` had a single 16×16 frame; earlier frames were fully opaque, squaring off the rounded tile | `scripts/generate-app-icons.mjs` — alpha preserved, 7-frame ICO, self-verifying |\n\n### Also included\n\n- **Long press** 1.5s → 0.45s with a 0.12s hold delay, so a quick click never flashes the outline. Shared `long_press_progress()` + unit tests.\n- **Drag anchoring** via grab offset, so the pill no longer jumps to centre itself on the cursor.\n- **GTK parity** — the pause control was missing there entirely.\n- **Docs** — ADR on why the app does not start elevated, plus a design-system baseline.\n- **Version** bumped `0.1.0` → `0.1.2` (incl. both `Cargo.lock` files, which the `--locked` release builds require).\n- **Publisher** set to `Owie Emmanuel`. It was never declared, so Tauri fell back to the second element of the identifier — installers were shipping as `mausinc`.\n\n### Two decisions I'd flag for review\n\n1. **Windows accessibility reports `Authorized`.** The suggested `Restricted` would have disabled dictation on every standard install, since that state gates both the key listener and the blocking permissions dialog. Reasoning is documented in the ADR.\n2. **The icon tile is intentional.** The black rounded tile is the artwork; the bug was *flattened alpha*, not the tile. Stripping it would make a light glyph invisible on light taskbars.\n\n## How is it tested?\n\n- [x] Automated tests\n- [x] Manual verification\n- [x] Code inspection\n\n- TypeScript error count **identical before and after (35, all pre-existing** — unbuilt `@maus-inc/functions`, not from this branch).\n- **238 unit tests pass**; prettier and oxlint clean.\n- Rust unit tests added for `long_press_progress()` and the control-layout helpers.\n- Drag state machine simulated exhaustively, including the exact *\"keeps moving after I let go\"* case (missed mouse-up, stolen capture, early release).\n- Icon output verified programmatically: 7 frames, 32bpp, transparent corners. The verifier was tested against the old broken `.ico` and correctly rejects it.\n\n### ⚠️ Needs a maintainer\n\n- **No Rust toolchain in the sandbox** (network-blocked), so the pill changes are reviewed and brace-checked but **not compiler-verified**. Please run `./scripts/verify-native-pills.sh` on a machine with `cargo`.\n- **CI cannot be wired up from here** — the GitHub App lacks `workflows` permission. `scripts/verify-native-pills.sh` contains the exact snippet to paste into `.github/workflows/lint-desktop.yml`. **Adding that step is what prevents this class of silent breakage recurring**, since the pill crates are currently linted by nothing.\n- The Windows *\"Verified publisher\"* in SmartScreen/UAC comes from the Azure Trusted Signing certificate, not this repo — worth aligning separately.\n\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai -->\n\n## Summary by CodeRabbit\n\n* **New Features**\n  * Added tray controls to show or hide the dictation pill.\n  * Added a “Skip for now” option during accessibility onboarding.\n  * Reduced long-press activation time and improved pill dragging and control placement across platforms.\n  * Added consistent themed styling, smoother theme transitions, and improved title-bar maximize behavior.\n  * Added automated app icon generation and validation.\n\n* **Bug Fixes**\n  * Improved pill visibility synchronization and tooltip positioning.\n  * Improved Windows drag behavior and recovery when pointer capture is lost.\n  * Desktop and installer versions updated to 0.1.2.\n\n* **Documentation**\n  * Added guidance for unelevated startup and shared design-system standards.\n\n<!-- end of auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai -->"
