+      "description": "## Summary\n\nResolves all release-blocking bugs found during v1 testing, plus UX polish and animation refinement.\n\n## Changes\n\n### P0 — Accessibility Gate (Release Blocker)\n- Remove Windows elevation gate: accessibility always returns authorized on Windows\n- Skip a11y onboarding step on non-macOS platforms (goes directly to keybindings)\n- Fresh non-admin Windows installs can now complete onboarding\n\n### P0 — Pill Drag Redesign (Release Blocker)\n- Hold-to-drag duration: 5.0s to 0.8s (all platforms)\n- Replaced blue ring with pill-perimeter outline progress\n- Skip balloon pop, enter drag directly after hold\n- 100ms delay before showing outline (normal clicks unaffected)\n- Position persistence: pill stays where dropped (all platforms)\n- Fixed GTK/Wayland pill snapping back to center on release\n\n### P1 — Theme Toggle and Propagation\n- Replaced three-state cycle with explicit dropdown menu (Light/Dark/System + checkmark)\n- Added MorphIcon animation for smooth Sun/Moon/Monitor morphing\n- Fixed title bar text adapting to light/dark mode\n- Removed decorative rounded header surface\n\n### P2 — Pause/Cancel Controls\n- Moved pause/resume button to left side of pill (all platforms)\n- Tightened pause bar spacing\n- Replaced frozen waveform bars with static loading bar\n- Shortened pause toast message and duration\n\n### P2 — Onboarding and Branding\n- Marked Title and Company as optional in user details form\n- Regenerated all icon PNGs and ICOs from transparent source\n- Generated Windows tile icons\n- Added credit line in settings footer\n\n## Verification\n- TypeScript tsc passes (5 pre-existing errors unrelated)\n- Prettier formatted\n- Constants cross-referenced: no missing symbols\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai -->\n\n## Summary by CodeRabbit\n\n* **New Features**\n  * Choose Light, Dark, or System theme from a dedicated menu.\n  * Onboarding now guides macOS users through accessibility permissions and marks profile fields as optional.\n  * Settings now includes an attribution footer with an external link.\n  * Dictation controls provide clearer long-press feedback and support more direct dragging.\n  * Pill positions persist after being moved and remain within screen boundaries.\n\n* **Bug Fixes**\n  * Improved accessibility permission handling on Windows.\n  * Updated paused-state visuals and shortened pause notifications.\n  * Simplified and refined title bar and header presentation.\n\n<!-- end of auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai -->"
