+# AI-agent contribution review
+
+**Repository:** `maus-inc/mausVoice`  
+**Collection:** 2026-11-10 17:46 UTC; GitHub reports 168 merged PRs, all included.  
+**Code snapshot reviewed:** `16ef7e11b561a2d3d080027ccb562530b98e64e6` on the session branch, not a reconstructed tip of every PR's target branch.  
+**Inventory:** [merged-pr-inventory.json](merged-pr-inventory.json) contains every PR's number, title, author, UTC merge date, complete description as returned by GitHub, and all returned changed paths and statuses, ordered by merge date. The [discussion and commit index](discussion-commit-index.json) links to individual reviews, inline review comments, issue comments and commits for each PR. PR links below point to primary evidence.
+
+## Summary
+
+The 168 merged PRs include 120 authored by identifiable GitHub App accounts: 111 Arena, five Kilo Code, three CodeRabbit and one DeepSource; another 48 were authored by a human account, whose use of AI cannot be inferred reliably from the account name. Agent-authored work spans product features, cross-platform Rust and TypeScript fixes, security hardening, tests, CI and documentation, with substantial review-follow-up activity. Among those 120 PRs, 85 touched paths matching the test-file heuristic, and 43 had “review”, “audit”, or “finding” in the title; these are scope indicators, not quality or causality measurements. Evidence also shows material mistakes in feature and cleanup heads, including fabricated transcription, broken provider access and regressions in a subsequently reverted static-analysis sweep. Stacked PRs, environment restrictions and unexecuted release/model tests complicate attribution and verification; the analysis below separates head-level findings from confirmed post-merge behavior.
+
+## Method and scope
+
+GitHub's merged-PR list and search count both returned 168, fewer than the requested 200; PRs merged into non-default branches are included. For each PR, paginated GitHub endpoints supplied changed files, review comments, reviews, issue comments and commits; the inventory preserves the requested fields. File-list observations cover the full inventory; detailed code and discussion inspection was targeted to representative, evidence-rich PRs and follow-up chains, **not an exhaustive line-by-line audit of all 10,258 PR-file appearances**. Reported test results are PR-author claims unless stated otherwise; at the time of the historical review no build, runtime tests or platform smoke tests were independently run; subsequent local verification of the prevention changes is recorded below.
+
+The discussion and commit index covers 2,801 review records, 4,202 inline review comments, 1,784 issue comments and 2,319 PR-commit appearances across all 168 PRs. Among the 120 App-authored PRs, 102 have at least one review record and 87 have at least one inline review comment; those are records, not unique reviewers, confirmed defects or proof of independent review. Comments may have been created after merge, and the index does not establish whether a thread is resolved.
+
+The agent denominator is the 120 App-authored PRs, not all work possibly assisted by AI. Counts are PR counts, not distinct implementations: stacked PRs often contain overlapping files and commits. Test-path heuristic: a path contains a `test`, `tests` or `__tests__` directory, or `.test.`/`.spec.` in the filename; it does not capture every inline Rust test or prove that tests were added or executed. Documentation means a `.md` path or a path under `docs/`; workflow means `.github/workflows/`. Title counts use case-insensitive substring matches, not semantic classification.
+
+## Patterns
+
+| Pattern | Frequency | Example PRs | Impact |
