+
+## Recommendations
+
+1. **P0 — Protect release paths:** require packaged desktop startup and provider smoke tests for CSP, vendor chunking and native transport on relevant platforms. Track unchecked manual steps as release blockers, not as implied passes ([#58](https://github.com/maus-inc/mausVoice/pull/58), [#67](https://github.com/maus-inc/mausVoice/pull/67)).
+2. **P0 — Validate actual ASR outcomes:** run scheduled, pinned real-model inference tests with representative audio and expected model-dependent results, alongside fast invalid-artifact tests. Ensure integration targets compile in CI; [#42's review](https://github.com/maus-inc/mausVoice/pull/42#discussion_r3787016940) warned that `cargo test --lib` excluded the separate integration target.
+3. **P1 — Limit refactor blast radius:** split static-analysis fixes by component and verify semantic invariants, including Python import smoke tests, provider JSON-schema contracts and streaming metadata/tool-call behavior ([#107](https://github.com/maus-inc/mausVoice/pull/107), [#108](https://github.com/maus-inc/mausVoice/pull/108)).
+4. **P1 — Make stacked review auditable:** require each PR to identify its base, dependent fixes, tested commit and outstanding findings; check the final target tree and avoid counting overlapping PRs as independent changes ([#105](https://github.com/maus-inc/mausVoice/pull/105), [#118](https://github.com/maus-inc/mausVoice/pull/118), [#121](https://github.com/maus-inc/mausVoice/pull/121)).
+5. **P2 — Improve environments and signal:** provision native toolchains and workflow permissions before assignment; use deterministic tests for ordinary CI and dedicated runners for performance ([#103](https://github.com/maus-inc/mausVoice/pull/103), [#107](https://github.com/maus-inc/mausVoice/pull/107), [#121](https://github.com/maus-inc/mausVoice/pull/121)).
+
+## Prevention work started
+
+- **False-green ASR tests:** the transcription workflow now runs the Whisper test explicitly and offers the large ONNX tests as a manual Linux opt-in. The selected ONNX tests fail when their model-download opt-in is missing rather than returning success. A small runner checks that each exact ignored test exists before executing it, so a renamed or removed test cannot silently select zero tests. See `packages/rust_transcription/README.md` for commands and costs. This is an on-demand smoke test, not a scheduled or release-gating real-model benchmark; nonempty transcript output alone does not establish transcript accuracy or reject a fabricated constant. The bundled `test.wav` has no verified transcript identified in its history. An offline PocketSphinx run produced the tentative hypothesis “that,” not authoritative ground truth; no output-matching assertion was added without fixture provenance and real-model validation. A reviewed speech fixture with a transcript and model-appropriate tolerance remains necessary. For future evaluation, [Whisper's upstream test](https://github.com/openai/whisper/blob/main/tests/test_transcribe.py) uses its JFK audio and checks several recognizable phrases; licensing, conversion, and behavior across this project's models still require verification. Two distinct verified inputs are needed to detect a constant that happens to match one fixture.
+- **Python import and translation regressions:** `.github/workflows/test-python-tools.yml` installs the pinned developer-tool requirements and runs credential-free CLI/import and translation-file tests on relevant push and PR changes. The test suite rejected a scratch-copy reproduction of #107's self-referential import error. The old TypeScript writer also changed `username` when asked to update the later key `name`; parsing and writing now share exact object entries and reject duplicate keys or unsupported object syntax before writing. Tests cover the collision, comments, rollback and escaping. The web locale directory is absent in this checkout, so this parser was validated with fixtures rather than production locale files; missing translation keys still fail instead of being inserted. A local malformed-whitespace check took about 0.16, 1.4 and 14.65 ms for 8,000, 80,000 and 800,000 repetitions, respectively; this is a diagnostic, not a CI performance guarantee. The suite does not exercise real provider calls.
+- **Empty pnpm filter false greens:** with the pinned pnpm 10.34.5, a nonexistent `--filter` returned exit 0 while printing “No projects matched”; adding `--fail-if-no-match` returned exit 1. Direct filtered pnpm commands in workflows now use the fail-closed form, including release signing; all six referenced package names resolved locally. A lightweight hygiene check prevents reintroducing the specific direct `pnpm --filter` spelling. It is a textual check, not a general shell or Turbo filter analyzer, and hosted workflows were not run.
+- **Shared retries and test coverage:** the retry helper previously used `Retry-After` only when the caller had wrapped an SDK error as `HttpError`; raw SDK 429s retried after the 20 ms fallback even when a hint was present. It now reads existing normalized header handling for delay calculation while preserving the originally thrown error, the cancellation behavior and the interactive two-second cap. Synthetic raw SDK errors and an OpenAI SDK request with mocked fetch verify the wait. A synthetic SDK error with an unreadable optional header bag exposed an additional failure: normalizing the hint could mask the actual error and stop retries. Header reading now falls back safely, including to `response.headers` if the first bag throws; focused normalization and retry tests pass. Real SDKs exhibiting that header behavior were not identified. Hints longer than the cap are deliberately not honored in full. The utilities and agent package unit suites were not run by any workflow; they now run in the existing desktop-unit workflow after its dependency build. Locally their 141 and 43 tests passed, respectively; hosted CI has not run. The existing desktop-unit workflow runs on matching branch pushes, not `pull_request` events, so fork-only pull requests are not covered by this change.
